DG.put("chaubees-avtaar-2/3",{"n":3,"title":"ਅਥ ਨਿਹਕਲੰਕੀ ਚੌਬੀਸਵੌ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਕਥਨੰ","title_roman":"Ath nihaklankee chaubeesvau avtaar kathnan","page":726,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[1],"number_text":"੧।","page":726,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਬ ਮੈ ਮਹਾ ਸੁਧ ਮਤਿ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ। ਕਹੋ ਕਥਾ ਚਿਤੁ ਲਾਇ ਬਿਚਰਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Ab mai mahaa sudh mati kari kai | kaho kathaa chitu laai bichri kai |","meaning_en":"Now, with a very pure mind, I tell the story, setting my heart on it and reflecting,","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਉਬੀਸਵੋ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰਾ। ਤਾ ਕਰ ਕਹੋ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਗ ਸੁਧਾਰਾ। ੧।","roman":"Chaubeesvo kalkee avtaaraa | taa kar kaho prasang sudhaaraa | 1 |","meaning_en":"the twenty-fourth incarnation, Kalki; I tell his episode in proper form.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[2],"number_text":"੨।","page":726,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਰਾਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਹੋਤ ਜਬ ਧਰਣੀ। ਪਾਪ ਗ੍ਰਸਤ ਕਛੁ ਜਾਤ ਨ ਬਰਣੀ।","roman":"Bhaaraakrit hot jab dharnee | paap grasat kachhu jaat na barnee |","meaning_en":"When the earth becomes weighed down, so seized by sin that it cannot be described,","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਤਨ ਹੋਤ ਉਤਪਾਤਾ। ਪੁਤ੍ਰਹਿ ਸੇਜਿ ਸੋਵਤ ਲੈ ਮਾਤਾ। ੨।","roman":"Bhaati bhaati tan hot utpaataa | putrahi seji sovat lai maataa | 2 |","meaning_en":"all kinds of disorders arise in bodies; the mother takes her son and sleeps with him on the bed.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[3],"number_text":"੩।","page":726,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਤਾ ਪਿਤਾ ਤਨ ਰਮਤ ਨਿਸੰਕਾ। ਭਗਨੀ ਭਰਤ ਭ੍ਰਾਤ ਕਹੁ ਅੰਕਾ।","roman":"Sutaa pitaa tan ramat nisankaa | bhagnee bharat bhraat kahu ankaa |","meaning_en":"The daughter enjoys her father's body without shame; the sister takes her brother into her embrace as husband.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਗਨੀ ਭਰਤ ਭ੍ਰਾਤ ਕਹੁ ਅੰਕਾ: read as 'the sister takes the brother as husband into her lap'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭ੍ਰਾਤ ਬਹਨ ਤਨ ਕਰਤ ਬਿਹਾਰਾ। ਇਸਤ੍ਰੀ ਤਜੀ ਸਕਲ ਸੰਸਾਰਾ। ੩।","roman":"Bhraat bahan tan karat bihaaraa | istree tajee sakal sansaaraa | 3 |","meaning_en":"Brother sports with sister's body; the whole world has abandoned its own wives.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[4],"number_text":"੪।","page":726,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕਰ ਬਰਣ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਸਭ ਹੋਈ। ਏਕ ਗ੍ਯਾਤ ਕੋ ਰਹਾ ਨ ਕੋਈ।","roman":"Sankar baran prajaa sabh hoee | ek gyaat ko rahaa na koee |","meaning_en":"All the people have become of mixed castes; not one remains of a single known lineage.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਏਕ ਗ੍ਯਾਤ: read as 'one (distinct) caste/kin known'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਬਿਭਚਾਰ ਫਸੀ ਬਰ ਨਾਰੀ। ਧਰਮ ਰੀਤ ਕੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਬਿਸਾਰੀ। ੪।","roman":"Ati bibhchaar phasee bar naaree | dharam reet kee preeti bisaaree | 4 |","meaning_en":"Fine women are caught in great adultery; they have forgotten love for the way of dharma.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[5],"number_text":"੫।","page":726,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਝੂਠ ਅਮਸਿਆ ਭਈ। ਸਾਚ ਕਲਾ ਸਸਿ ਕੀ ਦੁਰ ਗਈ।","roman":"Ghari ghari jhooth amsiaa bhaee | saach kalaa sasi kee dur gaee |","meaning_en":"In every house falsehood has become like the new-moon night; truth, like the moon's phase, has hidden away.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਹੋਨ ਲਗੇ ਉਤਪਾਤਾ। ਭੋਗਤ ਪੂਤ ਸੇਜਿ ਚੜਿ ਮਾਤਾ। ੫।","roman":"Jah tah hon lage utpaataa | bhogat poot seji chari maataa | 5 |","meaning_en":"Everywhere disorders began to arise; the son climbs on the bed and enjoys his mother.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[6],"number_text":"੬।","page":726,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਢੂੰਢਤ ਸਾਚ ਨ ਕਤਹੂੰ ਪਾਯਾ। ਝੂਠ ਹੀ ਸੰਗ ਸਬੋ ਚਿਤ ਲਾਯਾ।","roman":"Dhoondhat saach na kathoon paayaa | jhooth hee sang sabo chit laayaa |","meaning_en":"Searching, truth is found nowhere; everyone has set their mind on falsehood alone.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਮਤ ਹੋਈ। ਸਾਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਿਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਛੁਐ ਨ ਕੋਈ। ੬।","roman":"Bhinn bhinn grih grih mat hoee | saasatr simrit chhuai na koee | 6 |","meaning_en":"In each house there is a different creed; no one touches the Shastras or Smritis.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[7],"number_text":"੭।","page":726,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਿੰਦਵ ਕੋਈ ਨ ਤੁਰਕਾ ਰਹਿ ਹੈ। ਭਿਨ ਭਿਨ ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਮਤ ਗਹਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Hindav koee na turkaa rahi hai | bhin bhin ghari ghari mat gahi hai |","meaning_en":"No one will remain Hindu or Turk (Muslim); in each house they will hold a different creed.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਏਕ ਕੇ ਪੰਥ ਨ ਚਲਿ ਹੈ। ਏਕ ਏਕ ਕੀ ਬਾਤ ਉਥਲਿ ਹੈ। ੭।","roman":"Ek ek ke panth na chali hai | ek ek kee baat uthli hai | 7 |","meaning_en":"None will walk on another's path; each will overturn the other's word.","page":726,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[8],"number_text":"੮।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਰਾਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਧਰਾ ਸਬ ਹੁਇ ਹੈ। ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਪਰ ਚਲੈ ਨ ਕੁਇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Bhaaraakrit dharaa sab hui hai | dharam karam par chalai na kui hai |","meaning_en":"The whole earth will be weighed down; no one will walk in the duties of dharma.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਅਉਰ ਅਉਰ ਮਤ ਹੋਈ। ਏਕ ਧਰਮ ਪਰ ਚਲੈ ਨ ਕੋਈ। ੮।","roman":"Ghari ghari aur aur mat hoee | ek dharam par chalai na koee | 8 |","meaning_en":"In each house there will be yet another creed; no one will walk on one faith.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[9],"number_text":"੯।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਮਤੋ ਏਕ ਨ ਚਲ ਹੈ ਕੋਇ।","roman":"Bhinn bhinn ghari ghari mato ek na chal hai koi |","meaning_en":"Different creeds in every house; no one will walk in one way.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਭਯੋ ਧਰਮ ਨ ਕਤਹੂੰ ਹੋਇ। ੯।","roman":"Paap prachur jah tah bhayo dharam na kathoon hoi | 9 |","meaning_en":"Sin has become rampant everywhere; dharma is found nowhere.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[10],"number_text":"੧੦।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕਰ ਬਰਣ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਸਭ ਹੋਈ। ਛਤ੍ਰੀ ਜਗਤਿ ਨ ਦੇਖੀਐ ਕੋਈ।","roman":"Sankar baran prajaa sabh hoee | chhatree jagti na dekheeai koee |","meaning_en":"All the people have become of mixed castes; no Kshatriya is seen in the world.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਏਕ ਐਸੇ ਮਤ ਕੈ ਹੈ। ਜਾ ਤੇ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤਿ ਸੂਦ੍ਰਤਾ ਹੋਇ ਹੈ।੧੦।","roman":"Ek ek aise mat kai hai | jaa te praapti soodrataa hoi hai | 10 |","meaning_en":"Each will make such a creed that from it comes the state of a Shudra.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[11],"number_text":"੧੧।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਿੰਦੂ ਤੁਰਕ ਮਤ ਦੁਹੂੰ ਪ੍ਰਹਰਿ ਕਰਿ। ਚਲਿ ਹੈ ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਮਤ ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ।","roman":"Hindoo turak mat duhoon prahri kari | chali hai bhinn bhinn mat ghari ghari |","meaning_en":"Casting aside both the Hindu and the Turk creeds, different creeds will run in every house.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪ੍ਰਹਰਿ: read as 'striking down / discarding'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਏਕ ਕੇ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਨ ਗਹਿ ਹੈ। ਏਕ ਏਕ ਕੇ ਸੰਗਿ ਨ ਰਹਿ ਹੈ। ੧੧।","roman":"Ek ek ke mantr na gahi hai | ek ek ke sangi na rahi hai | 11 |","meaning_en":"None will take the other's counsel; none will stay in the other's company.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[12],"number_text":"੧੨।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਪੁ ਆਪੁ ਪਾਰਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਕਹੈ ਹੈ। ਨੀਚ ਊਚ ਕਹ ਸੀਸ ਨ ਨੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Aapu aapu paarbraham kahai hai | neech ooch kah sees na nai hai |","meaning_en":"Each will call himself the Supreme Brahm; high will not bow the head to low, nor low to high.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨੀਚ ਊਚ ਕਹ ਸੀਸ ਨ ਨੈ ਹੈ: possibly 'the low will not bow to the high'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਏਕ ਮਤ ਇਕ ਇਕ ਧਾਮਾ। ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਹੋਇ ਬੈਠ ਹੈ ਰਾਮਾ। ੧੨।","roman":"Ek ek mat ik ik dhaamaa | ghari ghari hoi baith hai raamaa | 12 |","meaning_en":"Each with his own creed, each with his own abode; in every house a 'Ram' will sit enthroned.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਾਮਾ: read as each person setting himself up as God; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[13],"number_text":"੧੩।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੜਿ ਹੈ ਕੋਇ ਨ ਭੂਲਿ ਪੁਰਾਨਾ। ਕੋਊ ਨ ਪਕਰ ਹੈ ਪਾਨਿ ਕੁਰਾਨਾ।","roman":"Pari hai koi na bhooli puraanaa | ko'oo na pakar hai paani kuraanaa |","meaning_en":"No one will even by mistake read the Puranas; no one will take the Quran in hand.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੇਦ ਕਤੇਬ ਜਵਨ ਕਰਿ ਲਹਿ ਹੈ। ਤਾ ਕਹੁ ਗੋਬਰਾਗਨਿ ਮੋ ਦਹਿ ਹੈ। ੧੩।","roman":"Bed kateb javan kari lahi hai | taa kahu gobraagni mo dahi hai | 13 |","meaning_en":"Whoever takes up the Vedas or Katebs, they will burn them in a fire of cow-dung.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗੋਬਰਾਗਨਿ: 'cow-dung fire'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[14],"number_text":"੧੪।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੀ ਪਾਪ ਕੀ ਜਗਤਿ ਕਹਾਨੀ। ਭਾਜਾ ਧਰਮ ਛਾਡ ਰਜਧਾਨੀ।","roman":"Chalee paap kee jagti kahaanee | bhaajaa dharam chhaad rajdhaanee |","meaning_en":"The tale of sin spread in the world; dharma fled, leaving its capital.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਮਤ ਚਲਾ। ਯਾ ਤੇ ਧਰਮ ਭਰਮਿ ਉਡਿ ਟਲਾ। ੧੪।","roman":"Bhinn bhinn ghari ghari mat chalaa | yaa te dharam bharmi udi talaa | 14 |","meaning_en":"Different creeds ran in each house; because of this dharma, in confusion, flew off and departed.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਰਮਿ: 'in confusion' or 'wandering'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[15],"number_text":"੧੫।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਏਕ ਮਤ ਐਸ ਉਚੈ ਹੈ। ਜਾ ਤੇ ਸਕਲ ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਹੁਇ ਜੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Ek ek mat ais uchai hai | jaa te sakal soodr hui jai hai |","meaning_en":"Each will raise up such a creed that all will become Shudras.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਤ੍ਰੀ ਬ੍ਰਹਮਨ ਰਹਾ ਨ ਕੋਈ। ਸੰਕਰ ਬਰਨ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਸਬ ਹੋਈ। ੧੫।","roman":"Chhatree brahman rahaa na koee | sankar baran prajaa sab hoee | 15 |","meaning_en":"No Kshatriya or Brahmin remained; all the people became of mixed caste.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[16],"number_text":"੧੬।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਧਾਮਿ ਬਸਿ ਹੈ ਬ੍ਰਹਮਣੀ। ਬਈਸ ਨਾਰਿ ਹੋਇ ਹੈ ਛਤ੍ਰਨੀ।","roman":"Soodr dhaami basi hai brahamnee | baees naari hoi hai chhatranee |","meaning_en":"The Brahmin woman will live in the Shudra's home; the Vaishya's wife will be the Kshatriya's woman.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਈਸ ਨਾਰਿ ਹੋਇ ਹੈ ਛਤ੍ਰਨੀ: could also be 'the Kshatriya woman will become a Vaishya's wife'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਸਿ ਹੈ ਛਤ੍ਰਿ ਧਾਮਿ ਬੈਸਾਨੀ। ਬ੍ਰਹਮਨ ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਇਸਤ੍ਰੀ ਸੂਦ੍ਰਾਨੀ। ੧੬।","roman":"Basi hai chhatri dhaami baisaanee | brahman grih istree soodraanee | 16 |","meaning_en":"The Vaishya woman will live in the Kshatriya's home; in the Brahmin's house the wife will be a Shudra woman.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[17],"number_text":"੧੭।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਧਰਮ ਪਰ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਨ ਚਲ ਹੈ। ਬੇਦ ਕਤੇਬ ਦੋਊ ਮਤ ਦਲ ਹੈ।","roman":"Ek dharam par prajaa na chal hai | bed kateb do'oo mat dal hai |","meaning_en":"The people will not walk on one faith; they will crush both creeds, of the Vedas and the Katebs.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਮਤ ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਹੋਈ। ਏਕ ਪੈਂਡ ਚਲ ਹੈ ਨਹੀ ਕੋਈ। ੧੭।","roman":"Bhinn bhinn mat ghari ghari hoee | ek paind chal hai nahee koee | 17 |","meaning_en":"There will be different creeds in each house; no one will walk on one path.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਗੀਤਾ ਮਾਲਤੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਗੀਤਾ ਮਾਲਤੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Geetaa maaltee chhand","meaning_en":"Geeta Malti metre.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[18],"number_text":"੧੮।","page":727,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਮਤੋ ਘਰੋ ਘਰਿ ਏਕ ਏਕ ਚਲਾਇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Bhinn bhinn mato gharo ghari ek ek chalaai hai |","meaning_en":"Each will start a different creed, house by house;","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਡ ਬੈਡ ਫਿਰੈ ਸਬੈ ਸਿਰ ਏਕ ਏਕ ਨ ਨ੍ਯਾਇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Aid baid phirai sabai sir ek ek na nyaai hai |","meaning_en":"all will go about haughty and crooked, and none will bow his head to another.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਐਡ ਬੈਡ: read as 'proud and perverse / crooked'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਅਉਰ ਅਉਰ ਨਏ ਨਏ ਮਤ ਮਾਸਿ ਮਾਸਿ ਉਚਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Puni aur aur nae nae mat maasi maasi uchaahige |","meaning_en":"Then they will raise new and ever newer creeds month after month;","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਪਿਤਰਨ ਪੀਰ ਕੋ ਨਹਿ ਭੂਲਿ ਪੂਜਨ ਜਾਹਿਗੇ। ੧੮।","roman":"Dev pitran peer ko nahi bhooli poojan jaahige | 18 |","meaning_en":"they will not even by mistake go to worship gods, ancestors, or pirs.","page":727,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[19],"number_text":"੧੯।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਪੀਰ ਬਿਸਾਰ ਕੈ ਪਰਮੇਸ੍ਰ ਆਪੁ ਕਹਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Dev peer bisaar kai parmesr aapu kahaahige |","meaning_en":"Forgetting gods and pirs, they will call themselves the Supreme Lord.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਰ ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਨ ਏਕ ਕੋ ਜੁਰਿ ਏਕ ਏਕ ਉਡਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Nar bhaati bhaatan ek ko juri ek ek udaahige |","meaning_en":"Men of all kinds will gather against one, and each will make the other fly away.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਉਡਾਹਿਗੇ: read as 'ridicule / drive away'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਮਾਸ ਦੁਮਾਸ ਲੌ ਅਧ ਮਾਸ ਲੌ ਤੁ ਚਲਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ek maas dumaas lau adh maas lau tu chalaahige |","meaning_en":"They will run their creed for a month, two months, or half a month;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤਿ ਬੂਬਰਿ ਪਾਨ ਜਿਉ ਮਤ ਆਪ ਹੀ ਮਿਟਿ ਜਾਹਿਗੇ। ੧੯।","roman":"Anti boobri paan jiu mat aap hee miti jaahige | 19 |","meaning_en":"in the end, like a bubble on water, the creeds will vanish of themselves.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੂਬਰਿ: read as 'bubble'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[20],"number_text":"੨੦।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੇਦ ਅਉਰ ਕਤੇਬ ਕੇ ਦੋ ਦੂਖ ਕੈ ਮਤ ਡਾਰਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Bed aur kateb ke do dookh kai mat daari hai |","meaning_en":"Finding fault with both the Vedas and the Katebs, they will cast aside those creeds;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੂਖ ਕੈ: 'finding fault / maligning'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਿਤ ਆਪਨੇ ਤਿਹ ਠਉਰ ਭੀਤਰ ਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਉਚਾਰਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Hit aapne tih thaur bheetar jantr mantr uchaari hai |","meaning_en":"for their own ends, within that place, they will utter yantras and mantras.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਖ ਬੇਦ ਅਉਰ ਕਤੇਬ ਕੋ ਕੋਈ ਨਾਮ ਲੇਨ ਨ ਦੇਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Mukh bed aur kateb ko koee naam len na dehige |","meaning_en":"They will not let anyone take the name of the Vedas or Katebs with the mouth;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਸਹੂੰ ਨ ਕਉਡੀ ਪੁਨਿ ਤੇ ਕਬਹੂੰ ਨ ਕਿਉ ਹੀ ਦੇਹਗੇ। ੨੦।","roman":"Kishoon na kaudee puni te kabhoon na kiu hee dehge | 20 |","meaning_en":"nor will they ever give anyone so much as a cowrie in charity.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੁਨਿ: read as 'punn' (merit, charity); uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[21],"number_text":"੨੧।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਕਰੈ ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਬਿਸਾਰਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Paap karam karai jahaa tahaa dharam karam bisaari kai |","meaning_en":"They will do sinful deeds everywhere, forgetting the deeds of dharma.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹਿ ਦ੍ਰਬ ਦੇਖਤ ਛੋਡ ਹੈ ਲੈ ਪੁਤ੍ਰ ਮਿਤ੍ਰ ਸੰਘਾਰਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Nahi drab dekhat chhod hai lai putr mitr sanghaari kai |","meaning_en":"Seeing wealth, they will not spare it; they will take it even by killing son or friend.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕਨੇਕ ਉਠਾਇ ਹੈ ਮਤਿ ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਦਿਨੰ ਦਿਨਾ।","roman":"Eknek uthaai hai mati bhinn bhinn dinan dinaa |","meaning_en":"Each of many will raise different creeds day after day;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਫੋਕਟੰ ਧਰਮ ਸਬੈ ਕਲਿ ਕੇਵਲੰ ਪ੍ਰਭਣੰ ਬਿਨਾ। ੨੧।","roman":"Phoktan dharam sabai kali kevlan prabhnan binaa | 21 |","meaning_en":"in the Kali age all religion is hollow without the Lord alone.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[22],"number_text":"੨੨।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਕ ਦਿਵਸ ਚਲੈ ਕੋਊ ਮਤਿ ਦੋਇ ਦਿਉਸ ਚਲਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ik divas chalai ko'oo mati doi dius chalaahige |","meaning_en":"Some creed will run for one day, they will run it for two days;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤਿ ਜੋਰਿ ਕੈ ਬਹਰੋ ਸਭੈ ਦਿਨ ਤੀਸਰੈ ਮਿਟ ਜਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Anti jori kai bahro sabhai din teesrai mit jaahige |","meaning_en":"in the end, gathering, all of them will be scattered again and vanish on the third day.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਹਰੋ: read as 'scattered'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਅਉਰ ਅਉਰ ਉਚਾਹਿਗੇ ਮਤਣੋ ਗਤੰ ਚਤੁਰਥ ਦਿਨੰ।","roman":"Puni aur aur uchaahige matno gatan chaturath dinan |","meaning_en":"Then they will raise others again; on the fourth day the creed is gone.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਫੋਕਟਣੰ ਸਬੰ ਇਕ ਕੇਵਲੰ ਕਲਿਨੰ ਬਿਨੰ। ੨੨।","roman":"Dharam phokatnan saban ik kevlan kalinan binan | 22 |","meaning_en":"All religion is hollow in Kali age without the One alone.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲਿਨੰ ਬਿਨੰ: printed so; read as 'in the Kali age, without (the One)'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[23],"number_text":"੨੩।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛੰਦ ਬੰਦ ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਨਰ ਨਾਰਿ ਨਿਤ ਨਏ ਕਰਹਿ।","roman":"Chhand band jahaa tahaa nar naari nit nae karhi |","meaning_en":"Everywhere men and women will daily make new charms and bindings;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛੰਦ ਬੰਦ: read as 'tricks and spells'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਨਹੀ ਤੰਤ੍ਰ ਕਰਤ ਕਛੂ ਡਰਹਿ।","roman":"Puni jantr mantr jahaa tahaa nahee tantr karat kachhoo darhi |","meaning_en":"then yantras and mantras everywhere; in doing tantras they will have no fear at all.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਉਤਾਰ ਕੈ ਰਨ ਛੋਰਿ ਛਤ੍ਰੀ ਭਾਜ ਹੈ।","roman":"Dharam chhatr utaar kai ran chhori chhatree bhaaj hai |","meaning_en":"Taking off the canopy of dharma, the Kshatriyas will flee, leaving the battlefield;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਬੈਸ ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਗਹਿ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਆਹਵ ਗਾਜ ਹੈ। ੨੩।","roman":"Soodr bais jahaa tahaa gahi asatr aahav gaaj hai | 23 |","meaning_en":"Shudras and Vaishyas everywhere will take up weapons and roar in battle.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[24],"number_text":"੨੪।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਤ੍ਰੀਆਨੀ ਛੋਰ ਕੈ ਨਰ ਨਾਹ ਨੀਚਨਿ ਰਾਵ ਹੈ।","roman":"Chhatreeaanee chhor kai nar naah neechni raav hai |","meaning_en":"Leaving their Kshatriya wives, kings of men will enjoy low women;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜਿ ਰਾਜ ਅਉਰ ਸਮਾਜ ਕੋ ਗ੍ਰਿਹਿ ਨੀਚਿ ਰਾਨੀ ਜਾਵ ਹੈ।","roman":"Taji raaj aur samaaj ko grihi neechi raanee jaav hai |","meaning_en":"leaving kingdom and court, the queen will go to the house of a low man.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਸੁਤਾ ਭਏ ਰਤਿ ਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਸੂਦ੍ਰੀ ਹੋਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Soodr braham sutaa bhae rati braham soodree hohige |","meaning_en":"Shudras will lie with Brahmin daughters; Brahmins will be attached to Shudra women.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਬ੍ਰਹਮ ਸੁਤਾ ਭਏ: read as 'Shudras united with Brahmins' daughters'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੇਸਿਯਾ ਬਾਲ ਬਿਲੋਕ ਕੈ ਮੁਨਿ ਰਾਜ ਧੀਰਜ ਖੋਹਿਗੇ। ੨੪।","roman":"Besiyaa baal bilok kai muni raaj dheeraj khohige | 24 |","meaning_en":"Seeing young courtesans, the kings of sages will lose their composure.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[25],"number_text":"੨੫।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਭਰਮਿ ਉਡ੍ਯੋ ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਪਾਪ ਪਗ ਪਗ ਪਰ ਹੋਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Dharam bharmi udyo jahaa tahaa paap pag pag par hohige |","meaning_en":"Dharma, confused, has flown away everywhere; sins will be at every step.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਜ ਸਿਖ ਨਾਰਿ ਗੁਰੂ ਰਮੈ ਗੁਰ ਦਾਰਾ ਸੋ ਸਿਖ ਸੋਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Nij sikh naari guroo ramai gur daaraa so sikh sohige |","meaning_en":"The guru will enjoy his own disciple's wife; the disciple will lie with the guru's wife.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੋਹਿਗੇ: read as 'lie with / sleep with' (sohi = sovahi); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਬਿਬੇਕ ਅਉਰ ਬਿਬੇਕ ਕੋ ਨ ਬਿਬੇਕ ਬੈਠਿ ਬਿਚਾਰ ਹੈ।","roman":"Abibek aur bibek ko na bibek baithi bichaar hai |","meaning_en":"Of wisdom and unwisdom, no one with discernment will sit and reflect;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਿ ਝੂਠ ਬੋਲਿ ਕਮਾਹਿਗੇ ਸਿਰ ਸਾਚ ਬੋਲ ਉਤਾਰ ਹੈ। ੨੫।","roman":"Puni jhooth boli kamaahige sir saach bol utaar hai | 25 |","meaning_en":"then they will earn by speaking lies, and cast off from their heads the speaking of truth.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਬ੍ਰਿਧ ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਧ ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bridh naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Bridh Naraj metre.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[26],"number_text":"੨੬।","page":728,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਕਾਰਣੋ ਅਨਿਤ ਨਿਤ ਹੋਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Akrit krit kaarno anit nit hohige |","meaning_en":"The cause of making the unmade will become; the transient will be taken as eternal.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line is compressed; read as 'what should not be done will be done, the impermanent taken as permanent'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਆਗਿ ਧਰਮਣੋ ਤ੍ਰੀਅੰ ਕੁਨਾਰਿ ਸਾਧ ਜੋਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Tiaagi dharamno treean kunaari saadh johige |","meaning_en":"Abandoning their wives of dharma, holy men will gaze at bad women.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਿਤ੍ਰਤੰ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਮਿਤ੍ਰ ਧੋਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Pavitr chitr chitratan bachitr mitr dhohige |","meaning_en":"Those with pure and fine minds will betray wonderful friends;","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਵਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਿਤ੍ਰਤੰ: uncertain; read as 'outwardly pure-seeming'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਿਤ੍ਰ ਮਿਤ੍ਰ ਭਾਵਣੋ ਸੁਮਿਤ੍ਰ ਅਮਿਤ੍ਰ ਹੋਹਿਗੇ। ੨੬।","roman":"Amitr mitr bhaavno sumitr amitr hohige | 26 |","meaning_en":"enemies will be regarded as friends, and good friends will become enemies.","page":728,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[27],"number_text":"੨੭।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲ੍ਯੰ ਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਕਰੰਮਣੋ ਅਭਛ ਭਛ ਜਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Kalyan kritan karanmno abhachh bhachh jaahige |","meaning_en":"In Kali age such deeds will be done: they will eat what is not to be eaten;","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਕੱਜ ਕਜੱਣੋ ਨਰੰ ਅਧਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਪਾਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Akajj kajnno naran adhram dharam paahige |","meaning_en":"men will do what ought not be done, and take unrighteousness as righteousness.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਧਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਧੋਹਿ ਹੈ ਧ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਧਰਾ ਧਰੇਸਣੰ।","roman":"Sudhram dharam dhohi hai dhritan dharaa dharesnan |","meaning_en":"They will betray good dharma; the lords who sustain the earth","page":729,"flags":[{"code":"space","reason":"word space printed as a gap (7.7pt), space inserted"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਧਰਾ ਧਰੇਸਣੰ: read as 'the kings who uphold the earth'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਧਰਮਣੋ ਧ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਕੁਕਰਮ ਕਰਮਣੋ ਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ। ੨੭।","roman":"Adhram dharamno dhritan kukram karamno kritan | 27 |","meaning_en":"will hold unrighteousness as dharma and do evil deeds as deeds.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[28],"number_text":"੨੮।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਉਲੰਘਿ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮਣੋ ਅਧਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਬਿਆਪ ਹੈ।","roman":"Ki ulanghi dharam karamno adhram dharam biaap hai |","meaning_en":"Transgressing the deeds of dharma, unrighteousness will pervade as dharma;","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਤਿਆਗਿ ਜੱਗਿ ਜਾਪਣੋ ਅਜੋਗ ਜਾਪ ਜਾਪ ਹੈ।","roman":"Su tiaagi jaggi jaapno ajog jaap jaap hai |","meaning_en":"abandoning sacrifice and repetition of the Name, they will chant improper chants.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮਣੰ ਭਯੋ ਅਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਨਿਰਭ੍ਰਮੰ।","roman":"Su dharam karamnan bhayo adhram karam nirbhraman |","meaning_en":"The deeds of good dharma have become unrighteous deeds, done without doubt;","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਸਾਧ ਸੰਕ੍ਰਤੰ ਚਿਤੰ ਅਸਾਧ ਨਿਰਭਯੰ ਡੁਲੰ। ੨੮।","roman":"Su saadh sankratan chitan asaadh nirabhyan dulan | 28 |","meaning_en":"the minds of holy men are fearful, while the wicked roam fearless.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਡੁਲੰ: read as 'roam'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[29],"number_text":"੨੯।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਕਰਮਣੋ ਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਸੁ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮਣੋ ਤਜੰ।","roman":"Adhram karamno kritan su dharam karamno tajan |","meaning_en":"They do unrighteous deeds and abandon the deeds of good dharma.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਹਰਖ ਬਰਖਣੰ ਧਨੰ ਨ ਕਰਖ ਸਰਬਤੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪੰ।","roman":"Prahrakh barakhnan dhanan na karakh sarabto nripan |","meaning_en":"Clouds pour no joyful rain of wealth; nowhere are kings concerned with tilling.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪ੍ਰਹਰਖ ਬਰਖਣੰ ਧਨੰ / ਕਰਖ: uncertain; possibly 'no joyous rain falls, no ploughing anywhere, O king'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਕੱਜ ਕਜੱਣੋ ਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਨ੍ਰਿੱਲਜ ਸਰਬਤੋ ਫਿਰੰ।","roman":"Akajj kajnno kritan nrillaj sarabto phiran |","meaning_en":"Doing what ought not to be done, they go about shameless everywhere.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨਰਥ ਬਰਤਿਤੰ ਭੂਅੰ ਨ ਅਰਥ ਕਥਤੰ ਨਰੰ। ੨੯।","roman":"Anrath bartitan bhooan na arath kathtan naran | 29 |","meaning_en":"Mischief prevails on earth; men speak nothing meaningful.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤਰਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤਰਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Taranraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Taranraj metre.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[30],"number_text":"੩੦।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰਨ ਹੈ ਅਬਰਨ ਕੋ। ਛਾਡਿ ਹਰਿ ਸਰਨ ਕੋ। ੩੦।","roman":"Baran hai abran ko | chhaadi hari saran ko | 30 |","meaning_en":"They will wed the casteless (forbidden), forsaking the refuge of the Lord.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਰਨ ਹੈ ਅਬਰਨ ਕੋ: read as 'will choose what should not be chosen'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[31],"number_text":"੩੧।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਡਿ ਸੁਭ ਸਾਜ ਕੋ। ਲਾਗ ਹੈ ਅਕਾਜ ਕੋ। ੩੧।","roman":"Chhaadi subh saaj ko | laag hai akaaj ko | 31 |","meaning_en":"Leaving good conduct, they will take to wrong-doing.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[32],"number_text":"੩੨।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਯਾਗ ਹੈ ਨਾਮ ਕੋ। ਲਾਗ ਹੈ ਕਾਮ ਕੋ। ੩੨।","roman":"Tyaag hai naam ko | laag hai kaam ko | 32 |","meaning_en":"They will abandon the Name and take to lust.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[33],"number_text":"੩੩।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਾਜ ਕੋ ਛੋਰ ਹੈ। ਦਾਨਿ ਮੁਖ ਮੋਰ ਹੈ। ੩੩।","roman":"Laaj ko chhor hai | daani mukh mor hai | 33 |","meaning_en":"They will cast off shame and turn their faces away from giving.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[34],"number_text":"੩੪।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਰਨ ਨਹੀ ਧਿਆਇ ਹੈ। ਦੁਸਟ ਗਤਿ ਪਾਇ ਹੈ। ੩੪।","roman":"Charan nahee dhiaai hai | dusat gati paai hai | 34 |","meaning_en":"They will not meditate on the Lord's feet; they will meet the fate of the wicked.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[35],"number_text":"੩੫।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਰਕ ਕਹੁ ਜਾਹਿਗੇ। ਅੰਤਿ ਪਛੁਤਾਹਿਗੇ। ੩੫।","roman":"Narak kahu jaahige | anti pachhutaahige | 35 |","meaning_en":"They will go to hell and repent in the end.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[36],"number_text":"੩੬।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਕਹਿ ਖੋਹਿਗੇ। ਪਾਪ ਕਰ ਰੋਹਿਗੈ। ੩੬।","roman":"Dharam kahi khohige | paap kar rohigai | 36 |","meaning_en":"They will lose dharma, and do sin and weep.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੋਹਿਗੈ: read as 'weep' (or 'rage'); uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[37],"number_text":"੩੭।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਰਕਿ ਪੁਨਿ ਬਾਸ ਹੈ। ਤ੍ਰਾਸ ਜਮ ਤ੍ਰਾਸ ਹੈ। ੩੭।","roman":"Narki puni baas hai | traas jam traas hai | 37 |","meaning_en":"Then they will dwell in hell, in the terror of Yama.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕੁਮਾਰਿ ਲਲਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਕੁਮਾਰਿ ਲਲਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Kumaari lalat chhand","meaning_en":"Kumar Lalit metre.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[38],"number_text":"੩੮।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਕੈ ਹੈ। ਨ ਭੂਲ ਨਾਮ ਲੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Adhram karam kai hai | na bhool naam lai hai |","meaning_en":"They will do unrighteous deeds and not even by mistake take the Name.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਸੂ ਨ ਦਾਨ ਦੇਹਿਗੇ। ਸੁ ਸਾਧ ਲੁਟਿ ਲੇਹਿਗੇ। ੩੮।","roman":"Kisoo na daan dehige | su saadh luti lehige | 38 |","meaning_en":"They will give charity to no one; they will rob the holy.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[39],"number_text":"੩੯।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਦੇਹ ਫੇਰਿ ਲੈ ਕੈ। ਨ ਦੇਹ ਦਾਨ ਕੈ ਕੈ।","roman":"Na deh pheri lai kai | na deh daan kai kai |","meaning_en":"They will not return what they take, nor give in charity;","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਨਾਮ ਕੌ ਨ ਲੈ ਹੈ। ਬਿਸੇਖ ਨਰਕਿ ਜੈ ਹੈ। ੩੯।","roman":"Hari naam kau na lai hai | bisekh narki jai hai | 39 |","meaning_en":"they will not take the Lord's Name; they will go especially to hell.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[40],"number_text":"੪੦।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਧਰਮ ਠਾਢਿ ਰਹਿ ਹੈ। ਕਰੈ ਨ ਜਉਨ ਕਹਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Na dharam thaadhi rahi hai | karai na jaun kahi hai |","meaning_en":"Dharma will not stand firm; they will not do what they say.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਮਾਤ ਸੰਗਾ। ਅਧੀਨ ਅਰਧੰਗਾ। ੪੦।","roman":"Na preeti maat sangaa | adheen ardhangaa | 40 |","meaning_en":"There is no love with the mother; men are subject to their wives.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਧੀਨ ਅਰਧੰਗਾ: 'subject to the half-body (wife)'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[41],"number_text":"੪੧।","page":729,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਭੱਛ ਭਛੱ ਭਛੈ। ਅਕੱਛ ਕਾਛ ਕੱਛੈ।","roman":"Abhacchh bhachh bhachhai | akacchh kaachh kacchhai |","meaning_en":"They eat what is forbidden to eat; they wear what is improper to wear.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਭਾਖ ਬੈਨ ਭਾਖੈ। ਕਿਸੂ ਨ ਕਾਣਿ ਰਾਖੈ। ੪੧।","roman":"Abhaakh bain bhaakhai | kisoo na kaani raakhai | 41 |","meaning_en":"They speak words not fit to be spoken; they keep regard for no one.","page":729,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[42],"number_text":"੪੨।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਕਰ ਹੈ। ਨ ਤਾਤ ਮਾਤ ਡਰਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Adhram karam kar hai | na taat maat dari hai |","meaning_en":"They do unrighteous deeds and fear neither father nor mother.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੈ ਹੈ। ਸੁਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੋ ਨ ਲੈ ਹੈ। ੪੨।","roman":"Kumantr mantr kai hai | sumantr ko na lai hai | 42 |","meaning_en":"They take evil counsel and will not accept good counsel.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[43],"number_text":"੪੩।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਕੈ ਹੈ। ਸੁ ਭਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਖੁਐ ਹੈ।","roman":"Adhram karam kai hai | su bharam dharam khuai hai |","meaning_en":"They will do unrighteous deeds and lose dharma in delusion;","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਕਾਲ ਫਾਸਿ ਫਸ ਹੈ। ਨਿਦਾਨ ਨਰਕ ਬਸਿ ਹੈ। ੪੩।","roman":"Su kaal phaasi phas hai | nidaan narak basi hai | 43 |","meaning_en":"they will be caught in the noose of death, and finally dwell in hell.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[44],"number_text":"੪੪।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਕਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਲਾਗੇ। ਸੁਧਰਮ ਛਾਡਿ ਭਾਗੇ।","roman":"Kukram karam laage | sudhram chhaadi bhaage |","meaning_en":"They took to evil deeds and ran, leaving good dharma.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਮਾਤ ਨਿਤੱ ਪਾਪੰ। ਬਿਸਾਰਿ ਸਰਬ ਜਾਪੰ। ੪੪।","roman":"Kamaat nit paapan | bisaari sarab jaapan | 44 |","meaning_en":"They earn sin daily, forgetting all remembrance of God.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[45],"number_text":"੪੫।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਮੱਦ ਮੋਹ ਮਤੇ। ਸੁ ਕਰਮ ਕੇ ਕੁੱਪਤੇ।","roman":"Su madd moh mate | su karam ke kuppte |","meaning_en":"Intoxicated with wine and attachment, they are unworthy in deeds;","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁੱਪਤੇ: read as 'ku-patra', unworthy; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਕਾਮ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਰਾਚੇ। ਉਤਾਰਿ ਲਾਜ ਨਾਚੇ। ੪੫।","roman":"Su kaam krodh raache | utaari laaj naache | 45 |","meaning_en":"absorbed in lust and anger, they dance, casting off shame.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਗ ਸਰੂਪੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਗ ਸਰੂਪੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Nag saroopee chhand","meaning_en":"Nag Saroopi metre.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[46],"number_text":"੪੬।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਕਉ ਕਰੈ। ਬ੍ਰਿਥਾ ਕਥਾ ਸੁਨੈ ਰਰੈ।","roman":"Na dharam karam kau karai | brithaa kathaa sunai rarai |","meaning_en":"They do no deeds of dharma; they hear and repeat idle talk.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਕਰਮ ਕਰਮਿ ਸੋ ਫਸੈ। ਸਤਿ ਛਾਡਿ ਧਰਮ ਵਾ ਨਸੈ। ੪੬।","roman":"Kukram karmi so phasai | sati chhaadi dharam vaa nasai | 46 |","meaning_en":"They are caught in evil deeds; leaving truth, dharma perishes for them.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[47],"number_text":"੪੭।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਰਾਣ ਕਾਬਿ ਨ ਪੜੈ। ਕੁਰਾਨ ਲੈ ਨ ਤੇ ਰੜੈ।","roman":"Puraan kaabi na parai | kuraan lai na te rarai |","meaning_en":"They read neither the Puranas nor poetry; they do not take the Quran and recite it.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਕੋ ਕਰੈ। ਸੁ ਧਰਮ ਜਾਸੁ ਤੇ ਡਰੈ। ੪੭।","roman":"Adhram karam ko karai | su dharam jaasu te darai | 47 |","meaning_en":"They do unrighteous deeds, and good dharma fears them.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[48],"number_text":"੪੮।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਾਕਿ ਵਰਣਤਾ ਭਈ। ਸੁ ਭਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਗਈ।","roman":"Dharaaki varantaa bhaee | su bharam dharam kee gaee |","meaning_en":"The earth has become of mixed castes; the honour of dharma has gone.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਰਾਕਿ ਵਰਣਤਾ: printed so; read as the earth's (mixed) caste condition; uncertain. ਭਰਮ: read as 'honour, credit'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗ੍ਰਿਹੰ ਗ੍ਰਿਹੰ ਨਯੰ ਮਤੰ। ਚਲੇ ਭੂਅੰ ਜਥਾ ਤਥੰ। ੪੮।","roman":"Grihan grihan nayan matan | chale bhooan jathaa tathan | 48 |","meaning_en":"In each house a new creed; they move upon the earth just as they please.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[49],"number_text":"੪੯।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗ੍ਰਿਹੰ ਗ੍ਰਿਹੰ ਨਏ ਮਤੰ। ਭਈ ਧਰੰ ਨਈ ਗਤੰ।","roman":"Grihan grihan nae matan | bhaee dharan naee gatan |","meaning_en":"In each house new creeds; the earth has come to a new state.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਰਾਜਤਾ ਲਈ। ਨਿਕਾਰਿ ਧਰਮ ਦੇਸ ਦੀ। ੪੯।","roman":"Adhram raajtaa laee | nikaari dharam des dee | 49 |","meaning_en":"Unrighteousness has taken the kingship and driven dharma out of the land.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[50],"number_text":"੫੦।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਬੋਧ ਏਕ ਨ ਲਗੈ। ਸੁ ਧਰਮ ਅਧਰਮ ਤੇ ਭਗੈ।","roman":"Prabodh ek na lagai | su dharam adhram te bhagai |","meaning_en":"No teaching has any effect; good dharma flees from unrighteousness.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਕਰਮ ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰਯੰ ਜਗੰ। ਸੁ ਕਰਮ ਪੰਖ ਕੈ ਭਗੰ। ੫੦।","roman":"Kukram prachuryan jagan | su karam pankh kai bhagan | 50 |","meaning_en":"Evil deeds abound in the world; good deeds have flown away as if on wings.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[51],"number_text":"੫੧।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਪੰਚ ਪੰਚ ਹੁਇ ਗਡਾ। ਅਪ੍ਰਪੰਚ ਪੰਖ ਕੇ ਉਡਾ।","roman":"Prapanch panch hui gadaa | aprapanch pankh ke udaa |","meaning_en":"Deceit has planted itself as the arbiter; the guileless has flown away on wings.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੰਚ: read as 'chief / arbiter'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਕਰਮ ਬਿਚਰਤੰ ਜਗੰ। ਸੁਕਰਮ ਸੁ ਭ੍ਰਮੰ ਭਗੰ। ੫੧।","roman":"Kukram bichartan jagan | sukram su bhraman bhagan | 51 |","meaning_en":"Evil deeds roam the world; good deeds, bewildered, have fled.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਮਾਣ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਮਾਣ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Ramaan chhand","meaning_en":"Raman metre.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[52],"number_text":"੫੨।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਤਜਿਹੈ। ਕੁਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਭਜਿ ਹੈ। ੫੨।","roman":"Sukritan tajihai | kukritan bhaji hai | 52 |","meaning_en":"They will abandon good deeds and take to evil deeds.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[53],"number_text":"੫੩।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭ੍ਰਮਣੰ ਭਰਿ ਹੈ। ਜਸ ਤੇ ਟਰਿ ਹੈ। ੫੩।","roman":"Bhramnan bhari hai | jas te tari hai | 53 |","meaning_en":"They will be filled with delusion and turn away from good repute.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[54],"number_text":"੫੪।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਹੈ ਕੁਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ। ਰਰਿ ਹੈ ਅਨ੍ਰਿਥੰ । ੫੪।","roman":"Kari hai kukritan | rari hai anrithan | 54 |","meaning_en":"They will do evil deeds and prattle mischief.","page":730,"flags":[{"code":"space","reason":"word space printed as a gap (5.8pt), space inserted"}],"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[55],"number_text":"੫੫।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਪ ਹੈ ਅਜਪੰ। ਕੁਥਪੇਣ ਥਪੰ। ੫੫।","roman":"Jap hai ajpan | kuthpen thapan | 55 |","meaning_en":"They will chant what ought not be chanted, and establish what ought not be established.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਮਰਾਜੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਮਰਾਜੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Somraajee chhand","meaning_en":"Somraji metre.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[56],"number_text":"੫੬।","page":730,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨੈ ਦੇਸਿ ਦੇਸੰ ਮੁਨੰ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮਾ। ਚੁਨੈ ਜੂਠ ਕੂਠੰ ਸ੍ਰੁਤੰ ਛੋਰ ਧਰਮਾ। ੫੬।","roman":"Sunai desi desan munan paap karmaa | chunai jooth koothan srutan chhor dharmaa | 56 |","meaning_en":"Hear: in land after land even sages do sinful deeds; they pick up falsehood and impurity, leaving the dharma of the Shrutis.","page":730,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਨੈ: could also be read as 'they hear'; ਜੂਠ ਕੂਠੰ: 'leftovers and falsehood'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[57],"number_text":"੫੭।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜੈ ਧਰਮ ਨਾਰੀ ਤਕੈ ਪਾਪ ਨਾਰੰ। ਮਹਾ ਰੂਪ ਪਾਪੀ ਕੁਵਿਤ੍ਰਾਧਿਕਾਰੰ। ੫੭।","roman":"Tajai dharam naaree takai paap naaran | mahaa roop paapee kuvitraadhikaaran | 57 |","meaning_en":"They abandon their wedded wives and gaze at sinful women; great in form but sinners, given to evil ways.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁਵਿਤ੍ਰਾਧਿਕਾਰੰ: read as 'possessed by wicked conduct'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[58],"number_text":"੫੮।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੈ ਨਿਤ ਅਨਰਥੰ ਸਮਰਥੰ ਨ ਏਤੀ। ਕਰੈ ਪਾਪ ਤੇਤੋ ਪਰਾਲਬਧ ਜੇਤੀ। ੫੮।","roman":"Karai nit anarthan samarthan na etee | karai paap teto paraalbadh jetee | 58 |","meaning_en":"They do mischief daily, though they have no such power; they sin as much as their destiny allows.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Second half uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[59],"number_text":"੫੯।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਏ ਨਿੱਤ ਮੱਤੰ ਉਠੈ ਏਕ ਏਕੰ। ਕਰੈ ਨਿੰਤ ਅਨਰਥੰ ਅਨੇਕੰ ਅਨੇਕੰ। ੫੯।","roman":"Nae nitt mattan uthai ek ekan | karai nint anarthan anekan anekan | 59 |","meaning_en":"New creeds rise daily, one after another; they do mischief daily, many and many.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Priyaa chhand","meaning_en":"Priya metre.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[60],"number_text":"੬੦।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੁਖ ਦੰਦ ਹੈ ਸੁਖਕੰਦ ਜੀ। ਨਹੀ ਬੰਧ ਹੈ ਜਗ ਬੰਦ ਜੀ। ੬੦।","roman":"Dukh dand hai sukhkand jee | nahee bandh hai jag band jee | 60 |","meaning_en":"The Lord, the root of joy, is the destroyer of sorrow; He who is bowed to by the world is not bound.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Uncertain reading; possibly 'they do not bow to the One the world bows to'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[61],"number_text":"੬੧।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਬੇਦ ਬਾਕ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਨ ਹੈ। ਮਤ ਭਿੰਨ ਭਿੰਨ ਬਖਾਨ ਹੈ। ੬੧।","roman":"Nahee bed baak pramaan hai | mat bhinn bhinn bakhaan hai | 61 |","meaning_en":"The words of the Vedas are not held as authority; they expound different creeds.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[62],"number_text":"੬੨।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਕੁਰਾਨ ਕੋ ਮਤੁ ਲੇਹ ਗੇ। ਨ ਪੁਰਾਨ ਦੇਖਨ ਦੇਹਗੇ। ੬੨।","roman":"Na kuraan ko matu leh ge | na puraan dekhan dehge | 62 |","meaning_en":"They will not take the creed of the Quran, nor let the Puranas be seen.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[63],"number_text":"੬੩।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਏਕ ਮੰਤ੍ਰਹਿ ਜਾਪ ਹੈ। ਦਿਨ ਦ੍ਵੈਕ ਥਾਪਨ ਥਾਪ ਹੈ। ੬੩।","roman":"Nahee ek mantrahi jaap hai | din dvaik thaapan thaap hai | 63 |","meaning_en":"They do not repeat one mantra; they establish something for a couple of days.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਗਾਹਾ ਛੰਦੁ ਦੂਜਾ","gurmukhi":"ਗਾਹਾ ਛੰਦੁ ਦੂਜਾ","roman":"Gaahaa chhandu doojaa","meaning_en":"Gaha metre, the second.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[64],"number_text":"੬੪।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੀਅਤੰ ਪਾਪਣੋ ਕਰਮੰ ਨ ਅਧਰਮੰ ਭਰਮਣੰ ਤ੍ਰਸਤਾਇ।","roman":"Kreeatan paapno karman na adharman bharamnan trastaai |","meaning_en":"They do sinful deeds and do not fear unrighteousness or delusion;","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਕਰਮ ਕਰਮਾਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਨ ਦੇਵ ਲੋਕੇਣ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤਹਿ। ੬੪।","roman":"Kukram karmaakritan na dev loken praapathi | 64 |","meaning_en":"doers of evil deeds, they do not reach the world of the gods.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[65],"number_text":"੬੫।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਤ੍ਯੰ ਅਨਰਥੰ ਨਿਤ੍ਯੰ ਸੁਅਰਥ ਅਰਥਿੰ ਨ ਬੁਝਿਯਮ।","roman":"Ratyan anarthan nityan suarath arthin na bujhiyam |","meaning_en":"Ever absorbed in mischief, they do not understand the true meaning of things;","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਪ੍ਰਹਰਖ ਬਰਖਣੰ ਧਨਿਨੰ ਚਿਤੰ ਬਸੀਅ ਬਿਰਾਟਕੰ। ੬੫।","roman":"Na prahrakh barakhnan dhaninan chitan baseea biraatkan | 65 |","meaning_en":"no joyous rain falls on the wealthy; the Vast One does not dwell in their minds.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿਰਾਟਕੰ: read as 'the Cosmic (Virat) Lord'; line uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[66],"number_text":"੬੬।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਤਵੰ ਮਦ੍ਯੰ ਕੁਨਾਰੰ ਅਨਰਤੰ ਧਰਮਣੋ ਤ੍ਰੀਆਇ।","roman":"Maatvan madyan kunaaran anartan dharamno treeaai |","meaning_en":"Intoxicated with wine and bad women, they are not attached to wives of dharma;","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਕਰਮਣੋ ਕਥਤੰ ਬਦਿਤੰ ਲਜਿਣੋ ਤਜਤੰ ਨਰੰ। ੬੬।","roman":"Kukramno kathtan baditan lajino tajtan naran | 66 |","meaning_en":"men speak of evil deeds and abandon shame.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[67],"number_text":"੬੭।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਜ੍ਯੰ ਕੁਤਿਸਿਤੰ ਕਰਮੰ ਭਜਿਤੰ ਤਜਤੰ ਨ ਲਜਾ ।","roman":"Sajyan kutisitan karman bhajitan tajtan na lajaa |","meaning_en":"They take up vile deeds and pursue them, and abandon shame;","page":731,"flags":[{"code":"space","reason":"word space printed as a gap (5.4pt), space inserted"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਜਤੰ ਨ ਲਜਾ: printed so; read as 'abandon shame' or 'do not abandon (them) for shame'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਵਿਰਤੰ ਨਿਤਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਤਣੇ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮੇਣ ਤਿਆਗਤੰ। ੬੭।","roman":"Kuvirtan nitprati kritne dharam karmen tiaagtan | 67 |","meaning_en":"they do evil conduct every day and abandon the deeds of dharma.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚਤੁਰਪਦੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਚਤੁਰਪਦੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Chaturapdee chhand","meaning_en":"Chatur-padi metre.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[68],"number_text":"੬੮।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਨਿਤ ਕਰਿ ਹੈ ਸੁਕ੍ਰਿਤਾਨੁ ਨ ਸਰ ਹੈ ਅਘ ਓਘਨ ਰੁਚਿ ਰਾਚੇ।","roman":"Kukritan nit kari hai sukritaanu na sar hai agh oghan ruchi raache |","meaning_en":"They will do evil deeds daily and not accomplish good deeds; they are absorbed in heaps of sins.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨ ਹੈ ਨ ਬੇਦਨ ਸਿੰਮ੍ਰਿਤਿ ਕਤੇਬਨ ਲੋਕ ਲਾਜ ਤਜਿ ਨਾਚੇ।","roman":"Maan hai na bedan sinmriti kateban lok laaj taji naache |","meaning_en":"They will not heed the Vedas, Smritis, or Katebs; they dance, abandoning public shame.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੀਨ ਹੈ ਨ ਬਾਨੀ ਸੁਭਗ ਭਵਾਨੀ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਰਤਿ ਹੁਇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Cheen hai na baanee subhag bhavaanee paap karam rati hui hai |","meaning_en":"They will not recognise the word of the blessed Bhavani; they will be devoted to sinful deeds.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗੁਰਦੇਵ ਨ ਮਾਨੈ ਭਲ ਨ ਬਖਾਨੈ ਅੰਤਿ ਨਰਕ ਕਹ ਜੈ ਹੈ। ੬੮।","roman":"Gurdev na maanai bhal na bakhaanai anti narak kah jai hai | 68 |","meaning_en":"They do not honour the divine Guru, nor speak well; in the end they will go to hell.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[69],"number_text":"੬੯।","page":731,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਪ ਹੈ ਨ ਭਵਾਨੀ ਅਕਥ ਕਹਾਨੀ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਰਤਿ ਐਸੇ।","roman":"Jap hai na bhavaanee akath kahaanee paap karam rati aise |","meaning_en":"They will not repeat Bhavani's indescribable story; so absorbed are they in sinful deeds.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਿ ਹੈ ਨ ਦੇਵੰ ਅਲਖ ਅਭੇਵੰ ਦੁਰਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਮੁਨਿ ਵਰ ਜੈਸੇ।","roman":"Maani hai na devan alakh abhevan durkritan muni var jaise |","meaning_en":"They will not honour the God unseen and mysterious; they do evil deeds, like eminent sages.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੁਰਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਮੁਨਿ ਵਰ ਜੈਸੇ: possibly ironic 'even the best sages do evil'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੀਨ ਹੈ ਨ ਬਾਤੰ ਪਰ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਰਾਤੰ ਧਰਮਣਿ ਕਰਮ ਉਦਾਸੀ।","roman":"Cheen hai na baatan par triyaa raatan dharamni karam udaasee |","meaning_en":"They will not recognise wise talk; attached to others' women, they are indifferent to the deeds of dharma.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਨਿ ਹੈ ਨ ਬਾਤੰ ਅਧਕ ਅਗਿਆਤੰ ਅੰਤ ਨਰਕ ਕੇ ਬਾਸੀ। ੬੯।","roman":"Jaani hai na baatan adhak agiaatan ant narak ke baasee | 69 |","meaning_en":"They will not understand the matter; deeply ignorant, in the end they dwell in hell.","page":731,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[70],"number_text":"੭੦।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਤ ਨਵ ਮਤਿ ਕਰ ਹੈ ਹਰਿ ਨ ਨਿਸਰਿ ਹੈ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਕੋ ਨਾਮ ਨ ਲੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Nit nav mati kar hai hari na nisri hai prabh ko naam na lai hai |","meaning_en":"They will make new creeds daily, will not remember the Lord, nor take the Name of God.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੁਤਿ ਸਮ੍ਰਿਤਿ ਨ ਮਾਨੈ ਤਜਤ ਕੁਰਾਨੈ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਪੈਂਡ ਬਤੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Sruti samriti na maanai tajat kuraanai aur hee paind batai hai |","meaning_en":"They will not heed Shruti or Smriti, abandoning the Quran, they will point out yet another path.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰ ਤ੍ਰੀਅ ਰਸ ਰਾਚੇ ਸਤ ਕੇ ਕਾਚੇ ਨਿਜ ਤ੍ਰੀਯ ਗਮਨ ਨ ਕਰ ਹੈ।","roman":"Par treea ras raache sat ke kaache nij treey gaman na kar hai |","meaning_en":"Absorbed in the pleasure of others' women, weak in truth, they will not go to their own wives.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨ ਹੈ ਨ ਏਕੰ ਪੂਜ ਅਨੇਕੰ ਅੰਤਿ ਨਰਕ ਮਹਿ ਪਰ ਹੈ। ੭੦।","roman":"Maan hai na ekan pooj anekan anti narak mahi par hai | 70 |","meaning_en":"They will not honour the One, but worship many; in the end they will fall into hell.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[71],"number_text":"੭੧।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਹਣ ਪੂਜੈ ਹੈ ਏਕ ਨ ਧਿਐ ਹੈ ਮਤਿ ਕੇ ਅਧਿਕ ਅੰਧੇਰਾ।","roman":"Paahan poojai hai ek na dhiai hai mati ke adhik andheraa |","meaning_en":"They will worship stones and not meditate on the One; their minds are in great darkness.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਕਹੁ ਤਜਿ ਹੈ ਬਿਖ ਕਹੁ ਭਜਿ ਹੈ ਸਾਝਹਿ ਕਹਹਿ ਸਵੇਰਾ।","roman":"Amrit kahu taji hai bikh kahu bhaji hai saajhhi kahhi saveraa |","meaning_en":"They will abandon nectar and take to poison; they call evening morning.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਫੋਕਟ ਧਰਮਣਿ ਰਤਿ ਕੁਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਬਿਨਾ ਮਤਿ ਕਹੋ ਕਹਾ ਫਲ ਪੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Phokat dharamni rati kukrit binaa mati kaho kahaa phal pai hai |","meaning_en":"Attached to hollow religion and evil deeds, without wisdom; say, what fruit will they obtain?","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਧੇ ਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਸਾਲੈ ਜਾਹਿ ਉਤਾਲੈ ਅੰਤ ਅਧੋਗਤਿ ਜੈ ਹੈ। ੭੧।","roman":"Baadhe mrit saalai jaahi utaalai ant adhogti jai hai | 71 |","meaning_en":"Bound in the house of death, they will go quickly; in the end they will go to the lowest state.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਸਾਲੈ: read as 'death's house/prison'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਏਲਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਏਲਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Elaa chhand","meaning_en":"Ela metre.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[72],"number_text":"੭੨।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰ ਹੈ ਨਿਤ ਅਨਰਥ ਅਰਥ ਨਹੀ ਏਕ ਕਮੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kar hai nit anrath arath nahee ek kamai hai |","meaning_en":"They will do mischief daily and earn not one good thing.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹਿ ਲੈ ਹੈ ਹਰਿ ਨਾਮੁ ਦਾਨ ਕਾਹੂੰ ਨਹੀ ਦੈ ਹੈ।","roman":"Nahi lai hai hari naamu daan kaahoon nahee dai hai |","meaning_en":"They will not take the Lord's Name, nor give charity to anyone.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਤ ਇਕ ਮਤ ਤਜੈ ਇਕ ਮਤਿ ਨਿਤ ਉਚੈ ਹੈ। ੭੨।","roman":"Nit ik mat tajai ik mati nit uchai hai | 72 |","meaning_en":"Daily they abandon one creed and daily raise another.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[73],"number_text":"੭੩।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਤ ਇਕ ਮਤਿ ਮਿਟੈ ਉਠੈ ਹੈ ਨਿਤ ਇਕ ਮਤਿ।","roman":"Nit ik mati mitai uthai hai nit ik mati |","meaning_en":"Daily one creed vanishes and daily one creed rises.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਰਹਿ ਗਇਓ ਭਈ ਬਸੁਧਾ ਅਉਰੈ ਗਤਿ।","roman":"Dharam karam rahi gaio bhaee basudhaa aurai gati |","meaning_en":"The deeds of dharma are left behind; the earth has come to another state.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਕੈ ਗਇਓ ਪਾਪ ਪ੍ਰਚਰਿਓ ਜਹਾ ਤਹ। ੭੩।","roman":"Bharam dharam kai gaio paap prachrio jahaa tah | 73 |","meaning_en":"The honour of dharma has gone; sin spread everywhere.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[74],"number_text":"੭੪।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰਿਸਟਿ ਇਸਟ ਤਜਿ ਦੀਨ ਕਰਤ ਆਰਿਸਟ ਪੁਸਟ ਸਬ।","roman":"Sristi isat taji deen karat aarisat pusat sab |","meaning_en":"Creation has abandoned its chosen deity; all strengthen misfortune.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆਰਿਸਟ ਪੁਸਟ: read as 'promote evil/ill omen'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿਸਟਿ ਸ੍ਰਿਸਟਿ ਤੇ ਮਿਟੀ ਭਏ ਪਾਪਿਸਟ ਭ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਤਬ।","roman":"Bristi sristi te mitee bhae paapisat bhrisat tab |","meaning_en":"Rain vanished from creation; then all became most sinful and corrupt.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਕ ਇਕ ਨਿੰਦ ਹੈ ਇਕ ਇਕ ਕਹਿ ਹਸਿ ਚਲੈ। ੭੪।","roman":"Ik ik nind hai ik ik kahi hasi chalai | 74 |","meaning_en":"One slanders another; one speaks of another and goes off laughing.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[75],"number_text":"੭੫।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜੀ ਆਨਿ ਜਹਾਨ ਕਾਨਿ ਕਾਹੂੰ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਨਹਿ।","roman":"Tajee aani jahaan kaani kaahoon nahee maanhi |","meaning_en":"They have abandoned the honour of the world; they heed no one's regard.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਤ ਮਾਤ ਕੀ ਨਿੰਦ ਨੀਚ ਊਚਹ ਸਮ ਜਾਨਹਿ।","roman":"Taat maat kee nind neech oochah sam jaanhi |","meaning_en":"They slander father and mother; they consider low and high the same.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਭਰਮ ਕੈ ਗਇਓ ਭਈ ਇਕ ਬਰਣ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਸਬ। ੭੫।","roman":"Dharam bharam kai gaio bhaee ik baran prajaa sab | 75 |","meaning_en":"The honour of dharma has gone; all the people became of one caste.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਘਤਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਘਤਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Ghataa chhand","meaning_en":"Ghatta metre.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਘਤਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[76],"number_text":"੭੬।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਹੈ ਪਾਪ ਅਨੇਕ ਨ ਏਕ ਧਰਮ ਕਰ ਹੈ ਨਰ।","roman":"Kari hai paap anek na ek dharam kar hai nar |","meaning_en":"Men will do many sins and not one deed of dharma.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਨੁੱਖ ਅਨੇਕ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਨਗੇ, ਪਰ ਧਰਮ ਦਾ ਇੱਕ ਵੀ ਕਰਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਨਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਿਟ ਜੈ ਹੈ ਸਭ ਖਸਟ ਕਰਮ ਕੇ ਧਰਮ ਘਰਨ ਘਰਿ।","roman":"Mit jai hai sabh khasat karam ke dharam gharan ghari |","meaning_en":"The dharma of the six duties will vanish from every house.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖਸਟ ਕਰਮ: the six duties (of Brahmins).","meaning_pa":"ਛੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ (ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣਾਂ ਦੇ) ਦਾ ਧਰਮ ਹਰ ਘਰ ਵਿੱਚੋਂ ਮਿਟ ਜਾਏਗਾ।","note_pa":"ਖਸਟ ਕਰਮ: ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣਾਂ ਦੇ ਛੇ ਕਰਮ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹਿ ਸੁਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਕਮੈ ਹੈ ਅਧੋਗਤਿ ਜੈ ਹੈ। ਅਮਰਲੋਗਿ ਜੈ ਹੈ ਨ ਬਰ। ੭੬।","roman":"Nahi sukrit kamai hai adhogti jai hai | amarlogi jai hai na bar | 76 |","meaning_en":"They will not earn good deeds; they will go to the lowest state, and will surely not go to the realm of the immortals.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਰ: read as 'surely / at all'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਚੰਗੇ ਕਰਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਮਾਉਣਗੇ, ਨੀਵੀਂ ਗਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਜਾਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਅਮਰ ਲੋਕ ਵਿੱਚ ਜ਼ਰੂਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਾਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਬਰ: ਜ਼ਰੂਰ ਜਾਂ ਬਿਲਕੁਲ ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[77],"number_text":"੭੭।","page":732,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਨ ਕਰ ਹੈ ਏਕ ਅਨੇਕ ਪਾਪ ਕੈ ਹੈ ਸਬ।","roman":"Dharam na kar hai ek anek paap kai hai sab |","meaning_en":"They will not do one deed of dharma; all will do many sins.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਇੱਕ ਵੀ ਧਰਮ ਦਾ ਕੰਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਨਗੇ; ਸਾਰੇ ਅਨੇਕ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਨਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਾਜ ਬੇਚਿ ਤਹ ਫਿਰੈ ਸਕਲ ਜਗੁ।","roman":"Laaj bechi tah phirai sakal jagu |","meaning_en":"The whole world goes about having sold its shame.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰਾ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਆਪਣੀ ਲਾਜ ਵੇਚ ਕੇ ਤੁਰਿਆ ਫਿਰਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਕਮੈ ਵਹ ਦੁਰਗਤਿ ਪੈ ਹੈ। ਪਾਪ ਸਮੁੰਦ ਜੈ ਹੈ ਨ ਤਾਰਿ। ੭੭।","roman":"Paap kamai vah duragti pai hai | paap samund jai hai na taari | 77 |","meaning_en":"Earning sin, they will get an evil fate; they will not cross the ocean of sin.","page":732,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਾਪ ਕਮਾ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਬੁਰੀ ਗਤੀ ਪਾਉਣਗੇ; ਪਾਪ ਦਾ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਪਾਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰ ਸਕਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ"},{"type":"verse","number":[78],"number_text":"੭੮।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਠਉਰ ਠਉਰ ਨਵ ਮਤ ਚਲੇ ਉਠਾ ਧਰਮ ਕੋ ਦੌਰ।","roman":"Thaur thaur nav mat chale uthaa dharam ko daur |","meaning_en":"In place after place new creeds ran; the era of dharma departed.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਉਠਾ ਧਰਮ ਕੋ ਦੌਰ: read as 'the time of dharma rose and left'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਥਾਂ ਥਾਂ ਨਵੇਂ ਮਤ ਚੱਲ ਪਏ; ਧਰਮ ਦਾ ਦੌਰ ਉੱਠ ਗਿਆ।","note_pa":"ਉਠਾ ਧਰਮ ਕੋ ਦੌਰ: ਇਹ 'ਧਰਮ ਦਾ ਦੌਰ ਉੱਠ ਕੇ ਚਲਾ ਗਿਆ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਦੁਰ ਰਹੀ ਪਾਪ ਭਇਓ ਸਿਰਮੌਰ। ੭੮।","roman":"Sukrit jah tah dur rahee paap bhaio sirmaur | 78 |","meaning_en":"Good deeds stayed hidden everywhere; sin became supreme.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੰਗੇ ਕਰਮ ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਲੁਕ ਗਏ; ਪਾਪ ਸਿਰਮੌਰ ਬਣ ਗਿਆ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਵਪਦੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਵਪਦੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Navapdee chhand","meaning_en":"Navpadi metre.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਵਪਦੀ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[79],"number_text":"੭੯।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਕਰਨ ਲਗੇ ਸਭ ਪਾਪਨ। ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਤਜਿ ਕਰ ਹਰਿ ਜਾਪਨ।","roman":"Jah tah karan lage sabh paapan | dharam karam taji kar hari jaapan |","meaning_en":"Everywhere all began to commit sins, abandoning the deeds of dharma and the remembrance of the Lord.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਸਭ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਨ ਲੱਗ ਪਏ, ਧਰਮ ਦੇ ਕਰਮ ਅਤੇ ਹਰੀ ਦਾ ਜਾਪ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਹਨ ਕਉ ਸੁ ਕਰਤ ਸਬ ਬੰਦਨ। ਡਾਰਤ ਧੂਪ ਦੀਪ ਸਿਰਿ ਚੰਦਨ। ੭੯।","roman":"Paahan kau su karat sab bandan | daarat dhoop deep siri chandan | 79 |","meaning_en":"All bow to stones, offering incense and lamps and putting sandal on their heads.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਪੱਥਰਾਂ ਅੱਗੇ ਮੱਥਾ ਟੇਕਦੇ ਹਨ; ਧੂਪ ਤੇ ਦੀਵੇ ਧੁਖਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਸਿਰ ਤੇ ਚੰਦਨ ਲਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[80],"number_text":"੮੦।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਤਜਿ ਭਾਗਤ। ਉਠਿ ਉਠਿ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਸੌ ਲਾਗਤ।","roman":"Jah tah dharam karam taji bhaagat | uthi uthi paap karam sau laagat |","meaning_en":"Everywhere they flee, abandoning the deeds of dharma; rising up, they take to sinful deeds.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਧਰਮ ਦੇ ਕਰਮ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ; ਉੱਠ ਉੱਠ ਕੇ ਪਾਪ ਦੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੱਗ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਭਈ ਧਰਮ ਗਤਿ ਲੋਪੰ। ਪਾਪਹਿ ਲਗੀ ਚਉਗਨੀ ਓਪੰ। ੮੦।","roman":"Jah tah bhaee dharam gati lopan | paaphi lagee chaugnee opan | 80 |","meaning_en":"Everywhere the way of dharma has disappeared; sin has gained a fourfold lustre.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਧਰਮ ਦਾ ਰਾਹ ਮੁੱਕ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ; ਪਾਪ ਨੇ ਚੌਗੁਣੀ ਚਮਕ ਪਾ ਲਈ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[81],"number_text":"੮੧।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜ੍ਯੋ ਧਰਮ ਭਰਮ ਤਜਿ ਅਪਨਾ। ਜਾਨੁਕ ਹੁਤੋ ਲਖਾ ਇਹ ਸੁਪਨਾ।","roman":"Bhaajyo dharam bharam taji apnaa | jaanuk huto lakhaa ih supnaa |","meaning_en":"Dharma fled, abandoning its honour, as though it had been seen only in a dream.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧਰਮ ਆਪਣੀ ਇੱਜ਼ਤ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਿਆ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਇਹ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਸੁਪਨੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਦੇਖਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੋਵੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਤਜੀ ਤ੍ਰੀਅ ਆਪਨ। ਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਕੁਮੰਤ੍ਰ ਲਗੇ ਮਿਲਿ ਜਾਪਨ। ੮੧।","roman":"Sabh sansaar tajee treea aapan | mantr kumantr lage mili jaapan | 81 |","meaning_en":"The whole world abandoned their own wives; together they began to chant evil mantras.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਨੇ ਆਪਣੀਆਂ ਤੀਵੀਆਂ ਛੱਡ ਦਿੱਤੀਆਂ; ਮਿਲ ਕੇ ਬੁਰੇ ਮੰਤਰ ਜਪਣ ਲੱਗ ਪਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[82],"number_text":"੮੨।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਹੁ ਦਿਸ ਘੋਰ ਪ੍ਰਚਰ ਭਇਓ ਪਾਪਾ। ਕੋਊ ਨ ਜਾਪ ਸਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਜਾਪਾ।","roman":"Chahu dis ghor prachar bhaio paapaa | ko'oo na jaap sakai hari jaapaa |","meaning_en":"On all four sides terrible sin spread; no one can repeat the remembrance of the Lord.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਰੇ ਪਾਸੇ ਘੋਰ ਪਾਪ ਫੈਲ ਗਿਆ; ਕੋਈ ਵੀ ਹਰੀ ਦਾ ਜਾਪ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰ ਸਕਦਾ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਸਭ ਜਾ ਚਲ ਪਈ। ਧਰਮ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਯਾ ਜਗ ਤੇ ਗਈ। ੮੨।","roman":"Paap kriaa sabh jaa chal paee | dharam kriaa yaa jag te gaee | 82 |","meaning_en":"The practice of sin went everywhere; the practice of dharma left this world.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਾਪ ਦੇ ਕਰਮ ਹਰ ਪਾਸੇ ਚੱਲ ਪਏ; ਧਰਮ ਦੇ ਕਰਮ ਇਸ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਤੋਂ ਚਲੇ ਗਏ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ ਦੂਜਾ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ ਦੂਜਾ","roman":"Aril doojaa","meaning_en":"Arill metre, the second.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ ਛੰਦ ਦੂਜਾ"},{"type":"verse","number":[83],"number_text":"੮੩।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਅਧਰਮ ਉਪਜਿਯਾ। ਜਾਨੁਕ ਧਰਮ ਪੰਖ ਕਰਿ ਭਜਿਯਾ।","roman":"Jahaa tahaa adhram upjiyaa | jaanuk dharam pankh kari bhajiyaa |","meaning_en":"Everywhere unrighteousness arose, as though dharma had taken wings and fled.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਥੇ ਤਿੱਥੇ ਅਧਰਮ ਉਪਜ ਪਿਆ; ਜਿਵੇਂ ਧਰਮ ਖੰਭ ਲਾ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਿਆ ਹੋਵੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡੋਲਤ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਪੁਰਖ ਅਪਾਵਨ। ਲਾਗਤ ਕਤ ਹੀ ਧਰਮ ਕੋ ਦਾਵਨ। ੮੩।","roman":"Dolat jah tah purakh apaavan | laagat kat hee dharam ko daavan | 83 |","meaning_en":"Impure men wander everywhere; nowhere does the hem of dharma touch them.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਾਵਨ: read as 'hem (daaman)'; i.e. no one holds on to dharma; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਅਪਵਿੱਤਰ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਭਟਕਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਿਤੇ ਵੀ ਉਹ ਧਰਮ ਦਾ ਪੱਲਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਫੜਦੇ।","note_pa":"ਦਾਵਨ: 'ਦਾਮਨ' (ਪੱਲਾ) ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਭਾਵ ਕੋਈ ਵੀ ਧਰਮ ਨੂੰ ਨਹੀਂ ਫੜਦਾ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[84],"number_text":"੮੪।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਥਹ ਛਾਡਿ ਅਨਰਥ ਬਤਾਵਤ। ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਚਿਤਿ ਏਕ ਨ ਲਿਆਵਤ।","roman":"Arthah chhaadi anrath bataavat | dharam karam chiti ek na liaavat |","meaning_en":"Leaving what is meaningful, they speak of mischief; they do not bring a single deed of dharma to mind.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਰਥ ਵਾਲੀ ਗੱਲ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਬੁਰੀਆਂ ਗੱਲਾਂ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਧਰਮ ਦਾ ਇੱਕ ਵੀ ਕੰਮ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਲਿਆਉਂਦੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਭੁਲਾਵਤ। ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਆਰਿਸਟ ਬਤਾਵਤ। ੮੪।","roman":"Karam dharam kee kriaa bhulaavat | jahaa tahaa aarisat bataavat | 84 |","meaning_en":"They make people forget the practice of dharmic deeds and everywhere speak of evil.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਲੋਕਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਧਰਮ ਦੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦਾ ਅਭਿਆਸ ਭੁਲਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਬੁਰੀਆਂ ਗੱਲਾਂ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕੁਲਕ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਕੁਲਕ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Kulak chhand","meaning_en":"Kulak metre.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕੁਲਕ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[85],"number_text":"੮੫।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਨ ਕਰਹੀ। ਹਰਿ ਨ ਉਚਰਹੀ।","roman":"Dharam na karhee | hari na ucharhee |","meaning_en":"They do not practise dharma, nor utter the Lord's Name.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਰਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦੇ, ਅਤੇ ਹਰੀ ਦਾ ਨਾਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਉਚਾਰਦੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰ ਘਰਿ ਡੋਲੈ। ਜਲਹ ਬਿਰੋਲੈ। ੮੫।","roman":"Par ghari dolai | jalah birolai | 85 |","meaning_en":"They wander into others' houses; they churn water.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Churning water: proverbial for futile effort.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਦੂਜਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਘਰਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਟਕਦੇ ਹਨ; ਪਾਣੀ ਰਿੜਕਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਪਾਣੀ ਰਿੜਕਣਾ: ਬੇਕਾਰ ਮਿਹਨਤ ਦਾ ਮੁਹਾਵਰਾ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[86],"number_text":"੮੬।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਹੈ ਨ ਅਰਥੰ। ਕਹੈ ਅਨਰਥੰ।","roman":"Lahai na arthan | kahai anarthan |","meaning_en":"They grasp no meaning, and speak mischief.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਅਰਥ ਨੂੰ ਨਹੀਂ ਸਮਝਦੇ, ਅਤੇ ਬੁਰੀਆਂ ਗੱਲਾਂ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਚਨ ਨ ਸਾਚੇ। ਮਤਿ ਕੇ ਕਾਚੇ। ੮੬।","roman":"Bachan na saache | mati ke kaache | 86 |","meaning_en":"Their words are not true; they are unripe in understanding.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੇ ਬਚਨ ਸੱਚੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਹਨ; ਉਹ ਸਮਝ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੱਚੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[87],"number_text":"੮੭।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰਤ੍ਰੀਆ ਰਾਚੈ। ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਜਾਚੈ।","roman":"Partreeaa raachai | ghari ghari jaachai |","meaning_en":"They are absorbed in others' women, and beg from house to house.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪਰਾਈਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੀਨ ਰਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਤੇ ਘਰ ਘਰ ਮੰਗਦੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਡੋਲੈ। ਰਹਿ ਰਹਿ ਬੋਲੈ। ੮੭।","roman":"Jah tah dolai | rahi rahi bolai | 87 |","meaning_en":"They wander here and there and keep on chattering.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਇੱਧਰ ਉੱਧਰ ਭਟਕਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਲਗਾਤਾਰ ਬੋਲਦੇ ਰਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[88],"number_text":"੮੮।","page":733,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਨ ਨਹੀ ਛੋਰੈ। ਨਿਸਿ ਘਰ ਫੋਰੈ।","roman":"Dhan nahee chhorai | nisi ghar phorai |","meaning_en":"They spare no wealth; at night they break into houses.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਨ ਨਹੀਂ ਛੱਡਦੇ; ਰਾਤ ਨੂੰ ਘਰ ਪਾੜਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹਿ ਬਹੁ ਮਾਰੀਅਤ। ਨਰਕਹਿ ਡਾਰੀਅਤ। ੮੮।","roman":"Gahi bahu maareeat | narakhi daareeat | 88 |","meaning_en":"Caught, they are beaten much and cast into hell.","page":733,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਫੜੇ ਜਾ ਕੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਮਾਰ ਖਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਤੇ ਨਰਕ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੁੱਟੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[89],"number_text":"੮੯।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸ ਦੁਰ ਕਰਮੰ। ਛੁਟ ਜਗਿ ਧਰਮੰ।","roman":"As dur karman | chhut jagi dharman |","meaning_en":"Such are the evil deeds; dharma has left the world.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਹੋ ਜਿਹੇ ਹਨ ਬੁਰੇ ਕਰਮ; ਸੰਸਾਰ ਤੋਂ ਧਰਮ ਚਲਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਤਿ ਪਿਤ ਭਰਮੈ। ਧਸਤ ਨ ਘਰ ਮੈ। ੮੯।","roman":"Mati pit bharmai | dhasat na ghar mai | 89 |","meaning_en":"Mother and father wander about; they cannot enter the house.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਤਿ ਪਿਤ ਭਰਮੈ: printed so; read as 'mother and father wander (homeless)'; possibly 'mind and..'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਪਿਓ ਭਟਕਦੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਉਹ ਘਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੜ ਨਹੀਂ ਸਕਦੇ।","note_pa":"ਮਤਿ ਪਿਤ ਭਰਮੈ: ਛਪਿਆ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਹੀ ਹੈ; 'ਮਾਂ ਤੇ ਪਿਓ ਬੇਘਰ ਭਟਕਦੇ ਹਨ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[90],"number_text":"੯੦।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਖ ਮੁਖ ਮੋਰੈ। ਭ੍ਰਿਤ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਿ ਛੋਰੈ।","roman":"Sikh mukh morai | bhrit nripi chhorai |","meaning_en":"The disciple turns his face from the guru; the servant leaves the king.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੇਲਾ ਗੁਰੂ ਵੱਲੋਂ ਮੂੰਹ ਮੋੜਦਾ ਹੈ; ਨੌਕਰ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਛੱਡਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜਿ ਤ੍ਰੀਆ ਭਰਤਾ। ਬਿਸਰੋ ਕਰਤਾ। ੯੦।","roman":"Taji treeaa bhartaa | bisro kartaa | 90 |","meaning_en":"The wife leaves her husband; the Creator is forgotten.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਤਨੀ ਪਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਛੱਡ ਦਿੰਦੀ ਹੈ; ਕਰਤਾ (ਰੱਬ) ਭੁੱਲ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[91],"number_text":"੯੧।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਵ ਨਵ ਕਰਮੰ। ਬਢਿ ਗਇਓ ਭਰਮੰ।","roman":"Nav nav karman | badhi gaio bharman |","meaning_en":"New and newer deeds; delusion has grown.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਵੇਂ ਤੋਂ ਨਵੇਂ ਕਰਮ; ਭਰਮ ਵਧ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਜਗ ਪਾਪੀ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਜਾਪੀ। ੯੧।","roman":"Sabh jag paapee | kahoon na jaapee | 91 |","meaning_en":"The whole world is sinful; nowhere is anyone who remembers God.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰਾ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਪਾਪੀ ਹੈ; ਕਿਤੇ ਵੀ ਕੋਈ ਰੱਬ ਦਾ ਜਾਪ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪਦਮਾਵਤੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪਦਮਾਵਤੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Padmaavtee chhand","meaning_en":"Padmavati metre.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਦਮਾਵਤੀ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[92],"number_text":"੯੨।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖੀਅਤ ਸਬ ਪਾਪੀ ਨਹ ਹਰਿ ਜਾਪੀ ਤਦਿਪ ਮਹਾ ਰਿਸ ਠਾਨੈ।","roman":"Dekheeat sab paapee nah hari jaapee tadip mahaa ris thaanai |","meaning_en":"All are seen to be sinners, none remembering the Lord; even so they bear great anger.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਪਾਪੀ ਦਿਸਦੇ ਹਨ, ਕੋਈ ਹਰੀ ਦਾ ਜਾਪ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦਾ; ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਉਹ ਬਹੁਤ ਗੁੱਸਾ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਬਿਭਚਾਰੀ ਪਰਤ੍ਰਿਅ ਭਾਰੀ ਦੇਵ ਪਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਹੀ ਮਾਨੈ।","roman":"Ati bibhchaaree partria bhaaree dev pitr nahee maanai |","meaning_en":"Greatly debauched, heavily given to others' women, they honour neither gods nor ancestors.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਵਿਭਚਾਰੀ, ਪਰਾਈਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੱਡੇ ਰੁੱਝੇ ਹੋਏ, ਉਹ ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਤੇ ਪਿਤਰਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਨਦੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਦਿਪ ਮਹਾ ਬਰ ਕਹਤੇ ਧਰਮ ਧਰ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਅਧਿਕਾਰੀ।","roman":"Tadip mahaa bar kahte dharam dhar paap karam adhikaaree |","meaning_en":"Even so they call themselves very great upholders of dharma, these masters of sinful deeds.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਉਹ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨੂੰ ਧਰਮ ਦੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਧਾਰਨੀ ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਇਹ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦੇ ਅਧਿਕਾਰੀ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧ੍ਰਿਗ ਧ੍ਰਿਗ ਸਭ ਆਖੈ ਮੁਖ ਪਰ ਨਹੀ ਭਾਖੈ ਦੇਹਿ ਪ੍ਰਿਸਟ ਚੜਿ ਗਾਰੀ। ੯੨।","roman":"Dhrig dhrig sabh aakhai mukh par nahee bhaakhai dehi prisat chari gaaree | 92 |","meaning_en":"All say 'shame, shame' on them; not to their faces, but they curse them behind their backs.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਭ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ 'ਧਿੱਕ ਧਿੱਕ' ਆਖਦੇ ਹਨ; ਮੂੰਹ ਉੱਤੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਹਿੰਦੇ, ਪਰ ਪਿੱਠ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਗਾਲ੍ਹਾਂ ਕੱਢਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[93],"number_text":"੯੩।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖੀਅਤ ਬਿਨ ਕਰਮੰ ਤਜ ਕੁਲ ਧਰਮੰ ਤਦਿਪ ਕਹਾਤ ਸੁ ਮਾਨਸ।","roman":"Dekheeat bin karman taj kul dharman tadip kahaat su maanas |","meaning_en":"They are seen without good deeds, having left the dharma of their families; yet they are called good men.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਚੰਗੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾਂ ਦਿਸਦੇ ਹਨ, ਕੁਲ ਦਾ ਧਰਮ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ; ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਚੰਗੇ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਕਿਹਾ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਰਤਿ ਲੋਭੰ ਰਹਤ ਸਛੋਭੰ ਲੋਕ ਸਗਲ ਭਲੁ ਜਾਨਸ।","roman":"Ati rati lobhan rahat sachhobhan lok sagal bhalu jaanas |","meaning_en":"Deeply attached to greed, they remain agitated, yet all the people take them as good.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲੋਭ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਹੁਤ ਰੁੱਝੇ, ਬੇਚੈਨ ਰਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਸਾਰੇ ਲੋਕ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਭਲਾ ਜਾਣਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਦਿਪ ਬਿਨਾ ਗਤਿ ਚਲਤ ਬੁਰੀ ਮਤਿ ਲੋਭ ਮੋਹ ਬਸਿ ਭਾਰੀ।","roman":"Tadip binaa gati chalat buree mati lobh moh basi bhaaree |","meaning_en":"Yet they go without a good end, with wicked minds, heavily under greed and attachment.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਉਹ ਬੁਰੀ ਮਤ ਨਾਲ, ਲੋਭ ਤੇ ਮੋਹ ਦੇ ਵੱਸ ਪਏ ਭਾਰੀ, ਬਿਨਾਂ ਚੰਗੀ ਗਤੀ ਦੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਿਤ ਮਾਤ ਨ ਮਾਨੈ ਕਛੁ ਨ ਜਾਨੈ ਲੈਹ ਘਰਣ ਤੇ ਗਾਰੀ। ੯੩।","roman":"Pit maat na maanai kachhu na jaanai laih gharan te gaaree | 93 |","meaning_en":"They do not heed father or mother, they know nothing; they take abuse from their wives.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਘਰਣ: read as 'gharni', the housewife; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪਿਓ ਮਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਨਦੇ, ਕੁਝ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਾਣਦੇ; ਘਰਵਾਲੀ ਤੋਂ ਗਾਲ੍ਹਾਂ ਲੈਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਘਰਣ: 'ਘਰਨੀ' (ਘਰਵਾਲੀ) ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[94],"number_text":"੯੪।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਅਤ ਜੇ ਧਰਮੀ ਤੇ ਭਏ ਅਕਰਮੀ ਤਦਿਪ ਕਹਾਤ ਮਹਾ ਮਤਿ।","roman":"Dekha'at je dharmee te bhae akarmee tadip kahaat mahaa mati |","meaning_en":"Those who were seen to be righteous have become doers of wrong; yet they are called very wise.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਧਰਮੀ ਦਿਸਦੇ ਸਨ, ਉਹ ਅਧਰਮੀ ਬਣ ਗਏ ਹਨ; ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਬਹੁਤ ਬੁੱਧੀਮਾਨ ਕਿਹਾ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਬਸ ਨਾਰੀ ਅਬਗਤਿ ਭਾਰੀ ਜਾਨਤ ਸਕਲ ਬਿਨਾ ਜਤ।","roman":"Ati bas naaree abagti bhaaree jaanat sakal binaa jat |","meaning_en":"Greatly under women's control, in a very low state; all know them to be without continence.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਦੇ ਵੱਸ ਪਏ, ਬਹੁਤ ਨੀਵੀਂ ਹਾਲਤ ਵਿੱਚ; ਸਭ ਜਾਣਦੇ ਹਨ ਕਿ ਉਹ ਸੰਜਮ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾਂ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਦਿਪ ਨ ਮਾਨਤ ਕੁਮਤਿ ਪ੍ਰਠਾਨਤ ਮਤਿ ਅਰੁ ਗਤਿ ਕੇ ਕਾਚੇ।","roman":"Tadip na maanat kumti prathaanat mati aru gati ke kaache |","meaning_en":"Yet they do not heed, they establish evil counsel, unripe in mind and conduct.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਉਹ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਨਦੇ, ਬੁਰੀ ਸਲਾਹ ਚਲਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਮਨ ਤੇ ਚਾਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੱਚੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਤਿਹ ਘਰਿ ਡੋਲਤ ਭਲੇ ਨ ਬੋਲਤ ਲੋਗ ਲਾਜ ਤਜਿ ਨਾਚੇ। ੯੪।","roman":"Jih tih ghari dolat bhale na bolat log laaj taji naache | 94 |","meaning_en":"They wander into this house and that, speak no good, and dance, abandoning public shame.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇੱਧਰ ਉੱਧਰ ਘਰਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਟਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਚੰਗਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਬੋਲਦੇ, ਅਤੇ ਲੋਕ-ਲਾਜ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕਿਲਕਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਕਿਲਕਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Kilkaa chhand","meaning_en":"Kilka metre.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਲਕਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[95],"number_text":"੯੫।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਕਰੈ ਨਿਤ ਪ੍ਰਾਤਿ ਘਨੇ। ਜਨੁ ਦੋਖਨ ਕੇ ਤਰੁ ਸੁਧ ਬਨੇ।","roman":"Paap karai nit praati ghane | janu dokhan ke taru sudh bane |","meaning_en":"They commit many sins every morning, as though they have become pure trees of faults.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਰੋਜ਼ ਸਵੇਰੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਉਹ ਔਗੁਣਾਂ ਦੇ ਪੂਰੇ ਰੁੱਖ ਬਣ ਗਏ ਹੋਣ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਛੋਰਿ ਭਜਾ ਗਤਿ ਧਰਮਣ ਕੀ। ਸੁ ਜਹਾ ਤਹਾ ਪਾਪ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰੀ। ੯੫।","roman":"Jag chhori bhajaa gati dharman kee | su jahaa tahaa paap kriaa prachuree | 95 |","meaning_en":"The way of dharma has left the world and fled; everywhere the practice of sin has spread.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧਰਮ ਦੀ ਗਤੀ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਈ ਹੈ; ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਪਾਪ ਦੇ ਕਰਮ ਫੈਲ ਗਏ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[96],"number_text":"੯੬।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗ ਲਏ ਫਿਰੈ ਪਾਪਨ ਹੀ। ਤਜਿ ਭਾਜ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਜਗ ਜਾਪਨ ਕੀ।","roman":"Sang lae phirai paapan hee | taji bhaaj kriaa jag jaapan kee |","meaning_en":"They go about with only sins in their company; the practice of the world's remembrance of God has fled.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਪਾਪਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਨਾਲ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਸੰਸਾਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੱਬ ਦੇ ਜਾਪ ਦਾ ਕੰਮ ਭੱਜ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਪਿਤ੍ਰ ਨ ਪਾਵਕ ਮਾਨਹਿਗੇ। ਸਭ ਆਪਨ ਤੇ ਘਟਿ ਜਾਨਹਿਗੇ। ੯੬।","roman":"Dev pitr na paavak maanhige | sabh aapan te ghati jaanhige | 96 |","meaning_en":"They will honour neither gods, nor ancestors, nor fire; they will consider all lesser than themselves.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ, ਪਿਤਰਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਅੱਗ ਨੂੰ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਨਣਗੇ; ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣੇ ਤੋਂ ਨੀਵਾਂ ਸਮਝਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Madhubhaar chhand","meaning_en":"Madhubhar metre.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[97],"number_text":"੯੭।","page":734,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਜਿਓ ਸੁ ਧਰਮ। ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰਿਓ ਕੁਕਰਮ।","roman":"Bhajio su dharam | prachurio kukram |","meaning_en":"Good dharma has fled; evil deeds have spread.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੰਗਾ ਧਰਮ ਭੱਜ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ; ਬੁਰੇ ਕਰਮ ਫੈਲ ਗਏ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਜਹਾਨ। ਤਜਿ ਭਾਜ ਆਨਿ। ੯੭।","roman":"Jah tah jahaan | taji bhaaj aani | 97 |","meaning_en":"Everywhere in the world honour has left and fled.","page":734,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆਨਿ: read as 'honour, pledge'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੰਸਾਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਇੱਜ਼ਤ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਈ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਆਨਿ: 'ਇੱਜ਼ਤ, ਵਚਨ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[98],"number_text":"੯੮।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਤਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਅਨਰਥ। ਕਰ ਹੈ ਸਮਰਥ।","roman":"Nitprati anrath | kar hai samrath |","meaning_en":"Every day the powerful will do mischief.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਰੋਜ਼ ਤਾਕਤਵਾਲੇ ਬੁਰਾਈ ਕਰਨਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠਿ ਭਾਜ ਧਰਮ। ਲੈ ਸੰਗਿ ਸੁਕਰਮ। ੯੮।","roman":"Uthi bhaaj dharam | lai sangi sukram | 98 |","meaning_en":"Dharma has risen and fled, taking good deeds with it.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧਰਮ ਉੱਠ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ, ਚੰਗੇ ਕਰਮ ਆਪਣੇ ਨਾਲ ਲੈ ਕੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[99],"number_text":"੯੯।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰ ਹੈ ਕੁਚਾਰ। ਤਜਿ ਸੁਭ ਅਚਾਰ।","roman":"Kar hai kuchaar | taji subh achaar |","meaning_en":"They will do bad conduct, leaving good conduct.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬੁਰਾ ਆਚਰਣ ਕਰਨਗੇ, ਚੰਗਾ ਆਚਰਣ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਈ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਅਉਰ। ਸਬ ਠੌਰ ਠੌਰ। ੯੯।","roman":"Bhaee kriaa aur | sab thaur thaur | 99 |","meaning_en":"The practice has become different in every place.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਕੰਮ-ਕਾਰ ਵੱਖਰਾ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[100],"number_text":"੧੦੦।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਕਰਤ ਸੰਗ। ਪ੍ਰੇਰਤਿ ਅਨੰਗ।","roman":"Nahee karat sang | prerti anang |","meaning_en":"They keep no proper company; Kama (desire) drives them on.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਹੀ ਕਰਤ ਸੰਗ: possibly 'they feel no shame (sang)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਚੰਗੀ ਸੰਗਤ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦੇ; ਕਾਮ (ਵਾਸਨਾ) ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਪ੍ਰੇਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਨਹੀ ਕਰਤ ਸੰਗ: ਸ਼ਾਇਦ 'ਸ਼ਰਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦੇ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਸੁਤਾ ਭੋਗ। ਜੋ ਹੈ ਅਜੋਗ। ੧੦੦।","roman":"Kari sutaa bhog | jo hai ajog | 100 |","meaning_en":"They enjoy even a daughter, which is improper.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧੀ ਨਾਲ ਵੀ ਭੋਗ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜੋ ਅਯੋਗ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[101],"number_text":"੧੦੧।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜਿ ਲਾਜ ਭਾਜ। ਸੰਜੁਤ ਸਮਾਜ।","roman":"Taji laaj bhaaj | sanjut samaaj |","meaning_en":"Shame has abandoned and fled the whole of society;","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਸਮਾਜ ਵਿੱਚੋਂ ਲਾਜ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਈ ਹੈ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਟ ਚਲਾ ਧਰਮ। ਬਢਿਓ ਅਧਰਮ। ੧੦੧।","roman":"Ghat chalaa dharam | badhio adhram | 101 |","meaning_en":"dharma has gone on decreasing; unrighteousness has grown.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧਰਮ ਘਟਦਾ ਜਾ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੈ; ਅਧਰਮ ਵਧ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[102],"number_text":"੧੦੨।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੀੜਤ ਕੁਨਾਰਿ। ਤਜਿ ਧਰਮ ਵਾਰਿ।","roman":"Kreerat kunaari | taji dharam vaari |","meaning_en":"They sport with bad women, leaving their wedded wives.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਰਮ ਵਾਰਿ: read as 'wife of dharma (wedded wife)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬੁਰੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਨਾਲ ਖੇਡਦੇ ਹਨ, ਆਪਣੀਆਂ ਵਿਆਹੀਆਂ ਪਤਨੀਆਂ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ।","note_pa":"ਧਰਮ ਵਾਰਿ: 'ਧਰਮ ਦੀ ਵਿਆਹੀ ਪਤਨੀ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਢਿ ਗਯੋ ਭਰਮ। ਭਾਜੰਤ ਧਰਮ। ੧੦੨।","roman":"Badhi gayo bharam | bhaajant dharam | 102 |","meaning_en":"Delusion has grown; dharma is fleeing.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਰਮ ਵਧ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ; ਧਰਮ ਭੱਜ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[103],"number_text":"੧੦੩।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਸਨ ਬਿਦੇਸ। ਪਾਪੀ ਨਰੇਸ।","roman":"Desan bides | paapee nares |","meaning_en":"In lands home and foreign the kings are sinners.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੇਸਾਂ-ਵਿਦੇਸਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਰਾਜੇ ਪਾਪੀ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮੀ ਨ ਕੋਇ। ਪਾਪ ਅਤਿ ਹੋਇ। ੧੦੩।","roman":"Dharmee na koi | paap ati hoi | 103 |","meaning_en":"None is righteous; there is great sin.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕੋਈ ਧਰਮੀ ਨਹੀਂ; ਬਹੁਤ ਪਾਪ ਹੋ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[104],"number_text":"੧੦੪।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਧੂ ਸਤ੍ਰਾਸ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਉਦਾਸ।","roman":"Saadhoo satraas | jah tah udaas |","meaning_en":"The holy are terrified, sad everywhere.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਧੂ ਡਰੇ ਹੋਏ ਹਨ, ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਉਦਾਸ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪੀਨ ਰਾਜ। ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਸਰਬ ਸਾਜ।੧੦੪।","roman":"Paapeen raaj | grih sarab saaj | 104 |","meaning_en":"The sinners rule, with every comfort in their homes.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਾਪੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਰਾਜ ਹੈ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੇ ਘਰਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਰ ਸੁੱਖ ਸਾਧਨ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਹਰਿ ਗੀਤਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਗੀਤਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Hari geetaa chhand","meaning_en":"Hari Geeta metre.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰਿ ਗੀਤਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[105],"number_text":"੧੦੫।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਦ੍ਰੋਨ ਗਿਰਵਰ ਸਿਖਰ ਤਰ ਨਰ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਭਏ ਭਨੰ।","roman":"Sab dron girvar sikhar tar nar paap karam bhae bhanan |","meaning_en":"In all the valleys, beneath the peaks of great mountains, men are said to have taken to sinful deeds.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦ੍ਰੋਨ: read as 'valley'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠਿ ਭਾਜ ਧਰਮ ਸਭਰਮ ਹੁਐ ਚਮਕੰਤ ਦਾਮਿਨਿ ਸੋ ਮਨੰ।","roman":"Uthi bhaaj dharam sabhram huai chamkant daamini so manan |","meaning_en":"Dharma rose and fled in fear, like lightning flashing away.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਧੌ ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਸੁਭਟ ਸਮਾਜ ਸੰਜੁਤ ਜੀਤ ਹੈ ਬਸੁਧਾ ਬਲੀ।","roman":"Kidhau soodr subhat samaaj sanjut jeet hai basudhaa balee |","meaning_en":"Or it seems the Shudras, with their warrior bands, will conquer the earth by force;","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਧੌ ਅਤ੍ਰ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਤਜੇ ਭਜੇ ਅਰੁ ਅਉਰ ਅਉਰ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਚਲੀ। ੧੦੫।","roman":"Kidhau atr chhatr taje bhaje aru aur aur kriaa chalee | 105 |","meaning_en":"or the Kshatriyas have abandoned weapons and canopy and fled, and other and other practices have begun.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਤ੍ਰ: read as 'astra', weapons."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[106],"number_text":"੧੦੬।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਦੇਸ ਦੇਸ ਬਿਦੇਸ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਸਬੈ ਲਗੇ।","roman":"Nrip des des bides jah tah paap karam sabai lage |","meaning_en":"Kings in land after land, home and abroad, have all taken to sinful deeds.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਰ ਲਾਜ ਛਾਡਿ ਨਿਲਾਜ ਹੁਐ ਫਿਰੈ ਧਰਮ ਕਰਮ ਸਬੈ ਭਗੇ।","roman":"Nar laaj chhaadi nilaaj huai phirai dharam karam sabai bhage |","meaning_en":"Men have cast off shame and go about shameless; all the deeds of dharma have fled.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਧੌ ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਸਰਬ ਮਹਿ ਮਹਾਰਾਜ੍ਯ ਪਾਇ ਪ੍ਰਹਰਖ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kidhau soodr jah tah sarab mahi mahaaraajy paai prahrakh hai |","meaning_en":"Or the Shudras everywhere, having gained great rule over all, are rejoicing;","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਧੌ ਚੋਰ ਛਾਡਿ ਅਚੋਰ ਕੇ ਗਹਿ ਸਰਬ ਦਰਬ ਆਕਰਖ ਹੈ। ੧੦੬।","roman":"Kidhau chor chhaadi achor ke gahi sarab darab aakrakh hai | 106 |","meaning_en":"or the thieves are let go and the honest seized, and all their wealth is drawn off.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤ੍ਰਿਭੰਗੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿਭੰਗੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tribhangee chhand","meaning_en":"Tribhangi metre.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[107],"number_text":"੧੦੭।","page":735,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਜਗ ਪਾਪੀ ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਜਾਪੀ ਅਥਪਨ ਥਾਪੀ ਦੇਸ ਦਿਸੰ।","roman":"Sabh jag paapee kahoon na jaapee athpan thaapee des disan |","meaning_en":"The whole world is sinful, no one remembers God; in every land and direction they set up what should not be set up.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਮਤਵਾਰੇ ਭ੍ਰਮਤ ਭ੍ਰਮਾਰੇ ਮਤਿ ਨ ਉਜਿਯਾਰੇ ਬਾਧ ਰਿਸੰ।","roman":"Jah tah matvaare bhramat bhramaare mati na ujiyaare baadh risan |","meaning_en":"Everywhere intoxicated people wander deluded; their minds are not enlightened, they are bound by anger.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪਨ ਰਸ ਰਾਤੇ ਦੁਰਮਤਿ ਮਾਤੇ ਕੁਮਤਨ ਦਾਤੇ ਮਤ ਨੇਕੰ।","roman":"Paapan ras raate duramti maate kumtan daate mat nekan |","meaning_en":"Steeped in the taste of sins, drunk with evil thinking, givers of evil counsel, of many creeds;","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਤ ਨੇਕੰ: read as 'many creeds' (anek); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਉਠਿ ਧਾਵੈ ਚਿਤ ਲਲਚਾਵੈ ਕਛੁਹੂੰ ਨ ਪਾਵੈ ਬਿਨੁ ਏਕੰ। ੧੦੭।","roman":"Jah tah uthi dhaavai chit lalchaavai kachhuhoon na paavai binu ekan | 107 |","meaning_en":"they rise and run here and there, their minds full of craving, but they gain nothing without the One.","page":735,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[108],"number_text":"੧੦੮।","page":736,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜਿ ਹਰਿ ਧਰਮੰ ਗਹਤ ਕੁਕਰਮੰ ਬਿਨ ਪ੍ਰਭ ਕਰਮੰ ਸਬ ਭਰਮੰ।","roman":"Taji hari dharman gahat kukarman bin prabh karman sab bharman |","meaning_en":"Leaving the dharma of the Lord, they take up evil deeds; without the deeds of the Lord, all is delusion.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਾਗਤ ਨਹੀ ਤੰਤ੍ਰੰ ਫੁਰਤ ਨ ਮੰਤ੍ਰੰ ਚਲਤ ਨ ਜੰਤ੍ਰੰ ਬਿਨ ਮਰਮੰ।","roman":"Laagat nahee tantran phurat na mantran chalat na jantran bin marman |","meaning_en":"Without the inner secret, tantras do not take effect, mantras do not work, and yantras do not run.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਪ ਹੈ ਨ ਦੇਵੀ ਅਲਖ ਅਭੇਵੀ ਆਦਿ ਅਜੇਵੀ ਪਰਮ ਜੁਧੀ।","roman":"Jap hai na devee alakh abhevee aadi ajevee param judhee |","meaning_en":"They do not remember the Goddess, the unseen, the mysterious, the primal, the unconquerable, the supreme warrior.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਬੁਧਨ ਤਨ ਰਾਚੇ ਕਹਤ ਨ ਸਾਚੇ ਪ੍ਰਭਹਿ ਨ ਜਾਚੇ ਤਮਕ ਬੁਧੀ। ੧੦੮।","roman":"Kubudhan tan raache kahat na saache prabhhi na jaache tamak budhee | 108 |","meaning_en":"Their bodies absorbed in evil wisdom, they do not speak truth nor ask of the Lord, their intellect dark.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਮਕ ਬੁਧੀ: read as 'tamasic (dark) intellect'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਹੀਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਹੀਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Heer chhand","meaning_en":"Heer metre.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[109],"number_text":"੧੦੯।","page":736,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਪੰਡਿਤ ਗੁਣ ਮੰਡਿਤ ਸੁਬੁਧਿਨਿ ਖੰਡਿਤ ਦੇਖੀਐ।","roman":"Apandit gun mandit subudhini khandit dekheeai |","meaning_en":"The unlearned are seen adorned with merits, and those of good intellect are seen broken down.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਤ੍ਰੀ ਬਰ ਧਰਮ ਛਾਡਿ ਅਕਰਮ ਧਰਮ ਲੇਖੀਐ।","roman":"Chhatree bar dharam chhaadi akram dharam lekheeai |","meaning_en":"Kshatriyas leave their noble dharma, and wrong deeds are reckoned as dharma.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤਿ ਰਹਤ ਪਾਪ ਗ੍ਰਹਿਤ ਕ੍ਰੁਧ ਚਹਤ ਜਾਨੀਐ।","roman":"Sati rahat paap grahit krudh chahat jaaneeai |","meaning_en":"They are known to be without truth, seized by sin, seeking anger;","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਧਰਮ ਲੀਣ ਅੰਗ ਛੀਣ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਪੀਣ ਮਾਨੀਐ। ੧੦੯।","roman":"Adhram leen ang chheen krodh peen maaneeai | 109 |","meaning_en":"absorbed in unrighteousness, weak in body, drinkers of anger they are reckoned.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[110],"number_text":"੧੧੦।","page":736,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਤ੍ਰੀਅਨ ਰਸ ਚਾਹੀ ਗੁਣਨ ਨ ਗ੍ਰਾਹੀ ਜਾਨੀਐ।","roman":"Kutreean ras chaahee gunan na graahee jaaneeai |","meaning_en":"They are known to desire the pleasure of bad women, not to grasp virtues;","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤ ਕਰਮ ਛਾਡ ਕੇ ਅਸਤ ਕਰਮ ਮਾਨੀਐ।","roman":"Sat karam chhaad ke asat karam maaneeai |","meaning_en":"leaving true deeds, they honour false deeds.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਪ ਰਹਿਤ ਜੂਪ ਗ੍ਰਹਿਤ ਪਾਪ ਸਹਿਤ ਦੇਖੀਐ।","roman":"Roop rahit joop grahit paap sahit dekheeai |","meaning_en":"They are seen without beauty, caught in gambling, full of sin;","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜੂਪ: read as 'juaa', gambling."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਕਰਮ ਲੀਨ ਧਰਮ ਛੀਨ ਨਾਰਿ ਅਧੀਨ ਪੇਖੀਐ। ੧੧੦।","roman":"Akram leen dharam chheen naari adheen pekheeai | 110 |","meaning_en":"absorbed in wrong deeds, weak in dharma, they are seen subject to women.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪਧਿਸਟਕਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪਧਿਸਟਕਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Padhisatkaa chhand","meaning_en":"Padhistaka metre.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[111],"number_text":"੧੧੧।","page":736,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਪਾਪਨ ਤੇ ਜਗ ਛਾਇ ਰਹਿਓ। ਕਛੁ ਬੁਧਿ ਬਲ ਧਰਮ ਨ ਜਾਤ ਕਹਿਓ।","roman":"Ati paapan te jag chhaai rahio | kachhu budhi bal dharam na jaat kahio |","meaning_en":"The world is covered with great sins; intellect, strength and dharma cannot be spoken of at all.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਿਸ ਬਦਿਸਨ ਕੇ ਜੀਅ ਦੇਖਿ ਸਬੈ। ਬਹੁ ਪਾਪ ਕਰਮ ਰਤਿ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਅਬੈ। ੧੧੧।","roman":"Dis badisan ke jeea dekhi sabai | bahu paap karam rati hai su abai | 111 |","meaning_en":"See all the beings of every direction and quarter: now they are deeply devoted to sinful deeds.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[112],"number_text":"੧੧੨।","page":736,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਿਤਮਾਨ ਨ ਨਰ ਕਹੂੰ ਦੇਖ ਪਰੈ। ਕਛੁ ਬੁਧਿ ਬਲ ਬਚਨ ਬਿਚਾਰ ਕਰੈ।","roman":"Pritmaan na nar kahoon dekh parai | kachhu budhi bal bachan bichaar karai |","meaning_en":"Nowhere is a man of standing seen who reflects with some intellect, strength or word.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪ੍ਰਿਤਮਾਨ: read as 'worthy, of measure'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਰ ਨਾਰਿਨ ਏਕ ਨ ਨੇਕ ਮਤੰ। ਨਿਤ ਅਰਥਾਨਰਥ ਗਨਿਤ ਗਤੰ। ੧੧੨।","roman":"Nar naarin ek na nek matan | nit arthaanrath ganit gatan | 112 |","meaning_en":"Among men and women, not one has a good mind; daily they go reckoning what profits and what harms.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Second half uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮਾਰਹ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰਹ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Maarah chhand","meaning_en":"Marah metre.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[113],"number_text":"੧੧੩।","page":736,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਿਤ ਸੰਗ ਕੁਨਾਰਿਨ ਅਤਿ ਬਿਭਚਾਰਿਨ ਜਿਨ ਕੇ ਐਸ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਰ।","roman":"Hit sang kunaarin ati bibhchaarin jin ke ais prakaar |","meaning_en":"They love the company of bad women, greatly debauched, of such a kind.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਡ ਕੁਲਿ ਜਦਪਿ ਉਪਜੀ ਬਹੁ ਛਬਿ ਬਿਗਸੀ ਤਦਿਪ ਪ੍ਰਿਅ ਬਿਭਚਾਰਿ।","roman":"Bad kuli jadpi upjee bahu chhabi bigsee tadip pria bibhchaari |","meaning_en":"Though born in great families and blossoming with great beauty, yet they love debauchery.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਿਤ੍ਰਤ ਬਹੁ ਚਿਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੁਸਮ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰਨ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਰੂਪ ਅਪਾਰ।","roman":"Chitrat bahu chitran kusam bachitran sundar roop apaar |","meaning_en":"Painted with many designs, wonderful with flowers, of boundless lovely form;","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਧੋ ਦੇਵ ਲੋਕ ਤਜਿ ਸੁਢਰ ਸੁੰਦਰੀ ਉਪਜੀ ਬਿਬਿਧ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਰ। ੧੧੩।","roman":"Kidho dev lok taji sudhar sundree upjee bibidh prakaar | 113 |","meaning_en":"as if shapely beauties of many kinds had left the world of the gods and been born here.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[114],"number_text":"੧੧੪।","page":736,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਿਤ ਅਤਿ ਦੁਰ ਮਾਨਸ ਕਛੂ ਨ ਜਾਨਸ ਨਰ ਹਰ ਅਰੁ ਬਟ ਪਾਰ।","roman":"Hit ati dur maanas kachhoo na jaanas nar har aru bat paar |","meaning_en":"They love very wicked men who know nothing, man-killers and highway robbers.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਰ ਹਰ ਅਰੁ ਬਟ ਪਾਰ: 'killers of men and waylayers'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਛੁ ਸਾਸਤ੍ਰ ਨ ਮਾਨਤ ਸਿਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਨ ਜਾਨਤ ਬੋਲਤ ਕੁਬਿਧਿ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਰ।","roman":"Kachhu saasatr na maanat simrit na jaanat bolat kubidhi prakaar |","meaning_en":"They heed no Shastra, know no Smriti, and speak in evil ways.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁਸਟਿਤ ਤੇ ਅੰਗਨ ਗਲਿਤ ਕੁਰੰਗਨ ਅਲਪ ਅਜੋਗਿ ਅਛਜਿ।","roman":"Kustit te angan galit kurangan alap ajogi achhji |","meaning_en":"With leprous limbs, rotting, ugly, petty, unfit, without shame,","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁਰੰਗਨ: read as 'of bad colour'; ਅਛਜਿ: printed so, read as 'shameless/unworthy'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਧੋ ਨਰਕ ਛੋਰਿ ਅਵਤਰੇ ਮਹਾ ਪਸੁ ਡੋਲਤ ਪ੍ਰਿਥੀ ਨਿਲਜ। ੧੧੪।","roman":"Kidho narak chhori avatre mahaa pasu dolat prithee nilaj | 114 |","meaning_en":"as if great beasts had left hell and been incarnated, they roam the earth shamelessly.","page":736,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[115],"number_text":"੧੧੫।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕਰ ਬਰਨ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਭਈ ਇਕ ਬ੍ਰਨ ਰਹਾ ਨ ਕੋਇ।","roman":"Sankar baran prajaa bhaee ik bran rahaa na koi |","meaning_en":"The people became of mixed castes; not one caste remained.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਲ ਸੂਦ੍ਰਤਾ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤਿ ਭੇ ਦਈਵ ਕਰੈ ਸੋ ਹੋਇ। ੧੧੫।","roman":"Sakal soodrataa praapti bhe daeev karai so hoi | 115 |","meaning_en":"All attained the state of Shudras; what Providence does, that comes to pass.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[116],"number_text":"੧੧੬।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕਰ ਬ੍ਰਨ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਭਈ ਧਰਮ ਨ ਕਤਹੂੰ ਰਹਾਨ।","roman":"Sankar bran prajaa bhaee dharam na kathoon rahaan |","meaning_en":"The people became of mixed castes; dharma remained nowhere.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰ ਰਾਜਾ ਭਏ ਭਈ ਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਹਾਨਿ। ੧੧੬।","roman":"Paap prachur raajaa bhae bhaee dharam kee haani | 116 |","meaning_en":"Kings became abundant in sin; there was the ruin of dharma.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[117],"number_text":"੧੧੭।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਨ ਕਤਹੂੰ ਰਹਾਨ ਪਾਪ ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰ ਜਗ ਮੋ ਧਰਾ।","roman":"Dharam na kathoon rahaan paap prachur jag mo dharaa |","meaning_en":"Dharma remained nowhere; sin spread abundantly in the world and on earth.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਸਬਨ ਬਿਸਰਾਨ ਪਾਪ ਕੰਠ ਸਬ ਜਗ ਕੀਓ। ੧੧੭।","roman":"Dharam saban bisraan paap kanth sab jag keeo | 117 |","meaning_en":"All forgot dharma; the whole world got sin by heart.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[118],"number_text":"੧੧੮।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲਿਜੁਗ ਚੜ੍ਯੋ ਅਸੰਭ ਜਗਤ ਕਵਨ ਬਿਧਿ ਬਾਚ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kalijug charyo asanbh jagat kavan bidhi baach hai |","meaning_en":"The Kali age has risen beyond measure; by what means will the world be saved?","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਸੰਭ: read as 'immensely / unbearably'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੰਗਹੁ ਏਕਹਿ ਰੰਗਿ ਤਬ ਛੁਟਿ ਹੋ ਕਲਿ ਕਾਲ ਤੇ। ੧੧੮।","roman":"Ranghu ekhi rangi tab chhuti ho kali kaal te | 118 |","meaning_en":"Dye yourself in the colour of the One alone; then you will be freed from the age of Kali.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਹੰਸਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਹੰਸਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Hansaa chhand","meaning_en":"Hansa metre.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[119],"number_text":"੧੧੯।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਬਢਾ ਪਾਪ ਕਾ ਕਰਮ। ਜਗ ਤੇ ਘਟਾ ਧਰਮ ਕਾ ਭਰਮ। ੧੧੯।","roman":"Jah tah badhaa paap kaa karam | jag te ghataa dharam kaa bharam | 119 |","meaning_en":"Everywhere the work of sin increased; the honour of dharma decreased in the world.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[120],"number_text":"੧੨੦।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਜਗਿ ਭਇਓ। ਪੰਖਨ ਧਾਰ ਧਰਮ ਉਡਿ ਗਇਓ। ੧੨੦।","roman":"Paap prachur jah tah jagi bhaio | pankhan dhaar dharam udi gaio | 120 |","meaning_en":"Sin became abundant everywhere in the world; dharma put on wings and flew away.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[121],"number_text":"੧੨੧।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਈ ਨਈ ਹੋਨ ਲਗੀ ਨਿਤ ਬਾਤ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਬਾਢਿ ਚਲਿਓ ਉਤਪਾਤ। ੧੨੧।","roman":"Naee naee hon lagee nit baat | jah tah baadhi chalio utpaat | 121 |","meaning_en":"New and newer things began to happen daily; everywhere disorder went on increasing.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[122],"number_text":"੧੨੨।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਜਗਿ ਚਲਤ ਔਰ ਹੀ ਕਰਮ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਘਟ ਗਇਓ ਧਰਾ ਤੇ ਧਰਮ। ੧੨੨।","roman":"Sab jagi chalat aur hee karam | jah tah ghat gaio dharaa te dharam | 122 |","meaning_en":"In all the world quite different deeds go on; everywhere dharma has diminished from the earth.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮਾਲਤੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮਾਲਤੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Maaltee chhand","meaning_en":"Malti metre.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[123],"number_text":"੧੨੩।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਦੇਖੀਅਤ। ਤਹ ਤਹ ਪੇਖੀਅਤ।","roman":"Jah tah dekheeat | tah tah pekheeat |","meaning_en":"Wherever one looks, there one sees","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਲ ਕੁਕਰਮੀ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਧਰਮੀ। ੧੨੩।","roman":"Sakal kukarmee | kahoon na dharmee | 123 |","meaning_en":"all doing evil deeds; nowhere anyone righteous.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[124],"number_text":"੧੨੪।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਗੁਨੀਅਤ। ਤਹ ਤਹ ਸੁਨੀਅਤ।","roman":"Jah tah guneeat | tah tah suneeat |","meaning_en":"Wherever one reflects, there one hears","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਜਗ ਪਾਪੀ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਜਾਪੀ। ੧੨੪।","roman":"Sab jag paapee | kahoon na jaapee | 124 |","meaning_en":"the whole world sinful; nowhere anyone who remembers God.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[125],"number_text":"੧੨੫।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਲ ਕੁਕਰਮੰ। ਭਜਿ ਗਇਓ ਧਰਮੰ।","roman":"Sakal kukarman | bhaji gaio dharman |","meaning_en":"All are evil deeds; dharma has fled.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਨ ਸੁਨੀਅਤ। ਹੋਮ ਨ ਗੁਨੀਅਤ। ੧੨੫।","roman":"Jag na suneeat | hom na guneeat | 125 |","meaning_en":"No sacrifice is heard of; no fire-offering is thought of.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[126],"number_text":"੧੨੬।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਕਲ ਕੁਕਰਮੀ। ਜਗੁ ਭਇਓ ਅਧਰਮੀ।","roman":"Sakal kukarmee | jagu bhaio adharmee |","meaning_en":"All do evil deeds; the world has become unrighteous.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਪੂਜਾ। ਬਸ ਰਹ੍ਯੋ ਦੂਜਾ। ੧੨੬।","roman":"Kahoon na poojaa | bas rahyo doojaa | 126 |","meaning_en":"Nowhere is there worship; duality has come to dwell.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅਤਿ ਮਾਲਤੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਮਾਲਤੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Ati maaltee chhand","meaning_en":"Ati Malti metre.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[127],"number_text":"੧੨੭।","page":737,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਪੂਜਾ ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਅਰਚਾ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਸ੍ਰੁਤਿ ਧੁਨਿ ਸਿੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਨ ਚਰਚਾ।","roman":"Kahoon na poojaa kahoon na archaa | kahoon na sruti dhuni sinmrit na charchaa |","meaning_en":"Nowhere worship, nowhere offering; nowhere the sound of the Shrutis, nor discourse on the Smritis.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਹੋਮੰ ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਦਾਨੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਸੰਜਮ ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਇਸਨਾਨੰ। ੧੨੭।","roman":"Kahoon na homan kahoon na daanan | kahoon na sanjam kahoon na isnaanan | 127 |","meaning_en":"Nowhere fire-offering, nowhere charity; nowhere self-discipline, nowhere bathing.","page":737,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[128],"number_text":"੧੨੮।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਚਰਚਾ ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਬੇਦੰ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨਿਵਾਜ ਨ ਕਹੂੰ ਕਤੇਬੰ।","roman":"Kahoon na charchaa kahoon na bedan | kahoon nivaaj na kahoon kateban |","meaning_en":"Nowhere discourse, nowhere the Vedas; nowhere namaz, nowhere the Katebs.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਤਸਬੀ ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਮਾਲਾ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਹੋਮੰ ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਜ੍ਵਾਲਾ। ੧੨੮।","roman":"Kahoon na tasbee kahoon na maalaa | kahoon na homan kahoon na jvaalaa | 128 |","meaning_en":"Nowhere the tasbih, nowhere the rosary; nowhere fire-offering, nowhere sacred flame.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਸਬੀ: Muslim prayer beads."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[129],"number_text":"੧੨੯।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਕਰਮੰ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਧਰਮੰ। ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਭਾਵੰ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਮਰਮੰ।","roman":"Aur hee karman aur hee dharman | aur hee bhaavan aur hee marman |","meaning_en":"Quite other deeds, quite other religion; quite other feelings, quite other secrets;","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਰੀਤਾ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਚਰਚਾ। ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਰੀਤੰ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਅਰਚਾ। ੧੨੯।","roman":"Aur hee reetaa aur hee charchaa | aur hee reetan aur hee archaa | 129 |","meaning_en":"quite other customs, quite other discourse; quite other ways, quite other worship.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[130],"number_text":"੧੩੦।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਭਾਤੰ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਬਸਤ੍ਰੰ। ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਬਾਣੀ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਅਸਤ੍ਰੰ।","roman":"Aur hee bhaatan aur hee bastran | aur hee baanee aur hee astran |","meaning_en":"Quite other manners, quite other clothes; quite other speech, quite other weapons;","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਰੀਤਾ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਭਾਯੰ। ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਰਾਜਾ ਅਉਰ ਹੀ ਨ੍ਯਾਯੰ। ੧੩੦।","roman":"Aur hee reetaa aur hee bhaayan | aur hee raajaa aur hee nyaayan | 130 |","meaning_en":"quite other customs, quite other affections; quite other kings, quite other justice.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅਭੀਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਅਭੀਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Abheer chhand","meaning_en":"Abhir metre.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[131],"number_text":"੧੩੧।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਸਾਧੂ ਅਤਿ ਰਾਜਾ। ਕਰਨ ਲਗੇ ਦੁਰ ਕਾਜਾ।","roman":"Ati saadhoo ati raajaa | karan lage dur kaajaa |","meaning_en":"Even great holy men and great kings began doing evil deeds.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਹਿਰਦੇ ਮਹਿ ਠਾਨਿ। ਕਰਤ ਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਹਾਨਿ। ੧੩੧।","roman":"Paap hirde mahi thaani | karat dharam kee haani | 131 |","meaning_en":"Setting sin in their hearts, they cause the ruin of dharma.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[132],"number_text":"੧੩੨।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਕੁਚਾਲ ਅਰੁ ਕ੍ਰੂਰ। ਅਤਿ ਪਾਪਿਸਟ ਕਠੂਰ।","roman":"Ati kuchaal aru kroor | ati paapisat kathoor |","meaning_en":"Of very bad conduct and cruel, very sinful and hard,","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਥਿਰ ਨਹੀ ਰਹਤ ਪਲਾਧ। ਕਰਤ ਅਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਸਾਧਿ। ੧੩੨।","roman":"Thir nahee rahat palaadh | karat adhram kee saadhi | 132 |","meaning_en":"they do not stay steady for half a moment; they practise unrighteousness.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਲਾਧ: read as 'half a moment'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[133],"number_text":"੧੩੩।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਪਾਪਿਸਟ ਅਜਾਨ। ਕਰਤ ਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਹਾਨਿ।","roman":"Ati paapisat ajaan | karat dharam kee haani |","meaning_en":"Very sinful and ignorant, they cause the ruin of dharma.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਤ ਜੰਤ੍ਰ ਨ ਤੰਤ੍ਰ। ਜਾਪਤ ਕੋਈ ਨ ਮੰਤ੍ਰ। ੧੩੩।","roman":"Maanat jantr na tantr | jaapat koee na mantr | 133 |","meaning_en":"They heed neither yantra nor tantra; no one repeats any mantra.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[134],"number_text":"੧੩੪।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਬਡਾ ਅਧਰਮ। ਧਰਮ ਭਜਾ ਕਰਿ ਭਰਮ।","roman":"Jah tah badaa adhram | dharam bhajaa kari bharam |","meaning_en":"Everywhere unrighteousness has grown; dharma has fled in confusion.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਵ ਨਵ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਭਈ। ਦੁਰਮਤਿ ਛਾਇ ਰਹੀ। ੧੩੪।","roman":"Nav nav kriaa bhaee | duramti chhaai rahee | 134 |","meaning_en":"New and newer practices have arisen; evil thinking has spread over all.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕੁੰਡਰੀਆ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਡਰੀਆ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Kundreeaa chhand","meaning_en":"Kundaria metre.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[135],"number_text":"੧੩੫।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਏ ਨਏ ਮਾਰਗ ਚਲੇ ਜਗ ਮੋ ਬਢਾ ਅਧਰਮ।","roman":"Nae nae maarag chale jag mo badhaa adhram |","meaning_en":"New and newer paths began in the world; unrighteousness grew.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਜਾ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਸਭੈ ਲਗੇ ਜਹ ਜਹ ਕਰਨ ਕੁਕਰਮ।","roman":"Raajaa prajaa sabhai lage jah jah karan kukram |","meaning_en":"King and subjects alike, wherever they were, began doing evil deeds.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਕਰਨ ਕੁਕਰਮ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਰਾਜਾ ਨਰ ਨਾਰੀ।","roman":"Jah tah karan kukram prajaa raajaa nar naaree |","meaning_en":"Everywhere subjects and kings, men and women, began doing evil deeds.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਪੰਖ ਕਰ ਉਡਾ ਪਾਪ ਕੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਬਿਥਾਰੀ। ੧੩੫।","roman":"Dharam pankh kar udaa paap kee kriaa bithaaree | 135 |","meaning_en":"Dharma took wings and flew away; the practice of sin spread out.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[136],"number_text":"੧੩੬।","page":738,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਲੋਪ ਜਗ ਤੇ ਭਏ ਪਾਪ ਪ੍ਰਗਟ ਬਪੁ ਕੀਨ।","roman":"Dharam lop jag te bhae paap pragat bapu keen |","meaning_en":"Dharma vanished from the world; sin took on a manifest body.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਊਚ ਨੀਚ ਰਾਜਾ ਪ੍ਰਜਾ ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਅਧਰਮ ਕੀ ਲੀਨ।","roman":"Ooch neech raajaa prajaa kriaa adhram kee leen |","meaning_en":"High and low, king and subject took up the practice of unrighteousness.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਆ ਪਾਪ ਕੀ ਲੀਨ ਨਾਰਿ ਨਰ ਰੰਕ ਅਰੁ ਰਾਜਾ।","roman":"Kriaa paap kee leen naari nar rank aru raajaa |","meaning_en":"Women and men, pauper and king took up the practice of sin.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰ ਬਪੁ ਕੀਨ ਧਰਮ ਧਰਿ ਪੰਖਨ ਭਾਜਾ। ੧੩੬।","roman":"Paap prachur bapu keen dharam dhari pankhan bhaajaa | 136 |","meaning_en":"Sin took on an abundant body; dharma put on wings and fled.","page":738,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[137],"number_text":"੧੩੭।","page":739,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪਾਕ੍ਰਾਂਤ ਧਰਾ ਭਈ ਪਲ ਨ ਸਕਤਿ ਠਹਰਾਇ।","roman":"Paapaakraant dharaa bhaee pal na sakti thahraai |","meaning_en":"The earth was overwhelmed by sin; it could not stay steady for a moment.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਪੁਰਖ ਕੋ ਧਿਆਨ ਧਰਿ ਰੋਵਤ ਭਈ ਬਨਾਇ।","roman":"Kaal purakh ko dhiaan dhari rovat bhaee banaai |","meaning_en":"Meditating on the Timeless Being (Kal Purakh), she began to weep greatly.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੋਵਤ ਭਈ ਬਨਾਇ ਪਾਪ ਭਾਰਨ ਭਰਿ ਧਰਣੀ।","roman":"Rovat bhaee banaai paap bhaaran bhari dharnee |","meaning_en":"The earth, laden with the weight of sin, began to weep greatly","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਪੁਰੁਖ ਕੇ ਤੀਰ ਬਹੁਤੁ ਬਿਧਿ ਜਾਤ ਨ ਬਰਣੀ। ੧੩੭।","roman":"Mahaa purukh ke teer bahutu bidhi jaat na barnee | 137 |","meaning_en":"before the Great Being, in so many ways it cannot be described.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[138],"number_text":"੧੩੮।","page":739,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰ ਕੈ ਪ੍ਰਿਥਮ ਸਮੋਧ ਬਹੁਰ ਬਿਦਾ ਪ੍ਰਿਥਵੀ ਕਰੀ।","roman":"Kar kai pritham samodh bahur bidaa prithvee karee |","meaning_en":"First consoling her, He then sent the Earth away;","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਪੁਰੁਖ ਬਿਨੁ ਰੋਗ ਭਾਰ ਹਰਣ ਬਸੁਧਾ ਨਿਮਿਤ। ੧੩੮।","roman":"Mahaa purukh binu rog bhaar haran basudhaa nimit | 138 |","meaning_en":"the Great Being, free of ailment, for the sake of removing the earth's burden.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line is elliptical; read as 'the Great Being (resolved to come) to remove the earth's burden'."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕੁੰਡਰੀਆ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਡਰੀਆ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Kundreeaa chhand","meaning_en":"Kundaria metre.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[139],"number_text":"੧੩੯।","page":739,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੀਨਨ ਕੀ ਰਛਾ ਨਿਮਿਤ ਕਰ ਹੈ ਆਪ ਉਪਾਇ।","roman":"Deenan kee rachhaa nimit kar hai aap upaai |","meaning_en":"For the protection of the humble, He Himself will devise the means.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰਮ ਪੁਰਖ ਪਾਵਨ ਸਦਾ ਆਪ ਪ੍ਰਗਟ ਹੈ ਆਇ।","roman":"Param purakh paavan sadaa aap pragat hai aai |","meaning_en":"The Supreme Being, ever pure, will Himself come and become manifest.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਪ ਪ੍ਰਗਟ ਹੈ ਆਇ ਦੀਨ ਰਛਾ ਕੇ ਕਾਰਣ।","roman":"Aap pragat hai aai deen rachhaa ke kaaran |","meaning_en":"He will Himself come and become manifest for the sake of protecting the humble;","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਵਤਾਰੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਧਰਾ ਕੇ ਪਾਪ ਉਤਾਰਣ। ੧੩੯।","roman":"Avtaaree avtaar dharaa ke paap utaaran | 139 |","meaning_en":"the Source of incarnations takes incarnation to remove the earth's sins.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[140],"number_text":"੧੪੦।","page":739,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲਿਜੁਗ ਕੇ ਅੰਤਹ ਸਮੈ ਸਤਿਜੁਗ ਲਾਗਤ ਆਦਿ।","roman":"Kalijug ke antah samai satijug laagat aadi |","meaning_en":"At the end of the Kali age, as the Satyuga begins,","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੀਨਨ ਕੀ ਰਛਾ ਲੀਏ ਧਰਿ ਹੈ ਰੂਪ ਅਨਾਦਿ।","roman":"Deenan kee rachhaa lee'e dhari hai roop anaadi |","meaning_en":"for the protection of the humble, the Beginningless One will take a form.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰ ਹੈ ਰੂਪ ਅਨਾਦਿ ਕਲਹਿ ਕਵਤੁਕ ਕਰਿ ਭਾਰੀ।","roman":"Dhar hai roop anaadi kalhi kavtuk kari bhaaree |","meaning_en":"The Beginningless One will take a form and make a great play of strife,","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲਹਿ ਕਵਤੁਕ: read as 'a play of battle'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤ੍ਰਨ ਕੇ ਨਾਸਾਰਥ ਨਮਿਤ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਅਵਤਾਰੀ। ੧੪੦।","roman":"Satran ke naasaarath namit avtaar avtaaree | 140 |","meaning_en":"the Source of incarnations incarnating for the destruction of enemies.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Savaiyaa chhand","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[141],"number_text":"੧੪੧।","page":739,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਸੰਬੂਹ ਬਿਨਾਸਨ ਕਉ ਕਲਿਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਕਹਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Paap sanbooh binaasan kau kalikee avtaar kahaavhige |","meaning_en":"To destroy the mass of sins, He will be called the Kalki incarnation.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਰਕਛਿ ਤੁਰੰਗ ਸਪਛ ਬਡੋ ਕਰਿ ਕਾਢਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕੰਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Turakchhi turang sapachh bado kari kaadhi kripaan kanpaavhige |","meaning_en":"Riding a great swift Turki horse, as if winged, drawing His sword He will make all tremble.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤੁਰਕਛਿ ... ਸਪਛ: read as 'a Turki horse, swift as if winged'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਕਸੇ ਜਿਮ ਕੇਹਰਿ ਪਰਬਤ ਤੇ ਤਸ ਸੋਭ ਦਿਵਾਲਯ ਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Nikse jim kehri parbat te tas sobh divaalay paavhige |","meaning_en":"As a lion comes out from the mountain, such splendour He will have, like a god's dwelling.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਿਵਾਲਯ: read as 'divine abode' or 'shining like a lamp'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੧।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 141 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sambhal: the town of Kalki's birth. ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ: read as Sambhal itself becoming the Lord's abode; refrain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[142],"number_text":"੧੪੨।","page":739,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਪ ਅਨੂਪ ਸਰੂਪ ਮਹਾ ਲਖਿ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਲਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Roop anoop saroop mahaa lakhi dev adev lajaavhige |","meaning_en":"Seeing His peerless and great form, gods and demons will be put to shame.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਮਾਰਿ ਸੁਧਾਰ ਕੇ ਟਾਰਿ ਘਣੇ ਬਹੁਰੋ ਕਲਿ ਧਰਮ ਚਲਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ari maari sudhaar ke taari ghane bahuro kali dharam chalaavhige |","meaning_en":"Killing the enemies, setting right and removing many, He will again set dharma going in the Kali age.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਸਾਧ ਉਬਾਰ ਲਹੈ ਕਰ ਦੈ ਦੁਖ ਆਂਚ ਨ ਲਾਗਨ ਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Sabh saadh ubaar lahai kar dai dukh aanch na laagan paavhige |","meaning_en":"Giving His hand, He will save all the holy, and will not let the heat of suffering touch them.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੨।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 142 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[143],"number_text":"੧੪੩।","page":739,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਾਨਵ ਮਾਰਿ ਅਪਾਰ ਬਡੇ ਰਣਿ ਜੀਤਿ ਨਿਸਾਨ ਬਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Daanav maari apaar bade rani jeeti nisaan bajaavhige |","meaning_en":"Killing countless great demons and winning in battle, He will beat the drums of victory.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਲ ਟਾਰਿ ਹਜਾਰ ਕਰੋਰ ਕਿਤੇ ਕਲਕੀ ਕਲਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਤਿ ਬਢਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Khal taari hajaar karor kite kalkee kali kriti badhaavhige |","meaning_en":"Removing thousands and crores of the wicked, Kalki will spread his glory in the Kali age.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਗਟਿ ਹੈ ਜਿਤਹੀ ਤਿਤ ਧਰਮ ਦਿਸਾ ਲਖਿ ਪਾਪਨ ਪੁੰਜ ਪਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Pragti hai jithee tit dharam disaa lakhi paapan punj paraavhige |","meaning_en":"Wherever He manifests, there the state of dharma will be; seeing it, the hosts of sins will flee.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੩।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 143 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":739,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[144],"number_text":"੧੪੪।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛੀਨ ਮਹਾ ਦਿਜ ਦੀਨ ਦਸਾ ਲਖਿ ਦੀਨ ਦਿਆਲ ਰਿਸਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Chheen mahaa dij deen dasaa lakhi deen diaal risaavhige |","meaning_en":"Seeing the Brahmins greatly weakened and in a wretched state, the Compassionate to the humble will grow angry.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਗ ਕਾਢਿ ਅਭੰਗ ਨਿਸੰਗ ਹਠੀ ਰਣ ਰੰਗਿ ਤੁਰੰਗ ਨਚਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Khag kaadhi abhang nisang hathee ran rangi turang nachaavhige |","meaning_en":"Drawing His sword, unbroken, fearless, steadfast, He will make His horse dance in the joy of battle.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਿਪੁ ਜੀਤਿ ਅਜੀਤ ਅਭੀਤ ਬਡੇ ਅਵਨੀ ਪੈ ਸਬੈ ਜਸੁ ਗਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ripu jeeti ajeet abheet bade avnee pai sabai jasu gaavhige |","meaning_en":"Conquering great enemies, unconquered and fearless, all on earth will sing His praise.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੪।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 144 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[145],"number_text":"੧੪੫।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੇਸ ਸੁਰੇਸ ਮਹੇਸ ਗਨੇਸ ਨਿਸੇਸ ਭਲੇ ਜਸੁ ਗਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ses sures mahes ganes nises bhale jasu gaavhige |","meaning_en":"Shesh, Indra, Shiva, Ganesh, and the Moon will sing His praise well.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਸੇਸ: lord of night, the Moon."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਭੂਤ ਪਰੇਤ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਪਰੀ ਜਯ ਸਦ ਨਿਨਦ ਸੁਨਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gan bhoot paret pisaach paree jay sad ninad sunaavhige |","meaning_en":"Ganas, ghosts, spirits, goblins, and fairies will make the sound of 'victory' heard.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਰ ਨਾਰਦ ਤੁੰਬਰ ਕਿੰਨਰ ਜਛ ਸੁ ਬੀਨ ਪ੍ਰਬੀਨ ਬਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Nar naarad tunbar kinnar jachh su been prabeen bajaavhige |","meaning_en":"Nar, Narad, Tumbar, Kinnars and Yakshas, skilled players, will play the vina.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੫।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 145 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[146],"number_text":"੧੪੬।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਲ ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ ਮੁਚੰਗ ਉਪੰਗ ਸੁਰੰਗ ਸੇ ਨਾਦ ਸੁਨਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Taal mridang muchang upang surang se naad sunaavhige |","meaning_en":"Cymbals, mridangs, muchangs and upangs will sound beautiful notes.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Names of musical instruments."},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਫ ਬਾਰ ਤਰੰਗ ਰਬਾਬ ਤੁਰੀ ਰਣਿ ਸੰਖ ਅਸੰਖ ਬਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Daph baar tarang rabaab turee rani sankh asankh bajaavhige |","meaning_en":"Tambourines, jal-tarang, rababs, trumpets, and countless conches will sound in battle.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਰ ਤਰੰਗ: read as 'jal-tarang' (water-bowls); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਦੁੰਦਭਿ ਢੋਲਨ ਘੋਰ ਘਨੀ ਸੁਨਿ ਸਤ੍ਰੁ ਸਬੈ ਮੁਰਛਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gan dundbhi dholan ghor ghanee suni satru sabai murchhaavhige |","meaning_en":"Hearing the loud roar of the hosts of kettle-drums and drums, all the enemies will faint.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੬।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 146 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[147],"number_text":"੧੪੭।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੀਰ ਤੁਫੰਗ ਕਮਾਨ ਸੁਰੰਗ ਦੁਰੰਗ ਨਿਖੰਗ ਸੁਹਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Teer tuphang kamaan surang durang nikhang suhaavhige |","meaning_en":"Arrows, muskets, fine bows and quivers of two colours will look splendid.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਰੰਗ ਦੁਰੰਗ: 'well-coloured, two-coloured'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰਛੀ ਅਰੁ ਬੈਰਖ ਬਾਨ ਧੁਜਾ ਪਟ ਬਾਤ ਲਗੇ ਫਹਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Barchhee aru bairakh baan dhujaa pat baat lage phahraavhige |","meaning_en":"Lances, banners, arrows and flags will flutter in the wind.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗੁਣ ਜੱਛ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਸੁ ਕਿੰਨਰ ਸਿਧੱ ਪ੍ਰਸਿਧ ਸਬੈ ਜਸੁ ਗਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gun jacchh bhujang su kinnar sidh prasidh sabai jasu gaavhige |","meaning_en":"Ganas, Yakshas, serpents, Kinnars, and famous Siddhas will all sing His praise.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗੁਣ: printed so; read as 'gan' (attendant spirits)."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੭।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 147 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[148],"number_text":"੧੪੮।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਉਚ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕਟਾਰਿ ਕਮਾਨ ਸੁਰੰਗ ਨਿਖੰਗ ਛਕਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Kauch kripaan kataari kamaan surang nikhang chhakaavhige |","meaning_en":"Armour, sword, dagger, bow and fine quiver will adorn Him.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਕਾਵਹਿਗੇ: read as 'will adorn / be worn'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰਛੀ ਅਰੁ ਢਾਲ ਗਦਾ ਪਰਸੋ ਕਰਿ ਸੂਲ ਤ੍ਰਿਸੂਲ ਭ੍ਰਮਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Barchhee aru dhaal gadaa parso kari sool trisool bhramaavhige |","meaning_en":"Lance and shield, mace, axe, spear and trident He will whirl in His hand.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਕ੍ਰੁਧਤ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਰਣ ਮੂਰਧਨ ਮੋ ਸਰ ਓਘ ਪ੍ਰਓਘ ਚਲਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ati krudhat hvai ran moordhan mo sar ogh praogh chalaavhige |","meaning_en":"Greatly enraged, at the head of the battle He will loose flood upon flood of arrows.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੮।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 148 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[149],"number_text":"੧੪੯।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇਜ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਅਖੰਡ ਮਹਾ ਛਬਿ ਦੁਜਨ ਦੇਖਿ ਪਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Tej prachand akhand mahaa chhabi dujan dekhi paraavhige |","meaning_en":"Seeing His fierce, unbroken splendour and great beauty, the wicked will flee,","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਮ ਪਉਨ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਬਹੈ ਪਤੂਆ ਸਬ ਆਪਨ ਹੀ ਉਡਿ ਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Jim paun prachand bahai patooaa sab aapan hee udi jaavhige |","meaning_en":"as when a fierce wind blows, the leaves all fly away of themselves.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਢਿ ਹੈ ਜਿਤ ਹੀ ਤਿਤ ਧਰਮ ਦਸਾ ਕਹੂੰ ਪਾਪ ਨ ਢੂੰਢਤ ਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Badhi hai jit hee tit dharam dasaa kahoon paap na dhoondhat paavhige |","meaning_en":"Wherever He advances, there the state of dharma will be; searching, they will find sin nowhere.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੪੯।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 149 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[150],"number_text":"੧੫੦।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛੂਟਤ ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨਿਨ ਕੇ ਰਣ ਛਾਡਿ ਭਟਵਾ ਭਹਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Chhootat baan kamaanin ke ran chhaadi bhatvaa bhahraavhige |","meaning_en":"As arrows fly from the bows, the warriors will leave the battlefield, trembling.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਟਵਾ ਭਹਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ: read as 'warriors will panic / tremble'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਬੀਰ ਬਿਤਾਲ ਕਰਾਲ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਰਣ ਮੂਰਧਨ ਮਧਿ ਸੁਹਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gan beer bitaal karaal prabhaa ran moordhan madhi suhaavhige |","meaning_en":"Ganas, heroic spirits, and Vetals of dreadful splendour will look splendid at the head of the battle.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਸਿਧੱ ਪ੍ਰਸਿੱਧ ਸਮ੍ਰਿੱਧ ਸਨੈ ਕਰ ਉਚਾਇ ਕੈ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਸੁਨਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gan sidh prasiddh samriddh sanai kar uchaai kai krit sunaavhige |","meaning_en":"Hosts of famous and accomplished Siddhas will raise their hands and proclaim His deeds.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਨੈ: uncertain; read as 'all together'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੫੦।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 150 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[151],"number_text":"੧੫੧।","page":740,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਪ ਅਨੂਪ ਸਰੂਪ ਮਹਾ ਅੰਗ ਦੇਖਿ ਅਨੰਗ ਲਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Roop anoop saroop mahaa ang dekhi anang lajaavhige |","meaning_en":"Seeing His peerless form and great limbs, Kama (the bodiless god of love) will be put to shame.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਵ ਭੂਤ ਭਵਿਖ ਭਵਾਨ ਸਦਾ ਸਬ ਠਉਰ ਸਭੈ ਠਹਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Bhav bhoot bhavikh bhavaan sadaa sab thaur sabhai thahraavhige |","meaning_en":"The world, past, future and present, He will forever establish in every place.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਵ ਭੂਤ ਭਵਿਖ ਭਵਾਨ: read as 'present, past, future'; line uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਵ ਭਾਰ ਅਪਾਰ ਨਿਵਾਰਨ ਕੌ ਕਲਿਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਕਹਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Bhav bhaar apaar nivaaran kau kalikee avtaar kahaavhige |","meaning_en":"To remove the boundless burden of the world, He will be called the Kalki incarnation.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੫੧।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 151 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":740,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[152],"number_text":"੧੫੨।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਮ ਕੋ ਭਾਰ ਉਤਾਰ ਬਡੇ ਬਡਆਛ ਬਡੀ ਛਬਿ ਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Bhoom ko bhaar utaar bade bada'aachh badee chhabi paavhige |","meaning_en":"Removing the great burden of the earth, the large-eyed One will gain great glory.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਡਆਛ: 'large-eyed'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਲ ਟਾਰਿ ਜੁਝਾਰ ਬਰਿਆਰ ਹਠੀ ਘਨ ਘੋਖਨ ਜਿਉ ਘਹਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Khal taari jujhaar bariaar hathee ghan ghokhan jiu ghahraavhige |","meaning_en":"Removing the wicked, the mighty, steadfast warrior will thunder like the roar of clouds.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲ ਨਾਰਦ ਭੂਤ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਪਰੀ ਜੈਪਤ੍ਰ ਧਰਤ੍ਰ ਸੁਨਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Kal naarad bhoot pisaach paree jaipatr dharatr sunaavhige |","meaning_en":"Narad, ghosts, goblins and fairies will proclaim His letter of victory over the earth.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲ: printed so; read as 'sweetly' or as Narad's epithet; ਜੈਪਤ੍ਰ ਧਰਤ੍ਰ: 'victory-letter on the earth'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੫੨।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 152 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[153],"number_text":"੧੫੩।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਝਾਰਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਜੁਝਾਰ ਬਡੇ ਰਣ ਮਧ ਮਹਾ ਛਬਿ ਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Jhaari kripaan jujhaar bade ran madh mahaa chhabi paavhige |","meaning_en":"Swinging His sword, the great warrior will gain great glory amid the battle.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਿ ਲੁਥ ਪਲੁਥ ਬਿਥਾਰ ਘਣੀ ਘਨ ਕੀ ਘਟ ਜਿਉ ਘਹਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Dhari luth paluth bithaar ghanee ghan kee ghat jiu ghahraavhige |","meaning_en":"Strewing heaps upon heaps of corpses, He will thunder like a mass of clouds.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਚਰਾਚਰ ਜੇ ਜਯ ਸਦ ਨਿਨਦ ਸੁਨਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Chaturaanan rudr charaachar je jay sad ninad sunaavhige |","meaning_en":"Brahma the four-faced, Rudra, and all moving and unmoving beings will make the sound of 'victory' heard.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੫੩।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 153 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[154],"number_text":"੧੫੪।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਰ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਨ ਉਚਾਨ ਧੁਜਾ ਲਖਿ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਤ੍ਰਸਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Taar pramaan uchaan dhujaa lakhi dev adev trasaavhige |","meaning_en":"Seeing His banner, tall as a palm tree, gods and demons will be terrified.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਰ: read as 'taad', palm tree; compare 3.220.1."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲਗੀ ਗਜਗਾਹ ਗਦਾ ਬਰਛੀ ਗਹਿ ਪਾਣਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਭ੍ਰਮਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Kalgee gajgaah gadaa barchhee gahi paani kripaan bhramaavhige |","meaning_en":"With plume and elephant-trappings, holding mace and lance, He will whirl the sword in His hand.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਜਗਾਹ: an ornament (of horse/elephant); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਪਾਪ ਸੰਬੂਹ ਬਿਨਾਸਨ ਕਉ ਕਲਕੀ ਕਲਿ ਧਰਮ ਚਲਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Jag paap sanbooh binaasan kau kalkee kali dharam chalaavhige |","meaning_en":"To destroy the mass of the world's sins, Kalki will set dharma going in the Kali age.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੫੪।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 154 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[155],"number_text":"੧੫੫।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਨਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਅਜਾਨੁ ਭੁਜਾ ਰਣਿ ਰੂਪ ਮਹਾਨ ਦਿਖਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Paani kripaan ajaanu bhujaa rani roop mahaan dikhaavhige |","meaning_en":"Sword in hand, arms reaching the knees, He will show His great form in battle.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਤਿਮਾਨ ਸੁਜਾਨ ਅਪ੍ਰਮਾਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਲਖਿ ਬਿਓਮ ਬਿਵਾਨ ਲਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Pratimaan sujaan apramaan prabhaa lakhi biom bivaan lajaavhige |","meaning_en":"Seeing the matchless, wise One of measureless splendour, the sky-chariots will be ashamed.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣਿ ਭੂਤ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਪਰੇਤ ਪਰੀ ਮਿਲਿ ਜੀਤ ਕੇ ਗੀਤ ਗਵਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gani bhoot pisaach paret paree mili jeet ke geet gavaavhige |","meaning_en":"Ganas, ghosts, goblins, spirits and fairies together will sing songs of victory.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੫੫।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 155 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[156],"number_text":"੧੫੬।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜਤ ਡੰਕ ਅਤੰਕ ਸਮੈ ਰਣ ਰੰਗਿ ਤੁਰੰਗ ਨਚਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Baajat dank atank samai ran rangi turang nachaavhige |","meaning_en":"As the drums beat in the time of terror, He will make His horse dance in the joy of battle.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਸਿ ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਗਦਾ ਬਰਛੀ ਕਰਿ ਸੂਲ ਤ੍ਰਿਸੂਲ ਭ੍ਰਮਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Kasi baan kamaan gadaa barchhee kari sool trisool bhramaavhige |","meaning_en":"Drawing arrows on the bow, He will whirl mace, lance, spear and trident in His hand.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਪਰੀ ਰਣ ਦੇਖਿ ਸਬੈ ਰਹਸਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gan dev adev pisaach paree ran dekhi sabai rahsaavhige |","meaning_en":"Ganas, gods, demons, goblins and fairies, seeing the battle, will all rejoice.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਲੁ ਭਾਗ ਭਯਾ ਇਹ ਸੰਭਲ ਕੇ ਹਰਿ ਜੂ ਹਰਿ ਮੰਦਰਿ ਆਵਹਿਗੇ। ੧੫੬।","roman":"Bhalu bhaag bhayaa ih sanbhal ke hari joo hari mandri aavhige | 156 |","meaning_en":"Good fortune has come to this Sambhal: the Lord will come to the Lord's temple.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕੁਲਕ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਕੁਲਕ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Kulak chhand","meaning_en":"Kulak metre.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[157],"number_text":"੧੫੭।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਸਿਜ ਰੂਪੰ। ਸਬ ਭਟ ਭੂਪੰ।","roman":"Sarsij roopan | sab bhat bhoopan |","meaning_en":"Lotus-like in form, king of all warriors,","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਛਬਿ ਸੋਭੰ। ਮੁਨਿ ਗਨ ਲੋਭੰ। ੧੫੭।","roman":"Ati chhabi sobhan | muni gan lobhan | 157 |","meaning_en":"glorious with great beauty, the hosts of sages long for Him.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[158],"number_text":"੧੫੮।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰ ਅਰਿ ਧਰਮੰ। ਪਰਹਰਿ ਕਰਮੰ।","roman":"Kar ari dharman | parahri karman |","meaning_en":"The enemies of dharma, abandoning good deeds,","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰ ਅਰਿ ਧਰਮੰ: read as 'making dharma an enemy'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਵੀਰੰ। ਪਰਹਰਿ ਧੀਰੰ। ੧੫੮।","roman":"Ghari ghari veeran | parahri dheeran | 158 |","meaning_en":"in every house are 'heroes', abandoning steadiness.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[159],"number_text":"੧੫੯।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਲ ਥਲ ਪਾਪੰ। ਹਰ ਹਰਿ ਜਾਪੰ।","roman":"Jal thal paapan | har hari jaapan |","meaning_en":"Sin in water and on land; the remembrance of the Lord taken away.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਰ ਹਰਿ ਜਾਪੰ: read as 'remembrance of Hari removed (har)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਦੇਖਾ। ਤਹ ਤਹ ਪੇਖਾ। ੧੫੯।","roman":"Jah tah dekhaa | tah tah pekhaa | 159 |","meaning_en":"Wherever one looked, there it was seen.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[160],"number_text":"੧੬੦।","page":741,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਪੇਖੈ। ਦਰ ਦਰ ਲੇਖੈ।","roman":"Ghari ghari pekhai | dar dar lekhai |","meaning_en":"He sees in every house, takes account at every door:","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਅਰਚਾ। ਕਹੂੰ ਨ ਚਰਚਾ। ੧੬੦।","roman":"Kahoon na archaa | kahoon na charchaa | 160 |","meaning_en":"nowhere is there worship, nowhere sacred discourse.","page":741,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਮਧੁਭਾਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Madhubhaar chhand","meaning_en":"Madhubhar metre.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[161],"number_text":"੧੬੧।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਦੇਸ ਢਾਲ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਕੁਚਾਲ।","roman":"Sab des dhaal | jah tah kuchaal |","meaning_en":"In all lands, the same mould: everywhere bad conduct.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਢਾਲ: read as 'manner / mould'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹ ਤਹ ਅਨਰਥ। ਨਹੀ ਹੋਤ ਅਰਥ। ੧੬੧।","roman":"Jah tah anrath | nahee hot arath | 161 |","meaning_en":"Everywhere mischief; nothing worthwhile is done.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[162],"number_text":"੧੬੨।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬ ਦੇਸ ਰਾਜ। ਨਿਤਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਕੁਕਾਜ।","roman":"Sab des raaj | nitprati kukaaj |","meaning_en":"In the rule of every land, every day wrong deeds;","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਹੋਤ ਨਿਆਇ। ਜਹ ਤਹ ਅਨ੍ਯਾਇ। ੧੬੨।","roman":"Nahee hot niaai | jah tah anyaai | 162 |","meaning_en":"no justice is done; everywhere injustice.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[163],"number_text":"੧੬੩।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਿਤ ਭਈ ਸੁਦ੍ਰ। ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਕਰਤ ਛੁਦ੍ਰ।","roman":"Chhit bhaee sudr | krit karat chhudr |","meaning_en":"The earth has become Shudra; it does petty deeds.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਹ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਏਕ। ਜਿਹ ਗੁਨ ਅਨੇਕ। ੧੬੩।","roman":"Tah bipr ek | jih gun anek | 163 |","meaning_en":"There was a Brahmin there who had many virtues.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Paadhree chhand","meaning_en":"Padhri metre.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[164],"number_text":"੧੬੪।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਤ ਜਪਤ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਦੇਬੀ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ। ਜਿਹ ਕੀਨ ਧੂਮ੍ਰ ਲੋਚਨ ਦੁਖੰਡ।","roman":"Nit japat bipr debee prachand | jih keen dhoomr lochan dukhand |","meaning_en":"The Brahmin daily remembered the fierce Goddess, who cut Dhumar Lochan in two,","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਕੀਨ ਦੇਵ ਦੇਵਿਸ ਸਹਾਇ। ਜਿਹ ਲੀਨ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਕਰਿ ਬਚਾਇ। ੧੬੪।","roman":"Jih keen dev devis sahaai | jih leen rudr kari bachaai | 164 |","meaning_en":"who gave help to the gods and the lord of gods, who saved Rudra (Shiva).","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੇਵਿਸ: read as 'lord of gods (Indra)'; ਜਿਹ ਲੀਨ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ ਕਰਿ ਬਚਾਇ: read as 'who saved Shiva'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[165],"number_text":"੧੬੫।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਹ ਹਤੇ ਸੁੰਭ ਨੈਸੁੰਭ ਬੀਰ। ਜਿਨ ਜੀਤ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਕੀਨੋ ਫਕੀਰ।","roman":"Jih hate sunbh naisunbh beer | jin jeet indr keeno phakeer |","meaning_en":"She who slew the warriors Sumbh and Nisumbh, who had conquered Indra and made him a beggar;","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਨਿ ਗਹੀ ਸਰਨ ਜਗਮਾਤ ਜਾਇ। ਤਿਹਿ ਕੀਅਸ ਚੰਡਿਕਾ ਦੇਵਰਾਇ। ੧੬੫।","roman":"Tini gahee saran jagmaat jaai | tihi keeas chandikaa devraai | 165 |","meaning_en":"he (Indra) went and took refuge with the Mother of the world; she, Chandika, made him king of the gods.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[166],"number_text":"੧੬੬।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹਿ ਜਪਤ ਰੈਣ ਦਿਨ ਦਿਜ ਉਦਾਰ। ਜਿਹਿ ਹਣਿਓ ਰੋਸਿ ਰਣਿ ਬਾਸਵਾਰ।","roman":"Tihi japat rain din dij udaar | jihi hanio rosi rani baasvaar |","meaning_en":"Her the noble Brahmin remembered night and day, she who in wrath slew in battle Indra's enemies.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਸਵਾਰ: read as 'Vasav-ari', enemies of Indra; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਹੁਤੀ ਤਾਸੁ ਇਸਤ੍ਰੀ ਕੁਚਾਰ। ਤਿਹ ਗਹਿਓ ਨਾਹ ਦਿਨ ਇਕ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ। ੧੬੬।","roman":"Grih hutee taasu istree kuchaar | tih gahio naah din ik nihaari | 166 |","meaning_en":"In his house was a wife of bad conduct; one day, watching, she seized hold of her husband.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਹਿਓ ਨਾਹ: read as 'confronted her husband'."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਤ੍ਰੀਯੋ ਬਾਚ ਪਤਿ ਸੋ","gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰੀਯੋ ਬਾਚ ਪਤਿ ਸੋ","roman":"Treeyo baach pati so","meaning_en":"The wife said to her husband:","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[167],"number_text":"੧੬੭।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਹ ਕਾਜ ਮੂੜ ਸੇਵੰਤ ਦੇਵਿ। ਕਿਹ ਹੇਤ ਤਾਸੁ ਬੁਲਤ ਅਭੇਵਿ।","roman":"Kih kaaj moor sevant devi | kih het taasu bulat abhevi |","meaning_en":"\"Fool, why do you serve the Goddess? Why do you call on her, the mysterious?","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਕਾਰਣ ਵਾਹਿ ਪਗਿਆਨ ਪਰੰਤ। ਕਿਮ ਜਾਨ ਬੂਝ ਦੋਜਖਿ ਗਿਰੰਤ। ੧੬੭।","roman":"Ih kaaran vaahi pagiaan parant | kim jaan boojh dojkhi girant | 167 |","meaning_en":"For this reason you fall at her feet? Why, knowingly, do you fall into hell?","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਗਿਆਨ: printed so; read as 'pagan' (at the feet); uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[168],"number_text":"੧੬੮।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਹ ਕਾਜ ਮੂਰਖ ਤਿਹ ਜਪਤ ਜਾਪ। ਨਹੀ ਡਰਤ ਤਉਨ ਕੋ ਥਪਤ ਥਾਪ।","roman":"Kih kaaj moorakh tih japat jaap | nahee darat taun ko thapat thaap |","meaning_en":"Fool, why do you repeat her chant? You do not fear, and you set her up (for worship).","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਹੀ ਡਰਤ ਤਉਨ ਕੋ ਥਪਤ ਥਾਪ: read as 'you are not afraid to set up her worship'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈਹੋ ਪੁਕਾਰ ਰਾਜਾ ਸਮੀਪ। ਦੈ ਹੈ ਨਿਕਾਰ ਤੁਹਿ ਬਾਧਿ ਦੀਪ। ੧੬੮।","roman":"Kaiho pukaar raajaa sameep | dai hai nikaar tuhi baadhi deep | 168 |","meaning_en":"I will complain to the king; he will bind you and banish you from the land.\"","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੀਪ: read as 'dweep', the land/country; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[169],"number_text":"੧੬੯।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਲਖਾ ਤਾਹਿ ਬ੍ਰਹਮਾ ਕੁਨਾਰਿ। ਧਰਮਾਰਥ ਆਨਿ ਲਿਨੋ ਵਤਾਰ।","roman":"Nahee lakhaa taahi brahmaa kunaari | dharmaarath aani lino vataar |","meaning_en":"That bad woman did not see that Brahm had come and taken incarnation for the sake of dharma,","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬ੍ਰਹਮਾ: read as Brahm/the Lord (the incarnation), not the god Brahma; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੂਦ੍ਰੰ ਸਮਸਤ ਨਾਸਾਰਥ ਹੇਤੁ। ਕਲਕੀ ਵਤਾਰ ਕਰਬੇ ਸਚੇਤ। ੧੬੯।","roman":"Soodran samsat naasaarath hetu | kalkee vataar karbe sachet | 169 |","meaning_en":"and, to destroy all the Shudras, was alert to become the Kalki incarnation.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[170],"number_text":"੧੭੦।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਿਤ ਜਾਨਿ ਤਾਸੁ ਹਟਕਿਓ ਕੁਨਾਰਿ। ਨਹੀ ਲੋਕ ਤ੍ਰਾਸ ਬੁਲੇ ਭਤਾਰ।","roman":"Hit jaani taasu hatkio kunaari | nahee lok traas bule bhataar |","meaning_en":"Knowing it was for her own good, the husband restrained the bad woman; fearless of people, he spoke to her.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Line uncertain; may read 'the bad wife tried to stop him'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਕੁੜੀ ਨਾਰਿ ਚਿਤ ਰੋਸ ਠਾਨਿ। ਸੰਭਲ ਨਰੇਸ ਤਨ ਕਹੀ ਆਨਿ। ੧੭੦।","roman":"Tab kuree naari chit ros thaani | sanbhal nares tan kahee aani | 170 |","meaning_en":"Then the woman grew angry, setting wrath in her heart, and came and told the king of Sambhal.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੁੜੀ: printed so; read as 'angered (kurhi)'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[171],"number_text":"੧੭੧।","page":742,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੂਜੰਤ ਦੇਵ ਦੀਨੋ ਦਿਖਾਇ। ਤਿਹ ਗਹਾ ਕੋਪ ਕਰਿ ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਰਾਇ।","roman":"Poojant dev deeno dikhaai | tih gahaa kop kari soodr raai |","meaning_en":"She showed him worshipping the Goddess; the Shudra king seized him in anger.","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹਿ ਤਾਹਿ ਅਧਿਕ ਦੀਨੀ ਸਜਾਇ। ਕੈ ਹਨਤ ਤੋਹਿ ਕੈ ਜਪ ਨ ਮਾਇ। ੧੭੧।","roman":"Gahi taahi adhik deenee sajaai | kai hanat tohi kai jap na maai | 171 |","meaning_en":"Seizing him, he punished him severely: \"Either I kill you, or you do not chant to the Mother.\"","page":742,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਰਾਜਾ ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਰਾਜਾ ਸੂਦ੍ਰ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Raajaa soodr baach","meaning_en":"The Shudra king said:","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[172],"number_text":"੧੭੨।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਹਨਤ ਤੋਹ ਦਿਜ ਕਹੀ ਆਜ। ਨਹੀ ਬੋਰ ਬਾਰ ਮੋ ਪੂਜ ਸਾਜ।","roman":"Nahee hanat toh dij kahee aaj | nahee bor baar mo pooj saaj |","meaning_en":"\"Brahmin, I tell you today, I will not kill you if you do not make your worship in my land.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੋਰ ਬਾਰ: uncertain; read as 'in my domain'; possibly 'I will drown you'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈ ਤਜਹੁ ਸੇਵ ਦੇਵੀ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ। ਨਹੀ ਕਰਤ ਆਜ ਤੋ ਕੋ ਦੁਖੰਡ। ੧੭੨।","roman":"Kai tajhu sev devee prachand | nahee karat aaj to ko dukhand | 172 |","meaning_en":"Either give up the service of the fierce Goddess, or else today I will cut you in two.\"","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਜਾ ਸੌ","gurmukhi":"ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਬਾਚ ਰਾਜਾ ਸੌ","roman":"Bipr baach raajaa sau","meaning_en":"The Brahmin said to the king:","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[173],"number_text":"੧੭੩।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੀਜੈ ਦੁਖੰਡ ਨਹਿ ਤਜੋ ਸੇਵ। ਸੁਨਿ ਲੇਹੁ ਸਾਚ ਤੁਹਿ ਕਹੋ ਦੇਵ।","roman":"Keejai dukhand nahi tajo sev | suni lehu saach tuhi kaho dev |","meaning_en":"\"Cut me in two, I will not give up her service; hear the truth, O lord, I tell you.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੇਵ: here an address to the king."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਉ ਨ ਹੋਹਿ ਟੂਕ ਤਨ ਕੇ ਹਜਾਰ। ਨਹੀ ਤਜੋ ਪਾਇ ਦੇਵੀ ਉਦਾਰ। ੧੭੩।","roman":"Kiu na hohi took tan ke hajaar | nahee tajo paai devee udaar | 173 |","meaning_en":"Even if my body be cut into a thousand pieces, I will not abandon the feet of the generous Goddess.\"","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[174],"number_text":"੧੭੪।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨ ਭਯੋ ਬੈਨ ਸੂਦਰ ਸੁ ਕ੍ਰੁਧ। ਜਣ ਜੁਟ੍ਯੋ ਆਣਿ ਮਕਰਾਛ ਜੁਧ।","roman":"Sun bhayo bain soodar su krudh | jan jutyo aani makraachh judh |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words the Shudra became enraged, as if Makrachh had come and joined battle.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Makrachh: a demon of the Ramayan tale."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੋਊ ਦ੍ਰਿਗ ਸਕ੍ਰੁਧ ਸ੍ਰੋਣਤ ਚੁਚਾਨ। ਜਨ ਕਾਲ ਤਾਹਿ ਦੀਨੀ ਨਿਸਾਨ। ੧੭੪।","roman":"Do'oo drig sakrudh sronat chuchaan | jan kaal taahi deenee nisaan | 174 |","meaning_en":"Both his eyes, in fury, dripped blood, as if Death had given him a sign.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[175],"number_text":"੧੭੫।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਗਰਬ ਮੂੜ ਭ੍ਰਿਤਨ ਬੁਲਾਇ। ਉਚਰੇ ਬੈਨ ਇਹ ਹਣੋ ਜਾਇ।","roman":"Ati garab moor bhritan bulaai | uchre bain ih hano jaai |","meaning_en":"In great pride the fool called his servants and spoke these words: \"Go and kill him.\"","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੈ ਗਏ ਤਾਸੁ ਦ੍ਰੋਹੀ ਦੁਰੰਤ। ਜਹ ਸੰਭ੍ਰ ਸੁਭ ਦੇਵਲ ਸੁਭੰਤ। ੧੭੫।","roman":"Lai gae taasu drohee durant | jah sanbhr subh deval subhant | 175 |","meaning_en":"The cruel traitors took him away to where the fine temple of Shiva shone.","page":743,"flags":[{"code":"ੰੰ","reason":"same sign typed twice; written once (prints as one)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਭ੍ਰ: read as 'Shambhu' (Shiva); uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[176],"number_text":"੧੭੬।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਬਾਧ ਆਖ ਮੁਸਕੈ ਚੜਾਇ। ਕਰਿ ਲੀਨ ਕਾਢਿ ਅਸਿ ਕੋ ਨਚਾਇ।","roman":"Tih baadh aakh muskai charaai | kari leen kaadhi asi ko nachaai |","meaning_en":"Binding him, blindfolding his eyes and tying his arms, they drew out a sword and made it dance in their hands.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੁਸਕੈ ਚੜਾਇ: 'tying the arms behind'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਲਗੇ ਦੇਨ ਤਿਹ ਤੇਗ ਤਾਨ। ਤਬ ਕੀਓ ਕਾਲ ਕੋ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਧਿਆਨ। ੧੭੬।","roman":"Jab lage den tih teg taan | tab keeo kaal ko bipr dhiaan | 176 |","meaning_en":"When they were about to bring the sword down on him, then the Brahmin meditated on Kal (the Timeless).","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[177],"number_text":"੧੭੭।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਕੀਯੋ ਚਿਤ ਮੋ ਬਿਪ੍ਰ ਧਿਆਨ। ਤਿਹ ਦੀਨ ਦਰਸ ਤਬ ਕਾਲ ਆਨਿ।","roman":"Jab keeyo chit mo bipr dhiaan | tih deen daras tab kaal aani |","meaning_en":"When the Brahmin meditated in his heart, then Kal came and gave him sight of Himself:","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਕਰੋ ਚਿੰਤ ਚਿਤ ਮਾਝਿ ਏਕ। ਤਵ ਹੇਤੁ ਸਤ੍ਰੁ ਹਨਿ ਹੈ ਅਨੇਕ। ੧੭੭।","roman":"Nahee karo chint chit maajhi ek | tav hetu satru hani hai anek | 177 |","meaning_en":"\"Have not one worry in your heart; for your sake I will slay many enemies.\"","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[178],"number_text":"੧੭੮।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਪਰੀ ਸੂੰਕ ਭੋਹਰ ਮਝਾਰ। ਉਪਜਿਓ ਆਨਿ ਕਲਕੀ ਵਤਾਰ।","roman":"Tab paree soonk bhohar majhaar | upjio aani kalkee vataar |","meaning_en":"Then a rumbling came in the cellar; the Kalki incarnation came forth and appeared,","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੂੰਕ: read as 'a hissing/rumbling sound'; ਭੋਹਰ: cellar/underground chamber; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾੜ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਨੁ ਕਰਿ ਅਸਿ ਉਤੰਗ। ਤੁਰਕਛ ਸੁਵਛ ਤਾਜੀ ਸੁਰੰਗ। ੧੭੮।","roman":"Taar pramaanu kari asi utang | turkachh suvachh taajee surang | 178 |","meaning_en":"holding a sword as tall as a palm tree, on a swift, fine-coloured Turki Arab horse.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਜੀ: Arab horse."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਿਰਖੰਡੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸਿਰਖੰਡੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Sirkhandee chhand","meaning_en":"Sirkhandi metre.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[179],"number_text":"੧੭੯।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਵਜੇ ਨਾਦ ਸੁਰੰਗੀ ਧਗਾ ਘੋਰੀਆ। ਨਚੇ ਜਾਣ ਫਿਰੰਗੀ ਵਜੇ ਘੁੰਘਰੂ।","roman":"Vaje naad surangee dhagaa ghoreeaa | nache jaan phirangee vaje ghunghroo |","meaning_en":"Fine-toned trumpets and great drums sounded with a terrible roar; as if Firangis danced, the ankle-bells rang.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਗਾ: large drums; ਫਿਰੰਗੀ: 'Europeans', the image of dancers; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਦਾ ਤ੍ਰਿਸੂਲ ਨਿਖੰਗੀ ਝੂਲਨ ਬੈਰਖਾ। ਸਾਵਨ ਜਾਣ ਉਮੰਗੀ ਘਟਾ ਡਰਾਵਣੀ। ੧੭੯।","roman":"Gadaa trisool nikhangee jhoolan bairkhaa | saavan jaan umangee ghataa daraavnee | 179 |","meaning_en":"Maces, tridents, quivers and banners swayed, like the frightening clouds swelling in Sawan (the rainy month).","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[180],"number_text":"੧੮੦।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਣੇ ਅੰਗ ਭੁਜੰਗੀ ਸਾਵਲ ਸੋਹਣੇ। ਤ੍ਰੈ ਸੈ ਹਥ ਉਤੰਗੀ ਖੰਡਾ ਧੂਹਿਆ।","roman":"Baane ang bhujangee saaval sohne | trai sai hath utangee khandaa dhoohiaa |","meaning_en":"Dressed in garments on their limbs, dark and handsome as serpents, He drew a broadsword three hundred hands tall.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤ੍ਰੈ ਸੈ ਹਥ ਉਤੰਗੀ: 'three hundred hands high'; hyperbole.","meaning_pa":"ਸੱਪਾਂ ਵਰਗੇ ਸਾਂਵਲੇ ਤੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਅੰਗਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਬਸਤਰ ਸਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਸਨ। ਤਿੰਨ ਸੌ ਹੱਥ ਉੱਚਾ ਖੰਡਾ ਖਿੱਚਿਆ ਗਿਆ।","note_pa":"ਤ੍ਰੈ ਸੈ ਹਥ ਉਤੰਗੀ: 'ਤਿੰਨ ਸੌ ਹੱਥ ਉੱਚਾ'; ਇਹ ਅਤਿਕਥਨੀ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਜੀ ਭਉਰ ਪਿਲੰਗੀ ਛਾਲਾ ਪਾਈਆ। ਭੰਗੀ ਜਾਣ ਭਿੜੰਗੀ ਨਚੇ ਦਾਇਰੀ। ੧੮੦।","roman":"Taajee bhaur pilangee chhaalaa paaeeaa | bhangee jaan bhirangee nache daairee | 180 |","meaning_en":"The black and spotted Arab horses leapt, as if hemp-drinkers dancing in a ring.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਉਰ ਪਿਲੰਗੀ: horse colours (dark, leopard-spotted); ਦਾਇਰੀ: 'in a circle'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲੇ ਤੇ ਚਿਤਕਬਰੇ ਤਾਜ਼ੀ (ਅਰਬੀ) ਘੋੜੇ ਛਾਲਾਂ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਭੰਗ ਪੀਤੇ ਹੋਏ ਲੋਕ ਘੇਰੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹੋਣ।","note_pa":"ਭਉਰ ਪਿਲੰਗੀ: ਘੋੜਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ (ਕਾਲਾ, ਚੀਤੇ ਵਰਗੇ ਧੱਬੇ); ਦਾਇਰੀ: 'ਘੇਰੇ ਵਿੱਚ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਲੱਗਦਾ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[181],"number_text":"੧੮੧।","page":743,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੇ ਨਾਦ ਸੁਰੰਗੀ ਅਣੀਆ ਜੁਟੀਆ। ਪੈਰੇ ਧਾਰ ਪਵੰਗੀ ਫਉਜਾ ਚੀਰ ਕੈ।","roman":"Baje naad surangee aneeaa juteeaa | paire dhaar pavangee phaujaa cheer kai |","meaning_en":"Fine trumpets sounded; the ranks clashed; the horsemen swam through, cutting the armies.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੈਰੇ ਧਾਰ ਪਵੰਗੀ: read as 'horses swam through the stream (of armies)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੁਰੀਲੇ ਨਗਾੜੇ ਵੱਜੇ, ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਆਹਮੋ-ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਹੋਈਆਂ। ਘੋੜ-ਸਵਾਰ ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਚੀਰਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਪਾਰ ਲੰਘ ਗਏ।","note_pa":"ਪੈਰੇ ਧਾਰ ਪਵੰਗੀ: ਇਸ ਨੂੰ 'ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਦੀ ਧਾਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਘੋੜੇ ਤਰਦੇ ਹੋਏ' ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠੈ ਛੈਲ ਛਲੰਗੀ ਛਾਲਾ ਪਾਈਆ। ਝਾੜਿ ਝੜਾਕ ਝੜੰਗੀ ਤੇਗਾ ਵਜੀਆ। ੧੮੧।","roman":"Uthai chhail chhalangee chhaalaa paaeeaa | jhaari jharaak jharangee tegaa vajeeaa | 181 |","meaning_en":"The gallant warriors rose and leapt; with a ringing clash the swords struck.","page":743,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਝਾੜਿ ਝੜਾਕ ਝੜੰਗੀ: sound-words, left as 'ringing clash'.","meaning_pa":"ਬਹਾਦਰ ਯੋਧੇ ਉੱਠੇ ਤੇ ਛਾਲਾਂ ਮਾਰੀਆਂ। ਝੜਾਕ ਦੀ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਨਾਲ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਵੱਜੀਆਂ।","note_pa":"ਝਾੜਿ ਝੜਾਕ ਝੜੰਗੀ: ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਾਲੇ ਸ਼ਬਦ; ਅਰਥ 'ਝਣਕਾਰ ਵਾਲੀ ਖੜਕਾਰ' ਰੱਖਿਆ ਗਿਆ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਮਾਨਕਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸਮਾਨਕਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Samaankaa chhand","meaning_en":"Samanka metre.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਮਾਨਕਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[182],"number_text":"੧੮੨।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁ ਦੇਖ ਦੇਖ ਕੈ ਸਬੈ। ਸੁ ਭਾਜਿ ਭਾਜਿ ਗੇ ਤਬੇ।","roman":"Ju dekh dekh kai sabai | su bhaaji bhaaji ge tabe |","meaning_en":"All who saw Him, then fled and fled away.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਦੇਖਿਆ, ਉਹ ਸਾਰੇ ਭੱਜ ਭੱਜ ਕੇ ਚਲੇ ਗਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹਿਓ ਸੁ ਸੋਭ ਸੋਭ ਹੀ । ਬਿਲੋਕਿ ਲੋਕ ਲੋਭ ਹੀ। ੧੮੨।","roman":"Kahio su sobh sobh hee | biloki lok lobh hee | 182 |","meaning_en":"He is called glory upon glory; seeing Him, people are filled with longing.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਉੱਤੇ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਆਖਿਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਲੋਕਾਂ ਦੇ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਲਾਲਸਾ ਜਾਗਦੀ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[183],"number_text":"੧੮੩।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਰੂਪ ਰਾਜਈ। ਬਿਲੋਕਿ ਭਾਨ ਲਾਜਈ।","roman":"Prachand roop raajaee | biloki bhaan laajaee |","meaning_en":"His fierce form shines; seeing it, the sun is ashamed.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਰੂਪ ਚਮਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਸੂਰਜ ਵੀ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦਾ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਚੰਡ ਤੇਜ ਇਉ ਲਸੈ। ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਜੋਤਿ ਕੋ ਹਸੈ। ੧੮੩।","roman":"Su chand tej iu lasai | prachand joti ko hasai | 183 |","meaning_en":"His fierce radiance gleams so that it mocks the fierce light (of the sun).","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦਾ ਤੇਜ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਲਿਸ਼ਕਦਾ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਜੋਤ ਵੀ ਮਜ਼ਾਕ ਉਡਾਉਂਦੀ ਜਾਪਦੀ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[184],"number_text":"੧੮੪।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਕੋਪਿ ਕੋਪ ਕੈ ਹਠੀ। ਚਪੈ ਚਿਰਾਇ ਜਿਉ ਭਠੀ।","roman":"Su kopi kop kai hathee | chapai chiraai jiu bhathee |","meaning_en":"The steadfast One in wrath upon wrath blazes like a furnace.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਪੈ ਚਿਰਾਇ: uncertain; read as 'blazes up'.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਹਠੀ ਪ੍ਰਭੂ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਉੱਤੇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਭੱਠੀ ਵਾਂਗ ਭੜਕ ਉੱਠਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਚਪੈ ਚਿਰਾਇ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ; 'ਭੜਕ ਉੱਠਦਾ ਹੈ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਮੰਡਲੀ ਲਸੈ। ਕਿ ਮਾਰਤੰਡ ਕੋ ਹਸੈ। ੧੮੪।","roman":"Prachand mandlee lasai | ki maartand ko hasai | 184 |","meaning_en":"His fierce circle (of glory) shines as if mocking the sun.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦਾ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਮੰਡਲ ਚਮਕਦਾ ਹੈ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਸੂਰਜ ਦਾ ਮਜ਼ਾਕ ਉਡਾ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੋਵੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[185],"number_text":"੧੮੫।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਕੋਪ ਓਪ ਦੈ ਬਲੀ। ਕਿ ਰਾਜ ਮੰਡਲੀ ਚਲੀ।","roman":"Su kop op dai balee | ki raaj mandlee chalee |","meaning_en":"The mighty One shines with wrath, as if a royal company were on the move.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਲਵਾਨ ਪ੍ਰਭੂ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਚਮਕਦਾ ਹੈ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਕਿਸੇ ਰਾਜ-ਮੰਡਲੀ ਦਾ ਕੂਚ ਹੋ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੋਵੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਪਾਨਿ ਲੈ। ਬਿਸੇਖ ਬੀਰ ਮਾਨ ਕੈ। ੧੮੫।","roman":"Su asatr sasatr paani lai | bisekh beer maan kai | 185 |","meaning_en":"Taking weapons and arms in hand, regarded especially as a hero.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਤੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਹੱਥਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਖ਼ਾਸ ਤੌਰ ਤੇ ਸੂਰਵੀਰ ਮੰਨਿਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tomar chhand","meaning_en":"Tomar metre.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[186],"number_text":"੧੮੬।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਟ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਨਚਾਇ। ਚਿਤ ਕੋਪ ਓਪ ਬਢਾਇ।","roman":"Bhat sasatr asatr nachaai | chit kop op badhaai |","meaning_en":"The warriors flourish their weapons and arms, increasing the glow of wrath in their minds,","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਸ਼ਸਤ੍ਰ ਤੇ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਨਚਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਤੇ ਜੋਸ਼ ਵਧਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਰਿਕਛ ਅਛ ਤੁਰੰਗ। ਰਣ ਰੰਗਿ ਚਾਰ ਉਤੰਗ। ੧੮੬।","roman":"Turikachh achh turang | ran rangi chaar utang | 186 |","meaning_en":"on fine swift Turki horses, lofty and beautiful in the colour of battle.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੇਜ਼ ਤੁਰਕੀ ਘੋੜਿਆਂ ਉੱਤੇ, ਜੋ ਉੱਚੇ ਤੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਜੰਗ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੰਗੇ ਹੋਏ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[187],"number_text":"੧੮੭।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਪੀਸਤ ਦਾਤ। ਕਹਿ ਆਪੁ ਆਪਨ ਬਾਤ।","roman":"Kari krodh peesat daat | kahi aapu aapan baat |","meaning_en":"In anger they grind their teeth, each speaking his own words.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਦੰਦ ਪੀਸਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹਰ ਕੋਈ ਆਪਣੀ ਗੱਲ ਆਖਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਟ ਭੈਰਹਵ ਹੈ ਧੀਰ। ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਛਾਡਤ ਤੀਰ। ੧੮੭।","roman":"Bhat bhairhav hai dheer | kari kop chhaadat teer | 187 |","meaning_en":"Warriors steady as Bhairav, in wrath, loose arrows.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੈਰਵ ਵਰਗੇ ਅਡੋਲ ਯੋਧੇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਿੱਚ ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[188],"number_text":"੧੮੮।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰ ਕੋਪ ਕਲਿ ਅਵਤਾਰ। ਗਹਿ ਪਾਨਿ ਅਜਾਨ ਕੁਠਾਰ।","roman":"Kar kop kali avtaar | gahi paani ajaan kuthaar |","meaning_en":"In wrath, the incarnation of the Kali age took a knee-long axe in hand.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਜਾਨ ਕੁਠਾਰ: read as 'axe reaching the knee'; or 'arms reaching the knee'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਲਿ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਨੇ ਗੋਡਿਆਂ ਤੱਕ ਲੰਮਾ ਕੁਹਾੜਾ ਹੱਥ ਵਿੱਚ ਫੜਿਆ।","note_pa":"ਅਜਾਨ ਕੁਠਾਰ: ਅਰਥ 'ਗੋਡਿਆਂ ਤੱਕ ਪਹੁੰਚਦਾ ਕੁਹਾੜਾ' ਜਾਂ 'ਗੋਡਿਆਂ ਤੱਕ ਲੰਮੀਆਂ ਬਾਹਾਂ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਨਕੇਕ ਕੀਨ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰ। ਭਟ ਜੂਝ ਗਯੋ ਸੈ ਚਾਰ। ੧੮੮।","roman":"Tankek keen prahaar | bhat joojh gayo sai chaar | 188 |","meaning_en":"He struck just a small blow, and four hundred warriors fell fighting.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੇ ਜ਼ਰਾ ਜਿੰਨੀ ਚੋਟ ਮਾਰੀ, ਅਤੇ ਚਾਰ ਸੌ ਯੋਧੇ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗ ਪਏ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭੜਥੂਆ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭੜਥੂਆ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bharthooaa chhand","meaning_en":"Bharthua metre.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੜਥੂਆ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[189],"number_text":"੧੮੯।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਢਢਕੰਤ ਢੋਲੰ। ਬਬਕੰਤ ਬੋਲੰ।","roman":"Dhadhkant dholan | babkant bolan |","meaning_en":"Drums thunder, war-cries roar;","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Battle passage with many sound-words; sense given.","meaning_pa":"ਢੋਲ ਢਮਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਵੰਗਾਰਾਂ ਗੂੰਜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰੇ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਾਲੇ ਸ਼ਬਦਾਂ ਵਾਲਾ ਯੁੱਧ-ਵਰਣਨ; ਅਰਥ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਛਕੰਤ ਤਾਜੀ। ਗਜਕੰਤ ਗਾਜੀ। ੧੮੯।","roman":"Uchhkant taajee | gajkant gaajee | 189 |","meaning_en":"Arab horses leap, warriors bellow.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਾਜੀ: 'warriors (ghazi)'.","meaning_pa":"ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਉਛਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਗਾਜੀ: 'ਯੋਧੇ (ਗਾਜੀ)'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[190],"number_text":"੧੯੦।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛੁਟਕੰਤ ਤੀਰੰ। ਬਬਕੰਤ ਬੀਰੰ।","roman":"Chhutkant teeran | babkant beeran |","meaning_en":"Arrows fly, heroes roar;","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਬਹਾਦਰ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਢਲਕੰਤ ਢਾਲੰ। ਉਠਕੰਤ ਤਾਲੰ। ੧੯੦।","roman":"Dhalkant dhaalan | uthkant taalan | 190 |","meaning_en":"shields clatter, rhythms rise.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਢਾਲਾਂ ਖੜਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਤਾਲਾਂ ਉੱਠਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[191],"number_text":"੧੯੧।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਿਮਕੰਤ ਖਗੰ। ਧਧਕੰਤ ਧਗੰ।","roman":"Khimkant khagan | dhadhkant dhagan |","meaning_en":"Swords flash, great drums boom;","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਚਮਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਵੱਡੇ ਨਗਾੜੇ ਗੂੰਜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੁਟਕੰਤ ਨਾਲੰ। ਉਠਕੰਤ ਜ੍ਵਾਲੰ। ੧੯੧।","roman":"Chhutkant naalan | uthkant jvaalan | 191 |","meaning_en":"guns fire, flames rise.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਾਲੰ: 'gun-barrels'.","meaning_pa":"ਬੰਦੂਕਾਂ ਚੱਲਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਅੱਗ ਦੀਆਂ ਲਪਟਾਂ ਉੱਠਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਨਾਲੰ: 'ਬੰਦੂਕ ਦੀਆਂ ਨਾਲੀਆਂ'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[192],"number_text":"੧੯੨।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹਤੰਤ ਘਾਯੰ। ਝਲਕੰਤ ਚਾਯੰ।","roman":"Bahtant ghaayan | jhalkant chaayan |","meaning_en":"Wounds flow, eagerness gleams;","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮਾਂ ਵਿੱਚੋਂ ਲਹੂ ਵਗਦਾ ਹੈ, ਚਾਅ ਝਲਕਦਾ ਹੈ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਿਗਤੰਤ ਬੀਰੰ। ਭਿਗਤੰਤ ਭੀਰੰ। ੧੯੨।","roman":"Digtant beeran | bhigtant bheeran | 192 |","meaning_en":"heroes fall, cowards are drenched (in fear).","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਿਗਤੰਤ: read as 'are soaked' or 'flee'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਬਹਾਦਰ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਪੋਕ ਡਰ ਨਾਲ ਭਿੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਭਿਗਤੰਤ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ; 'ਭਿੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ' ਜਾਂ 'ਭੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[193],"number_text":"੧੯੩।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਟੁਟੰਤੰਤ ਖੋਲੰ। ਢਮੰਕੰਤ ਢੋਲੰ।","roman":"Tutantant kholan | dhamankant dholan |","meaning_en":"Helmets break, drums boom;","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੋਲੰ: read as 'helmets / skull-caps'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਟੋਪ ਟੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਢੋਲ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਖੋਲੰ: ਟੋਪ ਜਾਂ ਖੋਪਰੀ ਦੀ ਢਾਲ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਟਟੰਕੰਤ ਤਾਲੰ। ਨਚੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਲੰ। ੧੯੩।","roman":"Tatankant taalan | nachantant baalan | 193 |","meaning_en":"cymbals clang, the young women dance.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਲੰ: read as celestial maidens; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤਾਲਾਂ ਟਣਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਅਪੱਛਰਾਵਾਂ ਨੱਚਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਬਾਲੰ: ਸਵਰਗੀ ਕੰਨਿਆਵਾਂ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[194],"number_text":"੧੯੪।","page":744,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੰਤੰਤ ਅੰਗੰ। ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਜੰਗੰ।","roman":"Girantant angan | katantant jangan |","meaning_en":"Limbs fall, the fighters cut;","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਲੜਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਵੱਢਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੰਤੰਤ ਤੀਰੰ। ਭਟੰਕੰਤ ਭੀਰੰ। ੧੯੪।","roman":"Chalantant teeran | bhatankant bheeran | 194 |","meaning_en":"arrows fly, cowards flee.","page":744,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਚੱਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[195],"number_text":"੧੯੫।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਝੰਤੰਤ ਵੀਰੰ। ਭਜੰਤੰਤ ਭੀਰੰ।","roman":"Jujhantant veeran | bhajantant bheeran |","meaning_en":"Heroes fight, cowards run;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੰਤੰਤ ਕ੍ਰੋਹੰ। ਭਰੰਤੰਤ ਰੋਹੰ। ੧੯੫।","roman":"Karantant krohan | bharantant rohan | 195 |","meaning_en":"they show wrath, they are filled with rage.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਿਖਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦਾ ਮਨ ਰੋਹ ਨਾਲ ਭਰਿਆ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[196],"number_text":"੧੯੬।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜੰਤੰਤ ਤੀਰੰ। ਭਜੰਤੰਤ ਭੀਰੰ।","roman":"Tajantant teeran | bhajantant bheeran |","meaning_en":"Arrows are loosed, cowards run;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੰਤੰਤ ਘਾਯੰ। ਝਲੰਤੰਤ ਜਾਯੰ। ੧੯੬।","roman":"Bahantant ghaayan | jhalantant jaayan | 196 |","meaning_en":"wounds flow, they bear them and go on.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਵਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉਹ ਸਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[197],"number_text":"੧੯੭।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਤਕੰਤ ਅੰਗੰ। ਜੁਟਕੰਤ ਜੰਗੰ।","roman":"Tatkant angan | jutkant jangan |","meaning_en":"Limbs quiver, warriors close in combat;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਕੰਬਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਜੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਲਥਥ ਲੁਥੰ। ਪਲੁਥਤ ਜੁਥੰ। ੧੯੭।","roman":"Ulthath luthan | paluthat juthan | 197 |","meaning_en":"corpses tumble over, heaps upon heaps.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲਾਸ਼ਾਂ ਉਲਟ-ਪੁਲਟ ਹੁੰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਢੇਰਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਢੇਰ ਲੱਗ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[198],"number_text":"੧੯੮।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਢਲੰਕੰਤ ਢਾਲੰ। ਪੁਅੰਤੰਤ ਮਾਲੰ।","roman":"Dhalankant dhaalan | puantant maalan |","meaning_en":"Shields clash; (Shiva) threads his garland;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੁਅੰਤੰਤ ਮਾਲੰ: Shiva stringing a garland of skulls; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਢਾਲਾਂ ਖੜਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; (ਸ਼ਿਵ) ਖੋਪਰੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਮਾਲਾ ਪਰੋਂਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਪੁਅੰਤੰਤ ਮਾਲੰ: ਸ਼ਿਵ ਖੋਪਰੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਮਾਲਾ ਪਰੋਂਦੇ ਹਨ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੰਤੰਤ ਈਸੰ। ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਸੀਸੰ। ੧੯੮।","roman":"Nachantant eesan | katantant seesan | 198 |","meaning_en":"the Lord (Shiva) dances; heads are cut.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪ੍ਰਭੂ (ਸ਼ਿਵ) ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਿਰ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[199],"number_text":"੧੯੯।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਛੰਕੰਤ ਤਾਜੀ। ਬਹੰਤੰਤ ਗਾਜੀ।","roman":"Uchhankant taajee | bahantant gaajee |","meaning_en":"Arab horses leap, warriors strike;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਉਛਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੁਟੰਤੰਤ ਲੁਥੰ। ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਮੁਖੰ। ੧੯੯।","roman":"Lutantant luthan | katantant mukhan | 199 |","meaning_en":"corpses roll, faces are cut.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲਾਸ਼ਾਂ ਰੁਲਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਚਿਹਰੇ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[200],"number_text":"੨੦੦।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਪੰਤੰਤ ਤੇਗੰ। ਚਮੰਕੰਤ ਬੇਗੰ।","roman":"Tapantant tegan | chamankant began |","meaning_en":"Swords blaze, flashing swiftly;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਦਮਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਤੇਜ਼ੀ ਨਾਲ ਲਿਸ਼ਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੇ ਮੁੰਡ ਮਾਲੀ। ਹਸੇਤਤ ਕਾਲੀ। ੨੦੦।","roman":"Nache mund maalee | hasetat kaalee | 200 |","meaning_en":"the wearer of the skull-garland dances; Kali laughs.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖੋਪਰੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਮਾਲਾ ਵਾਲਾ ਨੱਚਦਾ ਹੈ; ਕਾਲੀ ਹੱਸਦੀ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[201],"number_text":"੨੦੧।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਟੰਤੰਤ ਵੀਰੰ। ਛੁਟੰਤੰਤ ਤੀਰੰ।","roman":"Jutantant veeran | chhutantant teeran |","meaning_en":"Heroes close in, arrows are loosed;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹਾਦਰ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਲੰ। ਢਲੰਤੰਤ ਢਾਲੰ। ੨੦੧।","roman":"Barantant baalan | dhalantant dhaalan | 201 |","meaning_en":"maidens choose (the slain heroes as husbands); shields clatter.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਰੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਲੰ: heavenly maidens wedding fallen heroes; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕੰਨਿਆਵਾਂ ਵਰ ਚੁਣਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ (ਡਿੱਗੇ ਸੂਰਮਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਪਤੀ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ); ਢਾਲਾਂ ਖੜਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਬਰੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਲੰ: ਸਵਰਗੀ ਕੰਨਿਆਵਾਂ ਡਿੱਗੇ ਸੂਰਮਿਆਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਿਆਹ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[202],"number_text":"੨੦੨।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਮਤੰਤ ਮਦੰ। ਉਠੈ ਸਦ ਗਦੰ।","roman":"Sumtant madan | uthai sad gadan |","meaning_en":"Drunk with the intoxication (of battle), cries and shouts rise;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋਸ਼ ਦੇ ਨਸ਼ੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੱਤੇ, ਚੀਕਾਂ ਤੇ ਰੌਲਾ ਉੱਠਦਾ ਹੈ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਅੰਗੰ। ਗਿਰੰਤੰਤ ਜੰਗੰ। ੨੦੨।","roman":"Katantant angan | girantant jangan | 202 |","meaning_en":"limbs are cut, fighters fall.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਲੜਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[203],"number_text":"੨੦੩।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲਤੰਤਿ ਚਾਯੰ। ਜੁਝੰਤੰਤ ਜਾਯੰ।","roman":"Chaltanti chaayan | jujhantant jaayan |","meaning_en":"They move with zeal and go on fighting;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਚਾਅ ਨਾਲ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਅੱਗੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣੰਕੰਤ ਨਾਦੰ। ਬਜੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਦੰ। ੨੦੩।","roman":"Ranankant naadan | bajantant baadan | 203 |","meaning_en":"battle-sounds ring, instruments play.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਦੀਆਂ ਆਵਾਜ਼ਾਂ ਗੂੰਜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਵਾਜੇ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[204],"number_text":"੨੦੪।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਐਰੰਤ ਪਤ੍ਰੀ। ਲਗੰਤੰਤ ਅਤ੍ਰੀ।","roman":"Puairant patree | lagantant atree |","meaning_en":"Feathered arrows fly, weapons strike;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੁਐਰੰਤ ਪਤ੍ਰੀ: read as 'arrows swim (through the air)'.","meaning_pa":"ਖੰਭਾਂ ਵਾਲੇ ਤੀਰ ਉੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹਥਿਆਰ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਪੁਐਰੰਤ ਪਤ੍ਰੀ: 'ਤੀਰ ਹਵਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਤੈਰਦੇ ਹਨ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜਤੰਤ੍ਰ ਅਤ੍ਰੰ। ਜੁਝਤੰਤ ਛਤ੍ਰੰ। ੨੦੪।","roman":"Bajtantr atran | jujhtant chhatran | 204 |","meaning_en":"weapons clang, Kshatriyas fight.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰ ਖੜਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਛੱਤਰੀ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[205],"number_text":"੨੦੫।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੰਤੰਤ ਭੂਮੀ। ਉਠੰਤੰਤ ਝੂਮੀ।","roman":"Girantant bhoomee | uthantant jhoomee |","meaning_en":"They fall to the ground, rise up swaying;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਝੂਮ ਕੇ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਟੰਤੰਤ ਪਾਨੰ। ਜੁਝੰਤੰਤ ਜੁਆਨੰ। ੨੦੫।","roman":"Ratantant paanan | jujhantant juaanan | 205 |","meaning_en":"they cry for water, young warriors fight.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਾਣੀ ਲਈ ਤੜਪਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਵਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[206],"number_text":"੨੦੬।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਣੰ। ਰੁਕੰਤੰਤ ਦਿਸਾਣੰ।","roman":"Chalantant baanan | rukantant disaanan |","meaning_en":"Arrows fly, the directions are blocked;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਚੱਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਰੁਕ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੰਤੰਤ ਬੀਰੰ। ਭਜੰਤੰਤ ਭੀਰੰ। ੨੦੬।","roman":"Girantant beeran | bhajantant bheeran | 206 |","meaning_en":"heroes fall, cowards run.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[207],"number_text":"੨੦੭।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੰਤੰਤ ਈਸੰ। ਪੁਅੰਤੰਤ ਸੀਸੰ।","roman":"Nachantant eesan | puantant seesan |","meaning_en":"The Lord (Shiva) dances, stringing heads;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪ੍ਰਭੂ (ਸ਼ਿਵ) ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਿਰ ਪਰੋਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੰਤੰਤ ਡਉਰੂ। ਭ੍ਰਮੰਤੰਤ ਭਉਰੂ। ੨੦੭।","roman":"Bajantant dauroo | bhramantant bhauroo | 207 |","meaning_en":"damrus sound, Bhairavs roam.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਉਰੂ: read as Bhairav spirits; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਡਮਰੂ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਭੈਰਵ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਭਉਰੂ: ਭੈਰਵ ਆਤਮਾਵਾਂ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[208],"number_text":"੨੦੮।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਲੰ। ਤੁਟੰਤੰਤ ਤਾਲੰ।","roman":"Nachantant baalan | tutantant taalan |","meaning_en":"Maidens dance, rhythms break;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕੰਨਿਆਵਾਂ ਨੱਚਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਤਾਲਾਂ ਟੁੱਟਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਚੰਤੰਤ ਵੀਰੰ। ਭਜੰਤੰਤ ਭੀਰੰ। ੨੦੮।","roman":"Machantant veeran | bhajantant bheeran | 208 |","meaning_en":"heroes rage, cowards run.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[209],"number_text":"੨੦੯।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਗੰਤੰਤ ਬਾਣੰ। ਢਹੰਤੰਤ ਜੁਆਣੰ।","roman":"Lagantant baanan | dhahantant juaanan |","meaning_en":"Arrows strike, young warriors fall;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਲੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਵਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਅਧੰ। ਭਟੰਤੰਤ ਬਧੰ। ੨੦੯।","roman":"Katantant adhan | bhatantant badhan | 209 |","meaning_en":"they are cut in half, warriors are slain.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਅੱਧੇ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸੂਰਮੇ ਮਾਰੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[210],"number_text":"੨੧੦।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਹੰਤੰਤ ਖੂਨੀ। ਚੜੇ ਚਉਪ ਦੂਨੀ।","roman":"Khahantant khoonee | chare chaup doonee |","meaning_en":"The bloodthirsty clash, their zeal doubled;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖ਼ੂਨੀ ਟਕਰਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦਾ ਚਾਅ ਦੁੱਗਣਾ ਹੋ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੰਤੰਤ ਅਤ੍ਰੰ। ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਛਤ੍ਰੰ। ੨੧੦।","roman":"Bahantant atran | katantant chhatran | 210 |","meaning_en":"weapons are wielded, Kshatriyas are cut.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰ ਚਲਾਏ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਛੱਤਰੀ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[211],"number_text":"੨੧੧।","page":745,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੰਤੰਤ ਪਤ੍ਰੀ। ਜੁਝੰਤੰਤ ਅਤ੍ਰੀ।","roman":"Bahantant patree | jujhantant atree |","meaning_en":"Arrows fly, armed men fight;","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖੰਭਾਂ ਵਾਲੇ ਤੀਰ ਉੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹਥਿਆਰਬੰਦ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਿਣੰਕੰਤ ਤਾਜੀ। ਕਣੰਛੰਤ ਗਾਜੀ। ੨੧੧।","roman":"Hinankant taajee | kananchhant gaajee | 211 |","meaning_en":"Arab horses neigh, warriors groan.","page":745,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਣੰਛੰਤ: read as 'groan / moan'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਘੋੜੇ ਹਿਣਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਕਰਾਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਕਣੰਛੰਤ: 'ਕਰਾਹੁਣਾ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[212],"number_text":"੨੧੨।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਟੰਤੰਤ ਚਰਮੰ। ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਬਰਮੰ।","roman":"Tutantant charman | katantant barman |","meaning_en":"Shields break, armour is cut;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਢਾਲਾਂ ਟੁੱਟਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਬਸਤਰ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੰਤੰਤ ਭੂਮੀ। ਉਠੰਤੰਤ ਘੂਮੀ। ੨੧੨।","roman":"Girantant bhoomee | uthantant ghoomee | 212 |","meaning_en":"they fall to the ground, rise up reeling.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਚੱਕਰ ਖਾਂਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[213],"number_text":"੨੧੩।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਟੰਤੰਤ ਪਾਨੰ। ਕਟੰਤੰਤ ਜੁਆਨੰ।","roman":"Ratantant paanan | katantant juaanan |","meaning_en":"They cry for water, young warriors are cut;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਾਣੀ ਲਈ ਤੜਪਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਵਾਨ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਡੰਤੰਤ ਏਕੰ। ਗਡੰਤੰਤ ਨੇਕੰ। ੨੧੩।","roman":"Udantant ekan | gadantant nekan | 213 |","meaning_en":"one is hurled flying, many are pinned down.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਉਡੰਤੰਤ ਏਕੰ। ਗਡੰਤੰਤ ਨੇਕੰ: uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਇੱਕ ਉਡਾਇਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਬਹੁਤਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਗੱਡ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਉਡੰਤੰਤ ਏਕੰ। ਗਡੰਤੰਤ ਨੇਕੰ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅਨੂਪ ਨਿਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਅਨੂਪ ਨਿਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Anoop niraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Anoop Niraj metre.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਨੂਪ ਨਿਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[214],"number_text":"੨੧੪।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨੂਪ ਰੂਪ ਦਿਖ ਕੈ ਸੁ ਕ੍ਰੁਧ ਜੋਧਣੰ ਬਰੰ।","roman":"Anoop roop dikh kai su krudh jodhnan baran |","meaning_en":"Seeing the peerless form, the great warriors grew angry;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੇਮਿਸਾਲ ਰੂਪ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਮਹਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਆ ਗਏ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਨਧ ਬਧ ਉਦਿਤੰ ਸੁ ਕੋਪ ਓਪ ਦੇ ਨਰੰ।","roman":"Sanadh badh uditan su kop op de naran |","meaning_en":"the men, armoured and armed, rose up, shining with wrath.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਸਤਰ ਪਹਿਨੇ ਹੋਏ ਤੇ ਹਥਿਆਰਬੰਦ ਬੰਦੇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਚਮਕਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਉੱਠ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹੋਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਹੰਤ ਜੈਤ ਪਤ੍ਰਣੰ ਕਰੰਤ ਘਾਵ ਦੁਧਰੰ।","roman":"Chahant jait patranan karant ghaav dudhran |","meaning_en":"Seeking the letter of victory, they deal two-edged blows;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੁਧਰੰ: read as 'with double-edged blades' or 'fierce'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਤ ਦਾ ਪੱਤਰ ਲੈਣ ਦੀ ਇੱਛਾ ਨਾਲ ਉਹ ਦੋਧਾਰੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਦੁਧਰੰ: 'ਦੋਧਾਰੇ ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ' ਜਾਂ 'ਭਿਆਨਕ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਟੰਤ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਸਤ੍ਰਣੋ ਲਸੰਤ ਉਜਲੋ ਫਲੰ। ੨੧੪।","roman":"Tutant asatr sastrano lasant ujlo phalan | 214 |","meaning_en":"weapons and arms break, and their bright blades gleam.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰ ਤੇ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਟੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਤੇ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੇ ਚਮਕਦੇ ਫਲ ਲਿਸ਼ਕਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[215],"number_text":"੨੧੫।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠੰਤ ਭਉਰ ਭੂਰਣੋ ਕਢੰਤ ਭੈਕਰੀ ਸੁਰੰ।","roman":"Uthant bhaur bhoorno kadhant bhaikree suran |","meaning_en":"Whirlwinds of dust rise, fearful sounds are made;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਉਰ ਭੂਰਣੋ: read as 'swirls of dust'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਧੂੜ ਦੇ ਵਾਵਰੋਲੇ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਾਉਣੀਆਂ ਆਵਾਜ਼ਾਂ ਕੱਢੀਆਂ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਭਉਰ ਭੂਰਣੋ: 'ਧੂੜ ਦੇ ਵਾਵਰੋਲੇ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਜੰਤ ਭੀਰ ਭੈਕਰੰ ਬਜੰਤ ਬੀਰ ਸੁਪ੍ਰਭੰ।","roman":"Bhajant bheer bhaikran bajant beer suprabhan |","meaning_en":"cowards flee in terror, splendid heroes clash.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਡਰਪੋਕ ਡਰ ਕੇ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸ਼ਾਨਦਾਰ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਟਕਰਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਟੰਤ ਤਾਲ ਤਥਿਯੰ ਨਚੰਤ ਈਸ੍ਰਣੋ ਰਣੰ।","roman":"Tutant taal tathiyan nachant eesrano ranan |","meaning_en":"The rhythm breaks off 'tat-thai', Shiva dances on the battlefield;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਥਿਯੰ: dance syllables.","meaning_pa":"ਤਾਲ 'ਤਤ-ਥਈ' ਟੁੱਟ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ, ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਈਸ਼ਰ (ਸ਼ਿਵ) ਨੱਚਦਾ ਹੈ;","note_pa":"ਤਥਿਯੰ: ਨਾਚ ਦੇ ਬੋਲ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਹੰਤ ਖਤ੍ਰਿਣੋ ਖਗੰ ਨਿਨਦਿ ਗਦਿ ਘੁੰਘਰੰ। ੨੧੫।","roman":"Khahant khatrino khagan nindi gadi ghunghran | 215 |","meaning_en":"the swords of the Kshatriyas clash, bells sound and cries ring out.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖੱਤਰੀਆਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਖੜਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਘੁੰਗਰੂ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ ਚੀਕਾਂ ਗੂੰਜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[216],"number_text":"੨੧੬।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਜੰਤ ਆਸੁਰੀ ਸੁਤੰ ਉਠੰਤ ਭੈਕਰੀ ਧੁਣੰ।","roman":"Bhajant aasuree sutan uthant bhaikree dhunan |","meaning_en":"The sons of demons flee; a fearful din rises;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਸੁਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਪੁੱਤਰ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਾਉਣੀ ਗੂੰਜ ਉੱਠਦੀ ਹੈ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੰਤ ਤੀਛਣੋ ਸਰੰ ਸਿਲੇਣ ਉਜਲੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਤੰ।","roman":"Chalant teechhno saran silen ujlee kritan |","meaning_en":"sharp arrows fly, made bright on the whetstone.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਣ ਉੱਤੇ ਤੇਜ਼ ਕੀਤੇ ਹੋਏ ਚਮਕਦੇ ਤਿੱਖੇ ਤੀਰ ਚੱਲਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੰਤ ਰੰਗਿ ਜੋਗਣੰ ਚਚਕਿ ਚਉਦਣੋ ਦਿਸੰ।","roman":"Nachant rangi jognan chachki chaudno disan |","meaning_en":"Yoginis dance in delight; startled are the fourteen directions;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਉਦਣੋ ਦਿਸੰ: 'fourteen (worlds/directions)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜੋਗਣਾਂ ਖ਼ੁਸ਼ੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਨੱਚਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਚੌਦਾਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਹੈਰਾਨ ਹੋ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਚਉਦਣੋ ਦਿਸੰ: 'ਚੌਦਾਂ (ਲੋਕ ਜਾਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ)'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਪੰਤ ਕੁੰਦਨੋ ਗਿਰੰ ਤ੍ਰਸੰਤ ਸਰਬਤੋ ਦਿਸੰ। ੨੧੬।","roman":"Kapant kundno giran trasant sarabto disan | 216 |","meaning_en":"the golden mountain (Sumeru) trembles; all directions are afraid.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੁਨਹਿਰੀ ਪਰਬਤ (ਸੁਮੇਰ) ਕੰਬਦਾ ਹੈ, ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਡਰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[217],"number_text":"੨੧੭।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੰਤ ਬੀਰ ਬਾਵਰੰ ਖਹੰਤ ਬਾਹਣੀ ਧੁਜੰ।","roman":"Nachant beer baavran khahant baahnee dhujan |","meaning_en":"Frenzied heroes dance; armies' banners clash;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਹਣੀ: read as 'vahini', army.","meaning_pa":"ਬਾਵਲੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ, ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਦੇ ਝੰਡੇ ਟਕਰਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਬਾਹਣੀ: 'ਫ਼ੌਜ' (ਵਾਹਿਨੀ)।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰੰਤ ਅਛ੍ਰਣੋ ਭਟੰ ਪ੍ਰਬੀਨ ਚੀਨ ਸੁਪ੍ਰਭੰ।","roman":"Barant achhrano bhatan prabeen cheen suprabhan |","meaning_en":"Apsaras choose warriors, the skilled, discerning and splendid.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਪੱਛਰਾਵਾਂ ਸਿਆਣੇ, ਸੁੰਦਰ ਤੇ ਸ਼ਾਨਦਾਰ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਚੁਣਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਕੰਤ ਡਉਰ ਡਾਮਰੀ ਅਨੰਤ ਤੰਤ੍ਰਣੋ ਰਿਸੰ।","roman":"Bakant daur daamree anant tantrano risan |","meaning_en":"The damru resounds; there is endless tantric wrath;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਡਾਮਰੀ / ਤੰਤ੍ਰਣੋ ਰਿਸੰ: uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਡਮਰੂ ਵੱਜਦਾ ਹੈ, ਅਨੰਤ ਤੰਤਰ-ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਹੈ;","note_pa":"ਡਾਮਰੀ ਅਤੇ ਤੰਤ੍ਰਣੋ ਰਿਸੰ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸੰਤ ਜਛ ਗੰਧ੍ਰਬੰ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਭੂਤ ਪ੍ਰੇਤਨੰ। ੨੧੭।","roman":"Hasant jachh gandhraban pisaach bhoot pretnan | 217 |","meaning_en":"Yakshas, Gandharvas, goblins, ghosts and spirits laugh.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯਕਸ਼, ਗੰਧਰਵ, ਪਿਸ਼ਾਚ, ਭੂਤ ਅਤੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਹੱਸਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[218],"number_text":"੨੧੮।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਰੰਤ ਚੁਚ ਚਾਵਡੀ ਭਛੰਤ ਫਿਕ੍ਰਣੀ ਤਨੰ।","roman":"Bharant chuch chaavdee bhachhant phikranee tanan |","meaning_en":"Chamunda-like vultures fill their beaks, jackals eat the bodies;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਾਵਡੀ: read as 'vulture' or 'Chamunda'; ਫਿਕ੍ਰਣੀ: 'she-jackal'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਮੁੰਡਾ ਵਰਗੀਆਂ ਗਿਰਝਾਂ ਚੁੰਝਾਂ ਭਰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਮਾਦਾ ਗਿੱਦੜ ਲਾਸ਼ਾਂ ਖਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਚਾਵਡੀ: 'ਗਿਰਝ' ਜਾਂ 'ਚਾਮੁੰਡਾ'; ਫਿਕ੍ਰਣੀ: 'ਮਾਦਾ ਗਿੱਦੜ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਕੰਤ ਡਾਕਣੀ ਡੁਲੰ ਭਰੰਤ ਪਤ੍ਰ ਸ੍ਰੋਣਤੰ।","roman":"Dakant daaknee dulan bharant patr srontan |","meaning_en":"Dakinis shriek and roam, filling their bowls with blood;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਡਾਕਣੀਆਂ ਚੀਕਦੀਆਂ ਤੇ ਘੁੰਮਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਭਾਂਡੇ ਲਹੂ ਨਾਲ ਭਰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਿਪੰਤ ਯਾਸਵੰ ਸੁਭੰ ਹਸੰਤ ਮਾਰਜਨੀ ਮ੍ਰਿੜੰ।","roman":"Pipant yaasvan subhan hasant maarajnee mriran |","meaning_en":"they drink the fine liquor (of blood); Margani and Mrirani laugh;","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਾਰਜਨੀ ਮ੍ਰਿੜੰ: uncertain; read as names/forms of the Goddess or spirits.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸ਼ਰਾਬ ਪੀਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਮਾਰਜਨੀ ਤੇ ਮ੍ਰਿੜੀ ਹੱਸਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਮਾਰਜਨੀ ਮ੍ਰਿੜੰ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ; ਦੇਵੀ ਜਾਂ ਆਤਮਾਵਾਂ ਦੇ ਨਾਂ ਜਾਂ ਰੂਪ ਹੋ ਸਕਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਟੁਟ ਹਾਸਣੋ ਹਸੰ ਖਿਮੰਤ ਉਜਲੋ ਅਸੰ। ੨੧੮।","roman":"Atut haasno hasan khimant ujlo asan | 218 |","meaning_en":"with unbroken laughter they laugh; the bright swords flash.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੇਅੰਤ ਹਾਸਾ ਹੱਸਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਚਮਕਦੀਆਂ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਲਿਸ਼ਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅਕਵਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਅਕਵਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Akvaa chhand","meaning_en":"Akva metre.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਕਵਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[219],"number_text":"੨੧੯।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਟੇ ਵੀਰੰ। ਛੁਟੇ ਤੀਰੰ। ਜੁਝੇ ਤਾਜੀ। ਡਿਗੇ ਗਾਜੀ। ੨੧੯।","roman":"Jute veeran | chhute teeran | jujhe taajee | dige gaajee | 219 |","meaning_en":"Heroes close in, arrows fly; Arab horses fight, warriors fall.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੀਰ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ; ਘੋੜੇ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[220],"number_text":"੨੨੦।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੇ ਜੁਆਣੰ। ਬਾਹੇ ਬਾਣੰ। ਰੁਝੇ ਜੰਗੰ। ਜੁਝੇ ਅੰਗੰ। ੨੨੦।","roman":"Baje juaanan | baahe baanan | rujhe jangan | jujhe angan | 220 |","meaning_en":"Young warriors strike, arrows are shot; they are engaged in battle, limbs struggle.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਵਾਨ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਬਾਣ ਚਲਾਏ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ; ਲੜਾਈ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੁੱਝੇ ਹੋਏ ਹਨ, ਅੰਗ ਸੰਘਰਸ਼ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[221],"number_text":"੨੨੧।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਟੇ ਤੰਗੰ। ਫੁਟੇ ਅੰਗੰ। ਸਜੇ ਸੂਰੰ। ਘੁੰਮੀ ਹੂਰੰ। ੨੨੧।","roman":"Tute tangan | phute angan | saje sooran | ghunmee hooran | 221 |","meaning_en":"Girths break, limbs burst; warriors are adorned, heavenly nymphs roam about.","page":746,"flags":[{"code":"ੁ+ੂ","reason":"overlapping ੁ and ੂ drawn as one ੂ"}],"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪੇਟੀਆਂ ਟੁੱਟਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਅੰਗ ਫੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ; ਸੂਰਮੇ ਸਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹੂਰਾਂ ਘੁੰਮਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[222],"number_text":"੨੨੨।","page":746,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਝੇ ਹਾਥੀ। ਰੁਝੇ ਸਾਥੀ। ਉਭੇ ਉਸਟੰ। ਸੁਭੇ ਪੁਸਟੰ। ੨੨੨।","roman":"Jujhe haathee | rujhe saathee | ubhe ustan | subhe pustan | 222 |","meaning_en":"Elephants fight, companions are engaged; camels stand up, sturdy and splendid.","page":746,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਾਥੀ ਰੁੱਝੇ ਹਨ; ਊਠ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤਕੜੇ ਤੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[223],"number_text":"੨੨੩।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫੁਟੇ ਬੀਰੰ। ਛੁਟੇ ਤੀਰੰ। ਡਿਗੇ ਭੂਮੰ। ਉਠੇ ਘੂਮੰ। ੨੨੩।","roman":"Phute beeran | chhute teeran | dige bhooman | uthe ghooman | 223 |","meaning_en":"Heroes are broken, arrows fly; they fall to the ground and rise up reeling.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਫੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੀਰ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ; ਉਹ ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਚੱਕਰ ਖਾ ਕੇ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[224],"number_text":"੨੨੪।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਕੈ ਮਾਰੰ। ਚਕੈ ਚਾਰੰ। ਸਜੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰੰ। ਬਜੈ ਅਸਤ੍ਰੰ। ੨੨੪।","roman":"Bakai maaran | chakai chaaran | sajai sastran | bajai astran | 224 |","meaning_en":"They cry 'kill!', all four directions are startled; weapons are adorned, arms clash.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਚਾਰੇ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਹੈਰਾਨ ਹੁੰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਹਥਿਆਰ ਸਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਖੜਕਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚਾਚਰੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਚਾਚਰੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Chaachree chhand","meaning_en":"Chachari metre.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਚਰੀ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[225],"number_text":"੨੨੫।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੁਝਾਰੇ। ਅਪਾਰੇ। ਨਿਹਾਰੇ। ਬਿਚਾਰੇ। ੨੨੫।","roman":"Jujhaare | apaare | nihaare | bichaare | 225 |","meaning_en":"Countless warriors were seen and considered.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਯੋਧੇ ਵੇਖੇ ਗਏ ਤੇ ਵਿਚਾਰੇ ਗਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[226],"number_text":"੨੨੬।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਕਾਰੈ। ਪਚਾਰੈ। ਬਿਚਾਰੈ। ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰੈ। ੨੨੬।","roman":"Hakaarai | pachaarai | bichaarai | prahaarai | 226 |","meaning_en":"They shout, they challenge, they consider, they strike.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵੰਗਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਲਲਕਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਵਿਚਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[227],"number_text":"੨੨੭।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਤਾਜੀ। ਸਿਰਾਜੀ। ਸਲਾਜੀ। ਬਿਰਾਜੀ। ੨੨੭।","roman":"Su taajee | siraajee | salaajee | biraajee | 227 |","meaning_en":"Arab horses from Shiraz, well-formed, look splendid.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿਰਾਜੀ: 'from Shiraz'; ਸਲਾਜੀ: uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸਿਰਾਜ ਦੇ ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ, ਸੁੰਦਰ ਬਣਤਰ ਵਾਲੇ, ਸ਼ਾਨ ਨਾਲ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਸਿਰਾਜੀ: 'ਸ਼ਿਰਾਜ ਦੇ'; ਸਲਾਜੀ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[228],"number_text":"੨੨੮।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠਾਵੈ। ਦਿਖਾਵੈ। ਭ੍ਰਮਾਵੈ। ਚਖਾਵੈ। ੨੨੮।","roman":"Uthaavai | dikhaavai | bhramaavai | chakhaavai | 228 |","meaning_en":"They raise (their weapons), display them, whirl them, and make (the foe) taste them.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ (ਹਥਿਆਰ) ਚੁੱਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਵਿਖਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਘੁਮਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ (ਦੁਸ਼ਮਣ ਨੂੰ) ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦਾ ਸਵਾਦ ਚਖਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Kripaan krit chhand","meaning_en":"Kripan Krit metre.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[229],"number_text":"੨੨੯।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਾ ਤੀਰ ਛੁਟਤ। ਰਣੰਧੀਰ ਜੁਟਤ।","roman":"Jahaa teer chhutat | ranandheer jutat |","meaning_en":"Where arrows fly, the steadfast in battle close in;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਥੇ ਤੀਰ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਰਣ ਦੇ ਅਡੋਲ ਯੋਧੇ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰੰਬੀਰ ਉਠਤ। ਤਨੰ ਤ੍ਰਾਨ ਫੁਟਤ। ੨੨੯।","roman":"Baranbeer uthat | tanan traan phutat | 229 |","meaning_en":"great heroes rise; armour on bodies bursts.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੱਡੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ; ਸਰੀਰਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਬਸਤਰ ਫਟਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[230],"number_text":"੨੩੦।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣੰ ਬੀਰ ਗਿਰਤ। ਭਵੰ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਤਰਤ।","roman":"Ranan beer girat | bhavan sindhu tarat |","meaning_en":"Heroes fall in battle and cross the ocean of the world;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ ਭਵਸਾਗਰ ਪਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਭੰ ਹੂਰ ਫਿਰਤ। ਬਰੰ ਬੀਰ ਬਰਤ। ੨੩੦।","roman":"Nabhan hoor phirat | baran beer barat | 230 |","meaning_en":"nymphs roam the sky, choosing the great heroes.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਸਮਾਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੂਰਾਂ ਘੁੰਮਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਵੱਡੇ ਸੂਰਮਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਚੁਣਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[231],"number_text":"੨੩੧।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਨਾਦ ਬਜਤ। ਸੁਣਿ ਭੀਰ ਭਜਤ।","roman":"Ran naad bajat | suni bheer bhajat |","meaning_en":"Battle-sounds ring out; hearing them, cowards flee;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਦੇ ਵਾਜੇ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ; ਇਹ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਭੂਮਿ ਤਜਤ। ਮਨ ਮਾਝ ਲਜਤ। ੨੩੧।","roman":"Ran bhoomi tajat | man maajh lajat | 231 |","meaning_en":"they leave the battlefield, ashamed in their minds.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਛੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ, ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[232],"number_text":"੨੩੨।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰਿ ਫੇਰਿ ਲਰਤ। ਰਣ ਜੁਝਿ ਮਰਤ।","roman":"Phiri pheri larat | ran jujhi marat |","meaning_en":"Again and again they fight; they die fighting in battle;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵਾਰ-ਵਾਰ ਉਹ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ; ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਜੂਝ ਕੇ ਮਰਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹਿ ਪਾਵ ਟਰਤ। ਭਵ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਤਰਤ। ੨੩੨।","roman":"Nahi paav tarat | bhav sindhu tarat | 232 |","meaning_en":"they do not step back, and cross the ocean of the world.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪੈਰ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਹਟਾਉਂਦੇ, ਅਤੇ ਭਵਸਾਗਰ ਪਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[233],"number_text":"੨੩੩।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਰੰਗਿ ਮਚਤ। ਚਤੁਰੰਗ ਫਟਤ।","roman":"Ran rangi machat | chaturang phatat |","meaning_en":"The battle rages in its fervour; the fourfold army is torn apart;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਜੋਸ਼ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਚਦਾ ਹੈ; ਚਤੁਰੰਗ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਟੁੱਟ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਬੰਗ ਲਟਤ। ਮਨਿ ਮਾਨ ਘਟਤ। ੨੩੩।","roman":"Sarbang latat | mani maan ghatat | 233 |","meaning_en":"all limbs are plundered; pride in the mind decreases.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲਟਤ: read as 'are wounded / plundered'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਅੰਗ ਲੁੱਟੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ; ਮਨ ਦਾ ਮਾਣ ਘਟਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਲਟਤ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ; 'ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮੀ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ' ਜਾਂ 'ਲੁੱਟੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[234],"number_text":"੨੩੪।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰ ਬੀਰ ਭਿਰਤ। ਨਹੀ ਨੈਕੁ ਫਿਰਤ।","roman":"Bar beer bhirat | nahee naiku phirat |","meaning_en":"Great heroes clash and do not turn back at all;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੱਡੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਟਕਰਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ ਜ਼ਰਾ ਵੀ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਹਟਦੇ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਚਿਤ ਚਿਰਤ। ਉਠਿ ਸੈਨ ਘਿਰਤ। ੨੩੪।","roman":"Jab chit chirat | uthi sain ghirat | 234 |","meaning_en":"when their minds are angered, they rise and surround the army.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦੋਂ ਮਨ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਉਹ ਉੱਠ ਕੇ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਨੂੰ ਘੇਰ ਲੈਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[235],"number_text":"੨੩੫।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰ ਭੂਮਿ ਪਰਤ। ਸੁਰ ਨਾਰਿ ਬਰਤ।","roman":"Gir bhoomi parat | sur naari barat |","meaning_en":"They fall to the ground; the women of the gods choose them;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ; ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਚੁਣਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਪਾਵ ਟਰਤ। ਮਨਿ ਕੋਪ ਭਰਤ। ੨੩੫।","roman":"Nahee paav tarat | mani kop bharat | 235 |","meaning_en":"they do not step back; their minds fill with wrath.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪੈਰ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਹਟਾਉਂਦੇ; ਮਨ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਭਰ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[236],"number_text":"੨੩੬।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰ ਕੋਪ ਮੰਡਤ। ਪਗ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਨ ਭਜਤ।","roman":"Kar kop mandat | pag dvai na bhajat |","meaning_en":"In wrath they set to (battle), and do not run two steps;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਜੰਗ ਦੀ ਤਿਆਰੀ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਦੋ ਕਦਮ ਵੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਭੱਜਦੇ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਰੋਸ ਲਰਤ। ਗਿਰ ਭੂਮਿ ਪਰਤ। ੨੩੬।","roman":"Kari ros larat | gir bhoomi parat | 236 |","meaning_en":"in rage they fight, and fall to the ground.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰੋਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[237],"number_text":"੨੩੭।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਨਾਦ ਬਜਤ। ਸੁਣਿ ਮੇਘ ਲਜਤ।","roman":"Ran naad bajat | suni megh lajat |","meaning_en":"Battle-sounds ring out; hearing them, the clouds are ashamed;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਦੇ ਵਾਜੇ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ; ਇਹ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਬੱਦਲ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭ ਸਾਜ ਸਜਤ। ਪਗ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਨ ਭਜਤ। ੨੩੭।","roman":"Sabh saaj sajat | pag dvai na bhajat | 237 |","meaning_en":"all are equipped with their gear, and do not run two steps.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਸਾਜ਼-ਸਾਮਾਨ ਨਾਲ ਲੈਸ ਹਨ, ਤੇ ਦੋ ਕਦਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਭੱਜਦੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[238],"number_text":"੨੩੮।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਚਕ੍ਰ ਚਲਤ। ਦੁਤਿ ਮਾਨ ਦਲਤ।","roman":"Rani chakr chalat | duti maan dalat |","meaning_en":"Discuses fly in battle, crushing the pride of splendour;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਚੱਕਰ ਚਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸ਼ਾਨ ਦਾ ਮਾਣ ਦਲਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰਿ ਮੇਰੁ ਹਲਤ। ਭਟ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ ਪਲਤ। ੨੩੮।","roman":"Giri meru halat | bhat sron palat | 238 |","meaning_en":"Mount Meru shakes; warriors are drenched in blood.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਲਤ: read as 'soaked'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੁਮੇਰ ਪਰਬਤ ਹਿੱਲਦਾ ਹੈ; ਸੂਰਮੇ ਲਹੂ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਿੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਪਲਤ: 'ਭਿੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[239],"number_text":"੨੩੯।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਰੰਗਿ ਮਚਤ। ਬਰ ਬੰਬ ਬਜਤ।","roman":"Ran rangi machat | bar banb bajat |","meaning_en":"The battle rages in its fervour; great drums beat;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਜੋਸ਼ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਚਦਾ ਹੈ; ਵੱਡੇ ਢੋਲ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਖੰਭ ਗਡਤਿ। ਅਸਿਵਾਰ ਮੰਡਤ। ੨੩੯।","roman":"Ran khanbh gadti | asivaar mandat | 239 |","meaning_en":"battle-posts are planted firm; horsemen take their stand.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਣ ਖੰਭ ਗਡਤਿ: warriors standing firm like planted pillars; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਖੰਭੇ ਗੱਡੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ; ਘੋੜ-ਸਵਾਰ ਆਪਣੀ ਥਾਂ ਲੈਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਰਣ ਖੰਭ ਗਡਤਿ: ਯੋਧੇ ਗੱਡੇ ਹੋਏ ਥੰਮ੍ਹਾਂ ਵਾਂਗ ਅਡੋਲ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹਨ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[240],"number_text":"੨੪੦।","page":747,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕਿਰਤ। ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਭਿਰਤ।","roman":"Kripaan kirat | kari kop bhirat |","meaning_en":"Swords cut; in wrath they clash;","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਿਰਤ: read as 'cut / scatter'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਵੱਢਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਟਕਰਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਕਿਰਤ: 'ਵੱਢਣਾ ਜਾਂ ਖਿੰਡਾਉਣਾ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਹੀ ਫਿਰੈ ਫਿਰਤ। ਅਤਿ ਚਿਤ ਚਿਰਤ। ੨੪੦।","roman":"Nahee phirai phirat | ati chit chirat | 240 |","meaning_en":"they do not turn back, their minds greatly angered.","page":747,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੁੜਦੇ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੇ ਮਨ ਬਹੁਤ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚਾਚਰੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਚਾਚਰੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Chaachree chhand","meaning_en":"Chachari metre.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਚਰੀ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[241],"number_text":"੨੪੧।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਕਾਰੈ। ਪ੍ਰਚਾਰੈ। ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰੈ। ਕਰਵਾਰੈ। ੨੪੧।","roman":"Hakaarai | prachaarai | prahaarai | karvaarai | 241 |","meaning_en":"They shout, they challenge, they strike with swords.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰਵਾਰੈ: read as 'karvaar', sword.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵੰਗਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪ੍ਰਚਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਚਲਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਕਰਵਾਰੈ: 'ਕਰਵਾਰ' ਭਾਵ ਤਲਵਾਰ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[242],"number_text":"੨੪੨।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠਾਵੈ। ਦਿਖਾਵੈ। ਭ੍ਰਮਾਵੈ। ਚਲਾਵੈ। ੨੪੨।","roman":"Uthaavai | dikhaavai | bhramaavai | chalaavai | 242 |","meaning_en":"They raise (their weapons), display them, whirl them, and wield them.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ (ਹਥਿਆਰ) ਚੁੱਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਵਿਖਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਘੁਮਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ ਚਲਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[243],"number_text":"੨੪੩।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਧਾਵੈ। ਰਿਸਾਵੈ। ਉਠਾਵੈ। ਚਖਾਵੈ। ੨੪੩।","roman":"Su dhaavai | risaavai | uthaavai | chakhaavai | 243 |","meaning_en":"They charge, grow angry, raise (their weapons), and make (the foe) taste them.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਾਵਾ ਬੋਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਰੋਹ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, (ਹਥਿਆਰ) ਚੁੱਕਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ (ਦੁਸ਼ਮਣ ਨੂੰ) ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦਾ ਸਵਾਦ ਚਖਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[244],"number_text":"੨੪੪।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਝੁਝਾਰੇ। ਅਪਾਰੇ। ਹਜਾਰੇ। ਅਰਿਆਰੇ। ੨੪੪।","roman":"Jhujhaare | apaare | hajaare | ariaare | 244 |","meaning_en":"Warriors without number, thousands of them, unyielding.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਰਿਆਰੇ: read as 'stubborn, unyielding'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਯੋਧੇ, ਹਜ਼ਾਰਾਂ, ਅਡੋਲ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਅਰਿਆਰੇ: 'ਅੜਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ, ਨਾ ਝੁਕਣ ਵਾਲਾ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[245],"number_text":"੨੪੫।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਢੂਕੇ। ਕਿ ਕੂਕੇ। ਭਭੂਕੇ। ਕਿ ਝੂਕੇ। ੨੪੫।","roman":"Su dhooke | ki kooke | bhabhooke | ki jhooke | 245 |","meaning_en":"They close in, they shout, they blaze up, they lunge.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Short sound-like verbs; sense given.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਨੇੜੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਚੀਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਭੜਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਝੁਕਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਛੋਟੇ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਰਗੇ ਕਿਰਿਆ-ਸ਼ਬਦ; ਅਰਥ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[246],"number_text":"੨੪੬।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਬਾਣੰ। ਸੁਧਾਣੰ। ਅਚਾਣੰ। ਜੁਆਣੰ। ੨੪੬।","roman":"Su baanan | sudhaanan | achaanan | juaanan | 246 |","meaning_en":"Fine arrows, well aimed, suddenly (strike) the young warriors.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਧਾਣੰ / ਅਚਾਣੰ: uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੋਹਣੇ ਤੀਰ, ਚੰਗੀ ਨਿਸ਼ਾਨੇਬਾਜ਼ੀ ਨਾਲ, ਅਚਾਨਕ ਜਵਾਨ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਲੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਸੁਧਾਣੰ ਅਤੇ ਅਚਾਣੰ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[247],"number_text":"੨੪੭।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਮਕੇ। ਹਮਕੇ। ਝੜਕੇ। ਛਟਕੇ। ੨੪੭।","roman":"Dhamke | hamke | jharke | chhatke | 247 |","meaning_en":"They thud, they roar, they lash out, they spring away.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words; sense given.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਮਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹੂੰਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਝਪਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉਛਲ ਕੇ ਦੂਰ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਾਲੇ ਸ਼ਬਦ; ਅਰਥ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[248],"number_text":"੨੪੮।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਗਾਜੈ। ਸਸਾਜੈ। ਨ ਭਾਜੈ। ਬਿਰਾਜੈ। ੨੪੮।","roman":"Sagaajai | sasaajai | na bhaajai | biraajai | 248 |","meaning_en":"They thunder, they are well armed, they do not flee, they look splendid.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤਿਆਰ-ਬਰ-ਤਿਆਰ ਹਨ, ਭੱਜਦੇ ਨਹੀਂ, ਸ਼ਾਨ ਨਾਲ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[249],"number_text":"੨੪੯।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਖੰਗੀ। ਖਤੰਗੀ। ਸੁਰੰਗੀ। ਭਿੜੰਗੀ। ੨੪੯।","roman":"Nikhangee | khatangee | surangee | bhirangee | 249 |","meaning_en":"Bearers of quivers and arrows, finely coloured, combative.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਰਕਸਾਂ ਤੇ ਤੀਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਧਾਰਕ, ਸੋਹਣੇ ਰੰਗਾਂ ਵਾਲੇ, ਲੜਨ ਲਈ ਤਿਆਰ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[250],"number_text":"੨੫੦।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਮਕੈ। ਪਲਕੈ। ਹਸਕੈ। ਪ੍ਰਧਕੈ। ੨੫੦।","roman":"Tamkai | palkai | haskai | pradhkai | 250 |","meaning_en":"They flare up, flash in a moment, laugh, and blaze forth.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-like verbs; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਭੜਕ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਲਿਸ਼ਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹੱਸਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ ਅੱਗ ਵਾਂਗ ਭੜਕਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਰਗੇ ਕਿਰਿਆ-ਸ਼ਬਦ; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[251],"number_text":"੨੫੧।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਬੀਰੰ। ਸੁ ਧੀਰੰ। ਪ੍ਰਹੀਰੰ। ਤਤੀਰੰ। ੨੫੧।","roman":"Su beeran | su dheeran | praheeran | tateeran | 251 |","meaning_en":"Brave heroes, steadfast, strike with arrows.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪ੍ਰਹੀਰੰ। ਤਤੀਰੰ: uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਬੀਰ, ਅਡੋਲ ਤੇ ਧੀਰਜ ਵਾਲੇ, ਤੀਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਪ੍ਰਹੀਰੰ ਅਤੇ ਤਤੀਰੰ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[252],"number_text":"੨੫੨।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਲਟੈ। ਬਿਲਟੈ। ਨ ਛੁਟੈ। ਉਪਟੈ। ੨੫੨।","roman":"Paltai | biltai | na chhutai | uptai | 252 |","meaning_en":"They turn back, they writhe, they do not give way, they rise up.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਮੁੜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੜਫਦੇ ਹਨ, ਰਾਹ ਨਹੀਂ ਛੱਡਦੇ, ਉੱਪਰ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[253],"number_text":"੨੫੩।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਬਕੈ। ਨ ਥਕੈ। ਧਸਕੈ। ਝਝਕੈ। ੨੫੩।","roman":"Babkai | na thakai | dhaskai | jhajhkai | 253 |","meaning_en":"They roar, they do not tire, they press in, they flinch.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਦਹਾੜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਥੱਕਦੇ ਨਹੀਂ, ਦਬਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਝਿਜਕਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[254],"number_text":"੨੫੪।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਖਗੰ। ਅਦਗੰ। ਅਜਗੰ। ਅਭਗੰ। ੨੫੪।","roman":"Sakhgan | adgan | ajgan | abhgan | 254 |","meaning_en":"Sword-bearers, unburnt, unconquered, unbroken.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਦਗੰ: read as 'unmarked/unscathed'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰ ਵਾਲੇ, ਬੇਦਾਗ਼, ਅਜਿੱਤੇ ਤੇ ਅਟੁੱਟ।","note_pa":"ਅਦਗੰ: 'ਬਿਨਾਂ ਸੜੇ ਜਾਂ ਬਿਨਾਂ ਦਾਗ਼ ਵਾਲੇ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[255],"number_text":"੨੫੫।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਝਮਕੈ। ਖਿਮਕੈ। ਬਬਕੈ। ਉਥਕੈ। ੨੫੫।","roman":"Jhamkai | khimkai | babkai | uthkai | 255 |","meaning_en":"They flash, they gleam, they roar, they leap up.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-like verbs.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਝਲਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਚਮਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਦਹਾੜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉਛਲ ਕੇ ਉੱਪਰ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਰਗੇ ਕਿਰਿਆ-ਸ਼ਬਦ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭਗਉਤੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭਗਉਤੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhagautee chhand","meaning_en":"Bhagauti metre.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਗਉਤੀ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[256],"number_text":"੨੫੬।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਜੁਟੈਤ ਬੀਰੰ। ਕਿ ਛੁਟੈਤ ਤੀਰੰ।","roman":"Ki jutait beeran | ki chhutait teeran |","meaning_en":"Heroes close in, arrows fly,","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The repeated 'ਕਿ' here marks rhythm; left untranslated.","meaning_pa":"ਬਹਾਦਰ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੀਰ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ,","note_pa":"ਇੱਥੇ ਵਾਰ-ਵਾਰ ਆਉਂਦਾ 'ਕਿ' ਤਾਲ ਦਾ ਚਿੰਨ੍ਹ ਹੈ; ਇਸ ਦਾ ਅਨੁਵਾਦ ਨਹੀਂ ਕੀਤਾ ਗਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਫੁਟੈਤ ਅੰਗੰ। ਕਿ ਜੁਟੈਤ ਜੰਗੰ। ੨੫੬।","roman":"Ki phutait angan | ki jutait jangan | 256 |","meaning_en":"limbs burst, combat is joined.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਫੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜੰਗ ਜੁੱਟ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[257],"number_text":"੨੫੭।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਮਚੈਤ ਸੂਰੰ। ਕਿ ਘੁਮੈਤ ਹੂਰੰ।","roman":"Ki machait sooran | ki ghumait hooran |","meaning_en":"Warriors rage, nymphs roam,","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਜੋਸ਼ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਚਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹੂਰਾਂ ਘੁੰਮਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਬਜੈਤ ਖਗੰ। ਕਿ ਉਠੈਤ ਅਗੰ। ੨੫੭।","roman":"Ki bajait khagan | ki uthait agan | 257 |","meaning_en":"swords clang, fire rises.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਖੜਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਅੱਗ ਉੱਠਦੀ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[258],"number_text":"੨੫੮।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਫੁਟੇਤਿ ਅੰਗੰ। ਕਿ ਰੁਝੇਤਿ ਜੰਗੰ।","roman":"Ki phuteti angan | ki rujheti jangan |","meaning_en":"Limbs burst, all are engaged in battle,","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਫੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਾਰੇ ਜੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੁੱਝੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਨਚੇਤਿ ਤਾਜੀ। ਕਿ ਗਜੇਤਿ ਗਾਜੀ। ੨੫੮।","roman":"Ki nacheti taajee | ki gajeti gaajee | 258 |","meaning_en":"Arab horses dance, warriors roar.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[259],"number_text":"੨੫੯।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਘਲੈਤਿ ਘਾਯੰ। ਕਿ ਝਲੇਤਿ ਚਾਯੰ।","roman":"Ki ghalaiti ghaayan | ki jhaleti chaayan |","meaning_en":"They deal wounds and bear them eagerly,","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਦਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ ਚਾਅ ਨਾਲ ਸਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਡਿਗੈਤਿ ਧੁਮੀ। ਕਿ ਝੁਮੈਤਿ ਝੁਮੀ। ੨੫੯।","roman":"Ki digaiti dhumee | ki jhumaiti jhumee | 259 |","meaning_en":"they fall in a swirl, they sway and reel.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧੁਮੀ: read as 'dizzy / in smoke'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਚੱਕਰ ਖਾ ਕੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਝੂਮਦੇ ਤੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਧੁਮੀ: 'ਚੱਕਰ ਜਾਂ ਧੂੰਏਂ ਵਿੱਚ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[260],"number_text":"੨੬੦।","page":748,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਛਡੈਤਿ ਹੂਹੰ। ਕਿ ਸੁਭੇਤਿ ਬ੍ਯੂਹੰ।","roman":"Ki chhadaiti hoohan | ki subheti byoohan |","meaning_en":"They raise war-cries, the battle-arrays look splendid,","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਹੋਕੇ ਲਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੁੱਧ-ਕਤਾਰਾਂ ਸੋਹਣੀਆਂ ਲੱਗਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਡਿਗੈਤਿ ਚੇਤੰ। ਕਿ ਨਚੇਤਿ ਪ੍ਰੇਤੰ। ੨੬੦।","roman":"Ki digaiti chetan | ki nacheti pretan | 260 |","meaning_en":"they fall senseless, ghosts dance.","page":748,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬੇਸੁੱਧ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[261],"number_text":"੨੬੧।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਬੁਠੇਤਿ ਬਾਣੰ। ਕਿ ਜੁਝੇਤਿ ਜੁਆਣੰ।","roman":"Ki butheti baanan | ki jujheti juaanan |","meaning_en":"Arrows rain down, young warriors fight,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਵਰ੍ਹਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਵਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਮਥੇਤਿ ਨੂਰੰ। ਕਿ ਤਕੇਤਿ ਹੂਰੰ। ੨੬੧।","roman":"Ki matheti nooran | ki taketi hooran | 261 |","meaning_en":"brows shine with radiance, nymphs gaze at them.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਥੇਤਿ ਨੂਰੰ: read as 'radiance on their foreheads'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਮੱਥੇ ਨੂਰ ਨਾਲ ਚਮਕਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਪੱਛਰਾਵਾਂ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਵੱਲ ਤੱਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਮਥੇਤਿ ਨੂਰੰ: 'ਮੱਥਿਆਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਨੂਰ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[262],"number_text":"੨੬੨।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਜੁਜੇਤਿ ਹਾਥੀ। ਕਿ ਸਿਝੇਤਿ ਸਾਥੀ।","roman":"Ki jujeti haathee | ki sijheti saathee |","meaning_en":"Elephants are yoked (in battle), companions are slain,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿਝੇਤਿ: read as 'attain (heaven) / are accomplished'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀ ਜੋੜੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਾਥੀ ਮਾਰੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ,","note_pa":"ਸਿਝੇਤਿ: 'ਮੁਕਤੀ ਪਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਜਾਂ ਸਫ਼ਲ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਭਗੇਤਿ ਵੀਰੰ। ਕਿ ਲਗੇਤਿ ਤੀਰੰ। ੨੬੨।","roman":"Ki bhageti veeran | ki lageti teeran | 262 |","meaning_en":"heroes flee, arrows strike.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੀਰ ਲੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[263],"number_text":"੨੬੩।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਰਜੇਤਿ ਰੋਸੰ। ਕਿ ਤਜੇਤਿ ਹੋਸੰ।","roman":"Ki rajeti rosan | ki tajeti hosan |","meaning_en":"They are filled with rage, they lose their senses,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਰੋਸ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੇ ਹਨ, ਹੋਸ਼ ਗੁਆ ਬੈਠਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਖੁਲੇਤਿ ਕੇਸੰ। ਕਿ ਡੁਲੇਤਿ ਭੇਸੰ। ੨੬੩।","roman":"Ki khuleti kesan | ki duleti bhesan | 263 |","meaning_en":"their hair comes loose, their dress is disordered.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵਾਲ ਖੁੱਲ੍ਹ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪਹਿਰਾਵਾ ਵਿਗੜ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[264],"number_text":"੨੬੪।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਜੁਝੇਤਿ ਹਾਥੀ। ਕਿ ਲੁਝੇਤਿ ਸਾਥੀ।","roman":"Ki jujheti haathee | ki lujheti saathee |","meaning_en":"Elephants fight, companions grapple,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਾਥੀ ਗੁੱਥਮ-ਗੁੱਥਾ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਛੁਟੇਤਿ ਤਾਜੀ। ਕਿ ਗਜੇਤਿ ਗਾਜੀ। ੨੬੪।","roman":"Ki chhuteti taajee | ki gajeti gaajee | 264 |","meaning_en":"Arab horses run loose, warriors roar.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਖੁੱਲ੍ਹੇ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[265],"number_text":"੨੬੫।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਘੁਮੀਤਿ ਹੂਰੰ। ਕਿ ਭੁੰਮੀਤਿ ਪੂਰੰ।","roman":"Ki ghumeeti hooran | ki bhunmeeti pooran |","meaning_en":"Nymphs roam, the earth is filled,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੂਰਾਂ ਘੁੰਮਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਧਰਤੀ ਭਰ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਜੁਝੇਤਿ ਵੀਰੰ। ਕਿ ਲਗੇਤਿ ਤੀਰੰ। ੨੬੫।","roman":"Ki jujheti veeran | ki lageti teeran | 265 |","meaning_en":"heroes fight, arrows strike.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੀਰ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੀਰ ਲੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[266],"number_text":"੨੬੬।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਚਲੈਤਿ ਬਾਣੰ। ਕਿ ਰੁਕੀ ਦਿਸਾਣੰ।","roman":"Ki chalaiti baanan | ki rukee disaanan |","meaning_en":"Arrows fly, the directions are blocked,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਚੱਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਰੁਕ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਝਮਕੈਤਿ ਤੇਗੰ। ਕਿ ਨਭਿ ਜਾਨ ਬੇਗੰ। ੨੬੬।","roman":"Ki jhamkaiti tegan | ki nabhi jaan began | 266 |","meaning_en":"swords flash, like swift lightning in the sky.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਝਲਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਅਸਮਾਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਤੇਜ਼ ਬਿਜਲੀ ਵਾਂਗ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[267],"number_text":"੨੬੭।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਛੁਟੇਤਿ ਗੋਰੰ। ਕਿ ਬੁਠੇਤਿ ਓਰੰ।","roman":"Ki chhuteti goran | ki butheti oran |","meaning_en":"Shots are fired, hail rains down,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗੋਰੰ: read as 'shot / balls'; ਓਰੰ: read as 'hail (ole)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਗੋਲੀਆਂ ਛੁੱਟਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਓਲੇ ਵਰ੍ਹਦੇ ਹਨ,","note_pa":"ਗੋਰੰ: 'ਗੋਲੀਆਂ'; ਓਰੰ: 'ਓਲੇ (ਗੜੇ)'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਗਜੈਤਿ ਗਾਜੀ। ਕਿ ਪੇਲੇਤਿ ਤਾਜੀ। ੨੬੭।","roman":"Ki gajaiti gaajee | ki peleti taajee | 267 |","meaning_en":"warriors roar, Arab horses are driven on.","page":749,"flags":[{"code":"space","reason":"word space printed as a gap (8.3pt), space inserted"}],"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਅੱਗੇ ਧੱਕੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[268],"number_text":"੨੬੮।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਕਟੇਤਿ ਅੰਗੰ। ਕਿ ਡਿਗੇਤਿ ਜੰਗੰ।","roman":"Ki kateti angan | ki digeti jangan |","meaning_en":"Limbs are cut, fighters fall,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਵੱਢੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਲੜਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਮਤੇਤਿ ਮਾਣੰ। ਕਿ ਲੁਝੇਤਿ ਜੁਆਣੰ। ੨੬੮।","roman":"Ki mateti maanan | ki lujheti juaanan | 268 |","meaning_en":"intoxicated with pride, young warriors grapple.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਣ ਨਾਲ ਮਸਤ ਹੋ ਕੇ, ਜਵਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ ਗੁੱਥਮ-ਗੁੱਥਾ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[269],"number_text":"੨੬੯।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਬਕੈਤਿ ਮਾਰੰ। ਕਿ ਚਕੈਤਿ ਚਾਰੰ।","roman":"Ki bakaiti maaran | ki chakaiti chaaran |","meaning_en":"They cry 'kill!', the four directions are startled,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਚਾਰੇ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਹੈਰਾਨ ਹੁੰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਢੁਕੈਤਿ ਢੀਠੰ। ਨ ਦੇਵੇਤਿ ਪੀਠੰ । ੨੬੯।","roman":"Ki dhukaiti dheethan | na deveti peethan | 269 |","meaning_en":"the stubborn close in and do not turn their backs.","page":749,"flags":[{"code":"space","reason":"word space printed as a gap (5.3pt), space inserted"}],"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਢੀਠ ਨੇੜੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਤੇ ਪਿੱਠ ਨਹੀਂ ਦਿਖਾਉਂਦੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[270],"number_text":"੨੭੦।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਘਲੇਤਿ ਸਾਂਗੰ। ਕਿ ਬੁਕੈਤਿ ਬਾਂਗੰ।","roman":"Ki ghaleti saangan | ki bukaiti baangan |","meaning_en":"They hurl lances, they bellow war-cries,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬਰਛੇ ਸੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਲਲਕਾਰੇ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਮੁਛੇਤਿ ਬੰਕੀ। ਕਿ ਹਠੇਤਿ ਹੰਕੀ। ੨੭੦।","roman":"Ki muchheti bankee | ki hatheti hankee | 270 |","meaning_en":"with curling moustaches, the stubborn challengers.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹੰਕੀ: read as 'those who shout / challenge'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਮਰੋੜੀਆਂ ਮੁੱਛਾਂ ਵਾਲੇ, ਹਠੀ ਵੰਗਾਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ।","note_pa":"ਹੰਕੀ: 'ਵੰਗਾਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[271],"number_text":"੨੭੧।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਬਜੇਤਿ ਢੋਲੰ। ਕਿ ਬਕੈਤਿ ਬੋਲੰ।","roman":"Ki bajeti dholan | ki bakaiti bolan |","meaning_en":"Drums beat, war-cries are raised,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਢੋਲ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਵੰਗਾਰਾਂ ਉੱਠਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਬਜੇ ਨਗਾਰੇ। ਕਿ ਜੁਟੇ ਹਠਿਆਰੇ। ੨੭੧।","roman":"Ki baje nagaare | ki jute hathiaare | 271 |","meaning_en":"kettle-drums sound, the stubborn close in.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੱਡੇ ਨਗਾਰੇ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹਠੀ ਯੋਧੇ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[272],"number_text":"੨੭੨।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਛਕੈਤਿ ਤਾਜੀ। ਹਮਕੈਤ ਗਾਜੀ।","roman":"Uchhkaiti taajee | hamkait gaajee |","meaning_en":"Arab horses leap, warriors roar,","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਉਛਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਯੋਧੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛੁਟਕੈਤ ਤੀਰੰ। ਭਟਕੈਤ ਭੀਰੰ। ੨੭੨।","roman":"Chhutkait teeran | bhatkait bheeran | 272 |","meaning_en":"arrows fly, cowards wander off.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭਟਕ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਭਵਾਨੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਭਵਾਨੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bhavaanee chhand","meaning_en":"Bhavani metre.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਵਾਨੀ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[273],"number_text":"੨੭੩।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਾ ਬੀਰ ਜੁਟੈ। ਸਬੈ ਠਾਟ ਠਟੈ।","roman":"Jahaa beer jutai | sabai thaat thatai |","meaning_en":"Where the heroes close in, all set out their array;","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਥੇ ਬਹਾਦਰ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉੱਥੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਆਪਣੀ ਕਤਾਰ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿ ਨੇਜੇ ਪਲਟੈ। ਚਮਤਕਾਰ ਛੁਟੈ। ੨੭੩।","roman":"Ki neje paltai | chamatkaar chhutai | 273 |","meaning_en":"spears are turned, and flashes burst forth.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨੇਜ਼ੇ ਘੁੰਮਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੇ ਚਮਕਾਰ ਫੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[274],"number_text":"੨੭੪।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਾ ਸਾਰ ਬਜੈ। ਤਹਾ ਬੀਰ ਗਜੈ।","roman":"Jahaa saar bajai | tahaa beer gajai |","meaning_en":"Where steel clashes, there heroes roar;","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਥੇ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਵੱਜਦੀ ਹੈ, ਉੱਥੇ ਵੀਰ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਿਲੈ ਸੰਜ ਸਜੈ। ਨ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਪੈਗ ਭਜੈ। ੨੭੪।","roman":"Milai sanj sajai | na dvai paig bhajai | 274 |","meaning_en":"they meet, armoured, and do not run two steps.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਮਿਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਬਸਤਰ ਪਹਿਨੇ ਹੋਏ, ਤੇ ਦੋ ਕਦਮ ਵੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਭੱਜਦੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[275],"number_text":"੨੭੫।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਭੂਰ ਭਾਜੈ। ਕਹੂੰ ਵੀਰ ਗਾਜੈ।","roman":"Kahoon bhoor bhaajai | kahoon veer gaajai |","meaning_en":"Somewhere cowards flee, somewhere heroes roar;","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭੂਰ: printed so; read as 'bheer', cowards.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਭੂਰ: ਛਪਿਆ ਰੂਪ ਇਸੇ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਹੈ; ਇਸ ਨੂੰ 'ਭੀਰ' (ਡਰਪੋਕ) ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਜੋਧ ਜੁਟੈ। ਕਹੂੰ ਟੋਪ ਟੁਟੈ। ੨੭੫।","roman":"Kahoon jodh jutai | kahoon top tutai | 275 |","meaning_en":"somewhere warriors close in, somewhere helmets break.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਟੋਪ ਟੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[276],"number_text":"੨੭੬।","page":749,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਹਾ ਜੋਧ ਜੁਟੈ। ਤਹਾ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਛੁਟੈ।","roman":"Jahaa jodh jutai | tahaa asatr chhutai |","meaning_en":"Where warriors close in, there weapons are loosed;","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਥੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਜੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉੱਥੇ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਛੁੱਟਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਭੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਕਟੈ। ਕਹੂੰ ਬੀਰ ਲੁਟੈ। ੨੭੬।","roman":"Nribhai sasatr katai | kahoon beer lutai | 276 |","meaning_en":"fearless, they cut with weapons; somewhere heroes roll.","page":749,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਿਡਰ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵੱਢਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਿਤੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਰੁਲਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[277],"number_text":"੨੭੭।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਬਕੈ। ਕਿਤੇ ਬਾਜ ਉਥਕੈ।","roman":"Kahoon maar bakai | kite baaj uthkai |","meaning_en":"Somewhere they cry 'kill!', somewhere horses leap up;","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਘੋੜੇ ਉਛਲਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਸੈਣ ਹਕੈ। ਕਿਤੇ ਦਾਵ ਤਕੈ। ੨੭੭।","roman":"Kite sain hakai | kite daav takai | 277 |","meaning_en":"somewhere armies are driven, somewhere they watch for an opening.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਲਲਕਾਰਿਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕਿਤੇ ਮੌਕੇ ਦੀ ਉਡੀਕ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[278],"number_text":"੨੭੮।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਘਾਇ ਮੇਲੈ। ਕਿਤੇ ਸੈਣ ਪੇਲੈ।","roman":"Kite ghaai melai | kite sain pelai |","meaning_en":"Somewhere they deal wounds, somewhere they push the army on;","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਦਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਨੂੰ ਅੱਗੇ ਧੱਕਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਤੇ ਭੂਮਿ ਡਿਗੇ। ਤਨੰ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ ਭਿਗੇ। ੨੭੮।","roman":"Kite bhoomi dige | tanan sron bhige | 278 |","meaning_en":"somewhere they fall to the ground, their bodies soaked in blood.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੇ ਸਰੀਰ ਲਹੂ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਿੱਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ"},{"type":"verse","number":[279],"number_text":"੨੭੯।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਬਿਧਿ ਮਚਾ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਰਣ ਅਰਧ ਮਹੂਰਤ ਉਦੰਡ।","roman":"Ih bidhi machaa prachand ran aradh mahoorat udand |","meaning_en":"In this way the fierce, mighty battle raged for half a muhurat,","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Muhurat: a period of about 48 minutes.","meaning_pa":"ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ ਤੇ ਵੱਡਾ ਰਣ ਅੱਧੇ ਮੁਹੂਰਤ ਤੱਕ ਮਚਿਆ ਰਿਹਾ,","note_pa":"ਮੁਹੂਰਤ: ਲਗਭਗ ਅਠਤਾਲੀ ਮਿੰਟ ਦਾ ਸਮਾਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਸ ਅਯੁਤ ਦਸ ਸਤ ਸੁਭਟ ਜੁਝਤ ਭਏ ਅਡੰਡ। ੨੭੯।","roman":"Bees ayut das sat subhat jujhat bhae adand | 279 |","meaning_en":"and twenty ayuts (two hundred thousand) and ten hundred great warriors, unpunishable, fell fighting.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Ayut = 10,000; the count is read as 20 x 10,000 + 1,000; ਅਡੰਡ: 'unpunishable / invincible'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਵੀਹ ਅਯੁਤ ਤੇ ਦਸ ਸੌ ਵੱਡੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਜੂਝਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗ ਪਏ, ਜਿਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਕੋਈ ਸਜ਼ਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਦੇ ਸਕਦਾ।","note_pa":"ਅਯੁਤ: ਦਸ ਹਜ਼ਾਰ; ਗਿਣਤੀ ਨੂੰ 'ਵੀਹ ਗੁਣਾ ਦਸ ਹਜ਼ਾਰ ਅਤੇ ਇੱਕ ਹਜ਼ਾਰ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਡੰਡ: 'ਜਿਸ ਨੂੰ ਸਜ਼ਾ ਨਾ ਦਿੱਤੀ ਜਾ ਸਕੇ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaval metre.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[280],"number_text":"੨੮੦।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਣ੍ਯੋ ਸੰਭਰੇਸੰ। ਭਯੋ ਅਪ ਭੇਸੰ।","roman":"Sunyo sanbhresan | bhayo ap bhesan |","meaning_en":"The king of Sambhal heard, and was beside himself.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਪ ਭੇਸੰ: read as 'changed in appearance (with anger)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੰਭਲ ਦੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਸੁਣਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਾ ਭੁੱਲ ਗਿਆ।","note_pa":"ਅਪ ਭੇਸੰ: 'ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਰੂਪ ਬਦਲ ਗਿਆ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਡੀ ਬੰਬ ਰੈਣੰ। ਛੁਹੀ ਸੀਸ ਗੈਣੰ। ੨੮੦।","roman":"Udee banb rainan | chhuhee sees gainan | 280 |","meaning_en":"Dust from the great drums rose and touched the top of the sky.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੰਬ ਰੈਣੰ: read as 'dust (raised by the army)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਵੱਡੇ ਨਗਾਰਿਆਂ ਦੀ ਧੂੜ ਉੱਠੀ ਤੇ ਅਸਮਾਨ ਦੀ ਚੋਟੀ ਨੂੰ ਛੂਹ ਗਈ।","note_pa":"ਬੰਬ ਰੈਣੰ: 'ਫ਼ੌਜ ਦੀ ਉਡਾਈ ਧੂੜ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[281],"number_text":"੨੮੧।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਕੇ ਟੋਪ ਸੀਸੰ। ਘਣੰ ਭਾਨੁ ਦੀਸੰ।","roman":"Chhake top seesan | ghanan bhaanu deesan |","meaning_en":"Helmets adorned their heads, like suns seen behind clouds.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਿਰਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਟੋਪ ਸਜੇ ਸਨ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਬੱਦਲਾਂ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਦਿਸਦੇ ਸੂਰਜ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸੰ ਨਾਹ ਦੇਹੀ। ਕਥੰ ਉਕਤਿ ਕੇਹੀ। ੨੮੧।","roman":"Sasan naah dehee | kathan ukti kehee | 281 |","meaning_en":"The body (of the king) like the lord of the moon; what words can describe it?","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਸੰ ਨਾਹ ਦੇਹੀ: read as 'body like the moon'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਦਾ ਸਰੀਰ ਚੰਦਰਮਾ ਦੇ ਸੁਆਮੀ ਵਰਗਾ ਹੈ; ਉਸ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਕਿਹੜੇ ਸ਼ਬਦਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੋਵੇ?","note_pa":"ਸਸੰ ਨਾਹ ਦੇਹੀ: 'ਚੰਦਰਮਾ ਵਰਗਾ ਸਰੀਰ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[282],"number_text":"੨੮੨।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਸਿਧ ਸੁਧੰ। ਸੁਭੀ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਉਧੰ।","roman":"Mano sidh sudhan | subhee jvaal udhan |","meaning_en":"As if a pure Siddha, a flame shining upward,","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਵੇਂ ਕੋਈ ਸ਼ੁੱਧ ਸਿੱਧ ਹੋਵੇ, ਉੱਪਰ ਉੱਠਦੀ ਲਾਟ ਹੋਵੇ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਸੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਤ੍ਰੋਣੰ। ਗੁਰੂ ਜਾਣੁ ਦ੍ਰੋਣੰ। ੨੮੨।","roman":"Kase sasatr tronan | guroo jaanu dronan | 282 |","meaning_en":"girded with weapons and quiver, like the teacher Drona.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤ੍ਰੋਣੰ: 'quiver (tooneer)'.","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਤੇ ਤਰਕਸ਼ ਨਾਲ ਕੱਸਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਗੁਰੂ ਦ੍ਰੋਣ।","note_pa":"ਤ੍ਰੋਣੰ: 'ਤਰਕਸ਼ (ਤੀਰਾਂ ਦਾ ਭੱਥਾ)'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[283],"number_text":"੨੮੩।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਢੀਠ ਢੂਕੇ। ਮੁਖੰ ਮਾਰ ਕੂਕੇ।","roman":"Mahaa dheeth dhooke | mukhan maar kooke |","meaning_en":"The very stubborn closed in, crying 'kill!' with their mouths.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਢੀਠ ਨੇੜੇ ਆਏ, ਮੂੰਹੋਂ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਦੀਆਂ ਚੀਕਾਂ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹੋਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਪਾਤੰ। ਉਠੈ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਘਾਤੰ। ੨੮੩।","roman":"Karai sasatr paatan | uthai asatr ghaatan | 283 |","meaning_en":"They strike with weapons; blows of arms rise.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਘਾਤ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[284],"number_text":"੨੮੪।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਗੰ ਖਗ ਬਜੈ। ਨਦੰ ਮਛ ਲਜੈ।","roman":"Khagan khag bajai | nadan machh lajai |","meaning_en":"Sword clashes on sword; the fish in the rivers are ashamed.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਦੰ ਮਛ ਲਜੈ: uncertain; perhaps the flashing swords outshine leaping fish.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰ ਉੱਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਵੱਜਦੀ ਹੈ; ਦਰਿਆਵਾਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਮੱਛੀਆਂ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੀਆਂ ਹੁੰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਨਦੰ ਮਛ ਲਜੈ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ; ਸ਼ਾਇਦ ਚਮਕਦੀਆਂ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਮੱਛੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਤ ਪਾਉਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠੈ ਛਿਛ ਇਛੰ। ਬਹੈ ਬਾਣ ਤਿਛੰ। ੨੮੪।","roman":"Uthai chhichh ichhan | bahai baan tichhan | 284 |","meaning_en":"Spurts of blood rise as desired; sharp arrows fly.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਿਛ ਇਛੰ: uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਲਹੂ ਦੀਆਂ ਧਾਰਾਂ ਮਨ-ਚਾਹੇ ਉੱਠਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਤਿੱਖੇ ਤੀਰ ਚੱਲਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਛਿਛ ਇਛੰ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[285],"number_text":"੨੮੫।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੇ ਬੀਰ ਧੀਰੰ। ਧਰੇ ਬੀਰ ਚੀਰੰ।","roman":"Gire beer dheeran | dhare beer cheeran |","meaning_en":"Steadfast heroes fall; heroes are torn apart.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧੀਰਜ ਵਾਲੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ; ਸੂਰਮੇ ਚੀਰੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਖੰ ਮੁਛ ਬੰਕੀ। ਮਚੇ ਬੀਰ ਹੰਕੀ। ੨੮੫।","roman":"Mukhan muchh bankee | mache beer hankee | 285 |","meaning_en":"With curling moustaches on their faces, the challenging heroes rage.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੁੱਛਾਂ ਮਰੋੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਚਿਹਰਿਆਂ ਨਾਲ, ਵੰਗਾਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[286],"number_text":"੨੮੬।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛੁਟੈ ਬਾਣ ਧਾਰੰ। ਧਰੇ ਖਗ ਸਾਰੰ।","roman":"Chhutai baan dhaaran | dhare khag saaran |","meaning_en":"Streams of arrows fly; steel swords are wielded.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰਾਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਧਾਰਾਂ ਛੁੱਟਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਤਿੱਖੀਆਂ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਚੁੱਕੀਆਂ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੇ ਅੰਗ ਭੰਗੰ। ਚਲੇ ਜਾਇ ਜੰਗੰ। ੨੮੬।","roman":"Gire ang bhangan | chale jaai jangan | 286 |","meaning_en":"Broken limbs fall; they go on into battle.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਟੁੱਟੇ ਅੰਗ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ; ਉਹ ਜੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧਦੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[287],"number_text":"੨੮੭।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੇ ਮਾਸਹਾਰੰ। ਹਸੈ ਬਿਓਮ ਚਾਰੰ।","roman":"Nache maashaaran | hasai biom chaaran |","meaning_en":"The flesh-eaters dance; the sky-goers laugh.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿਓਮ ਚਾਰੰ: 'those who move in the sky'.","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਸ ਖਾਣ ਵਾਲੇ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ; ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਵਿੱਚ ਘੁੰਮਣ ਵਾਲੇ ਹੱਸਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਬਿਓਮ ਚਾਰੰ: 'ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਵਿੱਚ ਵਿਚਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ'।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਐ ਈਸ ਸੀਸੰ। ਛਲੀ ਬਾਰੁਣੀਸੰ। ੨੮੭।","roman":"Puai ees seesan | chhalee baaruneesan | 287 |","meaning_en":"Shiva strings heads; the lord of wine (Varuni) is gleeful.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਲੀ ਬਾਰੁਣੀਸੰ: uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸ਼ਿਵ ਖੋਪਰੀਆਂ ਪਰੋਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਸ਼ਰਾਬ ਦਾ ਸੁਆਮੀ (ਵਰੁਣੀ) ਖ਼ੁਸ਼ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਛਲੀ ਬਾਰੁਣੀਸੰ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[288],"number_text":"੨੮੮।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛੁਟੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਧਾਰੰ। ਕਟੈ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਝਾਰੰ।","roman":"Chhutai sasatr dhaaran | katai asatr jhaaran |","meaning_en":"Weapons are loosed in streams; arms cut and strike.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਧਾਰਾਂ ਛੁੱਟਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਕੱਟਦੇ ਤੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੇ ਰਤ ਖੇਤੰ। ਕਟੇ ਬੀਰ ਅਚੇਤੰ। ੨੮੮।","roman":"Gire rat khetan | kate beer achetan | 288 |","meaning_en":"They fall on the blood-red field; heroes lie cut and senseless.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਲਹੂ ਭਰੇ ਖੇਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ; ਵੱਢੇ ਹੋਏ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਬੇਸੁੱਧ ਪਏ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[289],"number_text":"੨੮੯।","page":750,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠੈ ਕ੍ਰੁਧ ਧਾਰੰ। ਮਚੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਝਾਰੰ।","roman":"Uthai krudh dhaaran | mache sasatr jhaaran |","meaning_en":"Streams of anger rise; the clash of weapons rages.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਦੀਆਂ ਧਾਰਾਂ ਉੱਠਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਦੀ ਖੜਕ ਮਚਦੀ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਹੈ ਖਗ ਖੂਨੀ। ਚੜੈ ਚਉਪ ਦੂਨੀ। ੨੮੯।","roman":"Khahai khag khoonee | charai chaup doonee | 289 |","meaning_en":"Bloodthirsty swords clash; zeal mounts twofold.","page":750,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖ਼ੂਨੀ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਟਕਰਾਉਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਚਾਅ ਦੁੱਗਣਾ ਚੜ੍ਹਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[290],"number_text":"੨੯੦।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਿਪੰ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ ਦੇਵੀ। ਹਸੈ ਅੰਸੁ ਭੇਵੀ।","roman":"Pipan sron devee | hasai ansu bhevee |","meaning_en":"The Goddess drinks blood; the mysterious one laughs,","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅੰਸੁ ਭੇਵੀ: uncertain; read as 'the mysterious (Goddess)'.","meaning_pa":"ਦੇਵੀ ਲਹੂ ਪੀਂਦੀ ਹੈ; ਭੇਤ ਵਾਲੀ ਹੱਸਦੀ ਹੈ,","note_pa":"ਅੰਸੁ ਭੇਵੀ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ; 'ਭੇਤ ਵਾਲੀ (ਦੇਵੀ)' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਟਾ ਅਟ ਹਾਸੰ। ਸੁ ਜੋਤੰ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸੰ। ੨੯੦।","roman":"Ataa at haasan | su jotan prakaasan | 290 |","meaning_en":"loud laughter upon laughter, her light shining forth.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੇਅੰਤ ਹਾਸਾ ਹੱਸਦੀ ਹੈ, ਉਸ ਦੀ ਜੋਤ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[291],"number_text":"੨੯੧।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਢੁਕੇ ਢੀਠ ਢਾਲੰ। ਨਚੇ ਮੁੰਡ ਮਾਲੰ।","roman":"Dhuke dheeth dhaalan | nache mund maalan |","meaning_en":"The stubborn close in with shields; the wearer of the skull-garland dances.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਢੀਠ ਢਾਲਾਂ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਨੇੜੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ; ਮੁੰਡਮਾਲਾ ਧਾਰੀ ਨੱਚਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੈ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਪਾਤੰ। ਉਠੈ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਘਾਤੰ। ੨੯੧।","roman":"Karai sasatr paatan | uthai asatr ghaatan | 291 |","meaning_en":"They strike with weapons; blows of arms rise.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਅਸਤ੍ਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਘਾਤ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[292],"number_text":"੨੯੨।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੁਪੇ ਵੀਰ ਧੀਰੰ। ਤਜੈ ਤਾਣ ਤੀਰੰ।","roman":"Rupe veer dheeran | tajai taan teeran |","meaning_en":"Steadfast heroes stand firm; drawing the bow, they loose arrows;","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਡੋਲ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹਨ; ਕਮਾਨ ਖਿੱਚ ਕੇ ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝਮੈ ਬਿਜੁ ਬੇਗੰ। ਲਸੈ ਏਮ ਤੇਗੰ। ੨੯੨।","roman":"Jhamai biju began | lasai em tegan | 292 |","meaning_en":"the swords gleam like swift flashing lightning.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਤੇਜ਼ ਬਿਜਲੀ ਵਾਂਗ ਚਮਕਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[293],"number_text":"੨੯੩।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਹੇ ਖਗ ਖੂਨੀ। ਚੜੈ ਚੌਪ ਦੂਨੀ।","roman":"Khahe khag khoonee | charai chaup doonee |","meaning_en":"Bloodthirsty swords clash; zeal mounts twofold.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖ਼ੂਨੀ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਟਕਰਾਉਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਚਾਅ ਦੁੱਗਣਾ ਚੜ੍ਹਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੈ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਾਰੰ। ਬਕੈ ਮਾਰੁ ਮਾਰੰ। ੨੯੩।","roman":"Karai chitr chaaran | bakai maaru maaran | 293 |","meaning_en":"They perform wondrous feats, crying 'kill, kill!'","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਅਨੋਖੇ ਕਰਤਬ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, 'ਮਾਰੋ, ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[294],"number_text":"੨੯੪।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਪੋ ਆਪ ਦਾਬੈ। ਰਣੰ ਬੀਰ ਫਾਬੈ।","roman":"Apo aap daabai | ranan beer phaabai |","meaning_en":"Each presses on the other; heroes look splendid in battle.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇੱਕ ਦੂਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਦਬਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਸ਼ੋਭਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਣੰ ਘਾਇ ਪੇਲੈ। ਮਹਾ ਵੀਰ ਝੇਲੈ। ੨੯੪।","roman":"Ghanan ghaai pelai | mahaa veer jhelai | 294 |","meaning_en":"They deal many wounds; the great heroes bear them.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬਹੁਤ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਦਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਵੱਡੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਸਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[295],"number_text":"੨੯੫।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੰਡੇ ਵੀਰ ਸੁਧੰ। ਕਰੈ ਮਲ ਜੁਧੰ।","roman":"Mande veer sudhan | karai mal judhan |","meaning_en":"True heroes take their stand and fight a wrestlers' battle;","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੱਚੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਅਡੋਲ ਖੜ੍ਹਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਕੁਸ਼ਤੀ ਵਾਂਗ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਪੋ ਆਪ ਬਾਹੈ। ਉਭੈ ਜੀਤ ਚਾਹੈ। ੨੯੫।","roman":"Apo aap baahai | ubhai jeet chaahai | 295 |","meaning_en":"each strikes at the other; both seek victory.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਇੱਕ ਦੂਜੇ ਉੱਤੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਦੋਵੇਂ ਜਿੱਤ ਚਾਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[296],"number_text":"੨੯੬।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣੰ ਰੰਗ ਰਤੇ। ਚੜੇ ਤੇਜ ਤਤੇ।","roman":"Ranan rang rate | chare tej tate |","meaning_en":"Dyed in the colour of battle, they are fired with hot fury;","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੰਗੇ ਹੋਏ, ਤੇਜ਼ ਜੋਸ਼ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੇ ਹੋਏ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੁਲੇ ਖਗ ਖੂਨੀ। ਚੜੇ ਚਉਪ ਦੂਨੀ। ੨੯੬।","roman":"Khule khag khoonee | chare chaup doonee | 296 |","meaning_en":"the bloodthirsty swords are bared; zeal mounts twofold.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਖ਼ੂਨੀ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਨੰਗੀਆਂ ਹੋਈਆਂ ਹਨ; ਚਾਅ ਦੁੱਗਣਾ ਚੜ੍ਹਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[297],"number_text":"੨੯੭।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਭੰ ਹੂਰ ਪੂਰੰ। ਭਏ ਵੀਰ ਚੂਰੰ।","roman":"Nabhan hoor pooran | bhae veer chooran |","meaning_en":"The sky is filled with nymphs; heroes are crushed;","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਹੂਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਭਰ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ; ਸੂਰਮੇ ਚੂਰ-ਚੂਰ ਹੋਏ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੈ ਤੂਰ ਤਾਲੀ। ਨਚੇ ਮੁੰਡ ਮਾਲੀ। ੨੯੭।","roman":"Bajai toor taalee | nache mund maalee | 297 |","meaning_en":"trumpets and cymbals sound; the wearer of the skull-garland dances.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਗਾੜੇ ਤੇ ਝਾਂਜਰਾਂ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ; ਮੁੰਡਮਾਲਾ ਧਾਰੀ ਨੱਚਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[298],"number_text":"੨੯੮।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣੰ ਰੂਹ ਉਠੈ। ਸਰੰ ਧਾਰ ਬੁਠੈ।","roman":"Ranan rooh uthai | saran dhaar buthai |","meaning_en":"Souls rise from the battlefield; streams of arrows rain down;","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੂਹ: Persian 'ruh', soul.","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਤੋਂ ਰੂਹਾਂ ਉੱਠਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਤੀਰਾਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਧਾਰਾਂ ਵਰ੍ਹਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਰੂਹ: ਫ਼ਾਰਸੀ ਦਾ ਸ਼ਬਦ, ਭਾਵ ਆਤਮਾ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਜੈ ਵੀਰ ਗਾਜੀ। ਤੁਰੇ ਤੁੰਦ ਤਾਜੀ। ੨੯੮।","roman":"Gajai veer gaajee | ture tund taajee | 298 |","meaning_en":"the heroic warriors roar; the fierce Arab horses race.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹਾਦਰ ਯੋਧੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹਨ; ਤੇਜ਼ ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਦੌੜਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ"},{"type":"verse","number":[299],"number_text":"੨੯੯।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਇਓ ਘੋਰ ਆਹਵ ਬਿਕਰਾਰਾ। ਨਾਚੇ ਭੂਤ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਬੈਤਾਰਾ।","roman":"Bhaio ghor aahav bikraaraa | naache bhoot pret baitaaraa |","meaning_en":"A terrible, dreadful battle took place; ghosts, spirits and Vetals danced.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੜਾ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਜੰਗ ਹੋਇਆ; ਭੂਤ, ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਅਤੇ ਬੇਤਾਲ ਨੱਚੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਰਕ ਬਾਣ ਗਗਨ ਗਇਓ ਛਾਈ। ਜਾਨੁਕ ਰੈਨ ਦਿਨਹਿ ਹੁਇ ਆਈ। ੨੯੯।","roman":"Bairak baan gagan gaio chhaaee | jaanuk rain dinhi hui aaee | 299 |","meaning_en":"Banners and arrows covered the sky, as if night had come in the daytime.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਝੰਡਿਆਂ ਤੇ ਤੀਰਾਂ ਨੇ ਅਸਮਾਨ ਢਕ ਲਿਆ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਦਿਨ ਵੇਲੇ ਰਾਤ ਆ ਗਈ ਹੋਵੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[300],"number_text":"੩੦੦।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਨਾਚੈ ਰਣਿ। ਜੂਝ ਜੂਝ ਕਹੂੰ ਗਿਰੇ ਸੁਭਟ ਗਣ।","roman":"Kahoon pisaach pret naachai rani | joojh joojh kahoon gire subhat gan |","meaning_en":"Somewhere goblins and ghosts dance on the battlefield; somewhere hosts of great warriors fall, fighting.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਪਿਸ਼ਾਚ ਤੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ; ਜੂਝ-ਜੂਝ ਕੇ ਕਿਤੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਟੋਲੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਈਰਵ ਕਰਤ ਕਹੂੰ ਭਭਕਾਰਾ। ਉਡਤ ਕਾਕ ਕੰਕੈ ਬਿਕਰਾਰਾ। ੩੦੦।","roman":"Bhaeerav karat kahoon bhabhkaaraa | udat kaak kankai bikraaraa | 300 |","meaning_en":"Somewhere Bhairav makes a roaring sound; crows and herons fly about, dreadful.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਭੈਰਵ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਕਾਂ ਤੇ ਬਗਲੇ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਰੂਪ ਵਿੱਚ ਉੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[301],"number_text":"੩੦੧।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜਤ ਢੋਲ ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ ਨਗਾਰਾ। ਤਾਲ ਉਪੰਗ ਬੇਣ ਬੰਕਾਰਾ।","roman":"Baajat dhol mridang nagaaraa | taal upang ben bankaaraa |","meaning_en":"Drums, mridangs and kettle-drums sound; cymbals, upangs and flutes ring loud;","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਢੋਲ, ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ ਤੇ ਨਗਾਰੇ ਵੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ; ਝਾਂਝਾਂ, ਉਪੰਗ ਤੇ ਬੰਸਰੀਆਂ ਉੱਚੀ ਵੱਜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਰਲੀ ਨਾਦ ਨਫੀਰੀ ਬਾਜੇ। ਭੀਰ ਭਯਾਨਕ ਹੁਐ ਤਜਿ ਭਾਜੇ। ੩੦੧।","roman":"Murlee naad napheeree baaje | bheer bhayaanak huai taji bhaaje | 301 |","meaning_en":"pipes and trumpets play; cowards, terrified, leave and flee.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੁਰਲੀ: flute; ਨਫੀਰੀ: a trumpet or pipe.","meaning_pa":"ਬੰਸਰੀ ਦੀ ਧੁਨ ਤੇ ਨਫ਼ੀਰੀ ਵੱਜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਡਰ ਨਾਲ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਮੁਰਲੀ: 'ਬੰਸਰੀ'; ਨਫੀਰੀ: 'ਤੁਰ੍ਹੀ ਜਾਂ ਬੰਸਰੀ ਦੀ ਕਿਸਮ'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[302],"number_text":"੩੦੨।","page":751,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਾ ਸੁਭਟ ਜੂਝੇ ਤਿਹ ਠਾਮਾ। ਖਰਭਰ ਪਰੀ ਇੰਦ੍ਰ ਕੇ ਧਾਮਾ।","roman":"Mahaa subhat joojhe tih thaamaa | kharbhar paree indr ke dhaamaa |","meaning_en":"Great warriors fell fighting in that place; there was commotion in Indra's abode.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਥਾਂ ਵੱਡੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਜੂਝ ਕੇ ਡਿੱਗੇ; ਇੰਦਰ ਦੇ ਮਹਿਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਫੜਾ-ਦਫੜੀ ਮੱਚ ਗਈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਰਕ ਬਾਣ ਗਗਨ ਗਇਓ ਛਾਈ। ਉਠੈ ਘਟਾ ਸਾਵਣ ਜਨੁ ਆਈ। ੩੦੨।","roman":"Bairak baan gagan gaio chhaaee | uthai ghataa saavan janu aaee | 302 |","meaning_en":"Banners and arrows covered the sky, as if the clouds of Sawan had risen.","page":751,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਝੰਡਿਆਂ ਤੇ ਤੀਰਾਂ ਨੇ ਅਸਮਾਨ ਢਕ ਲਿਆ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਸਾਵਣ ਦੀਆਂ ਘਟਾਵਾਂ ਚੜ੍ਹ ਆਈਆਂ ਹੋਣ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Tomar chhand","meaning_en":"Tomar metre.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੋਮਰ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[303],"number_text":"੩੦੩।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁ ਭਾਤਿ ਕੋਪੇ ਸਬੀਰ। ਧਨੁ ਤਾਨਿ ਤਿਆਗਤ ਤੀਰ।","roman":"Bahu bhaati kope sabeer | dhanu taani tiaagat teer |","meaning_en":"The heroes grew angry in many ways; drawing their bows, they loosed arrows.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੀਰ ਕਈ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਹੋਏ; ਧਨੁਸ਼ ਖਿੱਚ ਕੇ ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਅੰਗਿ ਜਾਸੁ ਲਗੰਤ। ਭਟ ਸੁਰਗਿ ਬਾਸ ਕਰੰਤ। ੩੦੩।","roman":"Sar angi jaasu lagant | bhat surgi baas karant | 303 |","meaning_en":"Whoever's body an arrow struck, that warrior went to dwell in heaven.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਸ ਦੇ ਸਰੀਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਤੀਰ ਲੱਗਿਆ, ਉਹ ਯੋਧਾ ਸਵਰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਜਾ ਵੱਸਿਆ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[304],"number_text":"੩੦੪।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਅੰਗ ਭੰਗ ਉਤੰਗ। ਕਹੂੰ ਤੀਰ ਤੇਗ ਸੁਰੰਗ।","roman":"Kahoon ang bhang utang | kahoon teer teg surang |","meaning_en":"Somewhere lie broken limbs, tall (warriors); somewhere arrows and fine-coloured swords;","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਉੱਚੇ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਅੰਗ ਟੁੱਟੇ ਪਏ ਹਨ; ਕਿਤੇ ਤੀਰ ਤੇ ਸੋਹਣੀਆਂ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਪਈਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਚਉਰ ਚੀਰ ਸੁਬਾਹ। ਕਹੂੰ ਸੁਧ ਸੇਲ ਸਨਾਹ। ੩੦੪।","roman":"Kahoon chaur cheer subaah | kahoon sudh sel sanaah | 304 |","meaning_en":"somewhere whisks and garments of fine-armed (warriors); somewhere fine lances and armour.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਚੌਰ ਤੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਬਸਤਰ ਪਏ ਹਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਨੇਜ਼ੇ ਤੇ ਬਖ਼ਤਰ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[305],"number_text":"੩੦੫।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਅੰਗ ਰੰਗਤ ਐਸ। ਜਨੁ ਫੁਲ ਕਿੰਸਕ ਜੈਸ।","roman":"Rani ang rangat ais | janu phul kinsak jais |","meaning_en":"In battle the limbs are coloured (with blood) like the flowers of the kinsuk (palash) tree.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਅੰਗ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਰੰਗੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਕਿਸੇ ਢਾਕ (ਕਿੰਸੁਕ) ਦੇ ਫੁੱਲ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਕ ਐਸ ਜੂਝ ਮਰੰਤ। ਜਨੁ ਖੇਲਿ ਫਾਗੁ ਬਸੰਤ। ੩੦੫।","roman":"Ik ais joojh marant | janu kheli phaagu basant | 305 |","meaning_en":"Some die fighting in such a way, as if playing Phag (Holi) in spring.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਜੂਝ ਕੇ ਮਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਬਸੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਫੱਗਣ ਦੀ ਹੋਲੀ ਖੇਡੀ ਜਾ ਰਹੀ ਹੋਵੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[306],"number_text":"੩੦੬।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਕ ਧਾਇ ਆਇ ਪਰੰਤ। ਪਗ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਨ ਭਾਗਿ ਚਲੰਤ।","roman":"Ik dhaai aai parant | pag dvai na bhaagi chalant |","meaning_en":"Some charge and fall upon (the foe), and do not run back two steps.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕੁਝ ਦੌੜ ਕੇ ਆ ਕੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਤੇ ਦੋ ਕਦਮ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਭੱਜਦੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜਿ ਤ੍ਰਾਸ ਕਰਤ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰ। ਜਨੁ ਖੇਲ ਫਾਗਿ ਧਮਾਰ। ੩੦੬।","roman":"Taji traas karat prahaar | janu khel phaagi dhamaar | 306 |","meaning_en":"Casting off fear, they strike, as if playing the Holi revels.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਮਾਰ: Holi songs and revelry.","meaning_pa":"ਡਰ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਹੋਲੀ ਦਾ ਰੰਗ ਖੇਡਿਆ ਜਾ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੋਵੇ।","note_pa":"ਧਮਾਰ: ਹੋਲੀ ਦੇ ਗੀਤ ਤੇ ਰੰਗ-ਰਲੀਆਂ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤਾਰਕ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤਾਰਕ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Taarak chhand","meaning_en":"Tarak metre.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਾਰਕ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[307],"number_text":"੩੦੭।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਰਿਸਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਭਟ ਓਘ ਪ੍ਰਓਘ ਗਿਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Kalkee avtaar risaavhige | bhat ogh praogh giraavhige |","meaning_en":"The Kalki incarnation will grow angry and fell hosts upon hosts of warriors.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਹੋਵੇਗਾ ਤੇ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਟੋਲੀਆਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਟੋਲੀਆਂ ਡੇਗੇਗਾ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁ ਭਾਤਨ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਅਰਿ ਓਘ ਪ੍ਰਓਘ ਸੰਘਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੦੭।","roman":"Bahu bhaatan sasatr prahaarhige | ari ogh praogh sanghaarhige | 307 |","meaning_en":"He will strike with weapons in many ways and destroy hosts upon hosts of enemies.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਕਈ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਚਲਾਵੇਗਾ ਤੇ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਟੋਲੀਆਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਟੋਲੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਨਾਸ਼ ਕਰੇਗਾ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[308],"number_text":"੩੦੮।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਸੇਲ ਸਨਾਹਰਿ ਛੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣ ਰੰਗਿ ਸੁਰਾਸੁਰ ਜੂਟਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Sar sel sanaahri chhoothige | ran rangi suraasur joothige |","meaning_en":"Arrows and lances will fly at the armoured; gods and demons will close in the fervour of battle.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਨਾਹਰਿ: read as 'at the armour-wearers'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤੀਰ, ਨੇਜ਼ੇ ਤੇ ਬਖ਼ਤਰਬੰਦਾਂ ਵੱਲ ਛੁੱਟਣਗੇ; ਦੇਵਤੇ ਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਰਣ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਜੁੱਟਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਸਨਾਹਰਿ: 'ਬਖ਼ਤਰ ਪਹਿਨਣ ਵਾਲਿਆਂ ਵੱਲ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਸੇਲ ਸਨਾਹਰਿ ਝਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਮੁਖ ਮਾਰ ਪਚਾਰ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੦੮।","roman":"Sar sel sanaahri jhaarhige | mukh maar pachaar prahaarhige | 308 |","meaning_en":"They will hurl arrows and lances at the armoured, and strike, crying 'kill!' and challenging.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬਖ਼ਤਰਬੰਦਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਤੀਰ ਤੇ ਨੇਜ਼ੇ ਚਲਾਉਣਗੇ ਤੇ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿ ਕੇ ਵੰਗਾਰਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਨਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[309],"number_text":"੩੦੯।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਮਡਢ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਨਿਕਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਸੁਰਾਸੁਰ ਝਾਰਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Jamdadh kripaan nikaarhige | kari kop suraasur jhaarhige |","meaning_en":"They will draw daggers and swords; in wrath they will strike down gods and demons.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਮਡਢ: a type of dagger (jamdadh).","meaning_pa":"ਜਮਦਾੜ੍ਹ ਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਕੱਢਣਗੇ; ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਿੱਚ ਆ ਕੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਮਾਰ ਦੇਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਜਮਡਢ: 'ਜਮਦਾੜ੍ਹ' ਨਾਂ ਦਾ ਇੱਕ ਖ਼ੰਜਰ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਲੁਥ ਪੈ ਲੁਥ ਗਿਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਲਖਿ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਪਰੀ ਰਹਸਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ੩੦੯।","roman":"Rani luth pai luth giraavhige | lakhi pret paree rahsaavhige | 309 |","meaning_en":"They will fell corpse upon corpse in battle; seeing it, ghosts and fairies will rejoice.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਲਾਸ਼ ਉੱਤੇ ਲਾਸ਼ ਡੇਗਣਗੇ; ਇਹ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਤੇ ਪਰੀਆਂ ਖ਼ੁਸ਼ ਹੋਣਗੀਆਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[310],"number_text":"੩੧੦।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਗੂੜ ਅਗੂੜਣਿ ਗਜਹਿਗੇ। ਲਖਿ ਭੀਰ ਭਯਾਹਵ ਭਜਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Rani goor agoorni gajhige | lakhi bheer bhayaahav bhajhige |","meaning_en":"In battle the hidden and the open will roar; seeing the dreadful fight, cowards will flee.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗੂੜ ਅਗੂੜਣਿ: uncertain; possibly 'seasoned and unseasoned (warriors)'.","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਗੂੜ ਤੇ ਅਗੂੜ ਗਰਜਣਗੇ; ਡਰਾਉਣੀ ਲੜਾਈ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਗੂੜ ਅਗੂੜਣਿ: ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ; ਸ਼ਾਇਦ 'ਤਜਰਬੇਕਾਰ ਤੇ ਅਣਤਜਰਬੇਕਾਰ' ਯੋਧੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਬਿੰਦ ਪ੍ਰਬਿੰਦ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣਰੰਗਿ ਅਭੀਤ ਬਿਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੦।","roman":"Sar bind prabind prahaarhige | ranrangi abheet bihaarhige | 310 |","meaning_en":"They will shoot multitudes upon multitudes of arrows and move fearless in the fervour of battle.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰੇ ਤੀਰ ਚਲਾਉਣਗੇ ਤੇ ਰਣ-ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਬੇਖ਼ੌਫ਼ ਵਿਚਰਨਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[311],"number_text":"੩੧੧।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਗ ਉਧ ਅਧੋ ਅਧ ਬਜਹਿਗੇ। ਲਖਿ ਜੋਧ ਮਹਾ ਜੁਧ ਗਜਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Khag udh adho adh bajhige | lakhi jodh mahaa judh gajhige |","meaning_en":"Swords will clang above and below; seeing the warriors, the great battle will roar.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਉੱਪਰ ਤੇ ਹੇਠਾਂ ਖੜਕਣਗੀਆਂ; ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਮਹਾਂ ਜੰਗ ਗਰਜੇਗੀ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਣਿਣੇਸ ਦੁਹੂੰ ਦਿਸ ਢੂਕਹਿਗੇ। ਮੁਖ ਮਾਰ ਮਹਾ ਸੁਰ ਕੂਕਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੧।","roman":"Anines duhoon dis dhookhige | mukh maar mahaa sur kookhige | 311 |","meaning_en":"The army commanders will close in from both sides, shouting 'kill!' loudly with their mouths.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਣਿਣੇਸ: 'lords of armies'.","meaning_pa":"ਸੈਨਾ ਦੇ ਸੈਨਾਪਤੀ ਦੋਹਾਂ ਪਾਸਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਨੇੜੇ ਆਉਣਗੇ, ਉੱਚੀ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਿੱਚ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹੋਏ।","note_pa":"ਅਣਿਣੇਸ: 'ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਦੇ ਸੁਆਮੀ'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[312],"number_text":"੩੧੨।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਗੰਧ੍ਰਵ ਦੇਵ ਨਿਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਜੈ ਸਦ ਨਿਨਦ ਪੁਕਾਰਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gan gandhrav dev nihaarhige | jai sad ninad pukaarhige |","meaning_en":"Ganas, Gandharvas and gods will watch and raise the cry of 'victory'.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗਣ, ਗੰਧਰਵ ਤੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਵੇਖਣਗੇ ਤੇ 'ਜੈ' ਦਾ ਨਾਅਰਾ ਲਾਉਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਮਦਾੜਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣਣਿ ਬਾਹਹਿਗੇ। ਅਧਅੰਗ ਅਧੋਅਧ ਲਾਹਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੨।","roman":"Jamdaari kripaanni baahhige | adha'ang adhoadh laahhige | 312 |","meaning_en":"They will wield daggers and swords and lop off limbs, cutting them in halves.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਦਾੜ੍ਹ ਵਾਲੀਆਂ ਕਟਾਰਾਂ ਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਚਲਾਉਣਗੇ ਤੇ ਅੰਗ ਵੱਢ ਕੇ ਅੱਧੇ-ਅੱਧੇ ਕਰਨਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[313],"number_text":"੩੧੩।","page":752,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਰੰਗਿ ਤੁਰੰਗੈ ਬਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ਡਫ ਝਾਂਝ ਨਫੀਰੀ ਗਾਜਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ranrangi turangai baajhige | daph jhaanjh napheeree gaajhige |","meaning_en":"Horses will charge in the fervour of battle; tambourines, cymbals and trumpets will roar.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ-ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਘੋੜੇ ਦੌੜਨਗੇ; ਡਫ, ਝਾਂਝਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਨਫ਼ੀਰੀਆਂ ਗਰਜਣਗੀਆਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਣਿਣੇਸ ਦੁਹੂੰ ਦਿਸ ਧਾਵਹਿਗੈ। ਕਰਿ ਕਾਢਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਕੰਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੩।","roman":"Anines duhoon dis dhaavhigai | kari kaadhi kripaan kanpaavhige | 313 |","meaning_en":"The army commanders will charge from both sides, and drawing their swords will make all tremble.","page":752,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਣਿਣੇਸ (ਸੈਨਾਪਤੀ) ਦੋਹਾਂ ਪਾਸਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਧਾਵਾ ਬੋਲਣਗੇ; ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਕੱਢ ਕੇ ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਕੰਬਾ ਦੇਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[314],"number_text":"੩੧੪।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਕੁੰਜਰ ਪੁੰਜ ਗਰਜਹਿਗੇ। ਲਖਿ ਮੇਘ ਮਹਾ ਦੁਤਿ ਲਜਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Rani kunjar punj garajhige | lakhi megh mahaa duti lajhige |","meaning_en":"Herds of elephants will trumpet in battle; seeing their great splendour the clouds will be ashamed.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਾਥੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਝੁੰਡ ਗਰਜਣਗੇ; ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੀ ਵੱਡੀ ਚਮਕ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਬੱਦਲ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੋਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਿਸ ਮੰਡਿ ਮਹਾ ਰਣ ਜੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ਛੁਟਿ ਛਤ੍ਰ ਛਟਾਛਟ ਛੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੪।","roman":"Ris mandi mahaa ran joothige | chhuti chhatr chhataachhat chhoothige | 314 |","meaning_en":"Filled with rage they will close in great battle; royal canopies will be struck off one after another.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਭਰ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਵੱਡੇ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਜੁੱਟਣਗੇ; ਛਤਰ ਇੱਕ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਇੱਕ ਡਿੱਗਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[315],"number_text":"੩੧੫।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਣੰਕ ਨਿਸਾਣ ਦਿਸਾਣ ਘੁਰੇ। ਗੜਗਜ ਹਠੀ ਰਣ ਰੰਗਿ ਫਿਰੇ।","roman":"Rannank nisaan disaan ghure | gargaj hathee ran rangi phire |","meaning_en":"The drums sounded and thundered in every direction; the steadfast, thundering like elephants, moved through the battle.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗੜਗਜ: read as 'thundering (like) elephants'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਹਰ ਦਿਸ਼ਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਰਣ ਦੇ ਨਗਾੜੇ ਤੇ ਨਿਸ਼ਾਨ ਵੱਜੇ; ਹਠੀ ਯੋਧੇ ਹਾਥੀਆਂ ਵਾਂਗ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਰਣ-ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਫਿਰੇ।","note_pa":"ਗੜਗਜ: 'ਹਾਥੀਆਂ ਵਾਂਗ ਗਰਜਦੇ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਭਟ ਘਾਇ ਝਟਾਝਟ ਝਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੫।","roman":"Kari kop kripaan prahaarhige | bhat ghaai jhataajhat jhaarhige | 315 |","meaning_en":"In wrath they will strike with swords and quickly strike warriors down with wounds.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਿੱਚ ਆ ਕੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਨਗੇ ਤੇ ਝਟਪਟ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਡੇਗਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[316],"number_text":"੩੧੬।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਕਾਢਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਕੰਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਕਲਿਕੀ ਕਲਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਬਢਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Kari kaadhi kripaan kanpaavhige | kalikee kali krit badhaavhige |","meaning_en":"Drawing His sword, He will make all tremble; Kalki will spread His glory in the Kali age.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰ ਕੱਢ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਕੰਬਾਉਣਗੇ; ਕਲਕੀ ਕਲਿਯੁਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਪਣੀ ਮਹਿਮਾ ਵਧਾਉਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਲੁਥ ਪਲੁਥ ਬਿਥਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਤਕਿ ਤੀਰ ਸੁ ਬੀਰਨ ਮਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੬।","roman":"Rani luth paluth bithaarhige | taki teer su beeran maarhige | 316 |","meaning_en":"He will strew heaps of corpses on the battlefield; aiming arrows, He will kill the heroes.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਲਾਸ਼ਾਂ ਦੇ ਢੇਰ ਲਾਉਣਗੇ; ਤੀਰ ਤਾਕ ਕੇ ਸੂਰਮਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਨਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[317],"number_text":"੩੧੭।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਣ ਘੁੰਘਰ ਘੋਰ ਘਮਕਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣ ਮੋ ਰਣਧੀਰ ਪਲਕਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ghan ghunghar ghor ghamakhige | ran mo randheer palakhige |","meaning_en":"The bells will clang loudly; the steadfast in battle will flash about.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਘੁੰਗਰੂ ਜ਼ੋਰ-ਜ਼ੋਰ ਦੀ ਛਣਕਣਗੇ; ਰਣ ਦੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਝਲਕਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹਿ ਤੇਗ ਝੜਾਝੜ ਝਾੜਹਿਗੇ। ਤਕਿ ਤੀਰ ਤੜਾਤੜ ਤਾੜਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੭।","roman":"Gahi teg jharaajhar jhaarhige | taki teer taraatar taarhige | 317 |","meaning_en":"Taking swords, they will strike again and again; aiming arrows, they will shoot in rapid volleys.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਝੜਾਝੜ, ਤੜਾਤੜ: sound-words.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰ ਫੜ ਕੇ ਵਾਰ-ਵਾਰ ਝਾੜਨਗੇ; ਤੀਰ ਤਾਕ ਕੇ ਤੜਾ-ਤੜ ਚਲਾਉਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਝੜਾਝੜ ਅਤੇ ਤੜਾਤੜ: ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਵਾਲੇ ਸ਼ਬਦ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[318],"number_text":"੩੧੮।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਜ ਬਾਜ ਰਥੀ ਰਥ ਕੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ਗਹਿ ਕੇਸਨ ਏਕਿਨ ਝੂਟਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gaj baaj rathee rath koothige | gahi kesan ekin jhoothige |","meaning_en":"They will smash elephants, horses, charioteers and chariots; seizing some by the hair, they will swing them.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀ, ਘੋੜੇ, ਰਥੀ ਤੇ ਰਥ ਕੁਚਲ ਦੇਣਗੇ; ਕਈਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਵਾਲਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਫੜ ਕੇ ਝੂਟੇ ਦੇਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਖ ਲਾਤਨ ਮੁਸਟ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣਿ ਦਾਤਨ ਕੇਸਨੁ ਪਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੮।","roman":"Lakh laatan musat prahaarhige | rani daatan kesnu paarhige | 318 |","meaning_en":"They will strike with countless kicks and fists; in battle they will tear with teeth and hair.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਾਤਨ ਕੇਸਨੁ ਪਾਰਹਿਗੇ: read as 'bite and pull hair'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਲੱਖਾਂ ਲੱਤਾਂ ਤੇ ਮੁੱਕਿਆਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਨਗੇ; ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਦੰਦਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵੱਢਣਗੇ ਤੇ ਵਾਲ ਪੁੱਟਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਦਾਤਨ ਕੇਸਨੁ ਪਾਰਹਿਗੇ: 'ਦੰਦਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵੱਢਣਾ ਤੇ ਵਾਲ ਪੁੱਟਣੇ'; ਪੱਕਾ ਪਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[319],"number_text":"੩੧੯।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਵਣੇਸ ਅਣੀਣਿ ਸੁਧਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਕਰਿ ਬਾਣ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਸੰਭਾਰਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Avnes aneeni sudhaarhige | kari baan kripaan sanbhaarhige |","meaning_en":"The kings will set their armies in order and take up arrows and swords in hand.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਵਣੇਸ: 'lords of the earth', kings.","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਆਪਣੀਆਂ ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਵਿਵਸਥਿਤ ਕਰਨਗੇ ਤੇ ਹੱਥਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਤੀਰ ਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਚੁੱਕਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਅਵਣੇਸ: 'ਧਰਤੀ ਦੇ ਸੁਆਮੀ' ਭਾਵ ਰਾਜੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਿ ਰੋਸ ਦੁਹੂੰ ਦਿਸਿ ਧਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣਿ ਸੀਝਿ ਦਿਵਾਲਯ ਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ੩੧੯।","roman":"Kari ros duhoon disi dhaavhige | rani seejhi divaalay paavhige | 319 |","meaning_en":"In rage they will charge from both sides, and, succeeding in battle, will reach the abode of the gods.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੀਝਿ: read as 'being accomplished / dying in battle'; ਦਿਵਾਲਯ: abode of gods.","meaning_pa":"ਰੋਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਦੋਹਾਂ ਪਾਸਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਧਾਵਾ ਬੋਲਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਫ਼ਲ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਲੋਕ ਨੂੰ ਪਹੁੰਚਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਸੀਝਿ: 'ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਫ਼ਲ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਜਾਂ ਸ਼ਹੀਦ ਹੋ ਕੇ'; ਦਿਵਾਲਯ: 'ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਦਾ ਲੋਕ'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[320],"number_text":"੩੨੦।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਣਣੰਕਿ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਛਣਕਹਿਗੀ। ਝਣਣਕਿ ਸੰਜੋਅ ਝਣਕਹਿਗੀ।","roman":"Chhannanki kripaan chhanakhigee | jhananki sanjoa jhanakhigee |","meaning_en":"Swords will clang with a ringing sound; armour will jangle and clatter;","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਣਣੰਕਿ, ਝਣਣਕਿ: sound-words for the ring of steel.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਛਣਣੰਕਿ ਛਣਕਣਗੀਆਂ। ਸੰਜੋਅ ਝਣਣਕਿ ਝਣਕੇਗੀ।","note_pa":"ਛਣਣੰਕਿ, ਝਣਣਕਿ: ਲੋਹੇ ਦੀ ਛਣਕਾਰ ਦੀ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਦੇ ਸ਼ਬਦ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਣਣੰਛਿ ਕੰਧਾਰਿ ਕਣਛਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣਰੰਗਿ ਸੁ ਚਾਚਰ ਮਚਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੦।","roman":"Kannanchhi kandhaari kanachhhige | ranrangi su chaachar machhige | 320 |","meaning_en":"the Kandahari horses will neigh, and in the colour of battle a wild revel (chachar) will break out.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੰਧਾਰਿ: read as 'Kandahari horses'; ਕਣਣੰਛਿ ... ਕਣਛਹਿਗੇ read as 'neigh'; uncertain. ਚਾਚਰ: the Holi song-and-dance revel.","meaning_pa":"ਕੰਧਾਰੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਹਿਣਹਿਣਾਉਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਰਣ-ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਚਾਚਰ ਮੱਚ ਉੱਠੇਗਾ।","note_pa":"ਕੰਧਾਰਿ: 'ਕੰਧਾਰੀ ਘੋੜੇ' ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਕਣਣੰਛਿ ... ਕਣਛਹਿਗੇ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਹਿਣਹਿਣਾਉਣਾ' ਲਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ। ਚਾਚਰ: ਹੋਲੀ ਦਾ ਗੀਤ-ਨਾਚ ਰੰਗ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[321],"number_text":"੩੨੧।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੁਹੂੰ ਓਰ ਤੇ ਸਾਂਗ ਅਨਚਹਿਗੀ। ਜਟਿ ਧੂਰਿ ਧਰਾਰੰਗਿ ਰਚਹਿਗੀ।","roman":"Duhoon or te saang anachhigee | jati dhoori dharaarangi rachhigee |","meaning_en":"Lances will be flung from both sides; Shiva, the matted-haired one, will delight in the play of the battlefield.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਨਚਹਿਗੀ: 'will be flung/drawn'; uncertain. ਜਟਿ ਧੂਰਿ read as Dhurjati (Shiva); ਧਰਾਰੰਗਿ ਰਚਹਿਗੀ read as 'will be absorbed in the play on the earth'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਾਂ ਪਾਸਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਰਛੇ ਸੁੱਟੇ ਜਾਣਗੇ; ਜਟਾਧਾਰੀ ਸ਼ਿਵ ਧਰਤੀ ਦੇ ਰਣ-ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਰਚ-ਮਿਚ ਜਾਵੇਗਾ।","note_pa":"ਅਨਚਹਿਗੀ: 'ਸੁੱਟੀ ਜਾਵੇਗੀ/ਖਿੱਚੀ ਜਾਵੇਗੀ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ। ਜਟਿ ਧੂਰਿ ਨੂੰ ਧੂਰਜਟੀ (ਸ਼ਿਵ) ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ; ਧਰਾਰੰਗਿ ਰਚਹਿਗੀ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਧਰਤੀ ਦੇ ਖੇਡ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੀਨ ਹੋਵੇਗੀ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਵਾਰਿ ਕਟਾਰੀਆ ਬਜਹਿਗੀ। ਘਟ ਸਾਵਣਿ ਜਾਣੁ ਸੁ ਗਜਹਿਗੀ। ੩੨੧।","roman":"Karvaari kataareeaa bajhigee | ghat saavni jaanu su gajhigee | 321 |","meaning_en":"Swords and daggers will clash, as though the clouds of Sawan were thundering.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਕਟਾਰੀਆਂ ਵੱਜਣਗੀਆਂ, ਮਾਨੋ ਸਾਵਣ ਦੇ ਬੱਦਲ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹੋਣ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[322],"number_text":"੩੨੨।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਟ ਦਾਤਨ ਪੀਸ ਰਿਸਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਦੁਹੁੰ ਓਰਿ ਤੁਰੰਗ ਨਚਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Bhat daatan pees risaavhige | duhun ori turang nachaavhige |","meaning_en":"Warriors, grinding their teeth, will rage; on both sides they will make their horses dance.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਦੰਦ ਪੀਸ ਕੇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਕਰਨਗੇ; ਦੋਹਾਂ ਪਾਸਿਓਂ ਉਹ ਆਪਣੇ ਘੋੜੇ ਨਚਾਉਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਬਾਣ ਕਮਾਣਣਿ ਛੋਰਹਿਗੇ। ਹਯ ਤ੍ਰਾਣ ਸਨਾਹਿਨ ਫੋਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੨।","roman":"Rani baan kamaanni chhorhige | hay traan sanaahin phorhige | 322 |","meaning_en":"In battle they will loose arrows from their bows and pierce the horses' armour and the coats of mail.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਕਮਾਨਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਣ ਛੱਡਣਗੇ ਅਤੇ ਘੋੜਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਕਵਚ ਤੇ ਜ਼ਰੀਂਹ ਤੋੜ ਦੇਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[323],"number_text":"੩੨੩।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਟਿ ਜਿਉ ਘਣਿ ਕੀ ਘੁਰਿ ਢੂਕਹਿਗੇ। ਮੁਖ ਮਾਰ ਦਸੋ ਦਿਸ ਕੂਕਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ghati jiu ghani kee ghuri dhookhige | mukh maar daso dis kookhige |","meaning_en":"Rumbling like massed clouds they will close in; crying 'Kill!' they will shout in all ten directions.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੱਦਲਾਂ ਦੀ ਗੜਗੜਾਹਟ ਵਾਂਗ ਉਹ ਨੇੜੇ ਆਉਣਗੇ; 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿ ਕੇ ਦਸਾਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਚੀਕਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਖ ਮਾਰ ਮਹਾ ਸੁਰ ਬੋਲਹਿਗੇ। ਗਿਰਿ ਕੰਚਨ ਜੇਮਿ ਨ ਡੋਲਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੩।","roman":"Mukh maar mahaa sur bolhige | giri kanchan jemi na dolhige | 323 |","meaning_en":"The great warriors will cry 'Kill!'; like the golden mountain (Sumeru) they will not waver.","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਿਰਿ ਕੰਚਨ: the golden mountain, i.e. Sumeru.","meaning_pa":"ਮਹਾਨ ਯੋਧੇ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿਣਗੇ; ਸੋਨੇ ਦੇ ਪਹਾੜ (ਸੁਮੇਰੂ) ਵਾਂਗ ਉਹ ਨਹੀਂ ਡੋਲਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਗਿਰਿ ਕੰਚਨ: ਸੋਨੇ ਦਾ ਪਹਾੜ, ਭਾਵ ਸੁਮੇਰੂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[324],"number_text":"੩੨੪।","page":753,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਯ ਕੋਟਿ ਗਜੀ ਗਜ ਜੁਝਹਿਗੇ। ਕਵਿ ਕੋਟਿ ਕਹਾ ਲਗ ਬੁਝਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Hay koti gajee gaj jujhhige | kavi koti kahaa lag bujhhige |","meaning_en":"Millions of horses, elephant-riders and elephants will fall fighting; how far could millions of poets comprehend it?","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲੱਖਾਂ ਘੋੜੇ, ਹਾਥੀ-ਸਵਾਰ ਅਤੇ ਹਾਥੀ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗਣਗੇ; ਕਰੋੜਾਂ ਕਵੀ ਵੀ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਕਿੱਥੋਂ ਤੱਕ ਸਮਝ ਸਕਣਗੇ?"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਨਿਹਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਜੈ ਸਦ ਨਿਨਦ ਪੁਕਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੪।","roman":"Gan dev adev nihaarhige | jai sad ninad pukaarhige | 324 |","meaning_en":"The ganas, gods and demons will watch, and will raise loud cries of 'Victory!'","page":753,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗਣ, ਦੇਵਤੇ ਅਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਵੇਖਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ 'ਜੈ!' ਦੇ ਉੱਚੇ ਨਾਅਰੇ ਲਾਉਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[325],"number_text":"੩੨੫।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਖ ਬੈਰਖ ਬਾਨ ਸੁਹਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣ ਰੰਗ ਸਮੈ ਫਹਰਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Lakh bairakh baan suhaavhige | ran rang samai phahraavhige |","meaning_en":"Lakhs of banners and pennants will look splendid; at the time of battle they will flutter.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਨ: here read as 'pennants'; it can also mean 'arrows'.","meaning_pa":"ਲੱਖਾਂ ਝੰਡੇ ਅਤੇ ਪਤਾਕੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਲੱਗਣਗੇ; ਰਣ-ਰੰਗ ਦੇ ਸਮੇਂ ਉਹ ਲਹਿਰਾਉਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਬਾਨ: ਇੱਥੇ 'ਪਤਾਕੇ' ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਇਸ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਤੀਰ' ਵੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰ ਢਾਲ ਢਲਾ ਢਲ ਢੂਕਹਿਗੇ। ਮੁਖ ਮਾਰ ਦਸੋ ਦਿਸਿ ਕੂਕਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੫।","roman":"Bar dhaal dhalaa dhal dhookhige | mukh maar daso disi kookhige | 325 |","meaning_en":"With fine shields they will close in, shield against shield; crying 'Kill!' they will shout in all ten directions.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੁੰਦਰ ਢਾਲਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਉਹ ਢਾਲ ਨਾਲ ਢਾਲ ਜੋੜ ਕੇ ਨੇੜੇ ਆਉਣਗੇ; 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿ ਕੇ ਦਸਾਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਚੀਕਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[326],"number_text":"੩੨੬।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਨ ਤ੍ਰਾਣ ਪੁਰਜਨ ਉਡਹਿਗੇ। ਗਡਵਾਰ ਗਾਡਾਗਡ ਗੁਡਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Tan traan purjan udhige | gadvaar gaadaagad gudhige |","meaning_en":"The pieces of body armour will fly apart; the firm-planted (weapons) will be driven in with a thud.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਡਵਾਰ ਗਾਡਾਗਡ ਗੁਡਹਿਗੇ: unclear; read as weapons (or those who stand firm) being driven deep; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸਰੀਰ ਦੇ ਕਵਚ ਦੇ ਟੁਕੜੇ ਉੱਡ ਜਾਣਗੇ; ਗੱਡੇ ਹੋਏ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਧੜੱਮ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਡੂੰਘੇ ਗੱਡੇ ਜਾਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਗਡਵਾਰ ਗਾਡਾਗਡ ਗੁਡਹਿਗੇ: ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ; ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਡੂੰਘੇ ਗੱਡੇ ਜਾਣ ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਬੈਰਖ ਬਾਨ ਝਮਕਹਿਗੇ। ਭਟ ਭੂਤ ਪਰੇਤ ਭਭਕਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੬।","roman":"Rani bairakh baan jhamakhige | bhat bhoot paret bhabhakhige | 326 |","meaning_en":"In battle the banners and arrows will glitter; warriors, ghosts and spirits will howl.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਭਕਹਿਗੇ: 'will howl/roar'; could also be 'will gush (with blood)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਾਣ ਅਤੇ ਝੰਡੇ ਚਮਕਣਗੇ; ਯੋਧੇ, ਭੂਤ ਅਤੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਚੀਕਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਭਭਕਹਿਗੇ: 'ਗਰਜਣਗੇ/ਚੀਕਣਗੇ'; ਇਸ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਲਹੂ ਵਹਿਣਾ' ਵੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[327],"number_text":"੩੨੭।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰ ਬੈਰਖ ਬਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਕਹੂੰ। ਰਣਿ ਬੋਲਤ ਆਜ ਲਗੇ ਅਜਹੂੰ।","roman":"Bar bairakh baan kripaan kahoon | rani bolat aaj lage ajhoon |","meaning_en":"Fine banners, arrows and swords here and there: of that battle men speak even to this day.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਣਿ ਬੋਲਤ ਆਜ ਲਗੇ ਅਜਹੂੰ: sense unclear; read as 'the battle is spoken of to this day'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੋਹਣੇ ਝੰਡੇ, ਬਾਣ ਅਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਇੱਥੇ-ਉੱਥੇ; ਉਸ ਯੁੱਧ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਅੱਜ ਤੱਕ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਰਣਿ ਬੋਲਤ ਆਜ ਲਗੇ ਅਜਹੂੰ: ਅਰਥ ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ; 'ਉਸ ਯੁੱਧ ਦੀ ਚਰਚਾ ਅੱਜ ਤੱਕ ਹੈ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹਿ ਕੇਸਨ ਤੇ ਭ੍ਰਮਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਦਸ ਹੂੰ ਦਿਸਿ ਤਾਕਿ ਚਲਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੭।","roman":"Gahi kesan te bhramaavhige | das hoon disi taaki chalaavhige | 327 |","meaning_en":"Seizing (foes) by the hair they will whirl them round, and, taking aim, hurl them in all ten directions.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵਾਲਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਫੜ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਘੁਮਾਉਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਨਿਸ਼ਾਨਾ ਬੰਨ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਦਸਾਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੁੱਟਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[328],"number_text":"੩੨੮।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰੁਣੰ ਬਰਣੰ ਭਟ ਪੇਖੀਅਹਿਗੇ। ਤਰਣੰ ਕਿਰਣੰ ਸਰ ਲੇਖੀਅਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Arunan barnan bhat pekheeahige | tarnan kirnan sar lekheeahige |","meaning_en":"The warriors will be seen red in colour; the arrows will seem like the rays of the sun.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਲਾਲ ਰੰਗ ਦੇ ਦਿਖਾਈ ਦੇਣਗੇ; ਬਾਣ ਸੂਰਜ ਦੀਆਂ ਕਿਰਨਾਂ ਵਰਗੇ ਜਾਪਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁ ਭਾਤਿ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਭਟ ਪਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਰੰਗ ਕਿੰਸੁਕ ਦੇਖਿ ਲਜਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੮।","roman":"Bahu bhaati prabhaa bhat paavhige | rang kinsuk dekhi lajaavhige | 328 |","meaning_en":"The warriors will take on splendour of many kinds; seeing their colour, the palas flower will be ashamed.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਿੰਸੁਕ: the kinsuk or palas tree, with bright red flowers.","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਕਈ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੀ ਚਮਕ ਪਾਉਣਗੇ; ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦਾ ਰੰਗ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਢਾਕ ਦਾ ਫੁੱਲ ਵੀ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦਾ ਹੋਵੇਗਾ।","note_pa":"ਕਿੰਸੁਕ: ਕਿੰਸੁਕ ਜਾਂ ਢਾਕ ਦਾ ਰੁੱਖ, ਜਿਸ ਦੇ ਲਾਲ ਫੁੱਲ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[329],"number_text":"੩੨੯।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਜ ਬਾਜ ਰਥੀ ਰਥ ਜੁਝਹਿਗੇ। ਕਵਿ ਲੋਗ ਕਹਾ ਲਗਿ ਬੁਝਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gaj baaj rathee rath jujhhige | kavi log kahaa lagi bujhhige |","meaning_en":"Elephants, horses, charioteers and chariots will fall fighting; how far can poets comprehend it?","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀ, ਘੋੜੇ, ਰਥਵਾਨ ਅਤੇ ਰਥ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗਣਗੇ; ਕਿੰਨੇ ਕੁ ਕਵੀ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਸਮਝ ਸਕਣਗੇ?"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਸੁ ਜੀਤ ਕੈ ਗੀਤ ਬਨਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਜੁਗ ਚਾਰ ਲਗੈ ਜਸੁ ਗਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ੩੨੯।","roman":"Jasu jeet kai geet banaavhige | jug chaar lagai jasu gaavhige | 329 |","meaning_en":"Having won glory, they will make songs of it; for four ages they will sing that glory.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਤ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਇਸ ਦੇ ਜਸ ਦੇ ਗੀਤ ਬਣਾਉਣਗੇ; ਚਾਰ ਜੁੱਗਾਂ ਤੱਕ ਉਹ ਇਸ ਜਸ ਨੂੰ ਗਾਉਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[330],"number_text":"੩੩੦।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਚਲੇਸ ਦੁਹੂੰ ਦਿਸਿ ਧਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਮੁਖਿ ਮਾਰੁ ਸੁ ਮਾਰੁ ਉਘਾਵਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Achles duhoon disi dhaavhige | mukhi maaru su maaru ughaavhige |","meaning_en":"The steadfast chiefs will charge from both sides, shouting 'Kill! Kill!' with their mouths.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਚਲੇਸ: 'lords who stand firm' (or 'lords of mountains'); uncertain. ਉਘਾਵਹਿਗੇ read as 'will shout out'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਅਚਲ ਸਰਦਾਰ ਦੋਹਾਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਦੌੜਨਗੇ, 'ਮਾਰੋ! ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿ ਕੇ ਉੱਚੀ ਬੋਲਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਅਚਲੇਸ: 'ਅਡੋਲ ਖੜ੍ਹਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਸਰਦਾਰ' (ਜਾਂ 'ਪਹਾੜਾਂ ਦੇ ਸੁਆਮੀ'); ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ। ਉਘਾਵਹਿਗੇ: 'ਉੱਚੀ ਬੋਲਣਗੇ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਥਿਯਾਰ ਦੁਹੂੰ ਦਿਸਿ ਛੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ਸਰ ਓਘ ਰਣੰ ਧਨੁ ਟੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੦।","roman":"Hathiyaar duhoon disi chhoothige | sar ogh ranan dhanu toothige | 330 |","meaning_en":"Weapons will be loosed from both sides; with the floods of arrows, bows will break in the battle.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਾਂ ਪਾਸਿਓਂ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਛੱਡੇ ਜਾਣਗੇ; ਬਾਣਾਂ ਦੇ ਹੜ੍ਹ ਨਾਲ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਮਾਨਾਂ ਟੁੱਟ ਜਾਣਗੀਆਂ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਹਰਿ ਬੋਲ ਮਨਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਬੋਲ ਮਨਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Hari bol manaa chhand","meaning_en":"Har Bol Mana metre.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਰਿ ਬੋਲ ਮਨਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[331],"number_text":"੩੩੧।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਟ ਗਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ਘਨ ਲਾਜਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Bhat gaajhige | ghan laajhige |","meaning_en":"The warriors will roar; the clouds will be shamed.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਗਰਜਣਗੇ; ਬੱਦਲ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੋਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਲ ਜੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ਸਰ ਛੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੧।","roman":"Dal joothige | sar chhoothige | 331 |","meaning_en":"The armies will clash; arrows will be loosed.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਫੌਜਾਂ ਭਿੜਨਗੀਆਂ; ਬਾਣ ਛੱਡੇ ਜਾਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[332],"number_text":"੩੩੨।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਬਰਖਹਿਗੇ। ਧਨੁ ਕਰਖਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Sar barakhhige | dhanu karakhhige |","meaning_en":"Arrows will rain down; bows will be drawn.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਾਣ ਵਰ੍ਹਣਗੇ; ਕਮਾਨਾਂ ਖਿੱਚੀਆਂ ਜਾਣਗੀਆਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸਿ ਬਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ਰਣਿ ਸਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੨।","roman":"Asi baajhige | rani saajhige | 332 |","meaning_en":"Swords will strike; (warriors) will look splendid in battle.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਣਿ ਸਾਜਹਿਗੇ: 'will be adorned/arrayed in battle'.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਵੱਜਣਗੀਆਂ; (ਯੋਧੇ) ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਲੱਗਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਰਣਿ ਸਾਜਹਿਗੇ: 'ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਜੇ ਹੋਏ ਹੋਣਗੇ'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[333],"number_text":"੩੩੩।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਅ ਡਿਗਹਿਗੇ। ਭਯ ਭਿਗਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Bhooa dighige | bhay bhighige |","meaning_en":"They will fall to the ground; (some) will be soaked with fear,","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਯ ਭਿਗਹਿਗੇ: lit. 'will be drenched in fear'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਡਿੱਗਣਗੇ; (ਕੁਝ) ਡਰ ਨਾਲ ਭਿੱਜ ਜਾਣਗੇ,","note_pa":"ਭਯ ਭਿਗਹਿਗੇ: ਸ਼ਾਬਦਿਕ 'ਡਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਿੱਜਣਗੇ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਠ ਭਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ਨਹੀ ਲਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੩।","roman":"Uth bhaajhige | nahee laajhige | 333 |","meaning_en":"will get up and run away, and will feel no shame.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉੱਠ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਜਾਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਕੋਈ ਸ਼ਰਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਆਵੇਗੀ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[334],"number_text":"੩੩੪।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਣ ਦੇਖਹਿਗੇ। ਜਯ ਲੇਖਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gan dekhhige | jay lekhhige |","meaning_en":"The ganas will watch and record the victory.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗਣ ਵੇਖਣਗੇ ਅਤੇ ਜਿੱਤ ਲਿਖਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਸੁ ਗਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ਮੁਸਕਯਾਵਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੪।","roman":"Jasu gaavhige | musakyaavhige | 334 |","meaning_en":"They will sing praise and smile.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਜਸ ਗਾਉਣਗੇ ਅਤੇ ਮੁਸਕਰਾਉਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[335],"number_text":"੩੩੫।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਣ ਪੂਰਹਿਗੇ। ਰਜਿ ਰੂਰਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Pran poorhige | raji roorhige |","meaning_en":"They will fulfil their vows; content, they will look fine.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਜਿ ਰੂਰਹਿਗੇ: 'satisfied, they will look handsome'; ਰਜਿ could also be 'covered in dust'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਆਪਣੀਆਂ ਸਹੁੰਆਂ ਪੂਰੀਆਂ ਕਰਨਗੇ; ਸੰਤੁਸ਼ਟ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਲੱਗਣਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਰਜਿ ਰੂਰਹਿਗੇ: 'ਸੰਤੁਸ਼ਟ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਲੱਗਣਗੇ'; ਰਜਿ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਧੂੜ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੇ' ਵੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣਿ ਰਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ਗਣ ਲਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੫।","roman":"Rani raajhige | gan laajhige | 335 |","meaning_en":"They will shine in battle; the ganas will be put to shame.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਸ਼ੋਭਣਗੇ; ਗਣ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੋਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[336],"number_text":"੩੩੬।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਿਸ ਮੰਡਹਿਗੇ। ਸਰ ਛੰਡਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Ris mandhige | sar chhandhige |","meaning_en":"Filled with rage, they will loose arrows.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਭਰ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਬਾਣ ਛੱਡਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਜੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ਅਸਿ ਟੂਟਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੬।","roman":"Ran joothige | asi toothige | 336 |","meaning_en":"They will clash in battle; swords will break.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਭਿੜਨਗੇ; ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਟੁੱਟ ਜਾਣਗੀਆਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[337],"number_text":"੩੩੭।","page":754,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਲ ਗਾਜਹਿਗੇ। ਨਹੀ ਭਾਜਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gal gaajhige | nahee bhaajhige |","meaning_en":"They will roar from their throats, and will not run away.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਗਲੇ ਤੋਂ ਗਰਜਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਭੱਜਣਗੇ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸਿ ਝਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ਅਰਿ ਮਾਰਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੭।","roman":"Asi jhaarhige | ari maarhige | 337 |","meaning_en":"They will swing their swords and strike down the foe.","page":754,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਘੁੰਮਾਉਣਗੇ ਅਤੇ ਵੈਰੀ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਨਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[338],"number_text":"੩੩੮।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਜ ਜੂਝਹਿਗੇ। ਹਯ ਲੂਝਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Gaj joojhhige | hay loojhhige |","meaning_en":"Elephants will fall fighting; horses will struggle.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗਣਗੇ; ਘੋੜੇ ਸੰਘਰਸ਼ ਕਰਨਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਟ ਮਾਰੀਅਹਿਗੇ। ਭਵ ਤਾਰੀਅਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੮।","roman":"Bhat maareeahige | bhav taareeahige | 338 |","meaning_en":"Warriors will be slain, and carried across the ocean of the world.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਮਾਰੇ ਜਾਣਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਸੰਸਾਰ-ਸਾਗਰ ਤੋਂ ਪਾਰ ਲੰਘਾਏ ਜਾਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[339],"number_text":"੩੩੯।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਿਵ ਦੇਖਹਿਗੇ। ਜਯ ਲੇਖਹਿਗੇ।","roman":"Div dekhhige | jay lekhhige |","meaning_en":"The gods will watch and record the victory.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੇਵਤੇ ਵੇਖਣਗੇ ਅਤੇ ਜਿੱਤ ਲਿਖਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਨਿ ਭਾਖਹਿਗੇ। ਚਿਤਿ ਰਾਖਹਿਗੇ। ੩੩੯।","roman":"Dhani bhaakhhige | chiti raakhhige | 339 |","meaning_en":"They will say 'Blessed!' and keep it in their minds.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ 'ਧੰਨ!' ਕਹਿਣਗੇ ਅਤੇ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੱਖਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[340],"number_text":"੩੪੦।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਯ ਕਾਰਣ ਹੈਂ। ਅਰਿ ਹਾਰਣ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Jay kaaran hain | ari haaran hain |","meaning_en":"He is the cause of victory; He is the vanquisher of foes.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"From here the verses describe Kalki.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਜਿੱਤ ਦਾ ਕਾਰਨ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਹਰਾਉਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਇੱਥੋਂ ਅੱਗੇ ਛੰਦ ਕਲਕੀ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਲ ਖੰਡਨੁ ਹੈਂ। ਮਹਿ ਮੰਡਨੁ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੦।","roman":"Khal khandnu hain | mahi mandnu hain | 340 |","meaning_en":"He is the destroyer of the wicked; He is the adornment of the earth.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਦੁਸ਼ਟਾਂ ਦਾ ਨਾਸ਼ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਧਰਤੀ ਦਾ ਸ਼ਿੰਗਾਰ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[341],"number_text":"੩੪੧।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਦੂਖਨ ਹੈਂ। ਭਵ ਭੂਖਨ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Ari dookhan hain | bhav bhookhan hain |","meaning_en":"He is the tormentor of foes; He is the ornament of the world.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਦੁੱਖ ਦੇਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਦਾ ਗਹਿਣਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਹਿ ਮੰਡਨੁ ਹੈਂ। ਅਰਿ ਡੰਡਨੁ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੧।","roman":"Mahi mandnu hain | ari dandnu hain | 341 |","meaning_en":"He is the adornment of the earth; He is the punisher of foes.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਰਤੀ ਦਾ ਸ਼ਿੰਗਾਰ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਸਜ਼ਾ ਦੇਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[342],"number_text":"੩੪੨।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਲ ਗਾਹਨ ਹੈਂ। ਅਸਿ ਬਾਹਨ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Dal gaahan hain | asi baahan hain |","meaning_en":"He tramples through armies; He wields the sword.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਫ਼ੌਜਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਰੌਂਦਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਚਲਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਕਾਰਨ ਹੈਂ। ਅਯ ਧਾਰਨ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੨।","roman":"Jag kaaran hain | ay dhaaran hain | 342 |","meaning_en":"He is the cause of the world; He bears arms of iron.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਯ ਧਾਰਨ: read as 'bearer of iron (weapons)'; ਅਯ may also mean 'good fortune'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਦਾ ਕਾਰਨ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਲੋਹੇ ਦੇ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਅਯ ਧਾਰਨ: 'ਲੋਹੇ (ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ) ਦਾ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਯ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਭਾਗ' ਵੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[343],"number_text":"੩੪੩।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨ ਮੋਹਨ ਹੈਂ। ਸੁਭ ਸੋਹਨ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Man mohan hain | subh sohan hain |","meaning_en":"He enchants the mind; He is auspiciously beautiful.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਮੋਹ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸ਼ੁਭ ਰੂਪ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੋਹਣਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਤਾਪਨ ਹੈਂ। ਜਗ ਜਾਪਨ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੩।","roman":"Ari taapan hain | jag jaapan hain | 343 |","meaning_en":"He scorches foes; the world repeats His name.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਝੁਲਸਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਸੰਸਾਰ ਉਸ ਦਾ ਨਾਮ ਜਪਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[344],"number_text":"੩੪੪।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਣ ਪੂਰਣ ਹੈਂ। ਅਰਿ ਚੂਰਣ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Pran pooran hain | ari chooran hain |","meaning_en":"He fulfils vows; He grinds foes to powder.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪ੍ਰਣ ਪੂਰੇ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਚੂਰ-ਚੂਰ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰ ਬਰਖਨ ਹੈਂ। ਧਨੁ ਕਰਖਨ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੪।","roman":"Sar barkhan hain | dhanu karkhan hain | 344 |","meaning_en":"He rains arrows; He draws the bow.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬਾਣ ਵਰ੍ਹਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਕਮਾਨ ਖਿੱਚਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[345],"number_text":"੩੪੫।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੀਅ ਮੋਹਨ ਹੈਂ। ਛਬਿ ਸੋਹਨ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Teea mohan hain | chhabi sohan hain |","meaning_en":"He enchants women; He is beautiful in His splendour.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਮੋਹ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਆਪਣੀ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੋਹਣਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨ ਭਾਵਨ ਹੈਂ। ਘਨ ਸਾਵਨ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੫।","roman":"Man bhaavan hain | ghan saavan hain | 345 |","meaning_en":"He is pleasing to the heart; He is (dark and welcome) like the clouds of Sawan.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਭਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸਾਵਣ ਦੇ ਬੱਦਲਾਂ ਵਾਂਗ (ਗੂੜ੍ਹਾ ਅਤੇ ਪਿਆਰਾ) ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[346],"number_text":"੩੪੬।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਵ ਭੂਖਨ ਹੈਂ। ਭ੍ਰਿਤ ਪੂਖਨ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Bhav bhookhan hain | bhrit pookhan hain |","meaning_en":"He is the ornament of the world; He nourishes His servants.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭ੍ਰਿਤ ਪੂਖਨ: read as 'nourisher of servants'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਦਾ ਗਹਿਣਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਆਪਣੇ ਸੇਵਕਾਂ ਦਾ ਪਾਲਣ-ਪੋਸ਼ਣ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਭ੍ਰਿਤ ਪੂਖਨ: 'ਸੇਵਕਾਂ ਦਾ ਪਾਲਕ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸਿ ਆਨਨ ਹੈਂ। ਸਮ ਭਾਨਨ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੬।","roman":"Sasi aanan hain | sam bhaanan hain | 346 |","meaning_en":"His face is like the moon; He is like the sun.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦਾ ਮੁਖੜਾ ਚੰਦ ਵਰਗਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸੂਰਜ ਵਰਗਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[347],"number_text":"੩੪੭।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਘਾਵਨ ਹੈ। ਸੁਖ ਦਾਵਨ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Ari ghaavan hai | sukh daavan hain |","meaning_en":"He wounds foes; He gives comfort.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਘਾਇਲ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸੁਖ ਦਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਨ ਘੋਰਨ ਹੈਂ। ਸਮ ਮੋਰਨ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੭।","roman":"Ghan ghoran hain | sam moran hain | 347 |","meaning_en":"He is like thundering clouds; (to Him His devotees) are like peacocks.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਮ ਮੋਰਨ: lit. 'like peacocks' (who rejoice at thunder); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਬੱਦਲਾਂ ਵਰਗਾ ਹੈ; (ਉਸ ਵੱਲ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਭਗਤ) ਮੋਰਾਂ ਵਰਗੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਸਮ ਮੋਰਨ: ਸ਼ਾਬਦਿਕ 'ਮੋਰਾਂ ਵਰਗੇ' (ਜੋ ਗਰਜ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਖੁਸ਼ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ); ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[348],"number_text":"੩੪੮।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗਤੇਸ੍ਵਰ ਹੈਂ। ਕਰੁਨਾਕਰ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Jagtesvar hain | karunaakar hain |","meaning_en":"He is the Lord of the world; He is a mine of compassion.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਜਗਤ ਦਾ ਸੁਆਮੀ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਦਇਆ ਦਾ ਸਾਗਰ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਵ ਭੂਖਨ ਹੈਂ। ਅਰਿ ਦੂਖਨ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੮।","roman":"Bhav bhookhan hain | ari dookhan hain | 348 |","meaning_en":"He is the ornament of the world; He torments foes.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਦਾ ਗਹਿਣਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਦੁੱਖ ਦਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[349],"number_text":"੩੪੯।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਬਿ ਸੋਭਿਤ ਹੈਂ। ਤ੍ਰੀਅ ਲੋਭਿਤ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Chhabi sobhit hain | treea lobhit hain |","meaning_en":"He shines with beauty; women are drawn to Him.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਨਾਲ ਸ਼ੋਭਦਾ ਹੈ; ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਉਸ ਵੱਲ ਖਿੱਚੀਆਂ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦ੍ਰਿਗ ਛਾਜਤ ਹੈਂ। ਮ੍ਰਿਗ ਲਾਜਤ ਹੈਂ। ੩੪੯।","roman":"Drig chhaajat hain | mrig laajat hain | 349 |","meaning_en":"His eyes are splendid; the deer are put to shame.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੀਆਂ ਅੱਖਾਂ ਸੋਹਣੀਆਂ ਲੱਗਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ; ਹਿਰਨ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[350],"number_text":"੩੫੦।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਣੀ ਪਤਿ ਸੇ। ਨਲਣੀ ਧਰ ਸੇ।","roman":"Harnee pati se | nalnee dhar se |","meaning_en":"Like the stag (lord of does), like the lotus-bearing (pool):","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਰਣੀ ਪਤਿ ਸੇ, ਨਲਣੀ ਧਰ ਸੇ: sense unclear; perhaps describing His eyes; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਹਿਰਨੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਪਤੀ ਵਰਗਾ, ਕਮਲਾਂ ਵਾਲੇ ਤਾਲਾਬ ਵਰਗਾ:","note_pa":"ਹਰਣੀ ਪਤਿ ਸੇ, ਨਲਣੀ ਧਰ ਸੇ: ਅਰਥ ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ; ਸ਼ਾਇਦ ਉਸ ਦੀਆਂ ਅੱਖਾਂ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੁਨਾਬੁਦ ਹੈਂ। ਸੁ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਧਰ ਹੈਂ। ੩੫੦।","roman":"Karunaabud hain | su prabhaa dhar hain | 350 |","meaning_en":"He is a cloud of compassion; He bears great splendour.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰੁਨਾਬੁਦ: karuna + ambud, 'cloud of compassion'.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਦਇਆ ਦਾ ਬੱਦਲ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੱਡੀ ਚਮਕ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਕਰੁਨਾਬੁਦ: ਕਰੁਣਾ + ਅੰਬੁਦ, 'ਦਇਆ ਦਾ ਬੱਦਲ'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[351],"number_text":"੩੫੧।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲਿ ਕਾਰਣ ਹੈ। ਭਵ ਉਧਾਰਣ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kali kaaran hai | bhav udhaaran hai |","meaning_en":"He has come for the sake of the Kali age; He is the saviour of the world.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲਿ ਕਾਰਣ: 'for the sake of the Kali age'; could also be 'cause of strife'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਕਲਿਯੁਗ ਦੇ ਕਾਰਨ ਆਇਆ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਦਾ ਉੱਧਾਰ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਕਲਿ ਕਾਰਣ: 'ਕਲਿਯੁਗ ਦੇ ਕਾਰਨ'; ਇਸ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਝਗੜੇ ਦਾ ਕਾਰਨ' ਵੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਬਿ ਛਾਜਤ ਹੈ। ਸੁਰ ਲਾਜਤ ਹੈ। ੩੫੧।","roman":"Chhabi chhaajat hai | sur laajat hai | 351 |","meaning_en":"His beauty is splendid; the gods are put to shame.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਚਮਕਦੀ ਹੈ; ਦੇਵਤੇ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[352],"number_text":"੩੫੨।","page":755,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸਯੁਪਾਸਕ ਹੈ। ਅਰਿ ਨਾਸਕ ਹੈ।","roman":"Asyupaasak hai | ari naasak hai |","meaning_en":"He is a worshipper of the sword; He destroys foes.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਦਾ ਉਪਾਸਕ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਨਾਸ਼ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਘਾਇਕ ਹੈ। ਸੁਖਦਾਇਕ ਹੈ। ੩੫੨।","roman":"Ari ghaaik hai | sukhdaaik hai | 352 |","meaning_en":"He kills foes; He gives comfort.","page":755,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸੁੱਖ ਦੇਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[353],"number_text":"੩੫੩।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਲਜੇਛਣ ਹੈ। ਪ੍ਰਣ ਪੇਛਣ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jaljechhan hai | pran pechhan hai |","meaning_en":"He is lotus-eyed; He keeps watch over His vow.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਲਜੇਛਣ: jalaj (lotus) + ikshan (eye). ਪ੍ਰਣ ਪੇਛਣ: read as 'one who keeps His vow in view'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਕਮਲ-ਨੈਣ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਆਪਣੇ ਪ੍ਰਣ ਦੀ ਰਖਵਾਲੀ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਜਲਜੇਛਣ: ਜਲਜ (ਕਮਲ) + ਈਕਸ਼ਣ (ਨੈਣ)। ਪ੍ਰਣ ਪੇਛਣ: 'ਆਪਣੇ ਪ੍ਰਣ ਨੂੰ ਨਜ਼ਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੱਖਣ ਵਾਲਾ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਿ ਮਰਦਨ ਹੈ। ਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਕਰਦਨ ਹੈ। ੩੫੩।","roman":"Ari mardan hai | mrit kardan hai | 353 |","meaning_en":"He crushes foes; He brings (them) death.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਕੁਚਲਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਮੌਤ ਦਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[354],"number_text":"੩੫੪।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਣੀਧਰ ਹੈ। ਕਰਣੀਕਰ ਹੈ।","roman":"Dharneedhar hai | karneekar hai |","meaning_en":"He is the upholder of the earth; He is the doer of all deeds.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਧਰਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਸਾਰੇ ਕੰਮ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਨੁ ਕਰਖਨ ਹੈ। ਸਰ ਬਖਣ ਹੈ। ੩੫੪।","roman":"Dhanu karkhan hai | sar bakhan hai | 354 |","meaning_en":"He draws the bow; He rains arrows.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਖਣ: printed so; read as ਬਰਖਣ ('raining').","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਕਮਾਨ ਖਿੱਚਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਬਾਣ ਵਰ੍ਹਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਬਖਣ: ਛਾਪੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਇਸੇ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਹੈ; ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਬਰਖਣ ('ਵਰ੍ਹਨਾ') ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[355],"number_text":"੩੫੫।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਟਿ ਛੈਲ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ। ਲਖਿ ਚੰਦ ਲਭਾ।","roman":"Chhati chhail prabhaa | lakhi chand labhaa |","meaning_en":"He has the radiance of a gallant youth; seeing Him, the moon is enamoured.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲਖਿ ਚੰਦ ਲਭਾ: read as 'the moon, seeing (Him), is charmed'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੀ ਚਮਕ ਕਿਸੇ ਛੈਲ ਜਵਾਨ ਵਰਗੀ ਹੈ; ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਚੰਦ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਲਖਿ ਚੰਦ ਲਭਾ: 'ਚੰਦ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਬਿ ਸੋਹਤ ਹੈ। ਤ੍ਰੀਯ ਮੋਹਤ ਹੈ। ੩੫੫।","roman":"Chhabi sohat hai | treey mohat hai | 355 |","meaning_en":"His beauty shines; He enchants women.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਸ਼ੋਭਦੀ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਮੋਹ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[356],"number_text":"੩੫੬।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਰਣੰ ਬਰਣੰ। ਧਰਣੰ ਧਰਣੰ।","roman":"Arnan barnan | dharnan dharnan |","meaning_en":"Red of hue, upholder of the earth,","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਰਣੰ: read as ਅਰੁਣੰ, 'red'.","meaning_pa":"ਲਾਲ ਰੰਗ ਵਾਲਾ, ਧਰਤੀ ਦਾ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ,","note_pa":"ਅਰਣੰ: ਅਰੁਣੰ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ, 'ਲਾਲ'।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਿ ਸੀ ਕਰਿ ਭਾ। ਸੁ ਸੁਭੰਤ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ। ੩੫੬।","roman":"Hari see kari bhaa | su subhant prabhaa | 356 |","meaning_en":"He has a radiance like the sun's rays; His splendour is beautiful.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਰਿ ਸੀ ਕਰਿ ਭਾ: ਹਰਿ read as 'the sun', ਕਰਿ as 'rays'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੀ ਚਮਕ ਸੂਰਜ ਦੀਆਂ ਕਿਰਨਾਂ ਵਰਗੀ ਹੈ; ਉਸ ਦਾ ਤੇਜ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਹਰਿ ਸੀ ਕਰਿ ਭਾ: ਹਰਿ ਨੂੰ 'ਸੂਰਜ' ਅਤੇ ਕਰਿ ਨੂੰ 'ਕਿਰਨਾਂ' ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[357],"number_text":"੩੫੭।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਣਾਲਯ ਹੈ। ਅਰਿ ਘਾਲਯ ਹੈ।","roman":"Sarnaalay hai | ari ghaalay hai |","meaning_en":"He is the home of refuge; He destroys foes.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸ਼ਰਨ ਦਾ ਘਰ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਨਾਸ਼ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਟਿ ਛੈਲ ਘਨੇ। ਅਤਿ ਰੂਪ ਸਨੇ। ੩੫੭।","roman":"Chhati chhail ghane | ati roop sane | 357 |","meaning_en":"He is a most handsome, gallant youth, steeped in great beauty.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬਹੁਤ ਸੋਹਣਾ ਛੈਲ ਜਵਾਨ ਹੈ, ਅਤਿ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੰਗਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[358],"number_text":"੩੫੮।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨ ਮੋਹਤ ਹੈ। ਛਬਿ ਸੋਹਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Man mohat hai | chhabi sohat hai |","meaning_en":"He enchants the mind; His beauty shines.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਮੋਹ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਉਸ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਸ਼ੋਭਦੀ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲ ਕਾਰਨ ਹੈ। ਕਰਣਾਧਰ ਹੈ। ੩੫੮।","roman":"Kal kaaran hai | karnaadhar hai | 358 |","meaning_en":"He is the cause of all skill and power; He is the bearer of compassion.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰਣਾਧਰ: read as karuna-dhar ('bearer of compassion'); could also be karnadhar ('helmsman'); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸਾਰੀ ਕਲਾ ਅਤੇ ਸ਼ਕਤੀ ਦਾ ਕਾਰਨ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਦਇਆ ਨੂੰ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਕਰਣਾਧਰ: 'ਦਇਆ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਇਸ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਮਲਾਹ' (ਕਰਣਧਾਰ) ਵੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[359],"number_text":"੩੫੯।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਰੂਪ ਸਨੇ। ਜਨੁ ਮੈਨੁ ਬਨੇ।","roman":"Ati roop sane | janu mainu bane |","meaning_en":"Steeped in great beauty, He is like Kamadeva, the god of love, himself.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੈਨੁ: Kamadeva.","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੰਗਿਆ, ਉਹ ਮਾਨੋ ਕਾਮਦੇਵ ਹੀ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਮੈਨੁ: ਕਾਮਦੇਵ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਤਿ ਕ੍ਰਾਂਤਿ ਧਰੇ। ਸਸਿ ਸੋਭ ਹਰੇ। ੩੫੯।","roman":"Ati kraanti dhare | sasi sobh hare | 359 |","meaning_en":"Bearing great radiance, He takes away the moon's glory.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੱਡੀ ਚਮਕ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰ ਕੇ, ਉਹ ਚੰਦ ਦੀ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਹਰ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[360],"number_text":"੩੬੦।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸ੍ਯ ਉਪਾਸਿਕ ਹੈਂ। ਅਰਿ ਨਾਸਿਕ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Asy upaasik hain | ari naasik hain |","meaning_en":"He is a worshipper of the sword; He destroys foes.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਦਾ ਉਪਾਸਕ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਨਾਸ਼ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰ ਦਾਇਕ ਹੈਂ। ਪ੍ਰਭ ਪਾਇਕ ਹੈਂ। ੩੬੦।","roman":"Bar daaik hain | prabh paaik hain | 360 |","meaning_en":"He is the giver of boons; He is the servant of the Lord.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪ੍ਰਭ ਪਾਇਕ: read as 'the Lord's servant (paik)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਵਰ ਦੇਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ; ਉਹ ਪ੍ਰਭੂ ਦਾ ਸੇਵਕ ਹੈ।","note_pa":"ਪ੍ਰਭ ਪਾਇਕ: 'ਪ੍ਰਭੂ ਦਾ ਸੇਵਕ (ਪਾਇਕ)' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Sangeet bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Sangeet Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[361],"number_text":"੩੬੧।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬੀਰੰ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੂਟੇ। ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤੀਰੰ। ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛੂਟੇ।","roman":"Baagardan beeran jaagardan joote | taagardan teeran | chhaagardan chhoote |","meaning_en":"The warriors clashed; arrows were loosed.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"In this metre each word is preceded by a rhythmic sound-word ending in -ਗੜਦੰ (ਬਾਗੜਦੰ, ਜਾਗੜਦੰ, etc.), which echoes the word after it; these are left untranslated.","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਭਿੜ ਗਏ; ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡੇ ਗਏ।","note_pa":"ਇਸ ਛੰਦ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਰ ਸ਼ਬਦ ਤੋਂ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਤਾਲ ਵਾਲੇ ਧੁਨੀ-ਸ਼ਬਦ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਜੋ ਅਗਲੇ ਸ਼ਬਦ ਵਾਂਗ ਹੀ -ਗੜਦੰ ਨਾਲ ਖਤਮ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਇਹਨਾਂ ਦਾ ਅਨੁਵਾਦ ਨਹੀਂ ਕੀਤਾ ਗਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੁਆਰੰ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੂਝੇ। ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੋਪੇ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੁਝੈ। ੩੬੧।","roman":"Saagardan suaaran jaagardan joojhe | kaagardan kope raagardan rujhai | 361 |","meaning_en":"The horsemen fought; in fury they were locked in combat.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਘੋੜ-ਸਵਾਰ ਲੜੇ; ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਆਪਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਲਝ ਗਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[362],"number_text":"੩੬੨।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਾਚਿਓ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਧੰ। ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੋਧਾ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕ੍ਰੁੰਧੰ।","roman":"Maagardan maachio jaagardan judhan | jaagardan jodhaa kaagardan krundhan |","meaning_en":"War broke out; the warriors were enraged.","page":756,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲੜਾਈ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਹੋ ਗਈ; ਯੋਧੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਰ ਗਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸਾਂਗੰ ਡਾਗੜਦੰ ਡਾਰੇ। ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬੀਰੰ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਉਤਾਰੇ। ੩੬੨।","roman":"Saagardan saangan daagardan daare | baagardan beeran aagardan utaare | 362 |","meaning_en":"Lances were thrust; warriors were brought down.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਉਤਾਰੇ: 'brought down', i.e. unhorsed or cut down.","meaning_pa":"ਬਰਛੇ ਚਲਾਏ ਗਏ; ਯੋਧੇ ਹੇਠਾਂ ਡੇਗੇ ਗਏ।","note_pa":"ਉਤਾਰੇ: 'ਘੋੜਿਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਹੇਠਾਂ ਸੁੱਟੇ ਗਏ', ਭਾਵ ਵੱਢੇ ਗਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[363],"number_text":"੩੬੩।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤੈ ਕੈ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਆਣੰ। ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛੋਰੈ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਣੰ।","roman":"Taagardan tai kai jaagardan juaanan | chhaagardan chhorai baagardan baanan |","meaning_en":"Growing hot, the young warriors loosed arrows.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤੈ ਕੈ: read as 'growing heated'; could be 'taking aim'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਗਰਮ ਜੋਸ਼ ਵਿੱਚ ਆ ਕੇ ਜਵਾਨ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੇ ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡੇ।","note_pa":"ਤੈ ਕੈ: 'ਜੋਸ਼ ਵਿੱਚ ਆ ਕੇ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ 'ਨਿਸ਼ਾਨਾ ਬੰਨ੍ਹ ਕੇ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੂਝੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਜੀ। ਡਾਗੜਦੰ ਡੋਲੈ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤਾਜੀ। ੩੬੩।","roman":"Jaagardan joojhe baagardan baajee | daagardan dolai taagardan taajee | 363 |","meaning_en":"Horses fell fighting; the Arab steeds staggered.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਜੀ: Tazi, Arab horses.","meaning_pa":"ਘੋੜੇ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗੇ; ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ ਡੋਲਣ ਲੱਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਤਾਜੀ: ਅਰਬੀ ਘੋੜੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[364],"number_text":"੩੬੪।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖਾਗੜਦੰ ਖੂਨੀ ਖਯਾਗੜਦੰ ਖੇਤੰ। ਝਾਗੜਦੰ ਝੂਝੇ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਅਚੇਤੰ।","roman":"Khaagardan khoonee khayaagardan khetan | jhaagardan jhoojhe aagardan achetan |","meaning_en":"The battlefield was bloody; those who fought lay senseless.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਲਹੂ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੀ ਹੋਈ ਸੀ; ਲੜਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਬੇਹੋਸ਼ ਪਏ ਸਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਗੜਦੰ ਉਠੇ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੋਪੇ। ਡਾਗੜਦੰ ਡਾਰੇ ਧਾਗੜਦੰ ਧੋਪੇ। ੩੬੪।","roman":"Aagardan uthe kaagardan kope | daagardan daare dhaagardan dhope | 364 |","meaning_en":"They rose up in fury and struck down (foes) with their swords.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧੋਪੇ: read as 'with the dhop (straight sword)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਉੱਠੇ ਅਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਡੇਗਿਆ।","note_pa":"ਧੋਪੇ: 'ਧੋਪ' (ਸਿੱਧੀ ਤਲਵਾਰ) ਨਾਲ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[365],"number_text":"੩੬੫।","page":756,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਗੜਦੰ ਨਾਚੇ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੁਦ੍ਰ੍ਰੰ। ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭਾਜੇ ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛੁਦ੍ਰੰ।","roman":"Naagardan naache raagardan rudrran | bhaagardan bhaaje chhaagardan chhudran |","meaning_en":"Rudra (Shiva) danced; the petty-hearted fled.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ੍ਰੰ: printed so.","meaning_pa":"ਰੁਦਰ (ਸ਼ਿਵ) ਨੱਚਿਆ; ਛੋਟੇ ਦਿਲ ਵਾਲੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ।","note_pa":"ਰੁਦ੍ਰ੍ਰੰ: ਛਾਪੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਇਸੇ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਛਪਿਆ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਝੇ ਵਾਗੜਦੰ ਵੀਰੰ। ਲਾਗੜਦੰ ਲਾਗੇ। ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤੀਰੰ। ੩੬੫।","roman":"Jaagardan jujhe vaagardan veeran | laagardan laage | taagardan teeran | 365 |","meaning_en":"Warriors fell fighting; arrows struck home.","page":756,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗੇ; ਤੀਰ ਜਾ ਲੱਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[366],"number_text":"੩੬੬।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੁਝੇ ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੂਰੰ। ਘਾਗੜਦੰ ਘੁਮੀ ਹਾਗੜਦੰ ਹੂਰੰ।","roman":"Raagardan rujhe saagardan sooran | ghaagardan ghumee haagardan hooran |","meaning_en":"The heroes were locked in battle; the houris (heavenly maidens) roamed about.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਲੜਾਈ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੁੱਝ ਗਏ; ਹੂਰਾਂ ਘੁੰਮਣ ਲੱਗੀਆਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤਕੈ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਆਨੰ। ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮੋਹੀ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤਾਨੰ। ੩੬੬।","roman":"Taagardan takai jaagardan juaanan | maagardan mohee taagardan taanan | 366 |","meaning_en":"They gazed at the young warriors and were enchanted by their bearing.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਨੰ: read as 'bearing/stance'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹਨਾਂ ਨੇ ਜਵਾਨ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਤੱਕਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਅਦਾ ਤੇ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਹੋ ਗਈਆਂ।","note_pa":"ਤਾਨੰ: 'ਅਦਾ/ਰੂਪ' ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[367],"number_text":"੩੬੭।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਾਗੜਦੰ ਦੇਖੈ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੂਪੰ। ਪਾਗੜਦੰ ਪ੍ਰੇਮੰ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੂਪੰ।","roman":"Daagardan dekhai raagardan roopan | paagardan preman kaagardan koopan |","meaning_en":"Seeing their beauty, (they fell) into the well of love;","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦਾ ਰੂਪ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ (ਉਹ) ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਦੇ ਖੂਹ ਵਿੱਚ ਜਾ ਡਿੱਗੇ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਾਗੜਦੰ ਡੁਬੀ ਪਾਗੜਦੰ ਪਿਆਰੀ। ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕਾਮੰ ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਾਰੀ। ੩੬੭।","roman":"Daagardan dubee paagardan piaaree | kaagardan kaaman maagardan maaree | 367 |","meaning_en":"the lovely one sank in it, struck by love.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪਿਆਰੀ ਉਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਡੁੱਬ ਗਈ, ਪਿਆਰ ਨਾਲ ਮਾਰੀ ਹੋਈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[368],"number_text":"੩੬੮।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮੋਹੀ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਲਾ। ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੂਪੰ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਉਜਾਲਾ।","roman":"Maagardan mohee baagardan baalaa | raagardan roopan aagardan ujaalaa |","meaning_en":"The maiden was enchanted by (his) radiant beauty.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਾਲੀ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਚਮਕਦੇ ਰੂਪ ਨਾਲ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਹੋ ਗਈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਾਗੜਦੰ ਦੇਖੈ ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੂਰੰ। ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਜੇ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤੂਰੰ। ੩੬੮।","roman":"Daagardan dekhai saagardan sooran | baagardan baaje taagardan tooran | 368 |","meaning_en":"She looked upon the hero; trumpets sounded.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖਦੀ ਹੈ; ਤੁਰ੍ਹੀਆਂ ਵੱਜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[369],"number_text":"੩੬੯।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੂਪੰ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕਾਮੰ। ਨਾਗੜਦੰ ਨਾਚੈ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਮੰ।","roman":"Raagardan roopan kaagardan kaaman | naagardan naachai baagardan baaman |","meaning_en":"Lovely as the god of love, the women danced.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮਦੇਵ ਵਰਗੇ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਰੂਪ ਵਾਲੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਨੱਚਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੀਝੇ ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੂਰੰ। ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਿਆਹੈ ਹਾਗੜਦੰ ਹੂਰੰ। ੩੬੯।","roman":"Raagardan reejhe saagardan sooran | baagardan biaahai haagardan hooran | 369 |","meaning_en":"The heroes were delighted; the houris married them.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੂਰਮੇ ਖੁਸ਼ ਹੋਏ; ਹੂਰਾਂ ਨੇ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਿਆਹ ਕਰਵਾਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[370],"number_text":"੩੭੦।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੋਪਾ। ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭੂਪੰ। ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕਾਲੰ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੂਪੰ।","roman":"Kaagardan kopaa | bhaagardan bhoopan | kaagardan kaalan raagardan roopan |","meaning_en":"The king grew angry, (taking on) a form like Death.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The king: the king of Sambhal (see the ending).","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜਾ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਇਆ, ਮੌਤ ਵਰਗਾ ਰੂਪ ਧਾਰ ਕੇ।","note_pa":"ਰਾਜਾ: ਸੰਭਲ ਦਾ ਰਾਜਾ (ਅੰਤ ਵੇਖੋ)।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੋਸੰ ਧਾਗੜਦੰ ਧਾਯੋ। ਚਾਗੜਦੰ ਚਲ੍ਯੋ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਆਯੋ। ੩੭੦।","roman":"Raagardan rosan dhaagardan dhaayo | chaagardan chalyo aagardan aayo | 370 |","meaning_en":"In fury he rushed forth; he set out and came (to the field).","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਹ ਦੌੜਿਆ; ਉਹ ਤੁਰਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਤੇ ਆ ਪਹੁੰਚਿਆ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[371],"number_text":"੩੭੧।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਗੜਦੰ ਅਰੜੇ ਗਾਗੜਦੰ ਗਾਜੀ। ਨਾਗੜਦੰ ਨਾਚੇ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤਾਜੀ।","roman":"Aagardan arre gaagardan gaajee | naagardan naache taagardan taajee |","meaning_en":"The warriors (ghazis) stood firm; the steeds danced.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਾਜੀ: ghazi, 'warrior'.","meaning_pa":"ਗਾਜ਼ੀ ਯੋਧੇ ਅਡੋਲ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਰਹੇ; ਘੋੜੇ ਨੱਚਣ ਲੱਗੇ।","note_pa":"ਗਾਜੀ: ਗ਼ਾਜ਼ੀ, 'ਯੋਧਾ'।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਝੇ ਖਾਗੜਦੰ ਖੇਤੰ। ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰਹਸੇ ਪਾਗੜਦੰ ਪ੍ਰੇਤੰ। ੩੭੧।","roman":"Jaagardan jujhe khaagardan khetan | raagardan rahse paagardan pretan | 371 |","meaning_en":"They fell fighting on the field; the ghosts rejoiced.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗੇ; ਭੂਤ ਖੁਸ਼ ਹੋਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[372],"number_text":"੩੭੨।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਾਰੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬੀਰੰ। ਪਾਗੜਦੰ ਪਰਾਨੇ ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭੀਰੰ।","roman":"Maagardan maare baagardan beeran | paagardan paraane bhaagardan bheeran |","meaning_en":"Warriors were slain; the cowards fled.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹਾਦਰ ਮਾਰੇ ਗਏ; ਡਰਪੋਕ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਗੜਦੰ ਧਾਯੋ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰਾਜਾ। ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰਣਕੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਜਾ। ੩੭੨।","roman":"Dhaagardan dhaayo raagardan raajaa | raagardan ranke baagardan baajaa | 372 |","meaning_en":"The king rushed forward; the battle-drums resounded.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜਾ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧਿਆ; ਰਣ-ਭੇਰੀਆਂ ਗੂੰਜਣ ਲੱਗੀਆਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[373],"number_text":"੩੭੩।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਟਾਗੜਦੰ ਟੂਟੇ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤਾਲੰ। ਆਗੜਦੰ ਉਠੇ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਆਲੰ।","roman":"Taagardan toote taagardan taalan | aagardan uthe jaagardan juaalan |","meaning_en":"The cymbals broke; flames leapt up.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਟੂਟੇ ਤਾਲੰ: 'the cymbals (or the rhythm) broke off'; uncertain. ਜੁਆਲੰ: perhaps sparks from clashing steel.","meaning_pa":"ਤਾਲ ਟੁੱਟ ਗਏ; ਅੱਗ ਦੀਆਂ ਲਪਟਾਂ ਉੱਠੀਆਂ।","note_pa":"ਟੂਟੇ ਤਾਲੰ: 'ਤਾਲ (ਜਾਂ ਤਾਲ ਦਾ ਵਾਜਾ) ਟੁੱਟ ਗਿਆ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ। ਜੁਆਲੰ: ਸ਼ਾਇਦ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਦੀ ਟੱਕਰ ਤੋਂ ਚਿਣਗਾਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭਾਜੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬੀਰੰ। ਲਾਗੜਦੰ ਲਾਗੇ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤੀਰੰ। ੩੭੩।","roman":"Bhaagardan bhaaje baagardan beeran | laagardan laage taagardan teeran | 373 |","meaning_en":"Warriors fled; arrows struck.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ; ਤੀਰ ਵੱਜੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[374],"number_text":"੩੭੪।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰਹਸੀ ਦਾਗੜਦੰ ਦੇਵੀ। ਗਾਗੜਦੰ ਗੈਣ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਭੇਵੀ।","roman":"Raagardan rahsee daagardan devee | gaagardan gain aagardan bhevee |","meaning_en":"The goddess rejoiced, (watching) from the sky;","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗੈਣ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਭੇਵੀ: ਗੈਣ = sky; ਭੇਵੀ unclear ('knower of secrets' or 'piercing'); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਦੇਵੀ ਖੁਸ਼ ਹੋਈ, ਅਕਾਸ਼ ਤੋਂ ਵੇਖਦੀ ਹੋਈ;","note_pa":"ਗੈਣ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਭੇਵੀ: ਗੈਣ = ਅਕਾਸ਼; ਭੇਵੀ ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ ('ਭੇਤ ਜਾਣਨ ਵਾਲੀ' ਜਾਂ 'ਵਿੰਨ੍ਹਣ ਵਾਲੀ'); ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭੈਰੰ ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਪ੍ਰੇਤੰ। ਹਾਗੜਦੰ ਹਸੇ ਖਾਗੜਦੰ ਖੇਤੰ। ੩੭੪।","roman":"Bhaagardan bhairan bhaagardan pretan | haagardan hase khaagardan khetan | 374 |","meaning_en":"Bhairav and the ghosts laughed on the field.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੈਰੋਂ ਅਤੇ ਭੂਤ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੱਸੇ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ"},{"type":"verse","number":[375],"number_text":"੩੭੫।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸਿ ਟੁਟੇ ਲੁਟੇ ਘਨੇ ਤੁਟੇ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਨੇਕ।","roman":"Asi tute lute ghane tute sasatr anek |","meaning_en":"Swords broke, many were laid low, and countless weapons were shattered.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲੁਟੇ ਘਨੇ: 'many were plundered/laid low'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਟੁੱਟ ਗਈਆਂ, ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰੇ ਡਿੱਗ ਪਏ, ਅਤੇ ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਚੂਰ-ਚੂਰ ਹੋ ਗਏ।","note_pa":"ਲੁਟੇ ਘਨੇ: 'ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰੇ ਡਿੱਗ ਪਏ/ਲੁੱਟੇ ਗਏ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਜੁਟੇ ਕੁਟੇ ਸਬੈ ਰਹਿ ਗਯੋ ਭੂਪਤਿ ਏਕ। ੩੭੫।","roman":"Je jute kute sabai rahi gayo bhoopti ek | 375 |","meaning_en":"All who joined the fight were beaten down; only the king was left.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਵੀ ਲੜਾਈ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਏ, ਸਾਰੇ ਕੁੱਟੇ ਗਏ; ਬੱਸ ਇੱਕ ਰਾਜਾ ਬਾਕੀ ਰਹਿ ਗਿਆ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪੰਕਜ ਬਾਟਿਕਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪੰਕਜ ਬਾਟਿਕਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Pankaj baatikaa chhand","meaning_en":"Pankaj Batika metre.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪੰਕਜ ਬਾਟਿਕਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[376],"number_text":"੩੭੬।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੈਨ ਜੁਝਤ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਭਯੋ ਅਤਿ ਆਕੁਲ। ਧਾਵਤ ਭਯੋ ਸਾਮੁਹਿ ਅਤਿ ਬਿਆਕੁਲ।","roman":"Sain jujhat nrip bhayo ati aakul | dhaavat bhayo saamuhi ati biaakul |","meaning_en":"Seeing his army fall, the king became greatly distressed; greatly agitated, he rushed to the front.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਆਪਣੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਨੂੰ ਡਿੱਗਦਿਆਂ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਰਾਜਾ ਬਹੁਤ ਘਬਰਾ ਗਿਆ; ਬੜੀ ਬੇਚੈਨੀ ਨਾਲ ਉਹ ਅੱਗੇ ਵੱਲ ਦੌੜਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਨਿਧ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਅਤਿ ਕ੍ਰੁਧਤ। ਆਵਤ ਭਯੋ ਰਿਸ ਕੈ ਕਰਿ ਜੁਧਤ। ੩੭੬।","roman":"Sannidh hvai chit mai ati krudhat | aavat bhayo ris kai kari judhat | 376 |","meaning_en":"Coming close, greatly enraged in his heart, he came on in fury to make war.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨੇੜੇ ਆ ਕੇ, ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਹੁਤ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਹੋ ਕੇ, ਉਹ ਯੁੱਧ ਕਰਨ ਲਈ ਜੋਸ਼ ਨਾਲ ਆਇਆ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[377],"number_text":"੩੭੭।","page":757,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰ ਅਨੇਕ ਕਰੇ ਤਬ। ਜੰਗ ਜੁਟਿਓ ਅਪਨੋ ਦਲ ਲੈ ਸਬ।","roman":"Sasatr prahaar anek kare tab | jang jutio apno dal lai sab |","meaning_en":"Then he struck many blows with his weapons; he joined battle, taking all his army with him.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਫਿਰ ਉਸ ਨੇ ਕਈ ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਾਰ ਕੀਤੇ; ਆਪਣੀ ਸਾਰੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਯੁੱਧ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਿੜ ਗਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜ ਉਠੇ ਤਹ ਕੋਟਿ ਨਗਾਰੇ। ਰੁਝ ਗਿਰੇ ਰਣ ਜੁਝ ਨਿਹਾਰੇ। ੩੭੭।","roman":"Baaj uthe tah koti nagaare | rujh gire ran jujh nihaare | 377 |","meaning_en":"Millions of kettle-drums sounded there; locked in battle, (warriors) fell, and the fighting was watched.","page":757,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੁਝ ਗਿਰੇ ਰਣ ਜੁਝ ਨਿਹਾਰੇ: sense of the last part unclear; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉੱਥੇ ਕਰੋੜਾਂ ਨਗਾਰੇ ਵੱਜੇ; ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ (ਯੋਧੇ) ਡਿੱਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਲੜਾਈ ਵੇਖੀ ਗਈ।","note_pa":"ਰੁਝ ਗਿਰੇ ਰਣ ਜੁਝ ਨਿਹਾਰੇ: ਆਖਰੀ ਹਿੱਸੇ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚਾਮਰ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਚਾਮਰ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Chaamar chhand","meaning_en":"Chamar metre.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਮਰ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[378],"number_text":"੩੭੮।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਲੈ ਸਕੋਪ ਬੀਰ ਬੋਲਿ ਕੈ ਸਬੈ।","roman":"Sasatr asatr lai sakop beer boli kai sabai |","meaning_en":"Taking arms and weapons, in fury, calling all the warriors together,","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰ ਲੈ ਕੇ, ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਸਾਰੇ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਲਾ ਕੇ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਓਪ ਦੈ ਹਠੀ ਸੁ ਧਾਇ ਕੈ ਪਰੇ ਸਬੈ।","roman":"Kop op dai hathee su dhaai kai pare sabai |","meaning_en":"the steadfast ones, blazing with anger, all rushed and fell upon (the foe).","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜੀਅਲ ਯੋਧੇ, ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਭਖਦੇ ਹੋਏ, ਸਾਰੇ ਦੌੜ ਕੇ (ਵੈਰੀ ਉੱਤੇ) ਟੁੱਟ ਪਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਨ ਕੇ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਨ ਬਾਨ ਤਾਨਿ ਤਾਨਿ ਤੋਰ ਹੀ।","roman":"Kaan ke pramaan baan taani taani tor hee |","meaning_en":"Drawing their arrows to the ear, they loose them again and again;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕੰਨਾਂ ਤੱਕ ਕਮਾਨਾਂ ਖਿੱਚ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਬਾਰ-ਬਾਰ ਤੀਰ ਛੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਜੂਝਿ ਜੂਝ ਕੈ ਪਰੈ ਨ ਨੈਕੁ ਮੁਖ ਮੋਰ ਹੀ। ੩੭੮।","roman":"Su joojhi joojh kai parai na naiku mukh mor hee | 378 |","meaning_en":"fighting on and on they fall, but do not turn their faces back in the least.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲੜ-ਲੜ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪਰ ਰਤਾ ਵੀ ਮੂੰਹ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੋੜਦੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[379],"number_text":"੩੭੯।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਪਾਨਿ ਲੈ ਸਬੈ ਸਕ੍ਰੁਧ ਸੂਰਮਾ ਚਲੇ।","roman":"Baan paani lai sabai sakrudh soormaa chale |","meaning_en":"Taking arrows in hand, all the warriors went forth in anger,","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੱਥਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਾਣ ਲੈ ਕੇ, ਸਾਰੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧੇ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਨਿ ਬੀਨਿ ਜੇ ਲਏ ਪ੍ਰਬੀਨ ਬੀਰਹਾ ਭਲੇ।","roman":"Beeni beeni je lae prabeen beerhaa bhale |","meaning_en":"excellent, skilled fighters, picked out one by one.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੁਣ-ਚੁਣ ਕੇ ਲਏ ਗਏ ਸਿਆਣੇ ਅਤੇ ਚੰਗੇ ਯੋਧੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਕ ਛੋਰ ਕੈ ਭਿਰੈ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਘਾਇ ਡਾਰ ਹੀ।","roman":"Sank chhor kai bhirai nisank ghaai daar hee |","meaning_en":"Casting off fear, they fight fearlessly and deal wounds;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਡਰ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਬੇਖੌਫ਼ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਅੰਗ ਭੰਗ ਹੁਇ ਗਿਰੈ ਨ ਜੰਗ ਤੇ ਪਧਾਰ ਹੀ। ੩੭੯।","roman":"Su ang bhang hui girai na jang te padhaar hee | 379 |","meaning_en":"their limbs broken, they fall, but do not leave the battle.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਟੁੱਟ ਕੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪਰ ਜੰਗ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਾਂਦੇ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਿਸਪਾਲਿਕ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਿਸਪਾਲਿਕ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Nispaalik chhand","meaning_en":"Nispalik metre.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਿਸਪਾਲਿਕ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[380],"number_text":"੩੮੦।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨਿ ਸਰ ਤਾਨਿ ਅਰੁ ਮਾਨ ਕਰਿ ਛੋਰ ਹੀਂ।","roman":"Aani sar taani aru maan kari chhor heen |","meaning_en":"Coming forward, they draw their arrows and loose them with pride;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੱਗੇ ਆ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਮਾਣ ਨਾਲ ਬਾਣ ਤਾਣ ਕੇ ਛੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਐਨ ਸਰ ਚੈਨ ਕਰਿ ਤੈਨ ਕਰਿ ਜੋਰ ਹੀਂ।","roman":"Ain sar chain kari tain kari jor heen |","meaning_en":"they fit the arrows true, calmly, and pull them taut with strength;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਐਨ ... ਤੈਨ ਕਰਿ: read as 'exactly ... drawing taut'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬਾਣਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਠੀਕ ਢੰਗ ਨਾਲ ਚੜ੍ਹਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸ਼ਾਂਤੀ ਨਾਲ, ਅਤੇ ਜ਼ੋਰ ਨਾਲ ਖਿੱਚਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਐਨ ... ਤੈਨ ਕਰਿ: 'ਠੀਕ ਨਿਸ਼ਾਨੇ ਨਾਲ ... ਖਿੱਚ ਕੇ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾਵ ਕਰਿ ਚਾਵ ਕਰਿ ਆਨਿ ਕਰਿ ਲਾਗ ਹੀਂ।","roman":"Ghaav kari chaav kari aani kari laag heen |","meaning_en":"eagerly they come and strike, dealing wounds;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਅ ਨਾਲ ਉਹ ਆ ਕੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਡਿ ਰਣਿ ਖਾਇ ਬ੍ਰਿਣ ਬੀਰ ਬਰ ਭਾਗ ਹੀਂ। ੩੮੦।","roman":"Chhaadi rani khaai brin beer bar bhaag heen | 380 |","meaning_en":"some fine warriors, taking wounds, leave the battle and flee.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕੁਝ ਚੰਗੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮੀ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਰਣ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[381],"number_text":"੩੮੧।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਕਰਿ ਬੋਧਿ ਹਰਿ ਸੋਧਿ ਅਰਿ ਧਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Krodh kari bodhi hari sodhi ari dhaavheen |","meaning_en":"In anger, beside themselves, they seek out the foe and charge;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੋਧਿ ਹਰਿ: 'losing (their) sense'.","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ, ਹੋਸ਼ ਗੁਆ ਕੇ, ਉਹ ਵੈਰੀ ਲੱਭ ਕੇ ਹਮਲਾ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਬੋਧਿ ਹਰਿ: 'ਹੋਸ਼ ਗੁਆ ਕੇ'।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਧ ਬਰ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਧਰਿ ਬਿਰੋਧਿ ਸਰ ਲਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Jodh bar krodh dhari birodhi sar laavheen |","meaning_en":"the fine warriors, full of wrath, strike with arrows in enmity.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹਾਦਰ ਯੋਧੇ, ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੇ ਹੋਏ, ਵੈਰ ਨਾਲ ਬਾਣ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਗ ਭਟ ਭੰਗ ਹੁਐ ਜੰਗ ਤਿਹ ਡਿਗਹੀਂ।","roman":"Ang bhat bhang huai jang tih digheen |","meaning_en":"Their limbs broken, the warriors fall there in the war;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੰਗ ਟੁੱਟ ਕੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਉੱਥੇ ਜੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗਿ ਬਿਨੁ ਰੰਗਿ ਰਣ ਸ੍ਰੋਣ ਤਨ ਭਿਗਹੀਂ। ੩੮੧।","roman":"Sangi binu rangi ran sron tan bhigheen | 381 |","meaning_en":"alone, coloured by battle, their bodies are soaked in blood.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਗਿ ਬਿਨੁ ਰੰਗਿ: sense unclear; read as 'without companions, coloured (by battle)'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਇਕੱਲੇ, ਰਣ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਰੰਗੇ, ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦੇ ਸਰੀਰ ਲਹੂ ਨਾਲ ਭਿੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਸੰਗਿ ਬਿਨੁ ਰੰਗਿ: ਅਰਥ ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ; 'ਸਾਥੀਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾਂ, ਰਣ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[382],"number_text":"੩੮੨।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਇ ਭਟਿ ਆਇ ਰਿਸ ਖਾਇ ਅਸਿ ਝਾਰਹੀਂ।","roman":"Dhaai bhati aai ris khaai asi jhaarheen |","meaning_en":"Rushing forward, the warriors come on and, in anger, swing their swords;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੌੜ ਕੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਘੁੰਮਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰ ਕਰਿ ਜੋਰਿ ਸਰ ਤੋਰ ਅਰਿ ਡਾਰਹੀਂ।","roman":"Sor kari jori sar tor ari daarheen |","meaning_en":"with a shout they fit their arrows, loose them, and cut down the foe.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਕਾਂ ਮਾਰ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਬਾਣ ਜੋੜਦੇ ਅਤੇ ਛੱਡਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਤੇ ਵੈਰੀ ਨੂੰ ਡੇਗ ਦਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਤਜਿ ਪੈ ਨ ਭਜਿ ਭੂਮਿ ਰਨ ਸੋਭਹੀਂ।","roman":"Praan taji pai na bhaji bhoomi ran sobhheen |","meaning_en":"They give up their lives but do not flee; they look splendid on the battleground.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਾਨ ਦੇ ਦਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ ਪਰ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਨਹੀਂ; ਉਹ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਲੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੇਖਿ ਛਬਿ ਦੇਖਿ ਦੁਤਿ ਨਾਰਿ ਸੁਰ ਲੋਭਹੀਂ। ੩੮੨।","roman":"Pekhi chhabi dekhi duti naari sur lobhheen | 382 |","meaning_en":"Seeing their beauty and radiance, the women of the gods are enamoured.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਚਮਕ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਹੁੰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[383],"number_text":"੩੮੩।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜ ਨਹ ਸਾਜਿ ਅਸਿ ਗਾਜਿ ਭਟ ਆਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Bhaaj nah saaji asi gaaji bhat aavheen |","meaning_en":"Not fleeing, but readying their swords, the warriors come on roaring;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭੱਜਦੇ ਨਹੀਂ, ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਸਜਾ ਕੇ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਯੋਧੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਕਰਿ ਬੋਧ ਹਰਿ ਜੋਧ ਅਸਿ ਲਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Krodh kari bodh hari jodh asi laavheen |","meaning_en":"in anger, beside themselves, the fighters strike with their swords.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਵਿੱਚ, ਹੋਸ਼ ਗੁਆ ਕੇ, ਯੋਧੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੂਝਿ ਰਣਿ ਝਾਲਿ ਬ੍ਰਿਣ ਦੇਵ ਪੁਰਿ ਪਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Joojhi rani jhaali brin dev puri paavheen |","meaning_en":"Fighting in battle and bearing wounds, they reach the city of the gods;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੜਦੇ ਅਤੇ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਸਹਿੰਦੇ ਹੋਏ, ਉਹ ਦੇਵਲੋਕ ਪਹੁੰਚਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਤਿ ਕੈ ਗੀਤ ਕੁਲਿ ਰੀਤ ਜਿਮ ਗਾਵਹੀਂ। ੩੮੩।","roman":"Jeeti kai geet kuli reet jim gaavheen | 383 |","meaning_en":"having won, they sing songs (of victory), as is the custom of their clan.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਤ ਕੇ, ਕੁਲ ਦੀ ਰੀਤ ਅਨੁਸਾਰ ਜਿੱਤ ਦੇ ਗੀਤ ਗਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Naraj metre.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[384],"number_text":"੩੮੪।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਜ ਸਾਜ ਕੈ ਸਬੈ ਸਲਾਜ ਬੀਰ ਧਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Saaj saaj kai sabai salaaj beer dhaavheen |","meaning_en":"Making all ready, the warriors, mindful of their honour, charge;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਭ ਸਾਜ-ਸਾਮਾਨ ਤਿਆਰ ਕਰ ਕੇ, ਆਪਣੀ ਇੱਜ਼ਤ ਦਾ ਖਿਆਲ ਰੱਖਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਯੋਧੇ ਦੌੜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੂਝਿ ਜੂਝ ਕੇ ਮਰੈ ਪ੍ਰਲੋਕ ਲੋਕ ਪਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Joojhi joojh ke marai pralok lok paavheen |","meaning_en":"fighting on, they die and reach the other world.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲੜ-ਲੜ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਮਰਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਪਰਲੋਕ ਪਹੁੰਚਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਇ ਧਾਇ ਕੈ ਹਠੀ ਅਘਾਇ ਘਾਇ ਝੇਲਹੀਂ।","roman":"Dhaai dhaai kai hathee aghaai ghaai jhelheen |","meaning_en":"Rushing on again and again, the steadfast ones bear wounds to the full;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵਾਰ-ਵਾਰ ਦੌੜ ਕੇ ਹਠੀ ਯੋਧੇ ਭਰਪੂਰ ਜ਼ਖ਼ਮ ਸਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਛੇਲ ਪਾਵ ਨ ਚਲੈ ਅਰੈਲ ਬੀਰ ਠੇਲਹੀਂ। ੩੮੪।","roman":"Pachhel paav na chalai arail beer thelheen | 384 |","meaning_en":"they do not step backward, and they push back the stubborn warriors.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਰੈਲ: 'obstinate, unyielding'.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਪੈਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਰੱਖਦੇ, ਅਤੇ ਅੜੀਅਲ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਧੱਕਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਅਰੈਲ: 'ਅੜੀਅਲ, ਨਾ ਝੁਕਣ ਵਾਲੇ'।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[385],"number_text":"੩੮੫।","page":758,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਓਪ ਦੈ ਸਬੈ ਸਰੋਖ ਸੂਰ ਧਾਇ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Kop op dai sabai sarokh soor dhaai hain |","meaning_en":"Blazing with anger, all the heroes will charge in wrath;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The verbs in -ਹੈਂ here may be read as future or present.","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਭਰ ਕੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਦੌੜਨਗੇ;","note_pa":"ਇੱਥੇ -ਹੈਂ ਵਾਲੇ ਕਿਰਿਆ-ਰੂਪ ਭਵਿੱਖ ਜਾਂ ਵਰਤਮਾਨ ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹੇ ਜਾ ਸਕਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਇ ਧਾਇ ਜੂਝ ਹੈਂ ਅਰੂਝਿ ਜੂਝਿ ਜਾਇ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Dhaai dhaai joojh hain aroojhi joojhi jaai hain |","meaning_en":"rushing on, they will fight, and, entangled in combat, fall fighting.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੌੜ-ਦੌੜ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਲੜਨਗੇ, ਅਤੇ ਲੜਾਈ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਲਝ ਕੇ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗਣਗੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਅਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਮੇਲ ਕੈ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰ ਆਨਿ ਡਾਰਹੀਂ।","roman":"Su asatr sasatr mel kai prahaar aani daarheen |","meaning_en":"Joining arms and weapons, they come and deal blows;","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਆ ਕੇ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਨਗੇ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ ਭਾਜਿ ਗਾਜ ਹੈ ਹਠੀ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਘਾਇ ਮਾਰਹੀਂ। ੩੮੫।","roman":"Na bhaaji gaaj hai hathee nisank ghaai maarheen | 385 |","meaning_en":"the steadfast do not flee but roar, and fearlessly strike blows.","page":758,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਠੀ ਯੋਧੇ ਭੱਜਣਗੇ ਨਹੀਂ, ਗਰਜਣਗੇ ਅਤੇ ਬੇਖੌਫ਼ ਵਾਰ ਕਰਨਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[386],"number_text":"੩੮੬।","page":759,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ ਢੋਲ ਬਾਸੁਰੀ ਸਨਾਇ ਝਾਂਝ ਬਾਜ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Mridang dhol baasuree sanaai jhaanjh baaj hain |","meaning_en":"Mridang drums, dhol drums, flutes, shehnais and cymbals sound;","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ, ਢੋਲ, ਬੰਸਰੀਆਂ, ਸ਼ਹਿਨਾਈਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਝਾਂਝਾਂ ਵੱਜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਪਾਵ ਰੋਪ ਕੈ ਬਲੀ ਸਕੋਪ ਆਨਿ ਗਾਜ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Su paav rop kai balee sakop aani gaaj hain |","meaning_en":"planting their feet firmly, the mighty ones come roaring in wrath.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪੈਰ ਮਜ਼ਬੂਤੀ ਨਾਲ ਜਮਾ ਕੇ, ਬਲਵਾਨ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਬੂਝਿ ਬੂਝ ਕੈ ਹਠੀ ਅਰੂਝਿ ਆਨਿ ਜੂਝ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Su boojhi boojh kai hathee aroojhi aani joojh hain |","meaning_en":"Knowingly, deliberately, the steadfast ones come, grapple and fight;","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਠੀ ਯੋਧੇ ਜਾਣ-ਬੁੱਝ ਕੇ ਉਲਝ ਕੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਲੜਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਅੰਧ ਧੁੰਧ ਹੁਇ ਰਹੀ ਦਿਸਾ ਵਿਸਾ ਨ ਸੂਝ ਹੈਂ। ੩੮੬।","roman":"Su andh dhundh hui rahee disaa visaa na soojh hain | 386 |","meaning_en":"such blinding dust has arisen that no direction, main or between, can be seen.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਿਸਾ ਵਿਸਾ: the directions and the intermediate directions.","meaning_pa":"ਏਨੀ ਧੂੜ ਉੱਠੀ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਕੋਈ ਦਿਸ਼ਾ, ਕੋਈ ਉਪ-ਦਿਸ਼ਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਦਿਸਦੀ।","note_pa":"ਦਿਸਾ ਵਿਸਾ: ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਵਿਚਕਾਰਲੀਆਂ ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[387],"number_text":"੩੮੭।","page":759,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰੋਖ ਕਾਲਿ ਕੇਸਰੀ ਸੰਘਾਰਿ ਸੈਣ ਧਾਇ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Sarokh kaali kesree sanghaari sain dhaai hain |","meaning_en":"In wrath, (Kalki), the lion of the Kali age, will charge, destroying the army;","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲਿ ਕੇਸਰੀ: 'lion of the Kali age' or 'lion like Death'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ, ਕਲਿਯੁਗ ਦਾ ਸ਼ੇਰ (ਕਲਕੀ) ਫ਼ੌਜ ਨੂੰ ਨਾਸ਼ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਹਮਲਾ ਕਰੇਗਾ;","note_pa":"ਕਾਲਿ ਕੇਸਰੀ: 'ਕਲਿਯੁਗ ਦਾ ਸ਼ੇਰ' ਜਾਂ 'ਮੌਤ ਵਰਗਾ ਸ਼ੇਰ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਗਸਤ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਕੀ ਜਿਮੰ ਪਚਾਇ ਸੈਨ ਜਾਇ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Agsat sindhu kee jiman pachaai sain jaai hain |","meaning_en":"as Agastya (swallowed) the ocean, so he will consume the army and go on.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Agastya: the sage said to have drunk up the ocean.","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਵੇਂ ਅਗਸਤ ਮੁਨੀ ਨੇ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਨੂੰ ਪੀ ਲਿਆ ਸੀ, ਉਸੇ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਉਹ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਨੂੰ ਖਤਮ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧੇਗਾ।","note_pa":"ਅਗਸਤ: ਉਹ ਰਿਸ਼ੀ ਜਿਸ ਬਾਰੇ ਕਿਹਾ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਉਸ ਨੇ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਪੀ ਲਿਆ ਸੀ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਘਾਰਿ ਬਾਹਣੀਸ ਕੋ ਅਨੀਸ ਤੀਰ ਗਾਜ ਹੈਂ।","roman":"Sanghaari baahnees ko anees teer gaaj hain |","meaning_en":"Having slain the commander of the army, he will roar near the leaderless (troops);","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਹਣੀਸ: 'lord of the army'. ਅਨੀਸ ਤੀਰ: read as 'beside the leaderless (troops)'; could also be 'lord of the army'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਫ਼ੌਜ ਦੇ ਸੈਨਾਪਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਕੇ, ਉਹ ਬਿਨਾਂ ਸਰਦਾਰ ਵਾਲੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਦੇ ਕੋਲ ਗਰਜੇਗਾ;","note_pa":"ਬਾਹਣੀਸ: 'ਫ਼ੌਜ ਦਾ ਸੁਆਮੀ/ਸੈਨਾਪਤੀ'। ਅਨੀਸ ਤੀਰ: 'ਬਿਨਾਂ ਸਰਦਾਰ ਵਾਲੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਦੇ ਕੋਲ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ 'ਫ਼ੌਜ ਦਾ ਸੁਆਮੀ' ਹੋਵੇ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਸੇਖ ਜੁਧ ਮੰਡ ਹੈ ਅਸੇਖ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਬਾਜ ਹੈਂ। ੩੮੭।","roman":"Bisekh judh mand hai asekh sasatr baaj hain | 387 |","meaning_en":"he will wage a mighty war, and countless weapons will clash.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਬੜਾ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਯੁੱਧ ਕਰੇਗਾ, ਅਤੇ ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਟਕਰਾਉਣਗੇ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Savaiyaa chhand","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਵੈਯਾ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[388],"number_text":"੩੮੮।","page":759,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਵਤ ਹੀ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੇ ਦਲ ਤੇ ਹਰਿ ਬਾਜ ਕਰੀ ਰਥ ਕੋਟਿਕ ਕੂਟੇ।","roman":"Aavat hee nrip ke dal te hari baaj karee rath kotik koote |","meaning_en":"As soon as the king's army came on, Hari (Kalki) crushed millions of its horses, elephants and chariots.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਦੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਦੇ ਅੱਗੇ ਆਉਂਦਿਆਂ ਹੀ, ਹਰੀ ਨੇ ਕਰੋੜਾਂ ਘੋੜੇ, ਹਾਥੀ ਅਤੇ ਰਥ ਕੁਚਲ ਦਿੱਤੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਜ ਗਿਰੇ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਰਾਜ ਕਹੂੰ ਬਰ ਬਾਜ ਫਿਰੈ ਹਿਹਨਾਵਤ ਛੂਟੇ।","roman":"Saaj gire nrip raaj kahoon bar baaj phirai hihnaavat chhoote |","meaning_en":"Here the trappings of kings fell; fine horses ran about loose, neighing.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਸਾਜ਼-ਸਾਮਾਨ ਇੱਥੇ ਡਿੱਗ ਪਏ; ਸੋਹਣੇ ਘੋੜੇ ਹਿਣਹਿਣਾਉਂਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਖੁੱਲ੍ਹੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਜ ਕਹੂੰ ਗਜਰਾਜ ਰਣੰ ਭਟ ਕੇਸਨ ਤੇ ਗਹਿ ਕੇਸਨ ਜੂਟੇ।","roman":"Taaj kahoon gajraaj ranan bhat kesan te gahi kesan joote |","meaning_en":"Here crowns, there great elephants lay on the field; warriors grappled, seizing one another by the hair.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਤਾਜ ਪਏ ਹਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਹਾਥੀ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਏ ਹਨ; ਯੋਧੇ ਇੱਕ-ਦੂਜੇ ਦੇ ਵਾਲ ਫੜ ਕੇ ਉਲਝ ਗਏ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਉਨ ਸਮਾਨ ਬਹੈ ਕਲਿ ਬਾਨ ਸਬੈ ਅਰਿ ਬਾਦਲ ਸੇ ਚਲਿ ਫੂਟੇ। ੩੮੮।","roman":"Paun samaan bahai kali baan sabai ari baadal se chali phoote | 388 |","meaning_en":"Kalki's arrows flew like the wind, and all the foes broke and scattered like clouds.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਲਕੀ ਦੇ ਬਾਣ ਹਵਾ ਵਾਂਗ ਚੱਲੇ, ਅਤੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਵੈਰੀ ਬੱਦਲਾਂ ਵਾਂਗ ਟੁੱਟ ਕੇ ਖਿੱਲਰ ਗਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[389],"number_text":"੩੮੯।","page":759,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਇ ਪਰੇ ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਬੜੇ ਭਟ ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਸੰਭਾਰੇ।","roman":"Dhaai pare kari kop bare bhat baan kamaan kripaan sanbhaare |","meaning_en":"Great warriors fell upon him in fury, wielding arrows, bows and swords;","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਆ ਕੇ ਬਾਣ, ਕਮਾਨਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਉੱਤੇ ਟੁੱਟ ਪਏ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਟਿਸ ਲੋਹਹਥੀ ਪਰਸਾ ਕਰਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਚਹੂੰ ਦਿਸ ਚਉਕ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰੇ।","roman":"Patis lohahthee parsaa kari krodh chahoon dis chauk prahaare |","meaning_en":"with double-edged swords, iron maces and axes they struck in anger, startled, on all four sides.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਟਿਸ: a double-edged sword; ਲੋਹਹਥੀ: an iron mace/club; ਚਉਕ: 'startled' or 'suddenly'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਧਾਰੀ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ, ਲੋਹੇ ਦੇ ਗਦੇ ਅਤੇ ਕੁਹਾੜੀਆਂ ਨਾਲ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਨੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਚਾਰੇ ਪਾਸਿਓਂ ਹਮਲੇ ਕੀਤੇ।","note_pa":"ਪਟਿਸ: ਦੋਧਾਰੀ ਤਲਵਾਰ; ਲੋਹਹਥੀ: ਲੋਹੇ ਦਾ ਗਦਾ; ਚਉਕ: 'ਅਚਾਨਕ' ਜਾਂ 'ਘਬਰਾ ਕੇ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੁੰਜਰ ਪੁੰਜ ਗਿਰੇ ਰਣਿ ਮੂਰਧਨ ਸੋਭਤ ਹੈ ਅਤਿ ਡੀਲ ਡਿਲਾਰੇ।","roman":"Kunjar punj gire rani moordhan sobhat hai ati deel dilaare |","meaning_en":"Masses of elephants fell headlong in battle, their huge bodies looking splendid,","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਢੇਰ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਿਰ ਭਾਰ ਡਿੱਗੇ; ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦੇ ਵੱਡੇ-ਵੱਡੇ ਸਰੀਰ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਲੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਵਣ ਰਾਮ ਸਮੈ ਰਣ ਕੇ ਗਿਰਿਰਾਜ ਨੋ ਹਨਵੰਤਿ ਉਖਾਰੇ। ੩੮੯।","roman":"Raavan raam samai ran ke giriraaj no hanvanti ukhaare | 389 |","meaning_en":"like the great mountains Hanuman uprooted in the battle of Ram and Ravan.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਵੇਂ ਰਾਮ ਅਤੇ ਰਾਵਣ ਦੀ ਲੜਾਈ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਨੂਮਾਨ ਨੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਪਹਾੜ ਪੁੱਟੇ ਸਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[390],"number_text":"੩੯੦।","page":759,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਓਪੁ ਚਰੀ ਚਤੁਰੰਗ ਚਮੂੰ ਕਰੁਣਾਲਯ ਕੇ ਪਰ ਸਿੰਧੁਰ ਪੇਲੇ।","roman":"Chaopu charee chaturang chamoon karunaalay ke par sindhur pele |","meaning_en":"Eagerly the fourfold army advanced and drove its elephants against the Abode of Mercy (Kalki).","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਰ ਅੰਗਾਂ ਵਾਲੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਉਤਸ਼ਾਹ ਨਾਲ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧੀ, ਅਤੇ ਦਇਆ ਦੇ ਘਰ (ਕਲਕੀ) ਵੱਲ ਹਾਥੀ ਹੱਕੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਇ ਪਰੇ ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਹਠੀ ਕਰ ਕਾਟਿ ਸਬੈ ਪਗ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਨ ਪਿਛੇਲੇ।","roman":"Dhaai pare kari kop hathee kar kaati sabai pag dvai na pichhele |","meaning_en":"The steadfast ones rushed upon him in fury; he cut them all down, yet they did not draw back even two steps.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Who 'cut them all down' is not stated; read as Kalki.","meaning_pa":"ਅੜੀਅਲ ਯੋਧੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਉਸ ਉੱਤੇ ਟੁੱਟ ਪਏ; ਉਸ ਨੇ ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਵੱਢ ਦਿੱਤਾ, ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਉਹ ਦੋ ਕਦਮ ਵੀ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਨਾ ਹਟੇ।","note_pa":"ਕੌਣ ਵੱਢਦਾ ਹੈ, ਇਹ ਨਹੀਂ ਲਿਖਿਆ; ਕਲਕੀ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨਨ ਕੇ ਘਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ ਘਨੇ ਤਨਿ ਆਯੁਧ ਝੇਲੇ।","roman":"Baan kamaan kripaanan ke ghan syaam ghane tani aayudh jhele |","meaning_en":"The cloud-dark one bore on his body many blows of arrows, bows and swords;","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਘਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ: 'dark as a cloud', an epithet of the Lord.","meaning_pa":"ਬੱਦਲ ਵਰਗਾ ਸਾਂਵਲਾ ਉਹ ਆਪਣੇ ਸਰੀਰ ਉੱਤੇ ਬਾਣਾਂ, ਕਮਾਨਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਵਾਰ ਸਹਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ;","note_pa":"ਘਨ ਸ੍ਯਾਮ: 'ਬੱਦਲ ਵਰਗਾ ਸਾਂਵਲਾ', ਪ੍ਰਭੂ ਦਾ ਇੱਕ ਵਿਸ਼ੇਸ਼ਣ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੋਨ ਰੰਗੇ ਰਮਣੀਅ ਰਮਾਪਤਿ ਫਾਗੁਨ ਅੰਤਿ ਬਸੰਤ ਸੇ ਖੇਲੇ। ੩੯੦।","roman":"Sron range ramneea ramaapti phaagun anti basant se khele | 390 |","meaning_en":"dyed red with blood, the lovely Lord of Lakshmi looked as if playing Holi at the end of Phagun, in spring.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰਮਾਪਤਿ: Lord of Rama (Lakshmi), i.e. Vishnu in his Kalki form.","meaning_pa":"ਲਹੂ ਨਾਲ ਲਾਲ ਰੰਗਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ, ਲਕਸ਼ਮੀ ਦਾ ਸੁਆਮੀ ਸੋਹਣਾ ਲੱਗਦਾ ਹੈ, ਮਾਨੋ ਫੱਗਣ ਦੇ ਅਖੀਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਸੰਤ ਰੁੱਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੋਲੀ ਖੇਡ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੋਵੇ।","note_pa":"ਰਮਾਪਤਿ: ਲਕਸ਼ਮੀ ਦਾ ਸੁਆਮੀ, ਭਾਵ ਕਲਕੀ ਰੂਪ ਵਿੱਚ ਵਿਸ਼ਨੂੰ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[391],"number_text":"੩੯੧।","page":759,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾਇ ਸਬੈ ਸਹਿ ਕੈ ਕਮਲਾਪਤਿ ਕੋਪਿ ਭਰ੍ਯੋ ਕਰਿ ਆਯੁਧ ਲੀਨੇ।","roman":"Ghaai sabai sahi kai kamlaapti kopi bharyo kari aayudh leene |","meaning_en":"Having borne all the wounds, the Lord of Lakshmi, filled with anger, took up weapons in his hands;","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਘਾਵ ਸਹਿ ਕੇ, ਲਕਸ਼ਮੀ ਦਾ ਸੁਆਮੀ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਨਾਲ ਭਰ ਗਿਆ, ਅਤੇ ਹੱਥਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਚੁੱਕ ਲਏ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੁਜਨ ਸੈਨ ਬਿਖੈ ਧਸਿ ਕੈ ਛਿਨ ਮੈ ਬਿਨ ਪ੍ਰਾਣ ਸਬੈ ਅਰਿ ਕੀਨੇ।","roman":"Dujan sain bikhai dhasi kai chhin mai bin praan sabai ari keene |","meaning_en":"plunging into the enemy army, in an instant he made all the foes lifeless.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੈਰੀ ਦੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੜ ਕੇ, ਇੱਕ ਪਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਸ ਨੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਵੈਰੀ ਪ੍ਰਾਣਹੀਣ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਟੂਟ ਪਰੇ ਰਮਣੀ ਅਸ ਭੂਖਣ ਬੀਰ ਬਲੀ ਅਤਿ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਚੀਨੇ।","roman":"Toot pare ramnee as bhookhan beer balee ati sundar cheene |","meaning_en":"The mighty, very handsome warriors lay broken like a woman's ornaments;","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਲਵਾਨ, ਬਹੁਤ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਔਰਤ ਦੇ ਗਹਿਣਿਆਂ ਵਾਂਗ ਟੁੱਟੇ ਪਏ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਉਪਮਾ ਉਪਜੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਰਣ ਭੂਮਿ ਕੋ ਮਾਨਹੁ ਭੂਖਨ ਦੀਨੇ। ੩੯੧।","roman":"Yau upmaa upjee man mai ran bhoomi ko maanhu bhookhan deene | 391 |","meaning_en":"this simile arose in the mind: as if ornaments had been given to the battlefield.","page":759,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਇਹ ਉਪਮਾ ਆਈ: ਮਾਨੋ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਨੂੰ ਗਹਿਣੇ ਪਹਿਨਾਏ ਗਏ ਹੋਣ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[392],"number_text":"੩੯੨।","page":760,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਉਪਿ ਚੜਿਓ ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਕਲੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਆਯੁਧ ਅੰਗ ਅਨੇਕਨ ਸਾਜੇ।","roman":"Chaupi chario kari kop kalee krit aayudh ang anekan saaje |","meaning_en":"Kalki rode out eagerly in his anger, with many weapons arrayed on his body;","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ: read as Kalki.","meaning_pa":"ਕਲਕੀ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਤਸ਼ਾਹ ਨਾਲ ਚੜ੍ਹਿਆ, ਅਨੇਕਾਂ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਸਰੀਰ ਉੱਤੇ ਸਜਾਏ ਹੋਏ;","note_pa":"ਕਲੀ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ: ਕਲਕੀ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਲ ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ ਉਪੰਗ ਮੁਚੰਗ ਸੁ ਭਾਤਿ ਅਨੇਕ ਭਲੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਬਾਜੇ।","roman":"Taal mridang upang muchang su bhaati anek bhalee bidhi baaje |","meaning_en":"tal, mridang, upang, muchang and many other instruments sounded finely.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Names of percussion and wind instruments.","meaning_pa":"ਤਾਲ, ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ, ਉਪੰਗ, ਮੁਚੰਗ ਅਤੇ ਹੋਰ ਕਈ ਸਾਜ਼ ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਵੱਜੇ।","note_pa":"ਤਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਫੂਕ ਵਾਲੇ ਸਾਜ਼ਾਂ ਦੇ ਨਾਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੂਰਿ ਫਟੀ ਛੁਟਿ ਧੂਰ ਜਟੀ ਜਟ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਦੋਊ ਉਠਿ ਭਾਜੇ।","roman":"Poori phatee chhuti dhoor jatee jat dev adev do'oo uthi bhaaje |","meaning_en":"(The earth) split, Shiva's matted locks came loose, and gods and demons both rose and fled,","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੂਰਿ ਫਟੀ ਛੁਟਿ ਧੂਰ ਜਟੀ ਜਟ: unclear; read as 'the earth split, and the locks of Dhurjati (Shiva) came loose'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਧਰਤੀ) ਫਟ ਗਈ, ਸ਼ਿਵ ਦੀਆਂ ਜਟਾਂ ਖੁੱਲ੍ਹ ਗਈਆਂ, ਅਤੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਦੋਵੇਂ ਉੱਠ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ,","note_pa":"ਪੂਰਿ ਫਟੀ ਛੁਟਿ ਧੂਰ ਜਟੀ ਜਟ: ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ; 'ਧਰਤੀ ਫਟ ਗਈ ਅਤੇ ਧੂਰਜਟੀ (ਸ਼ਿਵ) ਦੀਆਂ ਜਟਾਂ ਖੁੱਲ੍ਹ ਗਈਆਂ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਕਛੂ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਚਿਤ ਮੋ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਜਬੈ ਰਣਿ ਗਾਜੇ। ੩੯੨।","roman":"Kop kachhoo kari kai chit mo kalkee avtaar jabai rani gaaje | 392 |","meaning_en":"when Kalki Avtar, with some anger in his heart, roared on the battlefield.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗੁੱਸੇ ਦੀ ਕੁਝ ਕੁ ਭਾਵਨਾ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੈ ਕੇ, ਜਦੋਂ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਗਰਜਿਆ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[393],"number_text":"੩੯੩।","page":760,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜ ਹਨੇ ਗਜਰਾਜ ਹਨੇ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਰਾਜ ਹਨੇ ਰਣ ਭੂਮਿ ਗਿਰਾਏ।","roman":"Baaj hane gajraaj hane nripraaj hane ran bhoomi giraae |","meaning_en":"He slew horses, slew great elephants, slew great kings and felled them on the battlefield.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੇ ਘੋੜੇ ਮਾਰੇ, ਹਾਥੀ ਮਾਰੇ, ਵੱਡੇ-ਵੱਡੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਮਾਰੇ ਅਤੇ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਡੇਗ ਦਿੱਤੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡੋਲਿ ਗਿਰਿਓ ਗਿਰ ਮੇਰ ਰਸਾਤਲ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਸਬੈ ਭਹਰਾਏ।","roman":"Doli girio gir mer rasaatal dev adev sabai bhahraae |","meaning_en":"Mount Meru shook and fell into the netherworld; gods and demons all trembled.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੁਮੇਰ ਪਰਬਤ ਹਿੱਲ ਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਪਾਤਾਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਡਿੱਗ ਪਿਆ; ਦੇਵਤੇ ਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਸਾਰੇ ਕੰਬ ਗਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਤੋਊ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਸੁਕੀ ਸਰਤਾ ਸਬ ਲੋਕ ਅਲੋਕ ਸਬੈ ਥਹਰਾਏ।","roman":"Saato'oo sindhu sukee sartaa sab lok alok sabai thahraae |","meaning_en":"The seven seas and all the rivers dried up; all the worlds and the realms beyond shook.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੱਤੇ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਨਦੀਆਂ ਸੁੱਕ ਗਈਆਂ; ਸਾਰੇ ਲੋਕ ਅਤੇ ਅਲੋਕ ਕੰਬ ਗਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਉਕ ਚਕੇ ਦ੍ਰਿਗਪਾਲ ਸਬੈ ਕਿਹ ਪੈ ਕਲਕੀ ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਰਿਸਾਏ। ੩੯੩।","roman":"Chauk chake drigpaal sabai kih pai kalkee kari kop risaae | 393 |","meaning_en":"All the guardians of the directions were startled and amazed: 'Against whom has Kalki become so enraged?'","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦ੍ਰਿਗਪਾਲ: printed so; read as ਦਿਗਪਾਲ, guardians of the directions.","meaning_pa":"ਦਿਗਪਾਲ ਸਾਰੇ ਹੈਰਾਨ ਅਤੇ ਘਬਰਾ ਗਏ: 'ਕਲਕੀ ਕਿਸ ਉੱਤੇ ਇੰਨਾ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਹੋਇਆ ਹੈ?'","note_pa":"ਦ੍ਰਿਗਪਾਲ: ਛਾਪੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਇਸੇ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਹੈ; ਦਿਗਪਾਲ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ (ਦਿਸ਼ਾਵਾਂ ਦੇ ਰਖਵਾਲੇ)।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[394],"number_text":"੩੯੪।","page":760,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਹਠੀ ਹਠ ਠਾਨਿ ਹਠੀ ਰਣਿ ਕੋਟਿਕੁ ਮਾਰੇ।","roman":"Baan kamaan sanbhaari hathee hath thaani hathee rani kotiku maare |","meaning_en":"Wielding arrows and bow, the steadfast one, firm in his resolve, slew millions in battle.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਾਣ ਅਤੇ ਕਮਾਨ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਕੇ, ਪੱਕੇ ਇਰਾਦੇ ਵਾਲੇ ਹਠੀ ਨੇ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਰੋੜਾਂ ਮਾਰ ਦਿੱਤੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਂਘ ਕਹੂੰ ਸਿਰ ਬਾਹ ਕਹੂੰ ਅਸਿ ਰੇਣੁ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਣ ਸਬੈ ਕਰਿ ਡਾਰੇ।","roman":"Jaangh kahoon sir baah kahoon asi renu pramaan sabai kari daare |","meaning_en":"Thighs here, heads and arms there: with his sword he reduced them all to dust.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਪੱਟ, ਕਿਤੇ ਸਿਰ, ਕਿਤੇ ਬਾਂਹ; ਤਲਵਾਰ ਨਾਲ ਉਸ ਨੇ ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਧੂੜ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਿਲਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜ ਕਹੁੰ ਗਜਰਾਜ ਧੁਜਾ ਰਥ ਉਸਟ ਪਰੇ ਰਣਿ ਪੁਸਟ ਬਿਦਾਰੇ।","roman":"Baaj kahun gajraaj dhujaa rath usat pare rani pusat bidaare |","meaning_en":"Horses here, and great elephants, banners, chariots and camels lay on the field, their strong bodies torn apart,","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਉਸਟ: camel.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਘੋੜੇ, ਕਿਤੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਹਾਥੀ, ਝੰਡੇ, ਰਥ ਅਤੇ ਊਠ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਏ ਹਨ, ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦੇ ਮਜ਼ਬੂਤ ਸਰੀਰ ਚੀਰੇ ਹੋਏ;","note_pa":"ਉਸਟ: ਊਠ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਨੁਕ ਬਾਗ ਬਨਿਓ ਰਣਿ ਮੰਡਲ ਪੇਖਨ ਕਉ ਜਟਿ ਧੂਰ ਪਧਾਰੇ। ੩੯੪।","roman":"Jaanuk baag banio rani mandal pekhan kau jati dhoor padhaare | 394 |","meaning_en":"as if a garden had been laid out on the battlefield, and Shiva had come to see it.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਟਿ ਧੂਰ: Dhurjati, Shiva.","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਨੋ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਾਗ਼ ਲਾਇਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੋਵੇ, ਅਤੇ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖਣ ਲਈ ਸ਼ਿਵ ਆਏ ਹੋਣ।","note_pa":"ਜਟਿ ਧੂਰ: ਧੂਰਜਟੀ, ਸ਼ਿਵ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[395],"number_text":"੩੯੫।","page":760,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਾਜ ਭਰੇ ਅਰਿਰਾਜ ਚਹੂੰ ਦਿਸ ਭਾਜਿ ਚਲੇ ਨਹੀ ਆਨਿ ਘਿਰੇ।","roman":"Laaj bhare ariraaj chahoon dis bhaaji chale nahee aani ghire |","meaning_en":"Full of honour, the enemy kings did not flee in all directions, but came and surrounded (him).","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as 'did not flee ... but came and surrounded'; it could also be read 'fled ... and did not come back'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਣ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੇ ਵੈਰੀ ਰਾਜੇ ਚਾਰੇ ਪਾਸਿਓਂ ਨਾ ਭੱਜੇ, ਸਗੋਂ ਆ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਘੇਰ ਲਿਆ।","note_pa":"ਇਸ ਨੂੰ 'ਭੱਜ ਗਏ ... ਅਤੇ ਵਾਪਸ ਨਾ ਆਏ' ਵੀ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਹਿ ਬਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਗਦਾ ਬਰਛੀ ਛਟ ਛੈਲ ਛਕੇ ਚਿਤ ਚੌਪ ਚਿਰੇ।","roman":"Gahi baan kripaan gadaa barchhee chhat chhail chhake chit chaup chire |","meaning_en":"Taking arrows, swords, maces and spears, the gallant youths, long eager at heart,","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਕੇ ਚਿਤ ਚੌਪ ਚਿਰੇ: 'their hearts filled with long-held eagerness'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਬਾਣ, ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ, ਗਦੇ ਅਤੇ ਬਰਛੇ ਚੁੱਕ ਕੇ, ਛੈਲ ਜਵਾਨ, ਜਿਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੇ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਚਿਰਾਂ ਦਾ ਚਾਅ ਸੀ, ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਏ।","note_pa":"ਛਕੇ ਚਿਤ ਚੌਪ ਚਿਰੇ: ਅਰਥ ਅਸਪੱਸ਼ਟ; 'ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਚਿਰਾਂ ਦਾ ਚਾਅ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਤਿਮਾਨ ਸੁਜਾਨ ਅਜਾਨੁ ਭੁਜਾ ਕਰਿ ਪੈਜ ਪਰੇ ਨਹੀ ਫੇਰਿ ਫਿਰੇ।","roman":"Pratimaan sujaan ajaanu bhujaa kari paij pare nahee pheri phire |","meaning_en":"matchless and wise, with arms reaching to the knees, fell on, keeping their pledge, and did not turn back.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੇਮਿਸਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਸਿਆਣੇ, ਬਾਹਾਂ ਗੋਡਿਆਂ ਤੱਕ ਲੰਬੀਆਂ ਵਾਲੇ, ਆਪਣਾ ਪ੍ਰਣ ਨਿਭਾਉਂਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਅੱਗੇ ਵਧੇ, ਅਤੇ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਨਾ ਮੁੜੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਣ ਮੋ ਮਰਿ ਕੈ ਜਸ ਕੋ ਕਰਿ ਕੈ ਹਰਿ ਸੋ ਲਰਿ ਕੈ ਭਵ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਤਰੇ। ੩੯੫।","roman":"Ran mo mari kai jas ko kari kai hari so lari kai bhav sindhu tare | 395 |","meaning_en":"Dying in battle, winning glory, fighting with the Lord, they crossed the ocean of existence.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਰ ਕੇ, ਜਸ ਖੱਟ ਕੇ, ਹਰੀ ਨਾਲ ਲੜ ਕੇ, ਉਹ ਸੰਸਾਰ-ਸਾਗਰ ਤਰ ਗਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[396],"number_text":"੩੯੬।","page":760,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੰਗ ਸੋ ਜਾਨੁ ਸੁਰੰਗੇ ਹੈ ਸਿੰਧੁਰ ਛੂਟੀ ਹੈ ਸੀਸ ਪੈ ਸ੍ਰੋਨ ਅਲੇਲੈ।","roman":"Rang so jaanu surange hai sindhur chhootee hai sees pai sron alelai |","meaning_en":"The elephants seemed dyed in a fine colour, with blood gushing over their heads;","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਾਥੀ ਮਾਨੋ ਰੰਗ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੋਹਣੇ ਰੰਗੇ ਲੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ, ਸਿਰਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਲਹੂ ਦੀ ਧਾਰ ਵਗਦੀ ਹੈ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਜ ਗਿਰੇ ਭਟ ਰਾਜ ਕਹੂੰ ਬਿਚਲੇ ਕੁਪ ਕੈ ਕਲ ਕੇ ਅਸਿ ਕੇਲੈ।","roman":"Baaj gire bhat raaj kahoon bichle kup kai kal ke asi kelai |","meaning_en":"horses fell; here and there the chief warriors were routed as Kalki's sword sported in anger;","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲ ਕੇ ਅਸਿ: read as 'Kalki's sword'; could be 'the sword of Death'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਘੋੜੇ ਡਿੱਗੇ; ਇੱਥੇ-ਉੱਥੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਕਲਕੀ ਦੀ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਖੇਡ ਰਹੀ ਹੋਵੇ;","note_pa":"ਕਲ ਕੇ ਅਸਿ: 'ਕਲਕੀ ਦੀ ਤਲਵਾਰ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ 'ਮੌਤ ਦੀ ਤਲਵਾਰ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਚਰ ਜਾਨੁ ਕਰੈ ਬਸੁਧਾ ਪਰ ਜੂਝਿ ਗਿਰੇ ਪਗ ਦ੍ਵੈ ਨ ਪਛੇਲੈ।","roman":"Chaachar jaanu karai basudhaa par joojhi gire pag dvai na pachhelai |","meaning_en":"as if playing chachar on the earth, they fell fighting, not stepping back two paces,","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਾਚਰ: the Holi song-and-dance revel.","meaning_pa":"ਧਰਤੀ ਉੱਤੇ ਮਾਨੋ ਚਾਚਰ ਖੇਡੀ ਜਾ ਰਹੀ ਹੋਵੇ; ਉਹ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗੇ, ਪਿੱਛੇ ਦੋ ਕਦਮ ਵੀ ਨਾ ਹਟੇ,","note_pa":"ਚਾਚਰ: ਹੋਲੀ ਦਾ ਗੀਤ-ਨਾਚ ਰੰਗ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਨੁਕ ਪਾਨ ਕੈ ਭੰਗ ਮਲੰਗ ਸੁ ਫਾਗੁਨ ਅੰਤਿ ਬਸੰਤ ਸੋ ਖੇਲੈ। ੩੯੬।","roman":"Jaanuk paan kai bhang malang su phaagun anti basant so khelai | 396 |","meaning_en":"like malangs who had drunk bhang, playing Holi at the end of Phagun, in spring.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਲੰਗ: ecstatic wandering fakirs.","meaning_pa":"ਮਾਨੋ ਭੰਗ ਪੀ ਕੇ ਮਲੰਗ ਫੱਗਣ ਦੇ ਅਖੀਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਸੰਤ ਰੁੱਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੋਲੀ ਖੇਡ ਰਹੇ ਹੋਣ।","note_pa":"ਮਲੰਗ: ਮਸਤ ਭਟਕਦੇ ਫ਼ਕੀਰ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[397],"number_text":"੩੯੭।","page":760,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇਤਕ ਜੀਤਿ ਬਚੇ ਸੁ ਸਬੈ ਭਟ ਚਓਪ ਚੜੇ ਚਹੁੰ ਓਰਨ ਧਾਏ।","roman":"Jetak jeeti bache su sabai bhat chaop chare chahun oran dhaae |","meaning_en":"All the warriors who had survived and were victorious rushed eagerly from all four sides;","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੰਨੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਜਿੱਤ ਕੇ ਬਚੇ ਸਨ, ਉਹ ਸਾਰੇ ਉਤਸ਼ਾਹ ਨਾਲ ਚਾਰੇ ਪਾਸਿਓਂ ਦੌੜ ਪਏ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਗਦਾ ਬਰਛੀ ਅਸਿ ਕਾਢਿ ਲਏ ਕਰ ਮੋ ਚਮਕਾਏ।","roman":"Baan kamaan gadaa barchhee asi kaadhi lae kar mo chamkaae |","meaning_en":"drawing arrows, bows, maces, spears and swords, they flashed them in their hands.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਾਣ, ਕਮਾਨਾਂ, ਗਦੇ, ਬਰਛੇ ਅਤੇ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਕੱਢ ਕੇ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਨੇ ਹੱਥਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਚਮਕਾਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਬੁਕ ਮਾਰਿ ਤੁਰੰਗ ਧਸੇ ਰਨਿ ਸਾਵਨ ਕੀ ਘਟਿ ਜਿਉ ਘਹਰਾਏ।","roman":"Chaabuk maari turang dhase rani saavan kee ghati jiu ghahraae |","meaning_en":"Whipping their horses they plunged into the battle, rumbling like the clouds of Sawan.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚਾਬਕ ਮਾਰ ਕੇ ਘੋੜੇ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੜ ਗਏ, ਸਾਵਣ ਦੇ ਬੱਦਲਾਂ ਵਾਂਗ ਗਰਜਦੇ ਹੋਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਲਕੀ ਕਰਿ ਲੈ ਕਰਵਾਰਿ ਸੁ ਏਕ ਹਨੇ ਅਰਿ ਅਨੇਕ ਪਰਾਏ। ੩੯੭।","roman":"Sree kalkee kari lai karvaari su ek hane ari anek paraae | 397 |","meaning_en":"Sri Kalki took his sword in hand; some foes he slew and many fled.","page":760,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁ ਏਕ ਹਨੇ: 'some he slew' (or 'he slew one').","meaning_pa":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਲਕੀ ਨੇ ਹੱਥ ਵਿੱਚ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਲਈ; ਕੁਝ ਵੈਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ।","note_pa":"ਸੁ ਏਕ ਹਨੇ: 'ਕੁਝ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਿਆ' (ਜਾਂ 'ਇੱਕ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਿਆ')।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[398],"number_text":"੩੯੮।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰ ਮਚੀ ਬਿਸੰਭਾਰ ਜਬੈ ਤਬ ਆਯੁਧ ਛੋਰਿ ਸਬੈ ਭਟ ਭਾਜੇ।","roman":"Maar machee bisanbhaar jabai tab aayudh chhori sabai bhat bhaaje |","meaning_en":"When the slaughter grew beyond all bounds, all the warriors abandoned their weapons and fled.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦੋਂ ਕਤਲੇਆਮ ਹੱਦਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਵੱਧ ਗਿਆ, ਤਦ ਸਾਰੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਸੁੱਟ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਾਰਿ ਹਥ੍ਯਾਰ ਉਤਾਰਿ ਸਨਾਹਿ ਸੁ ਏਕ ਹੀ ਬਾਰ ਭਜੇ ਨਹੀ ਗਾਜੇ।","roman":"Daari hathyaar utaari sanaahi su ek hee baar bhaje nahee gaaje |","meaning_en":"Throwing down their arms and taking off their armour, they fled all at once and roared no more.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਥਿਆਰ ਸੁੱਟ ਕੇ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਰਾ ਬਸਤਰ ਉਤਾਰ ਕੇ, ਉਹ ਇੱਕੋ ਵਾਰ ਭੱਜ ਗਏ ਅਤੇ ਫਿਰ ਗਰਜੇ ਨਹੀਂ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਤਹਾ ਗਹਿ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਬੈ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਬਿਰਾਜੇ।","roman":"Sree kalkee avtaar tahaa gahi sasatr sabai ih bhaati biraaje |","meaning_en":"Sri Kalki Avtar, holding all his weapons, stood there in such splendour","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸ੍ਰੀ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਨੇ ਉੱਥੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਕੇ, ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੀ ਸ਼ਾਨ ਨਾਲ ਖੜ੍ਹੇ ਹੋ ਗਏ"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਮਿ ਅਕਾਸ ਪਤਾਰ ਚਕਿਓ ਛਬਿ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਦੋਊ ਲਖਿ ਲਾਜੇ। ੩੯੮।","roman":"Bhoomi akaas pataar chakio chhabi dev adev do'oo lakhi laaje | 398 |","meaning_en":"that earth, sky and the netherworld were amazed, and gods and demons both, seeing his beauty, were abashed.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਧਰਤੀ, ਅਕਾਸ਼ ਅਤੇ ਪਾਤਾਲ ਹੈਰਾਨ ਹੋ ਗਏ, ਅਤੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਦੋਵੇਂ ਉਸ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਸ਼ਰਮਿੰਦੇ ਹੋਏ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[399],"number_text":"੩੯੯।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਿ ਭਜੀ ਪ੍ਰਤਿਨਾ ਅਰਿ ਕੀ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਹਥ੍ਯਾਰ ਸੰਭਾਰੇ।","roman":"Dekhi bhajee pratinaa ari kee kalkee avtaar hathyaar sanbhaare |","meaning_en":"Seeing the enemy army fleeing, Kalki Avtar took up his weapons;","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੈਰੀ ਦੀ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਨੂੰ ਭੱਜਦਿਆਂ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ, ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਨੇ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਸੰਭਾਲੇ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਕਮਾਨ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਗਦਾ ਛਿਨ ਬੀਚ ਸਬੈ ਕਰਿ ਚੂਰਨ ਡਾਰੇ।","roman":"Baan kamaan kripaan gadaa chhin beech sabai kari chooran daare |","meaning_en":"in an instant he smashed all (their) arrows, bows, swords and maces to pieces.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇੱਕ ਪਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਸ ਨੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਬਾਣ, ਕਮਾਨਾਂ, ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਗਦੇ ਚੂਰ-ਚੂਰ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਗਿ ਚਲੇ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਭਟਾ ਜਿਮਿ ਪਉਨ ਬਹੇ ਦ੍ਰੁਮ ਪਾਤ ਨਿਹਾਰੇ।","roman":"Bhaagi chale ih bhaati bhataa jimi paun bahe drum paat nihaare |","meaning_en":"The warriors fled like the leaves of trees seen blowing in the wind.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਯੋਧੇ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਭੱਜੇ ਜਿਵੇਂ ਹਵਾ ਚੱਲਣ ਤੇ ਰੁੱਖਾਂ ਦੇ ਪੱਤੇ ਝੜਦੇ ਵੇਖੇ ਜਾਣ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੈਨ ਪਰੀ ਕਛੁ ਮਾਨ ਰਹਿਓ ਨਹਿ ਬਾਨਨ ਡਾਰਿ ਨਿਦਾਨ ਪਧਾਰੇ। ੩੯੯।","roman":"Pain paree kachhu maan rahio nahi baanan daari nidaan padhaare | 399 |","meaning_en":"They fell at his feet, no pride was left in them; throwing down their arrows, at last they went away.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪੈਨ ਪਰੀ: read as 'fell at (his) feet'; could also mean 'defeat befell them'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਪੈਰੀਂ ਪਏ, ਉਹਨਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੋਈ ਮਾਣ ਨਾ ਰਿਹਾ; ਆਖ਼ਰ ਬਾਣ ਸੁੱਟ ਕੇ ਉਹ ਚਲੇ ਗਏ।","note_pa":"ਪੈਨ ਪਰੀ: 'ਪੈਰਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਏ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਇਸ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ 'ਹਾਰ ਆ ਪਈ' ਵੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੁਪ੍ਰਿਆ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸੁਪ੍ਰਿਆ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Supriaa chhand","meaning_en":"Supriya metre.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੁਪ੍ਰਿਆ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[400],"number_text":"੪੦੦।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਭਟ ਮਿਲਤ ਮੁਖਿ ਮਾਰ ਉਚਾਰਤ। ਕਹੂੰ ਭਟ ਭਾਜਿ ਪੁਕਾਰਤ ਆਰਤ।","roman":"Kahoon bhat milat mukhi maar uchaarat | kahoon bhat bhaaji pukaarat aarat |","meaning_en":"Here warriors meet, crying 'Kill!'; there warriors flee, crying out in distress.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਮਿਲ ਕੇ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਕਹਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਿਤੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਦੁੱਖ ਵਿੱਚ ਪੁਕਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਤਕ ਜੋਧ ਫਿਰਤ ਦਲ ਗਾਹਤ। ਕੇਤਕ ਜੂਝ ਬਰੰਗਨ ਬ੍ਯਾਹਤ। ੪੦੦।","roman":"Ketak jodh phirat dal gaahat | ketak joojh barangan byaahat | 400 |","meaning_en":"Some fighters roam about, churning through the army; some fall fighting and marry the heavenly maidens.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਯੋਧੇ ਫ਼ੌਜ ਨੂੰ ਚੀਰਦੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਈ ਲੜਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਦੇਵ-ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਨਾਲ ਵਿਆਹ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[401],"number_text":"੪੦੧।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਬਰ ਬੀਰ ਫਿਰਤ ਸਰ ਮਾਰਤ। ਕਹੂੰ ਰਣ ਛੋਡਿ ਭਜਤ ਭਟ ਆਰਤ।","roman":"Kahoon bar beer phirat sar maarat | kahoon ran chhodi bhajat bhat aarat |","meaning_en":"Here fine warriors roam shooting arrows; there warriors leave the battle and flee in distress.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਤੀਰ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਿਤੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਰਣ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਦੁੱਖ ਵਿੱਚ ਭੱਜਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਈ ਡਰੁ ਡਾਰਿ ਹਨਤ ਰਣਿ ਜੋਧਾ। ਕੇਈ ਮੁਖਿ ਮਾਰ ਰਟਤ ਕਰਿ ਕ੍ਰੋਧਾ। ੪੦੧।","roman":"Ke'ee daru daari hanat rani jodhaa | ke'ee mukhi maar ratat kari krodhaa | 401 |","meaning_en":"Some, casting off fear, strike down fighters in battle; some, in anger, keep crying 'Kill!'","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਡਰ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਯੋਧਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਈ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ 'ਮਾਰੋ!' ਰਟਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[402],"number_text":"੪੦੨।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਈ ਖਗ ਖੰਡਿ ਗਿਰਤ ਰਣਿ ਛਤ੍ਰੀ। ਕੇਤਕ ਭਾਗਿ ਚਲਤ ਤ੍ਰਸਿ ਅਤ੍ਰੀ।","roman":"Ke'ee khag khandi girat rani chhatree | ketak bhaagi chalat trasi atree |","meaning_en":"Some Kshatriyas, cut down by swords, fall in battle; some, without weapons, flee in terror.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਤ੍ਰੀ: read as 'without weapons'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਖੱਤਰੀ ਤਲਵਾਰਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਕੱਟੇ ਜਾ ਕੇ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਈ ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾਂ ਡਰ ਕੇ ਭੱਜ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","note_pa":"ਅਤ੍ਰੀ: 'ਹਥਿਆਰਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾਂ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਤਕ ਨਿਭ੍ਰਮ ਜੁਧ ਮਚਾਵਤ। ਆਹਵ ਸੀਝਿ ਦਿਵਾਲਯ ਪਾਵਤ। ੪੦੨।","roman":"Ketak nibhram judh machaavat | aahav seejhi divaalay paavat | 402 |","meaning_en":"Some wage war without hesitation, and, winning in battle, attain the abode of the gods.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਬਿਨਾਂ ਝਿਜਕ ਜੰਗ ਛੇੜਦੇ ਹਨ, ਅਤੇ ਰਣ ਜਿੱਤ ਕੇ ਦੇਵਲੋਕ ਪਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[403],"number_text":"੪੦੩।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਤਕ ਜੂਝਿ ਮਰਤ ਰਣ ਮੰਡਲਿ। ਕੇਈਕੁ ਭੇਦਿ ਚਲੇ ਬ੍ਰਹਮੰਡਲ।","roman":"Ketak joojhi marat ran mandli | ke'eeku bhedi chale brahmandal |","meaning_en":"Some fall fighting and die on the field of battle; some pierce through the sphere of the universe (and go beyond).","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਰਣ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੜ ਕੇ ਮਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਈ ਬ੍ਰਹਮੰਡ ਨੂੰ ਵਿੰਨ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਅੱਗੇ ਲੰਘ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਈਕੁ ਆਨਿ ਪ੍ਰਹਾਰਤ ਸਾਂਗੈ। ਕੇਤਕ ਭੰਗ ਗਿਰਤ ਹੁਇ ਆਂਗੈ। ੪੦੩।","roman":"Ke'eeku aani prahaarat saangai | ketak bhang girat hui aangai | 403 |","meaning_en":"Some come and strike with lances; some fall with broken limbs.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਆ ਕੇ ਬਰਛੇ ਮਾਰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕਈ ਅੰਗ ਟੁੱਟ ਕੇ ਡਿੱਗਦੇ ਹਨ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਬਿਸੇਖ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਬਿਸੇਖ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Bisekh chhand","meaning_en":"Bisekh metre.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਿਸੇਖ ਛੰਦ"},{"type":"verse","number":[404],"number_text":"੪੦੪।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜਿ ਬਿਨਾ ਭਟ ਲਾਜ ਸਬੈ ਤਜਿ ਸਾਜ ਜਹਾ।","roman":"Bhaaji binaa bhat laaj sabai taji saaj jahaa |","meaning_en":"Where the warriors fled, casting off shame and all their gear,","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿੱਥੇ ਯੋਧੇ ਭੱਜੇ, ਸ਼ਰਮ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਰਾ ਸਾਜ਼-ਸਾਮਾਨ ਛੱਡ ਕੇ,"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਚਤ ਭੂਤ ਪਿਸਾਚ ਨਿਸਾਚਰ ਰਾਜ ਤਹਾ।","roman":"Naachat bhoot pisaach nisaachar raaj tahaa |","meaning_en":"there ghosts, goblins and night-demons danced in their glory.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨਿਸਾਚਰ ਰਾਜ: 'kings of the night-demons' or 'night-demons shone'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉੱਥੇ ਭੂਤ, ਪਿਸ਼ਾਚ ਅਤੇ ਨਿਸ਼ਾਚਰ ਰਾਜੇ ਆਪਣੀ ਸ਼ਾਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਨੱਚਦੇ ਸਨ।","note_pa":"ਨਿਸਾਚਰ ਰਾਜ: 'ਨਿਸ਼ਾਚਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਰਾਜੇ' ਜਾਂ 'ਨਿਸ਼ਾਚਰ ਚਮਕੇ'; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਤ ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਮਹਾ ਰਣ ਕੋ ਬਰਨੈ।","roman":"Dekhat dev adev mahaa ran ko barnai |","meaning_en":"Gods and demons watch; who can describe so great a battle?","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੇਵਤੇ ਅਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਵੇਖਦੇ ਹਨ; ਇੰਨੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਰਣ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਕੌਣ ਕਰ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ?"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੂਝ ਭਯੋ ਜਿਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੁ ਪਾਰਥ ਸੋ ਕਰਨੈ। ੪੦੪।","roman":"Joojh bhayo jih bhaati su paarath so karnai | 404 |","meaning_en":"The fighting was like that of Arjun with Karan.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਾਰਥ: Partha, Arjun.","meaning_pa":"ਲੜਾਈ ਉਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੀ ਸੀ ਜਿਵੇਂ ਅਰਜਨ ਦੀ ਕਰਨ ਨਾਲ ਹੋਈ ਸੀ।","note_pa":"ਪਾਰਥ: ਅਰਜਨ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[405],"number_text":"੪੦੫।","page":761,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਾਵ ਕਰੈ ਰਿਸ ਖਾਇ ਮਹਾ ਹਠ ਠਾਨ ਹਠੀ।","roman":"Daav karai ris khaai mahaa hath thaan hathee |","meaning_en":"The steadfast ones, firm in their resolve, filled with great rage, make their moves;","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹਠੀ ਯੋਧੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਹਠ ਤੇ ਅਡੋਲ, ਬਹੁਤ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਚਾਲਾਂ ਚਲਦੇ ਹਨ;"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋਪ ਭਰੇ ਇਹ ਭਾਤ ਸੁ ਪਾਵਕ ਜਾਨੁ ਭਠੀ।","roman":"Kop bhare ih bhaat su paavak jaanu bhathee |","meaning_en":"they are so full of anger, like the fire in a furnace.","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਇੰਨੇ ਗੁੱਸੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਭਰੇ ਹਨ ਜਿਵੇਂ ਭੱਠੀ ਦੀ ਅੱਗ ਹੋਵੇ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰੁਧ ਭਰੇ ਰਣਿ ਛਤ੍ਰਜ ਅਤ੍ਰਣ ਝਾਰਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Krudh bhare rani chhatraj atran jhaarat hai |","meaning_en":"Full of wrath, the Kshatriyas wield their weapons in battle;","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਤ੍ਰਣ: read as 'weapons'; could be 'the unprotected'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੇ ਖੱਤਰੀ ਰਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਹਥਿਆਰ ਚਲਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ;","note_pa":"ਅਤ੍ਰਣ: 'ਹਥਿਆਰ' ਵਜੋਂ ਪੜ੍ਹਿਆ ਗਿਆ; ਅਨਿਸ਼ਚਿਤ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜਿ ਚਲੈ ਨਹੀ ਪਾਵ ਸੁ ਮਾਰਿ ਪੁਕਾਰਤ ਹੈ। ੪੦੫।","roman":"Bhaaji chalai nahee paav su maari pukaarat hai | 405 |","meaning_en":"they do not run even a step, but cry out 'Kill!'","page":761,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[406],"number_text":"੪੦੬।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਖਤ ਹੈ ਦਿਵ ਦੇਵ ਧਨੈ ਧਨਿ ਜੰਪਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Dekhat hai div dev dhanai dhani janpat hai |","meaning_en":"The gods of heaven watch and cry 'Blessed, blessed!'","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੂਮ ਅਕਾਸ ਪਤਾਲ ਚਵੋ ਚਕ ਕੰਪਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Bhoom akaas pataal chavo chak kanpat hai |","meaning_en":"Earth, sky, the netherworld and the four quarters tremble.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜਤ ਨਾਹਿਨ ਬੀਰ ਮਹਾ ਰਣਿ ਗਾਜਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Bhaajat naahin beer mahaa rani gaajat hai |","meaning_en":"The great warriors do not flee but roar in battle;","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਛ ਭੁਜੰਗਨ ਨਾਰਿ ਲਖੇ ਛਬਿ ਲਾਜਤ ਹੈ। ੪੦੬।","roman":"Jachh bhujangan naari lakhe chhabi laajat hai | 406 |","meaning_en":"the women of the Yakshas and Nagas, seeing their beauty, are abashed.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[407],"number_text":"੪੦੭।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਕਰਿ ਕੋਪ ਮਹਾ ਸੁਰ ਸੂਰ ਤਹਾ।","roman":"Dhaavat hai kari kop mahaa sur soor tahaa |","meaning_en":"There the great heroes charge in fury,","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਹਾ ਸੁਰ ਸੂਰ: 'great heroes'; ਸੁਰ could also mean 'gods'."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਂਡਤ ਹੈ ਬਿਕਰਾਰ ਭਯੰਕਰ ਜੁਧ ਜਹਾ।","roman":"Maandat hai bikraar bhayankar judh jahaa |","meaning_en":"where they wage a fierce and dreadful war.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਵਤ ਹੈ ਸੁਰ ਨਾਰਿ ਸੁ ਸਾਮੁਹਿ ਜੁਝਤ ਹੈ।","roman":"Paavat hai sur naari su saamuhi jujhat hai |","meaning_en":"Those who fight face to face win the women of the gods;","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਗੰਧ੍ਰਬ ਸਬੈ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਸੁਝਤ ਹੈ। ੪੦੭।","roman":"Dev adev gandhrab sabai krit sujhat hai | 407 |","meaning_en":"gods, demons and Gandharvas all witness their deeds.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੰਚਲਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਚੰਚਲਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Chanchlaa chhand","meaning_en":"Chanchala metre.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[408],"number_text":"੪੦੮।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰਬੇ ਕੋ ਤਾਹਿ ਤਾਕਿ ਧਾਏ ਬੀਰ ਸਾਵਧਾਨ।","roman":"Maarbe ko taahi taaki dhaae beer saavdhaan |","meaning_en":"Taking aim to kill him, the warriors charged, alert;","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਹਿ: 'him', read as Kalki."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋਨ ਲਾਗੇ ਜੁਧ ਕੇ ਜਹਾਂ ਤਹਾ ਸਬੈ ਬਿਧਾਨ।","roman":"Hon laage judh ke jahaan tahaa sabai bidhaan |","meaning_en":"all the ways of war began to be practised everywhere.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੀਮ ਭਾਤਿ ਧਾਇ ਕੈ ਨਿਸੰਕ ਘਾਇ ਕਰਤ ਆਇ।","roman":"Bheem bhaati dhaai kai nisank ghaai karat aai |","meaning_en":"Rushing like Bhim, they come and fearlessly deal wounds;","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੂਝਿ ਜੂਝ ਕੈ ਮਰੈ ਸੁ ਦੇਵ ਲੋਕਿ ਬਸਤ ਜਾਇ। ੪੦੮।","roman":"Joojhi joojh kai marai su dev loki basat jaai | 408 |","meaning_en":"those who fall fighting go and dwell in the world of the gods.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[409],"number_text":"੪੦੯।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਨਿ ਤਾਨਿ ਬਾਨ ਕੋ ਅਜਾਨੁ ਬਾਹ ਧਾਵਹੀ।","roman":"Taani taani baan ko ajaanu baah dhaavhee |","meaning_en":"Drawing their arrows again and again, the long-armed ones charge;","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਜਾਨੁ ਬਾਹ: with arms reaching to the knees."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੂਝਿ ਜੂਝ ਕੈ ਮਰੈ ਅਲੋਕ ਲੋਕ ਪਾਵਹੀ।","roman":"Joojhi joojh kai marai alok lok paavhee |","meaning_en":"fighting on, they die and reach the world beyond.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੰਗ ਜੰਗਿ ਅੰਗ ਨੰਗ ਭੰਗ ਅੰਗਿ ਹੋਇ ਪਰਤ।","roman":"Rang jangi ang nang bhang angi hoi parat |","meaning_en":"Coloured by war, their bodies bared and limbs broken, they fall;","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਟੂਕਿ ਟੂਕਿ ਹੋਇ ਗਿਰੈ ਸੁ ਦੇਵ ਸੁੰਦ੍ਰੀਨਿ ਬਰਤ। ੪੦੯।","roman":"Tooki tooki hoi girai su dev sundreeni barat | 409 |","meaning_en":"cut to pieces they fall, and the beautiful women of the gods wed them.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਤ੍ਰਿੜਕਾ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿੜਕਾ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Trirkaa chhand","meaning_en":"Tririka metre.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[410],"number_text":"੪੧੦।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਤੀਰੰ। ਬ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਬੀਰੰ।","roman":"Trirrir teeran | brirrir beeran |","meaning_en":"Arrows (fly); warriors (rush);","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"In this metre each word is preceded by a sound-word (ਤ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ, ਬ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ, etc.) imitating the din of battle; these are left untranslated."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਢੋਲੰ। ਬ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਬੋਲੰ। ੪੧੦।","roman":"Drirrir dholan | brirrir bolan | 410 |","meaning_en":"drums (boom); (warriors) call out.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[411],"number_text":"੪੧੧।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਤਾਜੀ। ਬ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਬਾਜੀ।","roman":"Trirrir taajee | brirrir baajee |","meaning_en":"Steeds and horses (charge);","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਹਾਥੀ। ਸ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਸਾਥੀ। ੪੧੧।","roman":"Hrirrir haathee | srirrir saathee | 411 |","meaning_en":"elephants, and comrades.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[412],"number_text":"੪੧੨।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਬਾਣੰ। ਜ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਜੁਆਣੰ।","roman":"Brirrir baanan | jrirrir juaanan |","meaning_en":"Arrows the young warriors","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਛੋਰੈਂ। ਜ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਜੋਰੈਂ। ੪੧੨।","roman":"Chhrirrir chhorain | jrirrir jorain | 412 |","meaning_en":"loose, and fit to the string.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[413],"number_text":"੪੧੩।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਖੇਤੰ। ਪ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਪ੍ਰੇਤੰ।","roman":"Khrirrir khetan | prirrir pretan |","meaning_en":"On the battlefield the ghosts","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝ੍ਰਿੜੜਿੜ ਨਾਚੈ। ਰਿੜਝਿੜ ਰਾਚੈ। ੪੧੩।","roman":"Jhrirrir naachai | rirjhir raachai | 413 |","meaning_en":"dance, absorbed in revelry.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[414],"number_text":"੪੧੪।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਹੂਰੰ। ਪ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਪੂਰੰ।","roman":"Hrirrir hooran | prirrir pooran |","meaning_en":"The houris (heavenly maidens) fill (the sky);","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਕਾਛੀ। ਨ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਨਾਚੀ। ੪੧੪।","roman":"Krirrir kaachhee | nrirrir naachee | 414 |","meaning_en":"dressed for the dance, they dance.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਛੀ: 'dressed up (in dance attire)'."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[415],"number_text":"੪੧੫।","page":762,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਤੇਗੰ। ਬ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਬੇਗੰ।","roman":"Trirrir tegan | brirrir began |","meaning_en":"Swords (swing) swiftly;","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਚਮਕੈ। ਝ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਝਮਕੈ। ੪੧੫।","roman":"Chrirrir chamkai | jhrirrir jhamkai | 415 |","meaning_en":"they flash and glitter.","page":762,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[416],"number_text":"੪੧੬।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਜੋਧੰ। ਕ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਕ੍ਰੋਧੰ।","roman":"Jrirrir jodhan | krirrir krodhan |","meaning_en":"Warriors, in anger,","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਜੂਝੈ। ਲ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਲੂਝੈ। ੪੧੬।","roman":"Jrirrir joojhai | lrirrir loojhai | 416 |","meaning_en":"fight and struggle.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[417],"number_text":"੪੧੭।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਖੇਤੰ। ਅ੍ਰੜਰਿੜ ਅਚੇਤੰ।","roman":"Khrirrir khetan | rarrir achetan |","meaning_en":"On the battlefield (lie) senseless","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅ੍ਰੜਰਿੜ: printed so."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਬਾਜੀ। ਗ੍ਰ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਗਾਜੀ। ੪੧੭।","roman":"Brirrir baajee | grrirrir gaajee | 417 |","meaning_en":"horses and warriors.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਾਜੀ: ghazi, 'warrior'; ਗ੍ਰ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ printed so."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[418],"number_text":"੪੧੮।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਗਜਣੰ। ਭ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਭਜਣੰ।","roman":"Grirrir gajnan | bhrirrir bhajnan |","meaning_en":"There is roaring; there is fleeing;","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਰਾਜਾ। ਲ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਲਾਜਾ। ੪੧੮।","roman":"Rrirrir raajaa | lrirrir laajaa | 418 |","meaning_en":"the king is put to shame.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[419],"number_text":"੪੧੯।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਖਾਂਡੇ। ਬ੍ਰਿੜਿਰਿੜ ਬਾਂਡੇ।","roman":"Khrirrir khaande | briririr baande |","meaning_en":"Double-edged swords and curved blades:","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਂਡੇ: read as 'curved swords'; uncertain. ਬ੍ਰਿੜਿਰਿੜ printed so."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅ੍ਰੜਰਿੜ ਅੰਗੰ। ਜ੍ਰਿੜਰਿੜ ਜੰਗੰ। ੪੧੯।","roman":"Rarrir angan | jrirrir jangan | 419 |","meaning_en":"limbs (are cut) in the war.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪਾਧੜੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪਾਧੜੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Paadhree chhand","meaning_en":"Padhri metre.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[420],"number_text":"੪੨੦।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੈਨ ਜੁਝੀ ਅਪਾਰ। ਰਣਿ ਰੋਹ ਕ੍ਰੋਹ ਧਾਏ ਲੁਝਾਰ।","roman":"Ih bhaati sain jujhee apaar | rani roh kroh dhaae lujhaar |","meaning_en":"In this way the boundless army fell fighting; in fury and anger the warriors charged in battle.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜੰਤ ਬਾਣ ਗਜੰਤ ਬੀਰ। ਉਠੰਤ ਨਾਦ ਭਜੰਤ ਭੀਰ। ੪੨੦।","roman":"Tajant baan gajant beer | uthant naad bhajant bheer | 420 |","meaning_en":"Loosing arrows, the warriors roar; cries go up, and the cowards flee.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[421],"number_text":"੪੨੧।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਏ ਸਬਾਹ ਜੋਧਾ ਸਕੋਪ। ਕਢਤ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਣ ਬਾਹੰਤ ਧੋਪ।","roman":"Dhaae sabaah jodhaa sakop | kadhat kripaan baahant dhop |","meaning_en":"The warriors with their horses charged in fury; drawing their swords, they swing the straight blades.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਬਾਹ: read as 'with horses'; could be Persian 'at dawn'; uncertain. ਧੋਪ: a straight sword."},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੁਝੰਤ ਸੂਰ ਜੁਝੰਤ ਅਪਾਰ। ਜਣ ਸੇਤਬੰਧ ਦਿਖੀਅਤ ਪਹਾਰ। ੪੨੧।","roman":"Lujhant soor jujhant apaar | jan setbandh dikheeat pahaar | 421 |","meaning_en":"Heroes struggle and fall without number, looking like the mountains seen in the bridge to Lanka.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੇਤਬੰਧ: the bridge built by Ram's army to Lanka."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[422],"number_text":"੪੨੨।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਟੰਤ ਅੰਗ ਭਭਕੰਤ ਘਾਵ। ਸਿਝੰਤ ਸੂਰ ਜੁਝੰਤ ਚਾਵ।","roman":"Katant ang bhabhkant ghaav | sijhant soor jujhant chaav |","meaning_en":"Limbs are cut, wounds gush; heroes gain their end, fighting eagerly.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਰਖੰਤ ਸਿਧ ਚਾਰਣ ਅਨੰਤ। ਉਚਰੰਤ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਜੋਧਨ ਬਿਅੰਤ। ੪੨੨।","roman":"Nirkhant sidh chaaran anant | uchrant krit jodhan biant | 422 |","meaning_en":"Countless Siddhas and Charans watch and proclaim the deeds of the innumerable warriors.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[423],"number_text":"੪੨੩।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਚੰਤ ਆਪ ਈਸਰ ਕਰਾਲ। ਬਾਜੰਤ ਡਉਰੁ ਭੈਕਰਿ ਬਿਸਾਲ।","roman":"Naachant aap eesar karaal | baajant dauru bhaikri bisaal |","meaning_en":"The fearsome Lord Shiva himself dances; his huge, dreadful damru drum sounds.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਈਸਰ: Ishvar, here Shiva."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੋਅੰਤ ਮਾਲ ਕਾਲੀ ਕਪਾਲ। ਚਲ ਚਿਤ ਚਖ ਛਾਡੰਤ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ। ੪੨੩।","roman":"Poant maal kaalee kapaal | chal chit chakh chhaadant jvaal | 423 |","meaning_en":"Kali strings a garland of skulls; her restless eyes shoot flames.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਰਸਾਵਲ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Rasaaval chhand","meaning_en":"Rasaval metre.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[424],"number_text":"੪੨੪।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਜੇ ਘੋਰ ਬਾਜੇ। ਧੁਣੰ ਮੇਘ ਲਾਜੇ।","roman":"Baje ghor baaje | dhunan megh laaje |","meaning_en":"Dreadful instruments sounded; at their sound the clouds were shamed.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਹੇ ਖੇਤ ਖਤ੍ਰੀ। ਤਜੇ ਤਾਣਿ ਪਤ੍ਰੀ। ੪੨੪।","roman":"Khahe khet khatree | taje taani patree | 424 |","meaning_en":"Kshatriyas clashed on the field; drawing with strength, they loosed feathered arrows.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[425],"number_text":"੪੨੫।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੈ ਅੰਗ ਭੰਗੰ। ਨਚੇ ਜੰਗ ਰੰਗੰ।","roman":"Girai ang bhangan | nache jang rangan |","meaning_en":"Limbs fall broken; (warriors) dance in the colour of war.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖੁਲੇ ਖਗ ਖੂਨੀ। ਚੜੇ ਚਉਪ ਦੂਨੀ। ੪੨੫।","roman":"Khule khag khoonee | chare chaup doonee | 425 |","meaning_en":"Bloodthirsty swords are bared; zeal doubles.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[426],"number_text":"੪੨੬।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਯੋ ਘੋਰ ਜੁਧੰ। ਇਤੀ ਕਾਹਿ ਸੁਧੰ।","roman":"Bhayo ghor judhan | itee kaahi sudhan |","meaning_en":"A dreadful war took place; who has the wits (to tell) so much?","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਇਤੀ ਕਾਹਿ ਸੁਧੰ: read as 'who has so much awareness'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਣਿਓ ਕਾਲ ਰੂਪੰ। ਭਜੇ ਸਰਬ ਭੂਪੰ। ੪੨੬।","roman":"Jinio kaal roopan | bhaje sarab bhoopan | 426 |","meaning_en":"He of Death-like form won; all the kings fled.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲ ਰੂਪੰ: read as Kalki."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[427],"number_text":"੪੨੭।","page":763,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਬੈ ਸੈਣ ਭਾਜਾ। ਫਿਰ੍ਯੋ ਆਪ ਰਾਜਾ।","roman":"Sabai sain bhaajaa | phiryo aap raajaa |","meaning_en":"The whole army fled; the king himself turned back,","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਠਟ੍ਯੋ ਆਣਿ ਜੁਧੰ। ਭਇਓ ਨਾਦ ਉਧੰ। ੪੨੭।","roman":"Thatyo aani judhan | bhaio naad udhan | 427 |","meaning_en":"came and set up battle; a loud cry rose up.","page":763,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[428],"number_text":"੪੨੮।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜੇ ਬਾਣ ਐਸੇ। ਬਣੰ ਪਤ੍ਰ ਜੈਸੇ।","roman":"Taje baan aise | banan patr jaise |","meaning_en":"He loosed arrows as many as the leaves in a forest,","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਲੰ ਮੇਘ ਧਾਰਾ। ਨਭੰ ਜਾਣੁ ਤਾਰਾ। ੪੨੮।","roman":"Jalan megh dhaaraa | nabhan jaanu taaraa | 428 |","meaning_en":"as the streams of water from clouds, as the stars in the sky.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[429],"number_text":"੪੨੯।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰ ਅੰਸੁਮਾਲੀ। ਸਰੰ ਸਤ੍ਰੁ ਸਾਲੀ।","roman":"Kar ansumaalee | saran satru saalee |","meaning_en":"Like the rays of the sun, the arrows that pierce the foe","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅੰਸੁਮਾਲੀ: the sun; ਕਰ: rays."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਹੂੰ ਓਰਿ ਛੂਟੇ। ਮਹਾ ਜੋਧ ਜੂਟੇ। ੪੨੯।","roman":"Chahoon ori chhoote | mahaa jodh joote | 429 |","meaning_en":"flew on all four sides; great warriors clashed.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[430],"number_text":"੪੩੦।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲੇ ਕੀਟਕਾ ਸੇ। ਬਢੇ ਟਿਡਕਾ ਸੇ।","roman":"Chale keetkaa se | badhe tidkaa se |","meaning_en":"They moved like insects and swarmed like locusts,","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਨੰ ਸਿੰਧੁ ਰੇਤੰ। ਤਨੰ ਰੋਮ ਤੇਤੰ। ੪੩੦।","roman":"Kanan sindhu retan | tanan rom tetan | 430 |","meaning_en":"as many as the grains of sand of the sea, as the hairs on the body.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[431],"number_text":"੪੩੧।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛੁਟੇ ਸ੍ਵਰਣ ਪੁਖੀ। ਸੁਧੰ ਸਾਰ ਮੁਖੀ।","roman":"Chhute svaran pukhee | sudhan saar mukhee |","meaning_en":"Gold-feathered arrows were loosed, with tips of pure steel,","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਲੰ ਕੰਕ ਪਤ੍ਰੀ। ਤਜੇ ਜਾਣੁ ਛਤ੍ਰੀ। ੪੩੧।","roman":"Kalan kank patree | taje jaanu chhatree | 431 |","meaning_en":"fine heron-feathered arrows, loosed by the Kshatriyas.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੰਕ ਪਤ੍ਰੀ: arrows feathered with heron plumes. ਤਜੇ ਜਾਣੁ ਛਤ੍ਰੀ: lit. 'loosed, as it were, by Kshatriyas'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[432],"number_text":"੪੩੨।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਰੈ ਰੇਤ ਖੇਤੰ। ਨਚੈ ਭੂਤ ਪ੍ਰੇਤੰ।","roman":"Girai ret khetan | nachai bhoot pretan |","meaning_en":"(Warriors) fall in the dust of the field; ghosts and spirits dance.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰੈ ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਾਰੰ। ਤਜੈ ਬਾਣ ਧਾਰੰ। ੪੩੨।","roman":"Karai chitr chaaran | tajai baan dhaaran | 432 |","meaning_en":"(The archers) make wondrous moves and loose streams of arrows.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਚਾਰੰ: 'wondrous/graceful movements'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[433],"number_text":"੪੩੩।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਹੈ ਜੋਧ ਜੋਧੰ। ਕਰੈ ਘਾਇ ਕ੍ਰੋਧੰ।","roman":"Lahai jodh jodhan | karai ghaai krodhan |","meaning_en":"Warrior seeks out warrior; in anger they deal wounds.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਖਹੈ ਖਗ ਖਗੈ। ਉਠੈ ਝਾਲ ਅਗੈ। ੪੩੩।","roman":"Khahai khag khagai | uthai jhaal agai | 433 |","meaning_en":"Sword clashes with sword; flames fly up in front.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[434],"number_text":"੪੩੪।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੇ ਪਖਰਾਲੇ। ਚਲੇ ਬਾਲ ਆਲੇ।","roman":"Nache pakhraale | chale baal aale |","meaning_en":"Armoured horses dance; the young warriors go forth.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਖਰਾਲੇ: horses in armour (pakhar). ਬਾਲ ਆਲੇ: read as 'the young ones'; could be 'the long-haired ones'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਤ ਨਾਚੈ। ਰਣੰ ਰੰਗਿ ਰਾਚੈ। ੪੩੪।","roman":"Hase pret naachai | ranan rangi raachai | 434 |","meaning_en":"Ghosts laugh and dance, absorbed in the colour of battle.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[435],"number_text":"੪੩੫।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਚੇ ਪਾਰਬਤੀਸੰ। ਮੰਡਿਓ ਜੁਧ ਈਸੰ।","roman":"Nache paarabteesan | mandio judh eesan |","meaning_en":"Shiva, the Lord of Parbati, danced; the Lord waged war.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੰਡਿਓ ਜੁਧ ਈਸੰ: ਈਸੰ read as the Lord (Kalki); could refer to Shiva; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਸੰ ਦਿਉਸ ਕੁਧੰ। ਭਯੋ ਘੋਰ ਜੁਧੰ। ੪੩੫।","roman":"Dasan dius kudhan | bhayo ghor judhan | 435 |","meaning_en":"For ten days, in fury, a dreadful war went on.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[436],"number_text":"੪੩੬।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਰ ਬੀਰ ਤ੍ਯਾਗ੍ਯੋ। ਪਗੰ ਦ੍ਵੈਕੁ ਭਾਗ੍ਯੋ।","roman":"Punar beer tyaagyo | pagan dvaiku bhaagyo |","meaning_en":"Then the warrior (king) gave way and fled a couple of steps;","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as the king of Sambhal."},{"gurmukhi":"ਫਿਰ੍ਯੋ ਫੇਰਿ ਐਸੇ। ਕ੍ਰੋਧੀ ਸਾਂਪ ਜੈਸੇ। ੪੩੬।","roman":"Phiryo pheri aise | krodhee saanp jaise | 436 |","meaning_en":"then he turned back again like an angry snake.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[437],"number_text":"੪੩੭।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੁਨਰ ਜੁਧ ਮੰਡਿਓ। ਸਰੰ ਓਘ ਛੰਡਿਓ।","roman":"Punar judh mandio | saran ogh chhandio |","meaning_en":"Again he waged war and loosed floods of arrows.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਜੈ ਵੀਰ ਬਾਣੰ। ਮ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਆਇ ਤ੍ਰਾਣੰ। ੪੩੭।","roman":"Tajai veer baanan | mritan aai traanan | 437 |","meaning_en":"The hero loosed arrows; death came even to those in armour.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮ੍ਰਿਤੰ ਆਇ ਤ੍ਰਾਣੰ: sense unclear; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[438],"number_text":"੪੩੮।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭੈ ਸਿਧ ਦੇਖੈ। ਕਲੰਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਲੇਖੈ।","roman":"Sabhai sidh dekhai | kalankrit lekhai |","meaning_en":"All the Siddhas watch and record Kalki's deeds.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਲੰਕ੍ਰਿਤ: read as 'Kalki's deeds'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਧਨੰ ਧੰਨਿ ਜੰਪੈ। ਲਖੈ ਭੀਰ ਕੰਪੈ। ੪੩੮।","roman":"Dhanan dhanni janpai | lakhai bheer kanpai | 438 |","meaning_en":"They cry 'Blessed, blessed!'; seeing it, the cowards tremble.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਨਰਾਜ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Naraaj chhand","meaning_en":"Naraj metre.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[439],"number_text":"੪੩੯।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨਿ ਆਨਿ ਸੂਰਮਾ ਸੰਧਾਨਿ ਬਾਨ ਧਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Aani aani soormaa sandhaani baan dhaavheen |","meaning_en":"Coming on and on, the warriors charge with arrows fitted to the string;","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਝਿ ਜੂਝ ਕੈ ਮਰੈ ਸੁ ਦੇਵ ਨਾਰਿ ਪਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Roojhi joojh kai marai su dev naari paavheen |","meaning_en":"those who fight and die win the women of the gods.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਰੀਝਿ ਰੀਝਿ ਅਛਰਾ ਅਲਛ ਸੂਰਣੋ ਬਰੈਂ।","roman":"Su reejhi reejhi achhraa alachh soorno barain |","meaning_en":"Delighted, the apsaras, (themselves) unseen, wed the heroes;","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਲਛ: read as 'unseen'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪ੍ਰਬੀਨ ਬੀਨਿ ਬੀਨ ਕੈ ਸੁਧੀਨ ਪਾਨਿ ਕੈ ਧਰੈਂ। ੪੩੯।","roman":"Prabeen beeni been kai sudheen paani kai dharain | 439 |","meaning_en":"the skilful ones choose them carefully and take them by the hand into their keeping.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਧੀਨ ਪਾਨਿ ਕੈ ਧਰੈਂ: read as 'take them in hand as their own'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[440],"number_text":"੪੪੦।","page":764,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਨਧ ਬਧ ਅਧ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਬਿਰੁਧਿ ਸੂਰ ਧਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Sanadh badh adh hvai birudhi soor dhaavheen |","meaning_en":"Armed and girded, the heroes charge in enmity;","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਨਧ ਬਧ ਅਧ ਹ੍ਵੈ: read as 'armed and girded'; ਅਧ unclear."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਸਾਂਗ ਤੀਛਣੰ ਕਿ ਤਾਕਿ ਸਤ੍ਰੁ ਲਾਵਹੀਂ।","roman":"Su krodh saang teechhnan ki taaki satru laavheen |","meaning_en":"in wrath, taking aim at the foe, they strike with sharp lances.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁ ਜੂਝਿ ਜੂਝ ਕੈ ਗਿਰੈ ਅਲੂਝ ਲੂਝ ਕੈ ਹਠੀਂ।","roman":"Su joojhi joojh kai girai aloojh loojh kai hatheen |","meaning_en":"The steadfast ones fall fighting, grappling with the unyielding;","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਬੂਝ ਓਰਿ ਧਾਵਹੀ ਬਨਾਇ ਸੈਨ ਏਕਠੀਂ। ੪੪੦।","roman":"Aboojh ori dhaavhee banaai sain ektheen | 440 |","meaning_en":"gathering the army together, they charge toward the Unfathomable One.","page":764,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਬੂਝ ਓਰਿ: read as 'toward the unfathomable (Kalki)'; could mean 'heedlessly'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਸੰਗੀਤ ਭੁਜੰਗ ਪ੍ਰਯਾਤ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Sangeet bhujang prayaat chhand","meaning_en":"Sangeet Bhujang Prayat metre.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[441],"number_text":"੪੪੧।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੋਪਾ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰਾਜਾ। ਘਾਗੜਦੰ ਘੋਰੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਜਾ।","roman":"Kaagardan kopaa raagardan raajaa | ghaagardan ghore baagardan baajaa |","meaning_en":"The king grew angry; dreadful instruments sounded.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Sound-words in -ਗੜਦੰ are left untranslated. ਘੋਰੇ ਬਾਜਾ: 'dreadful music sounded', or 'horses and steeds'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਫਾਗੜਦੰ ਫੀਲੰ ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛੂਟੇ। ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੂਰੰ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੂਟੇ। ੪੪੧।","roman":"Phaagardan pheelan chhaagardan chhoote | saagardan sooran jaagardan joote | 441 |","meaning_en":"Elephants were let loose; heroes clashed.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[442],"number_text":"੪੪੨।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਜੇ ਨਾਗੜਦੰ ਨਗਾਰੇ। ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੋਧਾ ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਾਰੇ।","roman":"Baagardan baaje naagardan nagaare | jaagardan jodhaa maagardan maare |","meaning_en":"Kettle-drums sounded; warriors were slain.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਾਗੜਦੰ ਡਿਗੇ ਖਾਗੜਦੰ ਖੂਨੀ। ਚਾਗੜਦੰ ਚਉਪੈ ਦਾਗੜਦੰ ਦੂਨੀ। ੪੪੨।","roman":"Daagardan dige khaagardan khoonee | chaagardan chaupai daagardan doonee | 442 |","meaning_en":"The blood-soaked fell; zeal doubled.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[443],"number_text":"੪੪੩।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾਗੜਦੰ ਹਸੇ ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸਿਧੰ। ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭਾਜੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬ੍ਰਿਧੰ।","roman":"Haagardan hase saagardan sidhan | bhaagardan bhaaje baagardan bridhan |","meaning_en":"The Siddhas laughed; the old ones fled.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬ੍ਰਿਧੰ: 'the old (warriors)'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛੁਟੇ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤੀਰੰ। ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੁਟੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬੀਰੰ। ੪੪੩।","roman":"Chhaagardan chhute taagardan teeran | jaagardan jute baagardan beeran | 443 |","meaning_en":"Arrows were loosed; warriors clashed.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[444],"number_text":"੪੪੪।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੁਹਕੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਣੰ। ਫਾਗੜਦੰ ਫਰਕੇ ਨਾਗੜਦੰ ਨਿਸਾਣੰ।","roman":"Kaagardan kuhke baagardan baanan | phaagardan pharke naagardan nisaanan |","meaning_en":"Arrows whistled; banners fluttered.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਜੀ ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭੇਰੀ। ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੈਣੰ ਫਾਗੜਦੰ ਫੇਰੀ। ੪੪੪।","roman":"Baagardan baajee bhaagardan bheree | saagardan sainan phaagardan pheree | 444 |","meaning_en":"Bheri drums sounded; the army was turned back (to fight).","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[445],"number_text":"੪੪੫।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭੀਰੰ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੰਪੈ। ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਾਰੇ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੰਪੈ।","roman":"Bhaagardan bheeran kaagardan kanpai | maagardan maare jaagardan janpai |","meaning_en":"The cowards trembled; (the warriors) cried 'Kill!'","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛਪ੍ਰੰ ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭਾਜੇ। ਚਾਗੜਦੰ ਚਿਤੰ ਲਾਗੜਦੰ ਲਾਜੇ। ੪੪੫।","roman":"Chhaagardan chhapran bhaagardan bhaaje | chaagardan chitan laagardan laaje | 445 |","meaning_en":"Hiding, they fled, ashamed in their hearts.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਛਪ੍ਰੰ: read as 'hiding'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[446],"number_text":"੪੪੬।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛੋਰਿਓ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰਾਜੰ। ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੈਣੰ ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭਾਜਾ।","roman":"Chhaagardan chhorio raagardan raajan | saagardan sainan bhaagardan bhaajaa |","meaning_en":"The king was left alone; the army fled.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਛਾਗੜਦੰ ਛੂਟੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਣੰ। ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੋਕੀ ਦਾਗੜਦੰ ਦਿਸਾਣੰ।੪੪੬।","roman":"Chhaagardan chhoote baagardan baanan | raagardan rokee daagardan disaanan | 446 |","meaning_en":"Arrows were loosed, blocking all directions.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[447],"number_text":"੪੪੭।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਾਰੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਣੰ। ਟਾਗੜਦੰ ਟੂਟੇ ਤਾਗੜਦੰ ਤਾਣੰ।","roman":"Maagardan maare baagardan baanan | taagardan toote taagardan taanan |","meaning_en":"He struck with arrows; (the foe's) strength broke.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਾਣੰ: 'strength', or 'bows'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਾਗੜਦੰ ਲਾਗੇ ਦਾਗੜਦੰ ਦਾਹੇ। ਡਾਗੜਦੰ ਡਾਰੇ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਾਹੇ। ੪੪੭।","roman":"Laagardan laage daagardan daahe | daagardan daare baagardan baahe | 447 |","meaning_en":"The arrows struck and burned; (foes) were struck and thrown down.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[448],"number_text":"੪੪੮।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਰਖੇ ਫਾਗੜਦੰ ਫੂਲੰ। ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਿਟਿਓ ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸੂਲੰ।","roman":"Baagardan barkhe phaagardan phoolan | maagardan mitio saagardan soolan |","meaning_en":"Flowers rained down; the pain (of the world) was removed.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਗੜਦੰ ਮਾਰਿਓ ਭਾਗੜਦੰ ਭੂਪੰ। ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕੋਪੇ ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਰੂਪੰ। ੪੪੮।","roman":"Maagardan maario bhaagardan bhoopan | kaagardan kope raagardan roopan | 448 |","meaning_en":"The king was slain by the One of wrathful form.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"Read as Kalki slaying the king of Sambhal."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[449],"number_text":"੪੪੯।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜੰਪੈ ਪਾਗੜਦੰ ਪਾਨੰ। ਦਾਗੜਦੰ ਦੇਵੰ ਆਗੜਦੰ ਆਨੰ।","roman":"Jaagardan janpai paagardan paanan | daagardan devan aagardan aanan |","meaning_en":"The gods came and, with folded hands, sang praises.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਗੜਦੰ ਸਿਧੰ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ। ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਨਾਏ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕਬਿਤੰ। ੪੪੯।","roman":"Saagardan sidhan kaagardan krit | baagardan banaae kaagardan kabitan | 449 |","meaning_en":"The Siddhas made poems of his deeds.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[450],"number_text":"੪੫੦।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਗੜਦੰ ਗਾਵੈ ਕਾਗੜਦੰ ਕਬਿਤੰ। ਧਾਗੜਦੰ ਧਾਵੈ ਬਾਗੜਦੰ ਬਿਤ੍ਰੰ।","roman":"Raagardan gaavai kaagardan kabitan | dhaagardan dhaavai baagardan bitran |","meaning_en":"They sing the poems; they run to give wealth (in offering).","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਧਾਵੈ ਬਿਤ੍ਰੰ: unclear; ਬਿਤ੍ਰੰ read as 'wealth'; uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾਗੜਦੰ ਹੋਹੀ ਜਾਗੜਦੰ ਜਾਤ੍ਰਾ। ਨਾਗੜਦੰ ਨਾਚੈ ਪਾਗੜਦੰ ਪਾਤ੍ਰਾ। ੪੫੦।","roman":"Haagardan hohee jaagardan jaatraa | naagardan naachai paagardan paatraa | 450 |","meaning_en":"Festive processions are held; dancers dance.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਾਤ੍ਰਾ: pilgrimage or festive procession. ਪਾਤ੍ਰਾ: dancers."}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","gurmukhi":"ਪਾਧਰੀ ਛੰਦ","roman":"Paadhree chhand","meaning_en":"Padhri metre.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"type":"verse","number":[451],"number_text":"੪੫੧।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਭਰ ਨਰੇਸ ਮਾਰਿਓ ਨਿਦਾਨ। ਢੋਲੰ ਮਿਦੰਗ ਬਜੇ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਨ।","roman":"Sanbhar nares maario nidaan | dholan midang baje pramaan |","meaning_en":"At last the king of Sambhal was slain; dhol drums and mridangs sounded in full measure.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਜੇ ਸੁਬੀਰ ਤਜਿ ਜੁਧ ਤ੍ਰਾਸਿ। ਤਜਿ ਸਸਤ੍ਰ ਸਰਬ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਚਿਤਿ ਨਿਰਾਸ। ੪੫੧।","roman":"Bhaaje subeer taji judh traasi | taji sasatr sarab hvai chiti niraas | 451 |","meaning_en":"The warriors fled, leaving the battle in terror, abandoning all their weapons, hopeless at heart.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[452],"number_text":"੪੫੨।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਰਖੰਤ ਦੇਵ ਪੁਹਪਣ ਬ੍ਰਿਸਟ। ਹੋਵੰਤ ਜਗ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਸੁ ਇਸਟ।","roman":"Barkhant dev puhpan brisat | hovant jag jah tah su isat |","meaning_en":"The gods rain down showers of flowers; everywhere sacrifices are made to the chosen deity.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪੂਜੰਤ ਲਾਗ ਦੇਵੀ ਕਰਾਲ। ਹੋਵੰਤ ਸਿਧ ਕਾਰਜ ਸੁ ਢਾਲ। ੪੫੨।","roman":"Poojant laag devee karaal | hovant sidh kaaraj su dhaal | 452 |","meaning_en":"People begin to worship the fearsome goddess; their tasks are accomplished well.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁ ਢਾਲ: read as 'in good fashion'; uncertain."}]},{"type":"verse","number":[453],"number_text":"੪੫੩।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਵੰਤ ਦਾਨ ਜਾਚਕ ਦੁਰੰਤ। ਭਾਖੰਤ ਕ੍ਰਿਤ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਬਿਅੰਤ।","roman":"Paavant daan jaachak durant | bhaakhant krit jah tah biant |","meaning_en":"Beggars receive gifts beyond measure; everywhere (people) tell of (his) endless deeds.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਗ ਧੂਪ ਦੀਪ ਜਗਿ ਆਦਿ ਦਾਨ। ਹੋਵੰਤ ਹੋਮ ਬੇਦਨ ਬਿਧਾਨ। ੪੫੩।","roman":"Jag dhoop deep jagi aadi daan | hovant hom bedan bidhaan | 453 |","meaning_en":"In the world there are incense, lamps, sacrifices and gifts; fire-offerings are made by the rites of the Vedas.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[454],"number_text":"੪੫੪।","page":765,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੂਜੰਤ ਲਾਗ ਦੇਬੀ ਦੁਰੰਤ। ਤਜਿ ਸਰਬ ਕਾਮ ਜਹ ਤਹ ਮਹੰਤ।","roman":"Poojant laag debee durant | taji sarab kaam jah tah mahant |","meaning_en":"People worship the mighty goddess; everywhere the mahants give up all desire.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਧੀ ਧੁਜਾਨ ਪਰਮੰ ਪ੍ਰਚੰਡ। ਪ੍ਰਚੁਰਿਓ ਸੁ ਧਰਮ ਖੰਡੇ ਅਖੰਡ। ੪੫੪।","roman":"Baadhee dhujaan parman prachand | prachurio su dharam khande akhand | 454 |","meaning_en":"Supreme, mighty banners were raised; dharma spread, and those who had been unbroken were broken.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਖੰਡੇ ਅਖੰਡ: read as 'the unbroken were shattered'; could mean '(dharma spread) through all the regions, unbroken'; uncertain."}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਬਚਿਤ੍ਰ ਨਾਟਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥੇ ਕਲਕੀ ਅਵਤਾਰ ਸੰਭਰ ਨਰੇਸ ਬਧਹ ਬਿਜਯ ਭਏਤ","roman":"Iti sree bachitr naatak granthe kalkee avtaar sanbhar nares badhah bijay bhaet","meaning_en":"Here ends, in the granth Bachittar Natak, in Kalki Avtar, (the chapter) named 'The slaying of the king of Sambhal: victory achieved',","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੰਭਰ ਨਰੇਸ: the king of Sambhal."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਮ ਪ੍ਰਥਮ ਧਿਆਇ ਬਰਨਨੰ ਸਮਾਪਤੰ ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ। ੧।","roman":"Naam pratham dhiaai barannan samaaptan satu subham satu | 1 |","meaning_en":"the description of the first chapter, completed. All is true and auspicious. 1.","page":765,"meaning_status":"draft"}],"page":765,"number":[1]}});
